 enforces\nSUPER_ADMIN at the router level and reuses the Phase 2 auth/trial\nservices; frontend adds auth/toast context, protected routing, and the\nsuper-admin pages, plus a placeholder /admin landing page for shop\nowners ahead of Phase 4.\n\n70/70 backend tests passing, frontend lint and build clean.","tree":{"sha":"d83c4b7c2ff5f7081ef6a9695f543d89d7430b62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ImHarsh11/digital-catalog-saas/git/trees/d83c4b7c2ff5f7081ef6a9695f543d89d7430b62"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ImHarsh11/digital-catalog-saas/git/commits/bedf92d072e01108b409f298272cab194ff15d4f","verification":{"payload":"tree d83c4b7c2ff5f7081ef6a9695f543d89d7430b62\nparent 1314d726d3a8e392279ac157ea221622d31818ac\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787245120 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787245120 +0000\n\nPhase 3: Super Admin shop CRUD, activation, dashboard stats\n\nAdds the Super Admin surface end to end: shop creation (auto-provisions\na 14-day trial and the owner account in one request), listing, detail\nview with stats and recent activity, profile editing, and\nactivate/deactivate, plus dashboard aggregate counts. Backend enforces\nSUPER_ADMIN at the router level and reuses the Phase 2 auth/trial\nservices; frontend adds auth/toast context, protected routing, and the\nsuper-admin pages, plus a placeholder /admin landing page for shop\nowners ahead of Phase 4.\n\n70/70 backend tests passing, frontend lint and build clean.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMp5bdMZ\nC1x8QRYmrmdXR7nGOunK2vtG03o5mMO8wzMmu7Pkt1ZfhFckRakXFFNIFdUXmp0ocXsSjOQGnIDB\naQY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-22T04:57:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ImHarsh11/digital-catalog-saas/commit/bedf92d072e01108b409f298272cab194ff15d4f","node_id":"C_kwDOUAQopdoAKGJlZGY5MmQwNzJlMDExMDhiNDA5ZjI5ODI3MmNhYjE5NGZmMTVkNGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ImHarsh11/digital-catalog-saas/commit/1314d726d3a8e392279ac157ea221622d31818ac","sha":"1314d726d3a8e392279ac157ea221622d31818ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ImHarsh11/digital-catalog-saas/commits/1314d726d3a8e392279ac157ea221622d31818ac"}],"sha":"bedf92d072e01108b409f298272cab194ff15d4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ImHarsh11/digital-catalog-saas/commits/bedf92d072e01108b409f298272cab194ff15d4f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ImHarsh11/digital-catalog-saas/commits/1314d726d3a8e392279ac157ea221622d31818ac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T16:21:03Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T16:21:03Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Phase 2: database models, migrations, seed data, JWT auth, and RBAC\n\n- SQLAlchemy models for all 7 tables from the spec (users, shops,\n  categories, products, product_images, catalog_activity, customer_events)\n  with native Postgres enums, shop-scoped uniqueness constraints, and\n  cascade/restrict FK behavior matched to how each relationship should\n  behave (e.g. a category with products can''t be deleted out from under\n  them).\n- Initial Alembic migration, autogenerated then hand-fixed so its\n  downgrade() actually drops the enum types it creates (autogenerate\n  silently omits this, which breaks a downgrade/upgrade round-trip).\n  Verified upgrade -> downgrade -> upgrade cleanly against the dev DB.\n- bcrypt password hashing (used directly, not via passlib, which has a\n  known incompatibility with bcrypt >=4.1), JWT issuance/verification,\n  POST /api/auth/login and GET /api/auth/me.\n- Reusable role-based auth dependencies (require_role,\n  get_current_shop_owner) and a verify_shop_ownership guard for Phase 3/4\n  endpoints to enforce shop data isolation (404s rather than 403s, so it\n  doesn''t confirm another shop''s resource exists).\n- 14-day trial calculation service (days remaining / active / expired /\n  label).\n- Idempotent seed script: super admin, one demo shop on a live 14-day\n  trial, a shop owner, 5 categories, and 30 demo products with mixed\n  status and mixed created_by (shop owner vs. catalog team) to exercise\n  the catalog-service billing groundwork.\n- 46 pytest tests against a dedicated digital_catalog_test database\n  (transaction-per-test isolation): auth (valid/invalid/inactive login,\n  unauthorized access, role restrictions), shop isolation, model\n  constraints, trial math, password hashing, JWT edge cases.\n\nNo changes to the Phase 1 frontend or its architecture.","tree":{"sha":"ecfcddc196135884c047873305a4babbc0821782","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ImHarsh11/digital-catalog-saas/git/trees/ecfcddc196135884c047873305a4babbc0821782"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ImHarsh11/digital-catalog-saas/git/commits/1314d726d3a8e392279ac157ea221622d31818ac","verification":{"payload":"tree ecfcddc196135884c047873305a4babbc0821782\nparent 0332a13989d1593f29cc74db4d88134f3ae39fc3\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787242863 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787242863 +0000\n\nPhase 2: database models, migrations, seed data, JWT auth, and RBAC\n\n- SQLAlchemy models for all 7 tables from the spec (users, shops,\n  categories, products, product_images, catalog_activity, customer_events)\n  with native Postgres enums, shop-scoped uniqueness constraints, and\n  cascade/restrict FK behavior matched to how each relationship should\n  behave (e.g. a category with products can''t be deleted out from under\n  them).\n- Initial Alembic migration, autogenerated then hand-fixed so its\n  downgrade() actually drops the enum types it creates (autogenerate\n  silently omits this, which breaks a downgrade/upgrade round-trip).\n  Verified upgrade -> downgrade -> upgrade cleanly against the dev DB.\n- bcrypt password hashing (used directly, not via passlib, which has a\n  known incompatibility with bcrypt >=4.1), JWT issuance/verification,\n  POST /api/auth/login and GET /api/auth/me.\n- Reusable role-based auth dependencies (require_role,\n  get_current_shop_owner) and a verify_shop_ownership guard for Phase 3/4\n  endpoints to enforce shop data isolation (404s rather than 403s, so it\n  doesn''t confirm another shop''s resource exists).\n- 14-day trial calculation service (days remaining / active / expired /\n  label).\n- Idempotent seed script: super admin, one demo shop on a live 14-day\n  trial, a shop owner, 5 categories, and 30 demo products with mixed\n  status and mixed created_by (shop owner vs. catalog team) to exercise\n  the catalog-service billing groundwork.\n- 46 pytest tests against a dedicated digital_catalog_test database\n  (transaction-per-test isolation): auth (valid/invalid/inactive login,\n  unauthorized access, role restrictions), shop isolation, model\n  constraints, trial math, password hashing, JWT edge cases.\n\nNo changes to the Phase 1 frontend or its architecture.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCwzncxb\nMeCQny8e5vaC9o8cjW2mOgZcEORcWB8oecDyOkl7IeSBIi0XgiwoNetUSYkWeiPeCqL1K2Fi55P/\n+wU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-22T04:57:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://