ts":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/kageyama20/bimdec-document-system/commit/60d8ea714e118164a09e484dcbe6f696d03b2f34","sha":"60d8ea714e118164a09e484dcbe6f696d03b2f34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kageyama20/bimdec-document-system/commits/60d8ea714e118164a09e484dcbe6f696d03b2f34"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/kageyama20/bimdec-document-system/commit/1732442b42a426b3d64b11edd5b8249dced0e544","sha":"1732442b42a426b3d64b11edd5b8249dced0e544","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kageyama20/bimdec-document-system/commits/1732442b42a426b3d64b11edd5b8249dced0e544"}],"sha":"d104322ed5ed6cceda9aef27814ac293ac0afcb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kageyama20/bimdec-document-system/commits/d104322ed5ed6cceda9aef27814ac293ac0afcb4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23021923?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ldtan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ldtan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ldtan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ldtan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ldtan","id":23021923,"login":"ldtan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDIxOTIz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ldtan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ldtan/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ldtan/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ldtan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ldtan/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ldtan","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kageyama20/bimdec-document-system/commits/1732442b42a426b3d64b11edd5b8249dced0e544/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T10:42:46Z","email":"liel.onairam.tan@gmail.com","name":"Liel Onairam Tan"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T10:42:46Z","email":"liel.onairam.tan@gmail.com","name":"Liel Onairam Tan"},"message":"Move the frontend to Vite + React and deploy both services from Render\n\nThe repo root was the deployed site: eight hand-written HTML pages sharing\nportal.css and three classic-script globals, published by Netlify with no\nbuild step, while the email service ran separately on Render. This puts the\nwhole frontend in frontend/ as a Vite + React SPA and describes both halves\nin one Blueprint, so a push deploys everything and the infrastructure lives\nin git rather than across two dashboards.\n\nThe frontend becomes a Render Static Site: free, CDN-served, and unlike a\nfree web service it never sleeps. Next.js with SSR would have needed a free\nweb service that sleeps after 15 minutes and cold-starts for ~50s.\n\nRouting and session\n- Clean paths (/login, /admin/documents, ...) with redirects from the old\n  .html URLs in both the router and render.yaml, preserving ?role=.\n- DB.requireSession() is deleted, not ported. It decided where to redirect\n  by regex-matching /admin/ or /client/ in the pathname, which cannot\n  survive client-side routing. SessionProvider now resolves the session once\n  for the whole app and ProtectedRoute guards on it, rendering a splash\n  while the check is in flight so a signed-in admin is not bounced to login\n  on first paint.\n\nThe document generator\nPorted, not rewritten. It addresses ~180 element ids directly, autosaves by\nwalking .editor input[id] and reading el.value, and paginates by measuring\nlive element heights against an A4 page; React state would fight all three.\nThe markup is now real JSX, converted through an HTML parser rather than by\nhand, and renders exactly once - documentsController.js owns the DOM inside\nit, as the original page did. The invariants are documented in both files.\nInline on* attributes became data-on* dispatched by delegation, since React\ndrops string handlers and the line-item rows are still built as HTML\nstrings. html2pdf is an npm dependency loaded on demand, which also keeps\n640KB out of the initial bundle. Browser-save debris removed: the\n\"saved from url\" comment, the broken ./index_files/css2 link, the nordpass\nchrome-extension @font-face block, and two injected aria-live divs.\n\nThe generator''s 580-line stylesheet is scoped under .docgen. It and\nportal.css both define :root custom properties, both style body, and they\ncollide on .appbar, .appbar-inner, .field, .row2, .send-email-box,\n.send-email-row and .send-status - harmless when only one loaded per page,\nbroken when both live in one document. CSS Modules could not work here: the\nclass names are referenced from hardcoded ids and from HTML built as\nstrings. @page and the html/body print rules stay document-level because\nthey cannot be nested.\n\nTwo bugs fixed in passing, both noted in comments: the preview zoom is\nrestored in a finally block (it stuck at 100% when html2pdf threw), and the\ndraft is saved on route-away, since beforeunload does not fire on SPA\nnavigation.\n\nDeployment\nrender.yaml creates both services on the free tier. Note that nothing was\never deployed at bimdec-email.onrender.com - Render answers that hostname\nwith x-render-routing: no-server, and backend/.env only ever allowed\nlocalhost:5500. The frontend calls the backend from the browser, so it needs\nthe public URL at build time and Render assigns that at creation;\nfromService exposes private-network hostnames only, so the first deploy\ntakes two passes. The header comment explains it.\n\nVITE_API_BASE gives the backend URL a build-time default. Without it, moving\norigin would wipe every admin''s localStorage and leave the Email page and\nthe Send-to-email buttons dead with no explanation. The API key stays\nlocalStorage-only - a build-time value would be readable in the published\nbundle.\n\nVerified in a browser, not just built: all routes render with no console\nerrors, legacy bookmarks keep ?role=, guarded routes bounce to the right\nlogin tab, and on the generator tab switching, live preview, line items and\ntotals, lock toggles, zoom, the print modal and autosave all work. A real\n880KB PDF renders from the production bundle with all three letterhead\nlogos loading, and .appbar-inner measures 1200px outside .docgen against\n1680px inside, proving the scoping holds.\n\nThe old root HTML is left in place so Netlify keeps serving the live site\nuntil Render is verified; deleting it is a separate, revertible commit.\n\nOne thing to check before cutover: documents.html asked for IBM Plex 35\ntimes but its font link pointed at ./index_files/css2, which never existed,\nso every PDF so far rendered in Arial. portal.css loads IBM Plex globally,\nwhich changes text metrics and therefore where paginateSheet breaks pages.\nDiff a generated PDF against one from the old site and retune PAGE_H /\nPAD_TOP / PAD_BOTTOM if the page count moved.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XvLYXmS9GLtxnrJ5dnMurL","tree":{"sha":"cb2572ab517e3584efeb060752b8fbf243b611dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kageyama20/bimdec-document-system/git/trees/cb2572ab517e3584efeb060752b8fbf243b611dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kageyama20/bimdec-document-system/git/commits/1732442b42a426b3d64b11edd5b8249dced0e544","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23021923?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ldtan/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ldtan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ldtan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ldtan/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ldtan","id":23021923,"login":"ldtan","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDIxOTIz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ldtan/orgs","received_events_url":"https://ap