hi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commits/ca52861436c3a5798d40991d88a7313a2307a64c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T09:40:36Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T09:52:22Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump hex-service-kit to v0.0.11: trace only through the collector\n\nDecision D1: build_tracer refuses an unset OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT instead of\nexporting straight to Cloud Trace around the collector''s GenAI-content redaction, and\ntakes no project argument any more.\n\n- pyproject.toml and the locks: hex-service-kit v0.0.11 (ec2d724). The only other lock\n  movement is opentelemetry-exporter-gcp-trace and its dependencies leaving with the\n  kit''s otel extra, where this repo resolved it.\n- adapters/gcp/tracer.py: build_tracer(service=...) only.\n- tests/contract: the managed tracer''s documented refusal is now\n  CollectorEndpointRequiredError; on-prem keys off a new onprem_refuses field; a new\n  test keeps the old guarantee that with a collector configured and no SDK a span\n  degrades to a no-op.\n- settings, config, Terraform variable and adoption notes stop describing a direct\n  Cloud Trace path that no longer exists.\n\nRelocked without --upgrade: fleet-deps bump-commons'' --upgrade relock moved 0\nunrelated pins here, and those were reverted.","tree":{"sha":"efe3f83554d7455221612eb2230cc11e78d70bba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/git/trees/efe3f83554d7455221612eb2230cc11e78d70bba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/git/commits/ca52861436c3a5798d40991d88a7313a2307a64c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commit/ca52861436c3a5798d40991d88a7313a2307a64c","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh5LtoAKGNhNTI4NjE0MzZjM2E1Nzk4ZDQwOTkxZDg4YTczMTNhMjMwN2E2NGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commit/26e0dbe277634f56890c2099cab0266b9f2837dc","sha":"26e0dbe277634f56890c2099cab0266b9f2837dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commits/26e0dbe277634f56890c2099cab0266b9f2837dc"}],"sha":"ca52861436c3a5798d40991d88a7313a2307a64c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commits/ca52861436c3a5798d40991d88a7313a2307a64c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commits/26e0dbe277634f56890c2099cab0266b9f2837dc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T04:37:53Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T04:40:38Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Screen the investigation through a guardrail port, fail closed on Model Armor\n\nRule R1 (plan phase P3): adopt the fixed guardrail design from hex-service-template. A\nGuardrailPort with a local heuristic, a Model Armor adapter that allows only on NO_MATCH_FOUND\nwith invocation_result SUCCESS (read by enum name, never str()), and an on-prem placeholder that\nrefuses; the ATOINVEST_GUARDRAIL three-state switch with a disabled binding logged at startup;\nmodel_armor settings with a real default template, the regional host and a sanitize deadline;\nand a managed boot refusal when the guardrail is on with no template named.\n\nInvestigationService screens INPUT each caller key (masked, so the guardrail never sees the raw\nidentifier) before anything is fetched or scored, then the narration prompt as the narrator\nreceives it, and OUTPUT the narrative after the groundedness fallback. NarratorPort.narrate now\ntakes that screened prompt, so a model bound behind it sends exactly the text the screen passed.\nA refused key is audited BLOCKED with no severity and raises: the API answers 400, the CLI exits\n1, the agent tool returns a block. Narration is optional by design here, so a refused prompt or\nnarrative is audited BLOCKED and replaced by fixed \"narration withheld\" text while the engine''s\nresult stands. A guardrail that cannot decide is audited and its error propagates.\n\nTerraform: model_armor.tf (google-beta, template_metadata, the malicious-URI filter and\nmulti-language detection gated on model_armor_full_capabilities, partial invocations never\ntreated as complete), roles/modelarmor.user, the API enabled and inside the perimeter, the\nswitch on Cloud Run, a guardrail_blocks log metric, and tftest runs for both capability states.\ngoogle-cloud-modelarmor joins the gcp extra and requirements-gcp.lock; scripts/demo.py tours the\nguardrail exit call. Tests cover the switch, the heuristic, every screen and refusal path, the\nsurfaces, and the mapping against the real SDK enums and their SDK-free mirrors.","tree":{"sha":"3e022f4bc32ce62be50c99c9086acdf0b9183f9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/git/trees/3e022f4