":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commits/c3cd93eab6fe7a017d1d4f9068a92997f0e5dabb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T01:09:13Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T01:09:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Adopt the commons claim half in the IAP adapter (#14)\n\nresolve() no longer builds a Principal. Everything after the signature check\nis one hex_service_kit.federation.principal_from_iap_claims call under a\nreviewed FederationPolicy, and the cryptography stays in the adapter because\nthe kit''s core is stdlib with zero runtime dependencies and verifies nothing.\n\nThe policy states tenant_from_hosted_domain as an opt-in rather than leaving\nit to a fallback: this deployment configures no domain map and IAP already\nrestricts the audience to one organisation, so the hd claim IS the tenant id.\nLeft off, these same assertions resolve to no tenant at all, which is\nfail-closed and closed for every verified user, and no offline gate would see\nit because the local profile never constructs this adapter.\n\nExecuting the commons against this adapter over the same claim sets, rather\nthan reading it, found two behaviour changes. Both are recorded rather than\nnormalised away: assurance now prefers an acr claim where the shipped tail\nhardcoded \"iap\", and the tenant is lower-cased where the shipped tail passed\nhd through with only .strip().\n\ntests/unit/test_iap_claim_half.py was red first in three stages and red again\nagainst three deliberate defects afterwards. The counts are in\ndocs/practices-audit.md under C1.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"3a5c898061e2c511f30f4aea41199193521da362","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/git/trees/3a5c898061e2c511f30f4aea41199193521da362"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/git/commits/c3cd93eab6fe7a017d1d4f9068a92997f0e5dabb","verification":{"payload":"tree 3a5c898061e2c511f30f4aea41199193521da362\nparent f9966781f9769400a42e48af7ec8d00054e993b2\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787706553 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787706553 +0800\n\nAdopt the commons claim half in the IAP adapter (#14)\n\nresolve() no longer builds a Principal. Everything after the signature check\nis one hex_service_kit.federation.principal_from_iap_claims call under a\nreviewed FederationPolicy, and the cryptography stays in the adapter because\nthe kit''s core is stdlib with zero runtime dependencies and verifies nothing.\n\nThe policy states tenant_from_hosted_domain as an opt-in rather than leaving\nit to a fallback: this deployment configures no domain map and IAP already\nrestricts the audience to one organisation, so the hd claim IS the tenant id.\nLeft off, these same assertions resolve to no tenant at all, which is\nfail-closed and closed for every verified user, and no offline gate would see\nit because the local profile never constructs this adapter.\n\nExecuting the commons against this adapter over the same claim sets, rather\nthan reading it, found two behaviour changes. Both are recorded rather than\nnormalised away: assurance now prefers an acr claim where the shipped tail\nhardcoded \"iap\", and the tenant is lower-cased where the shipped tail passed\nhd through with only .strip().\n\ntests/unit/test_iap_claim_half.py was red first in three stages and red again\nagainst three deliberate defects afterwards. The counts are in\ndocs/practices-audit.md under C1.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjjy5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABj8QACMDTL5kjjnAxNJfMZolSIBJ\nxKr1wRgEzCkvdni91JN12/0horXHXcqk+DqbCYO7jXsxuMccv7hAMSN3t2/W2wXV\nmRAp2nvvqQ/BX0eB/zrqQYaFt1imhnF1kWjmsev0QUZOCtmRlZyK8ZJS3x4XrQDD\nEbyAPIGGGSB5nimX5T9w3yP6GQRL4na+WOFF3kyLTzNDpVQKqYNsTpBYFdl4FDmg\nqIDSpl6U57uoXPVvokOomKlTsxHmGGEM0x4U4Mvh7kukCFb9Cm63OieJO+Utl97T\n/rhEDWlj6XIJN5PO4lRROnbRYxGOl0XJoqAmYC3QH5EvJxwycmShX1EHaQlN2uSq\n9vpOMtojdFPpEFpIag8y2HgX50jUc2/l21s7veMOjvK8YdSRs2iYCCL+7IJbkENn\nFsyD7QFv3gcBCr4OP05BW2ggpvfX3jZcly77hA4PCUhHJU91n19zntZhd+0oou4L\nixcuoEoS4ElcoEplleXRtQnFT3UvqOH1KZB0i2Tdul73CkEOj4wbq4K+IuS3rLMO\nfGCR6ICiqXb7vftQ6G6v+r9tYiQ+JgaI5UiqA9VSWDkAKCCPJEHH456VzgJ4t+a6\n+CzeZJL7aWOgQ6hoR3Gg7qik6uZKYhmFh0Bspfpp+IBJKFiBmEztnahSklYBkaMp\nOM0RMyJHmaoqHfj7ufwA\n=2f5G\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T01:09:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commit/c3cd93eab6fe7a017d1d4f9068a92997f0e5dabb","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh5LtoAKGMzY2Q5M2VhYjZmZTdhMDE3ZDFkNGY5MDY4YTkyOTk3ZjBlNWRhYmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commit/f9966781f9769400a42e48af7ec8d00054e993b2","sha":"f9966781f9769400a42e48af7ec8d00054e993b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commits/f9966781f9769400a42e48af7ec8d00054e993b2"}],"sha":"c3cd93eab6fe7a017d1d4f9068a92997f0e5dabb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commits/c3cd93eab6fe7a017d1d4f9068a92997f0e5dabb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commits/f9966781f9769400a42e48af7ec8d00054e993b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:46:16Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:46:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Pin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#13)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","tree":{"sha":"7c700def01bf3d4769811833e903f814de957008","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/git/trees/7c700def01bf3d4769811833e903f814de957008"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/git/commits/f9966781f9769400a42e48af7ec8d00054e993b2","verification":{"payload":"tree 7c700def01bf3d4769811833e903f814de957008\nparent fcd2686e9b5a46a59940eb5bc54d112dcdc8ae88\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787672776 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787672776 +0800\n\nPin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#13)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbjICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAq1wQAG4kqMf/iIoevTz2Be6s5enY\nsy0K3XhzBYRTWAKOKvcZGHD9sAz08jIgrevChqhnOYIoBemtUqigyVmJAx+ZmlWg\nOw+zfSr7awSTnFLtXlI940S0pGcsSWj3OV5BCfXQL/UgHB4VqXqzkVptLVRVCWsd\nEsffwwZhHr1O1TcV4kXS/D8z5hytxKcXH4Yn2wMwwZozPhLn9pVpVTI5Cm/SDecm\nN/4gZuLwHx0Zd1/+cgf6dQF5ugcmf7tJsy5X2FnpcidxkzeIJIzyV09+AQL66VqN\nspuu2+3atMUnaa9IQN6oblFRkBMGMRByhkXxp8JK2xxLNArSrffzrJmdz3ZUJuHJ\nIDuscAYxyRgavpIqe6gFoqouknifmNbvcMf7kajT63XlgScL5veNOwTqI0fdlH/E\nEwhOZB7VanEi91D9HsJ7kkAQ83cIMDVQYDvh4+vWH8/uWcnWfd8/5duPrJXsWLD3\nKsihMOUGQpGluYPfJoindKnmz+yM3lkneZi0SrDW/iL7ExY1VOl1Bhen2Mf3ZWKw\nlrdAdHYnf9/DO77hAXV+CpqeLBbS380oOjypAYu5BXKaZPefspt9XJ9/LBy2X1Vr\nMkJvlqnbzNPn4APJx4EfkJ3PpR1fluiCyF6nJJFCbR8KvWbSdmJmooyh2LfHBJNv\n8mDe/lUoHNg/mhTRnguQ\n=8/YF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T15:46:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commit/f9966781f9769400a42e48af7ec8d00054e993b2","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh5LtoAKGY5OTY2NzgxZjk3Njk0MDBhNDJlNDhhZjdlYzhkMDAwNTRlOTkzYjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commit/fcd2686e9b5a46a59940eb5bc54d112dcdc8ae88","sha":"fcd2686e9b5a46a59940eb5bc54d112dcdc8ae88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commits/fcd2686e9b5a46a59940eb5bc54d112dcdc8ae88"}],"sha":"f9966781f9769400a42e48af7ec8d00054e993b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commits/f9966781f9769400a42e48af7ec8d00054e993b2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commits/fcd2686e9b5a46a59940eb5bc54d112dcdc8ae88/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:11:25Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:11:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Bind the IAP transport facts to hex-service-kit v0.0.3 (#12)\n\nThe assertion header, the issuer and the key set URL were declared here as literals, and the\nsame three literals are declared again in every repository that verifies an IAP assertion. That\nis one security decision written down once per repo, and a copy that drifts stays green: a\nliteral always agrees with itself. They are now rebound from hex_service_kit.federation.\n\nObserved failing first. Re-declaring the header while leaving the import in place is caught\nearlier by ruff F401, so the case only a test can see is the literal re-declared AND the import\ndropped. On that run \"ruff check\" reported \"All checks passed\" and the only failure was the new\ntest, reading ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assert'' against the kit''s ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assertion''. The existing\nliteral test stays, because it catches the other defect, a typo in the published value.\n\nPin moved to v0.0.3 and relocked with org-metadata scripts/fleet-deps.py refresh, which pins the\ncommit v0.0.3 dereferences to (d28baa1c) rather than the annotated tag object. No lockfile was\nhand-edited. v0.0.2 to v0.0.3 moves no dependency; it adds FederationPolicy.tenant_from_hosted_domain.\n\nThis change does NOT adopt principal_from_iap_claims. Executed against this adapter on a shared\nclaim set, with tenant_from_hosted_domain enabled, the kit still disagrees on four axes, so the\ntenant and principal half stays local for now with the reasons recorded in the wave-2 report.\n\nGate: make gate, exit 0, 462 passed, 1 skipped, 2 deselected, eval GATE PASS.","tree":{"sha":"f1f16741de24f025df377c56e115f291443f0056","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/git/trees/f1f16741de24f025df377c56e115f291443f0056"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/git/commits/fcd2686e9b5a46a59940eb5bc54d112dcdc8ae88","verification":{"payload":"tree f1f16741de24f025df377c56e115f291443f0056\nparent ca41916e91d959e03d663b49b460380df5209394\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787670685 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787670685 +0800\n\nBind the IAP transport facts to hex-service-kit v0.0.3 (#12)\n\nThe assertion header, the issuer and the key set URL were declared here as literals, and the\nsame three literals are declared again in every repository that verifies an IAP assertion. That\nis one security decision written down once per repo, and a copy that drifts stays green: a\nliteral always agrees with itself. They are now rebound from hex_service_kit.federation.\n\nObserved failing first. Re-declaring the header while leaving the import in place is caught\nearlier by ruff F401, so the case only a test can see is the literal re-declared AND the import\ndropped. On that run \"ruff check\" reported \"All checks passed\" and the only failure was the new\ntest, reading ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assert'' against the kit''s ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assertion''. The existing\nliteral test stays, because it catches the other defect, a typo in the published value.\n\nPin moved to v0.0.3 and relocked with org-metadata scripts/fleet-deps.py refresh, which pins the\ncommit v0.0.3 dereferences to (d28baa1c) rather than the annotated tag object. No lockfile was\nhand-edited. v0.0.2 to v0.0.3 moves no dependency; it adds FederationPolicy.tenant_from_hosted_domain.\n\nThis change does NOT adopt principal_from_iap_claims. Executed against this adapter on a shared\nclaim set, with tenant_from_hosted_domain enabled, the kit still disagrees on four axes, so the\ntenant and principal half stays local for now with the reasons recorded in the wave-2 report.\n\nGate: make gate, exit 0, 462 passed, 1 skipped, 2 deselected, eval GATE PASS.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbCdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzTYQACgOfHtML+QemrDkGI3Zak6N\nad1qwE/xT71ukzRa6OAocwVD+FhGCaoBF+Ed7B52UHUECYE8SilfkovJ0LxbgQX+\nABXAee0XVDyK6Q94gPbfjWeMjCO7+O1QhxZa0TSWLX5zBCy4C1wjnjyPUInXlwD2\nM4uBdzKu9r1InHhVuokzLF6rpIGNOc0n4zlQhIDA9TqOG9PigQ27z+FY225u6u8M\nUqmIxgh9R6xBgrFMwDB1rr7srDj6BVQaXvKbGvYAvBr3XJKufbv531a8KHrfupXa\nhC1su9nmKAaekiBBpWs8P0EiajZCYXkN6JR4CyxC48uOhF7ffws9HfUt7XCTFxUw\niEa2LIzNQU32Z5wIMAaq0sS+oQhQBLOwUhIVgqRVnIlu0FjYx7Kczb1+xxpjmu4M\npbLD8iUpV54nc40SF+QxNG2xSm/FNCdJqZX8Y22hpDjC1kL0+r99RyPg/OZqpSC/\n4msHShnQuQR9qgCSmlmkM1Nq8cBepDAHWdSBjRaQUlhnxpUwDynwCGdAfyJO/aRg\nvpJ8Mm1Nl9ooVmyYYVdSbk6xn947fWiup/BAs2u8KZmdZG9tKPd/ENJyGyqoDOC1\noaXLN1E2vpAw6noXABnLpKdpJLUc78NiMrKgUFawRJX4xToSGqfwHDSTNAERYFO7\n+G8vZ86+WqOhZnj5rv0G\n=70rl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T15:11:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commit/fcd2686e9b5a46a59940eb5bc54d112dcdc8ae88","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh5LtoAKGZjZDI2ODZlOWI1YTQ2YTU5OTQwZWI1YmM1NGQxMTJkY2RjOGFlODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commit/ca41916e91d959e03d663b49b460380df5209394","sha":"ca41916e91d959e03d663b49b460380df5209394","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commits/ca41916e91d959e03d663b49b460380df5209394"}],"sha":"fcd2686e9b5a46a59940eb5bc54d112dcdc8ae88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commits/fcd2686e9b5a46a59940eb5bc54d112dcdc8ae88"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commits/ca41916e91d959e03d663b49b460380df5209394/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T07:54:20Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T07:54:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Re-point the IAP negative matrix at the refusals the verifier actually raises (#10)\n\nThe module skipped wherever google-auth was absent, which is every SDK-free gate, so\nnothing had compared its expectations against the adapter in a long time. Run with the\nruntime lockfile installed it was 10 failed, 12 passed -- every failure a stale regex,\nnot a security hole: each cell rejected its assertion, with a more specific reason than\nthe generic \"verification failed\" the test still demanded.\n\nThe replacements are narrower than what they replace. Each cell now names the exact\nrefusal it exists to prove, so a refusal for the wrong reason fails the cell instead of\nsatisfying it: \"declares alg ''none'', which means it is UNSIGNED\" is a different property\nfrom \"unparseable\", and \"missing required claim(s): sub\" is a different property from\n\"missing required claim(s): email\".\n\n22 passed after the change, in all 31 repositories.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"01a452e0fa168f1604437dcc1732c73c5fa769cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/git/trees/01a452e0fa168f1604437dcc1732c73c5fa769cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/git/commits/ca41916e91d959e03d663b49b460380df5209394","verification":{"payload":"tree 01a452e0fa168f1604437dcc1732c73c5fa769cc\nparent 37d88e3ef24b748cdcaf89b84e7e21b347dca744\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787644460 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787644460 +0800\n\nRe-point the IAP negative matrix at the refusals the verifier actually raises (#10)\n\nThe module skipped wherever google-auth was absent, which is every SDK-free gate, so\nnothing had compared its expectations against the adapter in a long time. Run with the\nruntime lockfile installed it was 10 failed, 12 passed -- every failure a stale regex,\nnot a security hole: each cell rejected its assertion, with a more specific reason than\nthe generic \"verification failed\" the test still demanded.\n\nThe replacements are narrower than what they replace. Each cell now names the exact\nrefusal it exists to prove, so a refusal for the wrong reason fails the cell instead of\nsatisfying it: \"declares alg ''none'', which means it is UNSIGNED\" is a different property\nfrom \"unparseable\", and \"missing required claim(s): sub\" is a different property from\n\"missing required claim(s): email\".\n\n22 passed after the change, in all 31 repositories.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjUosCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAbUQAA2MlwAiNWGgtpGjstHEKQuR\nu6lQwSqt55pNlnatmmo5O0ztr4fqceZQWYN5VbNpuXIyNVZaYxL/XSVL3I/q8ce4\n8Xbva1H3vhDvZ9O+WepwPgjn4USWS9OglyGms1bZHvf26OsLIL/mGyWPI/dhoQ9e\nhECGF9YJotW+eYEh8w5YzvRIsg09bgtMsT0S//OA6JD1+Z5YAeP07D3MFrKZydnc\nQEyi8Gr/DL6JoL92alFdH3pDx0cn00CjBgRDDXt4ILTssZSYtqQpvTSmj/pBIUd6\nTiSs+vDNrdB/3PXiYpEc6xzIufD+pQuEltKn46b+qJIlqnjjgAWaxoYeeGRRt8qa\nkcJIKbcIeVkHzFiHAFLEpjocxPZfZgm6DXj0TvuI6TdPtM0f6X55exBi/OjdmzAu\n0NPqzCJfYt55BoAdrVukfNdbrfUT64WH3Wcn401+0ebYzaki0DuGDsLH4YdLtHni\ngQzrflh6dAvubpr7cV7w5iw+29bTCm9F9VzicORLLGNvfaMsfUDv3IZvOGN7iVyE\nF5GpqVi1r8/yymp9aKOsJ8PlBEfqGPXC2J97ZTI6WBgcI1F6kcxBoOgRAbhJ8WTo\n623OJKCbzb7tgbfVk+vf2qRKVTVex3rUaatyaMBh7IxJijb4hbNbT/sqnRuTrj8l\nBak0xK9aE2oFpyU5x20G\n=Ls/n\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T07:54:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commit/ca41916e91d959e03d663b49b460380df5209394","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh5LtoAKGNhNDE5MTZlOTFkOTU5ZTAzZDY2M2I0OWI0NjAzODBkZjUyMDkzOTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commit/37d88e3ef24b748cdcaf89b84e7e21b347dca744","sha":"37d88e3ef24b748cdcaf89b84e7e21b347dca744","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commits/37d88e3ef24b748cdcaf89b84e7e21b347dca744"}],"sha":"ca41916e91d959e03d663b49b460380df5209394","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/account-takeover-investigator/commits/ca41916e91d959e03d663b49b460380df5209394"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"h