hi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/aml-alert-triage/commit/bd376d034d2c1b2827b8651b5dce8039e3897156","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh5hdoAKGJkMzc2ZDAzNGQyYzFiMjgyN2I4NjUxYjVkY2U4MDM5ZTM4OTcxNTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/aml-alert-triage/commit/6224c7b1b6a6a2177a61382e2a61cc45b2a04880","sha":"6224c7b1b6a6a2177a61382e2a61cc45b2a04880","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/aml-alert-triage/commits/6224c7b1b6a6a2177a61382e2a61cc45b2a04880"}],"sha":"bd376d034d2c1b2827b8651b5dce8039e3897156","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/aml-alert-triage/commits/bd376d034d2c1b2827b8651b5dce8039e3897156"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/aml-alert-triage/commits/6224c7b1b6a6a2177a61382e2a61cc45b2a04880/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:03:52Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:06:25Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Build the suppression corpus, and record what it found\n\nThe pitch for alert triage is not \"it finds the structuring case\". A monitoring\nrule already found that, which is why the alert exists. The pitch is that it\ncloses the alerts that should never have reached an investigator, and nothing\nmeasured that: the golden set held ONE clean alert against three that escalate,\nand a false-positive rate over one negative is not a rate, it is an anecdote with\na percentage sign.\n\nEight benign alerts are added, each benign for a DIFFERENT reason, because a\nsuppression metric over one shape of clean alert proves only that the engine can\nclose that shape: a monthly salary run, a long-standing supplier settlement, a\nscheduled loan repayment, an intra-group treasury sweep, a seasonal turnover\nspike, one large receipt that stays put, a dormant account reactivating, and a\ntax payment. suppression_rate scores what share of them the engine closes.\n\nIt closes six of eight, and the two it does not are RECORDED rather than\nrelabelled. FCC-2001, a salary run to eight employees, fires the fan-out rule: a\nsalary run is structurally identical to a mule fan-out in transaction data alone.\nFCC-2004, a treasury sweep out and back to the SAME counterparty next day, fires\nthe rapid-movement rule: layering and a sweep differ by whether the counterparty\nis inside the same legal group. Both need counterparty context the transaction\nwindow does not carry, which is a product change rather than a threshold change.\nThe bar is set at the measured baseline so a regression is caught while the gap\nis open, and the rubric names the target and what would have to change to reach\nit. recommendation_accuracy reads 0.833 rather than 1.000 for the same reason,\nand that drop is the corpus working.\n\nThis repository had no rubric directory at all: every bar was an unlabelled\nmodule constant. Six rubric files now carry each number beside the argument for\nit, and assert_covers fails the build in both directions.\n\nWriting those arguments down surfaced a bar that had never been expressible:\nrecommendation_accuracy at 0.80 over four alerts, where a 0.80 bar tolerates one\nmiss only over five. Twelve alerts make it mean something for the first time. The\nsuppression corpus carries a floor of its own: the runner refuses a golden set\nwith fewer than five should-close alerts.\n\ndocs/evals.md is generated from the rubrics and the corpus, with --check in\n`make gate`. Pin: agent-eval-kit v0.0.2. practices-audit gains E4 and E5. The\npromotion bundle this repository names is now registered by the authority.\n\nVerified: `make gate` green end to end (472 passed, eval PASS over 12 alerts).","tree":{"sha":"8ee3d2814b73b58efdcd4c982561317f84457418","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/aml-alert-triage/git/trees/8ee3d2814b73b58efdcd4c982561317f84457418"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/aml-alert-triage/git/commits/6224c7b1b6a6a2177a61382e2a61cc45b2a04880","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashisha