.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/aml-alert-triage/commits/ad473944e016eff86064863fad83219da9449df6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:46:36Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:46:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Pin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#13)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","tree":{"sha":"f38cc1022bf17a542d129a85b12256f3e29b3f5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/aml-alert-triage/git/trees/f38cc1022bf17a542d129a85b12256f3e29b3f5e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/aml-alert-triage/git/commits/ad473944e016eff86064863fad83219da9449df6","verification":{"payload":"tree f38cc1022bf17a542d129a85b12256f3e29b3f5e\nparent 19a3e2e6915041fa28a5f0cf1f7709c19ec1da09\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787672796 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787672796 +0800\n\nPin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#13)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbjcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGvAQAGBkGcIWiopz5jZR/oFS8J+/\ncv9aS0nuVjq9lPoY3YrCyYhogKf722zHLjtrmd66wDx7ekyL3WaEZadYx3aWgX2k\nVE3jmbwzZz2xHBzl0Bn80TRQ8UiPold/BDL05F8oxWTt4KFr4ZdsXqJMf7PC4Hx3\nxa8ES1v+nzcIYg2gf7DHrQnQpCEB7L0zRR4uUG+0FY3xGaA20hFBV0RpGh/du5yX\niGJ5UFvc+fP5SDVMe2+fW94S0lICYFHvT4gn0vfLejZyDtaA8le+rsv5cKPND1vU\nPNC6hNQ6DrQIO/+MZicIO1n+/bflODGXFm6ADtmuur4c/N7URR3K5NIwXUBbjqcg\nSHyuNguSmTH8gRzKakuk9Ot0T3GQH87t5xbUWaLYtWz2KZS