github.com/repos/portable-genai/aml-alert-triage/commits/19a3e2e6915041fa28a5f0cf1f7709c19ec1da09"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/aml-alert-triage/commits/bc610b91f6193058d1a0f7e27d028943f795b023/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T07:54:39Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T07:54:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Re-point the IAP negative matrix at the refusals the verifier actually raises (#11)\n\nThe module skipped wherever google-auth was absent, which is every SDK-free gate, so\nnothing had compared its expectations against the adapter in a long time. Run with the\nruntime lockfile installed it was 10 failed, 12 passed -- every failure a stale regex,\nnot a security hole: each cell rejected its assertion, with a more specific reason than\nthe generic \"verification failed\" the test still demanded.\n\nThe replacements are narrower than what they replace. Each cell now names the exact\nrefusal it exists to prove, so a refusal for the wrong reason fails the cell instead of\nsatisfying it: \"declares alg ''none'', which means it is UNSIGNED\" is a different property\nfrom \"unparseable\", and \"missing required claim(s): sub\" is a different property from\n\"missing required claim(s): email\".\n\n22 passed after the change, in all 31 repositories.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"9cd0b8b3af12662dcb8aa1f6d26c6a9466732fac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/aml-alert-triage/git/trees/9cd0b8b3af12662dcb8aa1f6d26c6a9466732fac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/aml-alert-triage/git/commits/bc610b91f6193058d1a0f7e27d028943f795b023","verification":{"payload":"tree 9cd0b8b3af12662dcb8aa1f6d26c6a9466732fac\nparent 8066eed3cb415c814a0118358b3ce2c6ec55363e\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787644479 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787644479 +0800\n\nRe-point the IAP negative matrix at the refusals the verifier actually raises (#11)\n\nThe module skipped wherever google-auth was absent, which is every SDK-free gate, so\nnothing had compared its expectations against the adapter in a long time. Run with the\nruntime lockfile installed it was 10 failed, 12 passed -- every failure a stale regex,\nnot a security hole: each cell rejected its assertion, with a more specific reason than\nthe generic \"verification failed\" the test still demanded.\n\nThe replacements are narrower than what they replace. Each cell now names the exact\nrefusal it exists to prove, so a refusal for the wrong reason fails the cell instead of\nsatisfying it: \"declares alg ''none'', which means it is UNSIGNED\" is a different property\nfrom \"unparseable\", and \"missing required claim(s): sub\" is a different property from\n\"missing required claim(s): email\".\n\n22 passed after the change, in all 31 repositories.\n\nCo-authored-by: A