ommitter":{"date":"2026-09-25T03:27:49Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Correct the review-routing comments to the boot refusal\n\nThe variables.tf header and the review_url comment in settings.yaml still\nsaid the managed review router refuses to swallow an escalation when\nHUMAN_REVIEW_URL is empty. Since the runtime control switches landed that\nis false: the service refuses at BOOT when review routing is on and no console\nis named, and CLAIMSINTEG_REVIEW_ROUTING=false switches routing off, so\nhuman_review_url is only required with review_routing_enabled on.\n\nComment-only; no behaviour changes.","tree":{"sha":"0e463874d051b3015b5fcfb85ec0eeea4566e31b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/git/trees/0e463874d051b3015b5fcfb85ec0eeea4566e31b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/git/commits/c5e84a458fc42ce2b59cbdc031122db958ffe4de","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/commit/c5e84a458fc42ce2b59cbdc031122db958ffe4de","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh57doAKGM1ZTg0YTQ1OGZjNDJjZTJiNTljYmRjMDMxMTIyZGI5NThmZmU0ZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/commit/0a8aea5d72c682844db63706fdce5b0f7256ee7d","sha":"0a8aea5d72c682844db63706fdce5b0f7256ee7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/commits/0a8aea5d72c682844db63706fdce5b0f7256ee7d"}],"sha":"c5e84a458fc42ce2b59cbdc031122db958ffe4de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/commits/c5e84a458fc42ce2b59cbdc031122db958ffe4de"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/commits/0a8aea5d72c682844db63706fdce5b0f7256ee7d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T03:05:52Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T03:11:45Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Wire the console to the real assessment call\n\nThe console posted the template''s {subject, text} to POST /v1/triage, a route this service does\nnot serve, so every submit was a 404 and the console could never produce an assessment. The API\ntakes POST /v1/assess with AssessRequest{claim_id} and fetches the claimant, policy and\ndocuments server-side.\n\nThe console now assesses one claim by id, prefilled with CLM-1004 and suggesting the four claims\nthe local profile seeds (CLM-1001 to CLM-1004, all fictional). There is no list endpoint for\nclaims, so the id stays editable for a deployment with other ids. GET /v1/siu-queue is the\npost-assessment review queue rather than a list of assessable claims, so the console shows it\nbeneath the result, scoped to the persona''s tenant, and re-reads it after every assessment.\n\ntests/unit/test_console_matches_api.py reads every fetch(API + ...) in ui/app/ and holds it\nagainst the live route table: path and method served, every required field sent, no field the\nmodel silently drops. It failed against the old console (POST /v1/triage is not served) and\npasses against this one. The runbook and on-prem migration notes named /v1/triage too; they now\nname /v1/assess.","tree":{"sha":"d2e8dcf2e3e567ed27d325e8f233573d98cedd24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/git/trees/d2e8dcf2e3e567ed27d325e8f233573d98cedd24"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/git/commits/0a8aea5d72c682844db63706fdce5b0f7256ee7d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/commit/0a8aea5d72c682844db63706fdce5b0f7256ee7d","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh57doAKDBhOGFlYTVkNzJjNjgyODQ0ZGI2MzcwNmZkY2U1YjBmNzI1NmVlN2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/commit/0e736d6ae9d7dc36c8857a33b36810e63177b5cb","sha":"0e736d6ae9d7dc36c8857a33b36810e63177b5cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/commits/0e736d6ae9d7dc36c8857a33b36810e63177b5cb"}],"sha":"0a8aea5d72c682844db63706fdce5b0f7256ee7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/commits/0a8aea5d72c682844db63706fdce5b0f7256ee7d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/commits/0e736d6ae9d7dc36c8857a33b36810e63177b5cb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T10:13:26Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T10:15:59Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Switch review routing, refuse at boot without a console, report hand-offs\n\nTemplate-shape application of the fleet''s runtime-control contract. Review routing is the\none cheap runtime control this service has, so it is the one switch.\n\n- CLAIMSINTEG_REVIEW_ROUTING is read once at settings load in three states: unset is on, a\n  boolean wins, emptied or unrecognised refuses at boot. Off binds a disabled router and\n  logs one warning per process, however many containers are built.\n- Under gcp, routing on with no HUMAN_REVIEW_URL refuses at boot. It used to surface as a\n  failed request on the first escalation, after the assessment had been computed and audited.\n- POST /v1/assess, the assess_claim agent tool and the CLI hand off through a recording wrapper, so a hand-off that fails no longer\n  fails the assessment: the result carries review_routing (routed, failed, off, not_required)\n  and an empty review_ref, and the failure is logged. The console states the outcome in\n  plain words.\n- Terraform gains review_routing_enabled, sets the service''s switch from it, and relaxes the\n  edge''s console requirement only when routing is stated off; a new plan test holds that.\n- SPEC, COMPLIANCE, the practices audit, the compliance and features FAQs, .env.example and the runbook no longer say the managed router refuses at request time; they describe the boot refusal, the switch and the reported outcome.\n- pii-kit masking here protects the audit trail, tool results and the review payload rather\n  than a user''s free-text question, so it is not the redaction control the contract\n  switches, and it gains no switch.","tree":{"sha":"3c438b54dd73d98e39423333affce281974925ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/git/trees/3c438b54dd73d98e39423333affce281974925ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/git/commits/0e736d6ae9d7dc36c8857a33b36810e63177b5cb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/commit/0e736d6ae9d7dc36c8857a33b36810e63177b5cb","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh57doAKDBlNzM2ZDZhZTlkN2RjMzZjODg1N2EzM2IzNjgxMGU2MzE3N2I1Y2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/commit/e215b4aa37dbfdeea494eaedcef86f176d6deb04","sha":"e215b4aa37dbfdeea494eaedcef86f176d6deb04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/commits/e215b4aa37dbfdeea494eaedcef86f176d6deb04"}],"sha":"0e736d6ae9d7dc36c8857a33b36810e63177b5cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/commits/0e736d6ae9d7dc36c8857a33b36810e63177b5cb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/commits/e215b4aa37dbfdeea494eaedcef86f176d6deb04/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T03:49:36Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T03:54:54Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Take the default off the audit bucket lock\n\nworm_locked defaulted to true, so the first apply of this stack in any\nproject locked its audit bucket irreversibly for the whole retention window,\nwith nothing in that deployment''s own tfvars saying so. The fleet decided on\n2026-09-12 that an irreversible control takes no default; this stack was one\nof 33 that sweep never reached.\n\nA plan now refuses until the deployment states the lock. The Terraform tests\nstate it once per file in the production form, still assert that a stated\nlock sits on the six-month floor, and gain a run proving the unlocked posture\ncreates an unlocked bucket. That run fails if the lock is ever hard-coded\nback into the bucket, which every other run would miss.","tree":{"sha":"44b63b7bae605807cf9dbc3aa6c92433f8264a9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/git/trees/44b63b7bae605807cf9dbc3aa6c92433f8264a9e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/git/commits/e215b4aa37dbfdeea494eaedcef86f176d6deb04","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/commit/e215b4aa37dbfdeea494eaedcef86f176d6deb04","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh57doAKGUyMTViNGFhMzdkYmZkZWVhNDk0ZWFlZGNlZjg2ZjE3NmQ2ZGViMDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/commit/fcd483298df44ae3a1a3ad5edca75d178c4cc4f5","sha":"fcd483298df44ae3a1a3ad5edca75d178c4cc4f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/commits/fcd483298df44ae3a1a3ad5edca75d178c4cc4f5"}],"sha":"e215b4aa37dbfdeea494eaedcef86f176d6deb04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/commits/e215b4aa37dbfdeea494eaedcef86f176d6deb04"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","id":49699333,"login":"dependabot[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/commits/fcd483298df44ae3a1a3ad5edca75d178c4cc4f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T06:45:54Z","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dependabot[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T12:17:37Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump the npm-minor-patch group across 1 directory with 6 updates\n\nBumps the npm-minor-patch group with 6 updates in the /ui directory:\n\n| Package | From | To |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [next](https://github.com/vercel/next.js) | `16.3.4` | `16.3.5` |\n| [react](https://github.com/react/react/tree/HEAD/packages/react) | `19.2.8` | `19.3.0` |\n| [@types/react](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/react) | `19.2.18` | `19.3.0` |\n| [react-dom](https://github.com/react/react/tree/HEAD/packages/react-dom) | `19.2.8` | `19.3.0` |\n| [@types/react-dom](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/react-dom) | `19.2.5` | `19.3.0` |\n| [@types/node](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/node) | `26.4.0` | `26.5.1` |\n\n\n\nUpdates `next` from 16.3.4 to 16.3.5\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/compare/v16.3.4...v16.3.5)\n\nUpdates `react` from 19.2.8 to 19.3.0\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/react/react/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/react/react/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/react/react/commits/v19.3.0/packages/react)\n\nUpdates `@types/react` from 19.2.18 to 19.3.0\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/react)\n\nUpdates `react-dom` from 19.2.8 to 19.3.0\n- [Release notes](https://github.