cdb80b1"}],"sha":"027f7ec6a35fb14398b81fe4e3b11aa2c39fe906","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/commits/027f7ec6a35fb14398b81fe4e3b11aa2c39fe906"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/commits/9b3bc4f2f21436e69988c8adb2510a3fccdb80b1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:11:58Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:11:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Bind the IAP transport facts to hex-service-kit v0.0.3 (#12)\n\nWave 2 of the federation migration. Wave 1 moved the eight P0/P1 launch repositories; this is\none of the remaining forty-one.\n\nThe assertion header, the issuer and the key set URL were declared here as literals, and the\nsame three literals are declared again in every repository that verifies an IAP assertion. That\nis one security decision written down once per repo, and a copy that drifts stays green forever,\nbecause a literal always agrees with itself. They are now rebound from hex_service_kit.federation.\n\nObserved failing first. Re-declaring the header while leaving the import in place is caught\nearlier, by ruff F401, so the case only a test can see is the literal re-declared AND the import\ndropped. On that run ruff reported \"All checks passed\" and the only failure was the new test,\nreading ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assert'' against the kit''s ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assertion''. The existing literal\ntest stays, because it catches the other defect, a typo in the published value.\n\nThe pin moves to @v0.0.3 and the locks were rebuilt with org-metadata scripts/fleet-deps.py\nrefresh, which pins the commit the annotated tag dereferences to (d28baa1c). No lockfile was\nhand-edited. v0.0.2 to v0.0.3 moves no dependency.\n\nThis does NOT adopt principal_from_iap_claims. v0.0.3 adds\nFederationPolicy.tenant_from_hosted_domain, which was expected to close the gap that stopped wave\n1 adopting it. Executing this adapter and the kit function against the same claim sets shows they\nstill disagree on four axes, not one, so the tenant and principal half stays local. The four are\nrecorded in the wave-2 report.\n\nGate: make gate, exit 0, 491 passed 1 skipped 2 deselected. Run offline with the v0.0.3 lock installed, so the new\nassertion ran against the release it names.","tree":{"sha":"8268f024cb59130cbaaf6b9f05bf248cf9310615","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/git/trees/8268f024cb59130cbaaf6b9f05bf248cf9310615"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/claims-integrity-investigator/git/commits/9b3bc4f2f21436e69988c8adb2510a3fccdb80b1","verification":{"payload":"tree 8268f024cb59130cbaaf6b9f05bf248cf9310615\nparent 50ca8052bcc6f88e189e43b81bde26bfbb6a57b1\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787670718 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787670718 +0800\n\nBind the IAP transport facts to hex-service-kit v0.0.3 (#12)\n\nWave 2 of the federation migration. Wave 1 moved the eight P0/P1 launch repositories; this is\none of the remaining forty-one.\n\nThe assertion header, the issuer and the key set URL were declared here as literals, and the\nsame three literals are declared again in every repository that verifies an IAP assertion. That\nis one security decision written down once per repo, and a copy that drifts stays green forever,\nbecause a literal always agrees with itself. They are now rebound from hex_service_kit.federation.\n\nObserved failing first. Re-declaring the header while leaving the import in place is caught\nearlier, by ruff F401, so the case only a test can see is the literal re-declared AND the import\ndropped. On that run ruff reported \"All checks passed\" and the only failure was the new test,\nreading ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assert'' against the kit''s ''x-goog-iap-jwt-assertion''. The existing literal\ntest stays, because it catches the other defect, a typo in the published value.\n\nThe pin moves to @v0.0.3 and the locks were rebuilt with org-metadata scripts/fleet-deps.py\nrefresh, which pins the commit the annotated tag dereferences to (d28baa1c). No lockfile was\nhand-edited. v0.0.2 to v0.0.3 moves no dependency.\n\nThis does NOT adopt principal_from_iap_claims. v0.0.3 adds\nFederationPolicy.tenant_from_hosted_domain, which was expected to close the gap that stopped wave\n1 adopting it. Executing this adapter and the kit function against the same claim sets shows they\nstill disagree on four axes, not one, so the tenant and principal half stays local. The four are\nrecorded in the wave-2 report.\n\nGate: make gate, exit 0, 491 passed 1 skipped 2 deselected. Run offline with the v0.0.3 lock installed, so the new\nassertion ran against the release it names.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbC+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0YAQAJM7mbfXOg96Lst4HdFoski4\ndrB+seMU92zLYimQq9rCel1nh2v271Oh2UsPUwt9kGvW