user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/sanctions-screening/commits/86664cca319530f51603223796554d67f5ea7a90/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T06:54:57Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T06:59:53Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump shared kits: hex-service-kit v0.0.5","tree":{"sha":"bae951cc474df7adf1f40bf03cda4d57f6f57209","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/sanctions-screening/git/trees/bae951cc474df7adf1f40bf03cda4d57f6f57209"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/sanctions-screening/git/commits/86664cca319530f51603223796554d67f5ea7a90","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/sanctions-screening/commit/86664cca319530f51603223796554d67f5ea7a90","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh6UNoAKDg2NjY0Y2NhMzE5NTMwZjUxNjAzMjIzNzk2NTU0ZDY3ZjVlYTdhOTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/sanctions-screening/commit/2f42e83b7285e7fe0270100cb496fd69ff5c8485","sha":"2f42e83b7285e7fe0270100cb496fd69ff5c8485","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/sanctions-screening/commits/2f42e83b7285e7fe0270100cb496fd69ff5c8485"}],"sha":"86664cca319530f51603223796554d67f5ea7a90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/sanctions-screening/commits/86664cca319530f51603223796554d67f5ea7a90"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/sanctions-screening/commits/2f42e83b7285e7fe0270100cb496fd69ff5c8485/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T01:12:11Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T01:12:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Adopt the commons claim half in the IAP adapter (#14)\n\nresolve() no longer builds a Principal. Everything after the signature check\nis one hex_service_kit.federation.principal_from_iap_claims call under a\nreviewed FederationPolicy, and the cryptography stays in the adapter because\nthe kit''s core is stdlib with zero runtime dependencies and verifies nothing.\n\nThe policy states tenant_from_hosted_domain as an opt-in rather than leaving\nit to a fallback: this deployment configures no domain map and IAP already\nrestricts the audience to one organisation, so the hd claim IS the tenant id.\nLeft off, these same assertions resolve to no tenant at all, which is\nfail-closed and closed for every verified user, and no offline gate would see\nit because the local profile never constructs this adapter.\n\nExecuting the commons against this adapter over the same claim sets, rather\nthan reading it, found two behaviour changes. Both are recorded rather than\nnormalised away: assurance now prefers an acr claim where the shipped tail\nhardcoded \"iap\", and the tenant is lower-cased where the shipped tail passed\nhd through with only .strip().\n\ntests/unit/test_iap_claim_half.py was red first in three stages and red again\nagainst three deliberate defects afterwards. The counts are in\ndocs/practices-audit.md under C1.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4366d7b1592e902dfa7283d1f12a3370c1e6c6f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/sanctions-screening/git/trees/4366d7b1592e902dfa7283d1f12a3370c1e6c6f4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/sanctions-screening/git/commits/2f42e83b7285e7fe0270100cb496fd69ff5c8485","verification":{"payload":"tree 4366d7b1592e902dfa7283d1f12a3370c1e6c6f4\nparent f2e1cc2b99aa63e13d8424edc99df645600f1463\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787706731 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787706731 +0800\n\nAdopt the commons claim half in the IAP adapter (#14)\n\nresolve() no longer builds a Principal. Everything after the signature check\nis one hex_service_kit.federation.principal_from_iap_claims call under a\nreviewed FederationPolicy, and the cryptography stays in the adapter because\nthe kit''s core is stdlib with zero runtime dependencies and verifies nothing.\n\nThe policy states tenant_from_hosted_domain as an opt-in rather than leaving\nit to a fallback: this deployment configures no domain map and IAP already\nrestricts the audience to one organisation, so the hd claim IS the tenant id.\nLeft off, these same assertions resolve to no tenant at all, which is\nfail-closed and closed for every verified user, and no offline gate would see\nit because the local profile never constructs this adapter.\n\nExecuting the commons against this adapter over the same claim sets, rather\nthan reading it, found two behaviour changes. Both are recorded rather than\nnormalised away: assurance now prefers an acr claim where the shipped tail\nhardcoded \"iap\", and the tenant is lower-cased where the shipped tail passed\nhd through with only .strip().\n\ntests/unit/test_iap_claim_half.py was red first in three stages and red again\nagainst three deliberate defects afterwards. The counts are in\ndocs/practices-audit.md under C1.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjj1rCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAFFUQAC9acQJx9mjc+GU7Zz8C3k/g\n80xsk8CCSzQD2nDcfeY1okEpFhMnZBx+tV9C/r/caxoE7DtdrVuh+uRlgl8Bq7Ej\nRIZ71v4xE6UNcHlB5eXM0JOWeAHjMINp6mA4dMw3dnlY2AWHtIeeAqIrY7hu49KM\nu5FtfllZoYcDiK3T0sQtmOxYVf7l6mz7BR/Kg9VWhj5T/8ixVpo2eM8V2jWiCDmO\nsCnN+B96Svb2unN7L+8AY4kQQ5KsbQ8VMCxj8IWQQTKnHCUmZf35h0OJ3ewmWkgn\nIeLscb13G3iR8lVTLPG92hpzrzFsRgrzK5zofvucP1jvWyNFXfciRIswQPgl+y8D\nnwVIMmOxzH1JiQbSUa8KquL0Jyo9hnqLew9dwnxUH4m/UBJFwjCR1TEuwD2yPPUm\nDedn36UOskHSnpwpEtjfQCWRwU4MbHvHVsNFiyfDF7O1o4mal7QMA81HLFrhWecH\nvyYYknj8NWicVdAUINYq6oUHC3blLa7Ya7idWrxZp7tVltHiQSKBez/LRywwIlzO\ne+n5vySEtWZuggSWXkGNmifRrCBmh1EnH+/hCcdnHqb9cbQkJ5BHNyWxwmYDYIcX\n/cYrn2cBofON+bHxXo1g/7KZO3qyKxhHhHrpZwePTzHC+8xgHfgF4K1k07By+3ml\numw6BK0cAzHQ59mykA8p\n=Szao\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T01:12:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/sanctions-screening/commit/2f42e83b7285e7fe0270100cb496fd69ff5c8485","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh6UNoAKDJmNDJlODNiNzI4NWU3ZmUwMjcwMTAwY2I0OTZmZDY5ZmY1Yzg0ODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/sanctions-screening/commit/f2e1cc2b99aa63e13d8424edc99df645600f1463","sha":"f2e1cc2b99aa63e13d8424edc99df645600f1463","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/sanctions-screening/commits/f2e1cc2b99aa63e13d8424edc99df645600f1463"}],"sha":"2f42e83b7285e7fe0270100cb496fd69ff5c8485","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/sanctions-screening/commits/2f42e83b7285e7fe0270100cb496fd69ff5c8485"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/sanctions-screening/commits/f2e1cc2b99aa63e13d8424edc99df645600f1463/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:49:47Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:49:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Pin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#13)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","tree":{"sha":"eb349b143d3962aa3613c52fabec81b343b0bc45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/sanctions-screening/git/trees/eb349b143d3962aa3613c52fabec81b343b0bc45"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/sanctions-screening/git/commits/f2e1cc2b99aa63e13d8424edc99df645600f1463","verification":{"payload":"tree eb349b143d3962aa3613c52fabec81b343b0bc45\nparent be446b75272510afc26c973c5682c561165ce1b1\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787672987 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787672987 +0800\n\nPin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#13)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbmbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAB8oQAJ8y8jUKOjei90Q8hHsoar97\nWaD9Y4o/rncxLyq5DwiNd8it3wyZzaTT9PSHgvVfY1np7Un7SBJ+fSF/QIEtbIGx\nlEnH9q/2f/kGMDckgz70+HIuZRjhVo5qZ1HVT7BRKJY+yR73Nn6w9mPsPwV8WxTo\n8adaydlxA+2fXvhqeMPiOLoY4eU64Cn1J/WcKs0XyZrptE5HNZ+E3JVnxhVQEV6D\ngomYX+StoeqouquhMKpAZaRnelfBBENhLg14z1tUyjBz04DfQlWOlCppuEpXIPN4\n0zPvRkoZpQlo1m4lrJRV+ocKHO4rZjm3kPh5m7VgFo3vJoeO+wX0eiYCUz2LVfDd\nJAhN/6sIZPytj+/l7NWJZ4AoFhivRMNeI/76puWZt54BY8GW8aiOP3tPTeEm8cO2\nZxjkx/BzUdv/SERiV0Nn9Lo9wUuoIiTDsoChJXPXHyJay9QmXzfAF4qDhZu/hPa5\nWxj9Rmv7bslWWAYKZ812fOdh0Xwh/4z9DSr2YjNqlrXNF/g8yRQwiQzeLQm6