d906","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/app-fraud-interdiction/commits/2279effa7a8e5b54a3be2855e16b92e23eb7d906"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/app-fraud-interdiction/commits/859a720ab0cff54a1457d5d1d0991a020046f6e2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:46:36Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:46:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Pin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#13)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","tree":{"sha":"14a5e3535fdc2a2c8237c507f7546cf18980efab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/app-fraud-interdiction/git/trees/14a5e3535fdc2a2c8237c507f7546cf18980efab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/app-fraud-interdiction/git/commits/859a720ab0cff54a1457d5d1d0991a020046f6e2","verification":{"payload":"tree 14a5e3535fdc2a2c8237c507f7546cf18980efab\nparent 7ee8087854c6906d481d12b9785e0926f1e764a8\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787672796 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787672796 +0800\n\nPin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#13)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbjdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYhAQABYQ9BaM9Wp3Q4Rs2gwOKlAx\n6faEIdy1TTl8HRNg3STTM43YY+m3BMe8BOEjtpn8y6C5luDd5Q7LbHxe082yAfn6\nWGDhngeooiHGKTK6G7BsgJ98R7bFjbmkOG2a1jpwB6ThVugjPSe8GygOdKER8hin\np4FMrNqbQYoPgugVgkNRIRHJmCfQ2AdVak2t20