-genai/soc-fraud-fusion/commit/0d4c4d2df64eee577e92c00f42331045763ae1bb","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh7E9oAKDBkNGM0ZDJkZjY0ZWVlNTc3ZTkyYzAwZjQyMzMxMDQ1NzYzYWUxYmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/soc-fraud-fusion/commit/52cfcccc5155af72a06ed99990738d1f4ace4ef1","sha":"52cfcccc5155af72a06ed99990738d1f4ace4ef1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/soc-fraud-fusion/commits/52cfcccc5155af72a06ed99990738d1f4ace4ef1"}],"sha":"0d4c4d2df64eee577e92c00f42331045763ae1bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/soc-fraud-fusion/commits/0d4c4d2df64eee577e92c00f42331045763ae1bb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/soc-fraud-fusion/commits/52cfcccc5155af72a06ed99990738d1f4ace4ef1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T14:27:47Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T21:53:24Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Show the model that answered as two pills, not a banner, on hex-service-kit v0.0.10\n\nOwner decision 2026-09-23: the console shows two small pills at the top\nright, the model that ANSWERED and Search when an online search tool was\nused, in place of the full-width provenance banner.\n\n- hex-service-kit v0.0.10 (0e71fc7); the relock moved no other pin.\n- api/app.py installs install_answer_provenance(app).\n- Adapters note what answered: the Gemini narrator and the Gemini\n  indicator lookup note generation_model after each call; the local\n  narrator notes deterministic-offline-stub; the live narrator is noted by\n  the kit client. No adapter attaches an online search tool, so none\n  notes a search.\n- Sampling per call: NarrationRequest.temperature is float | None = None\n  and the Gemini narrator omits it when None, the live narrator passes it\n  through. Narration stays free. The indicator verdict lookup is pinned\n  at 0.0 because its verdict is a classification that is cited.\n- config.py: the use_hard_reasoning branch is gone from the resolver, so\n  generator_model is the setting the adapter calls.\n- ui: ModelPills.tsx, lib/answer-provenance.mjs (node-tested) and the\n  proxy forwarding x-answered-by / x-search-used, copied from the\n  template; ProvenanceBanner.tsx and its CSS are deleted.\n- tests: test_answer_provenance.py (the stub answers under local, a\n  searching call says so, the Gemini calls note their model, narration\n  sends no temperature, the lookup is pinned, no flag moves\n  generator_model), the pills contract in test_ui_surface.py, the banner\n  contract test renamed to test_model_pill_contract.py.","tree":{"sha":"60a2848d3164daf6cbfebbda519a22bd7b9669f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/soc-fraud-fusion/git/trees/60a2848d3164daf6cbfebbda519a22bd7b9669f8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/soc-fraud-fusion/git/commits/52cfcccc5155af72a06ed99990738d1f4ace4ef1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"u