b.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/soc-fraud-fusion/commit/9709ed31fe3dcf17a6ac0afee6493b16f8b24f32","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh7E9oAKDk3MDllZDMxZmUzZGNmMTdhNmFjMGFmZWU2NDkzYjE2ZjhiMjRmMzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/soc-fraud-fusion/commit/c0c3bd5c11ce5caceeb2d6ec4ba4205fb47233a1","sha":"c0c3bd5c11ce5caceeb2d6ec4ba4205fb47233a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/soc-fraud-fusion/commits/c0c3bd5c11ce5caceeb2d6ec4ba4205fb47233a1"}],"sha":"9709ed31fe3dcf17a6ac0afee6493b16f8b24f32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/soc-fraud-fusion/commits/9709ed31fe3dcf17a6ac0afee6493b16f8b24f32"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/soc-fraud-fusion/commits/c0c3bd5c11ce5caceeb2d6ec4ba4205fb47233a1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T13:27:46Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T13:35:55Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Create the alert dataset, filter it by tenant, and serve one book on both sides\n\nThree things, and the second is the one that matters.\n\nThe dataset did not exist. adapters/gcp/alerts.py has always queried\n<FRAUDFUSION_BQ_DATASET>.alerts and nothing in infra/terraform/ created it. Unlike the\nsibling repository that shipped the same gap, not even the API was enabled and no IAM\nrole named BigQuery, so the adapter referred to a store with no existence anywhere in\nthe deployment. The dataset, the table, the API, the two roles and the CMEK\nservice-agent binding all arrive together, because a dataset missing any one of them\nfails a different silent way.\n\nThe managed adapter ignored the tenant it was given. fetch() takes the VERIFIED\nprincipal''s tenant and the statement was SELECT * FROM alerts WHERE scope = @scope, so\nevery tenant''s alerts in a scope reached whoever asked, on the profile that faces real\nusers. The local adapter has always matched each row''s data tag against the principal\nand documents the fail-closed reading of an untagged row, so object-level authorization\nwas present in one profile and absent in the other, and no offline test could see it\nbecause the offline family does the right thing. The predicate is there now, an empty\ntenant reads nothing rather than everything, and the read set is declared rather than\nhidden inside SELECT *.\n\nThe test meant to prove that isolation asserted an empty result for a foreign\nprincipal, and the fixtures satisfied it by holding no foreign rows at all: switching\nthe filter off entirely would not have moved it. The book ships another tenant''s alert\nINSIDE a scope this tenant also uses, which is what a scope being a label rather than an\nentitlement looks like, and the assertion is now that each principal sees its own row\nand none of the other''s.\n\nThe alerts themselves move from a Python dict to\nsrc/soc_fraud_fusion/data/demo_book/, read by the DuckDB store the offline profiles\nserve, the loader that fills the dataset, the fixture map the demo and eval read, and\nthe tests. book_manifest is declared and the guard iterates load_order().\n\nGate green: 504 tests, eval 1.000 on all six metrics, terraform validate and 14\nterraform tests, docs, demo self-test 9 steps, portability 8 checks. The tenant guards\nwere watched failing against the shipped query and against a store without the\npredicate.","tree":{"sha":"ce63812cffafbf31ba3302bc168f421cddeb2fa0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/soc-fraud-fusion/git/trees/ce63812cffafbf31ba3302bc168f421cddeb2fa0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/soc-fraud-fusion/git/commits/c0c3bd5c11ce5caceeb2d6ec4ba4205fb47233a1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/soc-fraud-fusion/commit/c0c3bd5c11ce5caceeb2d6ec4ba4205fb47233a1","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh7E9oAKGMwYzNiZDVjMTFjZTVjYWNlZWIyZDZlYzRiYTQyMDVmYjQ3MjMzYTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/soc-fraud-fusion/commit/123e962e5f450ac345158b22fba677d114cc13fe","sha":"123e962e5f450ac345158b22fba677d114cc13fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/soc-fraud-fusion/commits/123e962e5f450ac345158b22fba677d114cc13fe"}],"sha":"c0c3bd5c11ce5caceeb2d6ec4ba4205fb47233a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/soc-fraud-fusion/commits/c0c3bd5c11ce5caceeb2d6ec4ba4205fb47233a1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/soc-fraud-fusion/commits/123e962e5f450ac345158b22fba677d114cc13fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T10:01:19Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T22:39:23Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Name the systems this repo depends on, instead of their catalog ids\n\nRepository names are unique across the organization, so a reader no longer has\nto resolve a code through a table to learn which system is meant. The catalog\ndropped its ID column, and this repository follows.\n\nBeyond prose, four identifier changes:\n\n- The review payload''s source_key prefix is the repository name. It is a dedup\n  key -- human-review-console queries on it and the local store makes it a\n  PRIMARY KEY -- so producers and the console have to agree, and the branch\n  carries the migration for rows written under the old prefix.\n- Terraform''s local.render_catalog_id becomes local.render_repository. It feeds\n  display names and descriptions, which update in place.\n- scripts/demo.py''s catalog id is deleted rather than renamed: a REPOSITORY\n  constant and a \"repository\" state key were already there beside it.\n- scripts/rename_fork.py loses --catalog-id, which had nothing left to rewrite.\n\nLines that outgrew the 100-column limit because a name is longer than an id are\nrewrapped rather than shortened by dropping the name. `ruff check`,\n`ruff format --check` and the offline tests are clean.\n\nDeployed resource identifiers are deliberately NOT changed: the Terraform\nname_prefix stems and the Secret Manager secret ids still carry the old\nlowercase id. Those name resources that exist in the deployment, and renaming a\nname_prefix destroys and recreates them, so they are an infrastructure\nmigration rather than a rename.","tree":{"sha":"445364620592f2e0303f72fbe823fa53ba0b7ce3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/soc-fraud-fusion/git/trees/445364620592f2e0303f72fbe823fa53ba0b7ce3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/soc-fraud-fusion/git/commits/123e962e5f450ac345158b22fba677d114cc13fe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/soc-fraud-fusion/commit/123e962e5f450ac345158b22fba677d114cc13fe","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh7E9oAKDEyM2U5NjJlNWY0NTBhYzM0NTE1OGIyMmZiYTY3N2QxMTRjYzEzZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/soc-fraud-fusion/commit/f2