mit/074a26bd40672863f789e8a5d79c8f26c351b4f2","sha":"074a26bd40672863f789e8a5d79c8f26c351b4f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/human-review-console/commits/074a26bd40672863f789e8a5d79c8f26c351b4f2"}],"sha":"bc3fe52bafb6ef8c90f73a64809a46d14dd0df07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/human-review-console/commits/bc3fe52bafb6ef8c90f73a64809a46d14dd0df07"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/human-review-console/commits/074a26bd40672863f789e8a5d79c8f26c351b4f2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T01:25:47Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T01:25:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Record why the commons claim half is not adopted here, by running both (#22)\n\nThis adapter is an authorization gate and the commons is not.\nREVIEW_IAP_ENTITLEMENTS_JSON is a reviewed map from a verified address to the\ntenant and the group principals that address holds; a subject absent from it\nis refused, and so is a deployment that has not configured it at all.\n\nFederationPolicy.domain_groups grants by domain and grants nothing to a domain\nit does not name, so the same unlisted subject there resolves to a well-formed\nprincipal holding no role. At the point a resource is refused that reads like\na permissions bug rather than a caller who was never admitted, and Hrz3 is the\nconsole a human uses to release a consequential decision.\n\nallowed_machine_subjects is the closest the commons comes and it applies only\nto callers whose address ends .gserviceaccount.com. There is no human-subject\nallowlist, and putting this deployment''s reviewed map into the commons would\npush a deployment-specific fact into the module whose whole point is the half\nthat must not vary.\n\nRed first: adopting the commons naively turned three of the five rows red, the\nlast reporting DID NOT RAISE where a reviewed subject signing in from an\nunexpected organisation must be refused. The exclusion is the claim half\nalone; the transport facts are still the commons values.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4a764728d2bd84bac049a3fad8b747d0bffb9a1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/human-review-console/git/trees/4a764728d2bd84bac049a3fad8b747d0bffb9a1f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/human-review-console/git/commits/074a26bd40672863f789e8a5d79c8f26c351b4f2","verification":{"payload":"tree 4a764728d2bd84bac049a3fad8b747d0bffb9a1f\nparent 44dee596742997e0603ab9e25dc936b82086cd55\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787707547 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787707547 +0800\n\nRecord why the commons claim half is not adopted here, by running both (#22)\n\nThis adapter is an authorization gate and the commons is not.\nREVIEW_IAP_ENTITLEMENTS_JSON is a reviewed map from a verified address to the\ntenant and the group principals that address holds; a subject absent from it\nis refused, and so is a deployment that has not configured it at all.\n\nFederationPolicy.domain_groups grants by domain and grants nothing to a domain\nit does not name, so the same unlisted subject there resolves to a well-formed\nprincipal holding no role. At the point a resource is refused that reads like\na permissions bug rather than a caller who was never admitted, and Hrz3 is the\nconsole a human uses to release a consequential decision.\n\nallowed_machine_subjects is the closest the commons comes and it applies only\nto callers whose address ends .gserviceaccount.com. There is no human-subject\nallowlist, and putting this deployment''s reviewed map into the commons would\npush a deployment-specific fact into the module whose whole point is the half\nthat must not vary.\n\nRed first: adopting the commons naively turned three of the five rows red, the\nlast reporting DID NOT RAISE where a reviewed subject signing in from an\nunexpected organisation must be refused. The exclusion is the claim half\nalone; the transport facts are still the commons values.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjkCbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAC54QAJM6D91085jknr3Cm1F8SKxd\n++LtxueKXCgQMLq1Oy/NsHiHwrQ8lhVtzlZ0wwz/iiiTPrkd3aXx/pz1Cl3VP/Mu\nZW0r8Zqe+r+oIOhkP1nKTtkOvEkhjxCCcsxC794EaE3BwuSb24+xjsLzU42uCzLv\nO8TtyonkSV7PCQRI4SDMuqlhi38djuDyUovcKN1MNF3cAm1Wb8Jm+N9TSuH0yvxT\nrbE9NqjObioZC6zPiwSwOv3lWZREtsMJmKDfwi0LtC6FdIpf7omyqdtDHCl1ruSB\ncxXrXawiZpYXZa5oPP1QnAGZcHaPdw+vkoB5mReP5cB5sa5rgTVdgrfnYeosWh+U\nUDKr90NoiMo7paRTT8kRItlTbUJGfHgRmk50obtje08gs8SnU5FwhsFyF8vBcdL2\nVrMRXDaZFPcvltFXK0uK3rfZ4quSoXX263e5tpOaazAepVhjeBp9b7Fry+9tVA4q\n4peXOe391kNH8Sb2XQVdoosG1JwS/Zdb/sIEY9d6QJ4h7U/AATvPjFZ0+1l0IMf0\nVZizMrx+gwoJ1noHVbwzz5PdFeUoqRxlpKnTY+cA7zrznUXoyIl6u1Lz+4Pn8O9m\ngk4DsmocxIFb/D3xoYyNUUxmcYAmVjzRQvMUAMnRnFuibD3QsZOGdABl2kYo+klt\nBr3S4iF2LZtuH6rF5hH6\n=ofih\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T01:25:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/human-review-console/commit/074a26bd40672863f789e8a5d79c8f26c351b4f2","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9ENoAKDA3NGEyNmJkNDA2NzI4NjNmNzg5ZThhNWQ3OWM4ZjI2YzM1MWI0ZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/human-review-console/commit/44dee596742997e0603ab9e25dc936b82086cd55","sha":"44dee596742997e0603ab9e25dc936b82086cd55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/human-review-console/commits/44dee596742997e0603ab9e25dc936b82086cd55"}],"sha":"074a26bd40672863f789e8a5d79c8f26c351b4f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/human-review-console/commits/074a26bd40672863f789e8a5d79c8f26c351b4f2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/human-review-console/commits/44dee596742997e0603ab9e25dc936b82086cd55/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T16:01:14Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T16:01:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Pin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#21)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","tree":{"sha":"c1693e99a99997b93466af0f253b3121b02b8a95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/human-review-console/git/trees/c1693e99a99997b93466af0f253b3121b02b8a95"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/human-review-console/git/commits/44dee596742997e0603ab9e25dc936b82086cd55","verification":{"payload":"tree c1693e99a99997b93466af0f253b3121b02b8a95\nparent b57b2ecfb643045645697a55b86c48502c2131fd\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787673674 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787673674 +0800\n\nPin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#21)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbxKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAST4QAJgmJLGuIpFXS93n25HIYPJd\nmHR/5qUj8BqWzi/Giw26RBZNMXXx06acb4KhAIorfl4aiXC4C/qDaZa2KhOQBVmY\nHAq3rwFKfbPQd54Jf/VbEn3mMMcwf7fgcLX4yTlrZ9pTPbhNNgi/MUi9s9cJX1K6\n1wvLnSXqvTn6fgG3LxILu2soX5J+J8bC5aSd1d5gXNA+uBgSOW566f3h3Z17SBOP\nUl5Kl2QvkphqjtcGSm1tUPrmnkETpr/Zer31F3KpWci7iDEo4WWX4lLB7qoxQbCs\n7/QVCMkRtxQ+RLfqzb/Dycm8r64KomEu1fW30RHB6Jf3kg6xnc0WOTPwJLimxir4\nJIcZcA30nEyg0IfBSw+ix1ESxNKkjgvQaebV+0yNM6ldqo3wOKivn/jzuPZy9J8e\njAaG4krMAPFWB88vXQABC5IRAbOtw/sFoesMRD/GH5V8ubNDV4x6BSW/Mt7kAFV9\nNGjzuI3bqbdzYsWARN/6XlOQAoZJjmbYYrSsW06sSveS2k5qaTpiDyR22jrsLvko\nglj5WTIHYd1nZ8bcH8OkYraAsE5IWuEH45nmCIpKahDCbjs