m/repos/portable-genai/human-review-console/commits/39e11da0e5ad9bce01ee9983136486eb6f23a25b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/human-review-console/commits/4af812df6ce82b1b09ab2a249fcb093b95b2e5f2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T14:25:10Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T14:25:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Execute the console origin policy instead of grepping for it (#18)\n\nThe second independent re-audit pass hunted evidence that RUNS and asserts the\nwrong thing, and this was one of three it proved. The guard read the JavaScript\npolicy module as text and asserted the literals it is written with were present.\n\nChanging the policy to `if (false && isWildcard(part))` leaves every one of those\nliterals exactly where it was. The whole Python suite stayed green with the\nclickjacking control switched off. A string a file contains is not a behaviour the\nfile has, and the only way to assert the second is to run it.\n\nThe guard now calls the real function through node and asserts what it DID: every\nwildcard spelling refused, the host-source form refused, and -- the assertion that\nstops a policy which refuses everything from passing -- a legitimate origin still\nallowed. Absent node it FAILS rather than skipping, because a skip is the same\ngreen for the same reason, and `make check` already needs node for the console\ngate so this adds no dependency the gate did not have.\n\nVerified by re-running the mutation: it now fails five tests where it previously\nfailed none.","tree":{"sha":"5aff4ac9fa0a1ccf33695b4364a1be2b91c0ebf1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/human-review-console/git/trees/5aff4ac9fa0a1ccf33695b4364a1be2b91c0ebf1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/human-review-console/git/commits/4af812df6ce82b1b09ab2a249fcb093b95b2e5f2","verification":{"payload":"tree 5aff4ac9fa0a1ccf33695b4364a1be2b91c0ebf1\nparent 00abd0426b993a1bfc1f9a87d0a5d0412b056dbf\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787667910 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787667910 +0800\n\nExecute the console origin policy instead of grepping for it (#18)\n\nThe second independent re-audit pass hunted evidence that RUNS and asserts the\nwrong thing, and this was one of three it proved. The guard read the JavaScript\npolicy module as text and asserted the literals it is written with were present.\n\nChanging the policy to `if (false && isWildcard(part))` leaves every one of those\nliterals exactly where it was. The whole Python suite stayed green with the\nclickjacking control switched off. A string a file contains is not a behaviour the\nfile has, and the only way to assert the second is to run it.\n\nThe guard now calls the real function through node and asserts what it DID: every\nwildcard spelling refused, the host-source form refused, and -- the assertion that\nstops a policy which refuses everything from passing -- a legitimate origin still\nallowed. Absent node it FAILS rather than skipping, because a skip is the same\ngreen for the same reason, and `make check` already needs node for the console\ngate so this adds no dependency the gate did not have.\n\nVerified by re-running the mutation: it now fails five tests where it previously\nfailed none.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjaXGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAz+MQACBl7UVaVaAqvrFKSwbBnCbF\nHuyDQnfIknsSstJTheUXNPBqRFqtODh6ju0lChBZSgYE3CZ0iyUxGne7wbhk4Yg5\nYp9bidlUnFfnoFhGHfoMOZYE0d4ZnhvQRizsDljoyZgylIIAm5IZ75jLcjb3WzN/\n5NTOjUrbha18wDiEoydkvXrMu/GIHIlSWn0VOsPBB5lZryxGztTisZB7XXv1w/Ra\niOOy6IWB7fOiy47O8eYyCpabo6H4tZaDFWWTeT2lWGQI2bRSisrBrjBPgfkd33O9\nMuHr+bLYMquiFH1hMy54NKRjrsfCUubBziHhsrCZQcAoTuClO+7Yd/4TRa2JTVUF\n/SEv1GcRoCn9cPqnUQNXNP1D6tdzolfnMFFmrj6nM5wxzhS+Jui0qBiuinYMaa4Q\nS6wBhXAcXprYQPnJeiR9Wllmevhbx18lyMl8pQxyYO6dsFHiQZ3dVBa3ZQ31mTn8\n00zZpGWXetkE98rc+2+2LK6Fu1Hk75ONJKEUaRP8o9wn8F3y+x9FE2NQlmq9WiPX\n2FVo9FXANk4V4g3tEhmm7xNcSGqYx3cGkle70KDHe8IGCRuvjJLJBOkhJPMSUju2\ndQBQXUH0Bw0I/SqwfLOhtt27DPJEqV+hJ/zhiVzW8e7MzwRXmtohVugi0XfDvngn\nO+ZIQgoyPYSHaNRwo7ab\n=CZW9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T14:25:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/human-review-console/commit/4af812df6ce82b1b09ab2a249fcb093b95b2e5f2","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9ENoAKDRhZjgxMmRmNmNlODJiMWIwOWFiMmEyNDlmY2IwOTNiOTViMmU1ZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/human-review-console/commit/00abd0426b993a1bfc1f9a87d0a5d0412b056dbf","sha":"00abd0426b993a1bfc1f9a87d0a5d0412b056dbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/human-review-console/commits/00abd0426b993a1bfc1f9a87d0a5d0412b056dbf"}],"sha":"4af812df6ce82b1b09ab2a249fcb093b95b2e5f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/human-review-console/commits/4af812df6ce82b1b09ab2a249fcb093b95b2e5f2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/human-review-console/commits/00abd0426b993a1bfc1f9a87d0a5d0412b056dbf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T22:47:23Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T22:47:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Bump the react pair together, not react alone (#14)\n\nThe held PR raised react to 19.2.8 and left react-dom at 19.2.7, which is the\nresolution failure that has already bitten one repository in this sweep: npm\nci cannot resolve the pair, and tsc then reports every JSX and node type as\nmissing, which reads like a TypeScript problem and is not one.\n\nreact-dom and the react-dom types move with it here.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"fdeddbdaa277c3a4be97212fc48f4762440797a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/human-review-console/git/trees/fdeddbdaa277c3a4be97212fc48f4762440797a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/human-review-console/git/commits/00abd0426b993a1bfc1f9a87d0a5d0412b056dbf","verification":{"payload":"tree fdeddbdaa277c3a4be97212fc48f4762440797a7\nparent d16695d090ba891125f1510c3aeea2d00601a8f4\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787525243 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787525243 +0800\n\nBump the react pair together, not react alone (#14)\n\nThe held PR raised react to 19.2.8 and left react-dom at 19.2.7, which is the\nresolution failure that has already bitten one repository in this sweep: npm\nci cannot resolve the pair, and tsc then reports every JSX and node type as\nmissing, which reads like a TypeScript problem and is not one.\n\nreact-dom and the react-dom types move with it here.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqi3h7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAreYQAJDWffVo8skqNH7FWu3I5VLg\nm5gzoN6J3Ye6SNNuHraDXPg+GgGUT0LG3PJk/9LlB9lBDsV/cx/pGJ8XWhjrZj4a\nxwREgB2+z1wAjO4/SEcBAVCWl8slW