0deac3f298addd6a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T14:36:11Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T14:54:02Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Clear the high npm advisories in both portal shells\n\nui-rm: next 16.3.4 to 16.3.8, past the critical RCE in next/og\n(GHSA-vcvr-r3jv-pc5j). Its overrides pinned sharp to 0.35.3, below the\n0.35.4 that next 16.3.8 itself asks for and inside a high advisory, and pinned\nnanoid and postcss to versions the tree now resolves on its own; the block is\nremoved rather than re-pinned, and sharp resolves to 0.35.5.\n\nui-ops: @angular/* 22.1.x to 22.2.1 as one set (@angular/router below 22.2.0\ncarries a high advisory), with the lock regenerated because the old lock''s\nexact peer pins could not move in place. The overrides block goes the same way:\nits @modelcontextprotocol/sdk pin held hono inside two advisories, and nothing\nneeds the postcss or sockjs/uuid pins any more. fast-uri, nanoid, qs and\nip-address move past their advisories with it.\n\nnpm audit reports no vulnerabilities in either; both pass tsc and build.","tree":{"sha":"8e25bf4ab7be7405899c5a39609897bd2ced286f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/8e25bf4ab7be7405899c5a39609897bd2ced286f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/3f86ef55f07bed413336fd4a0deac3f298addd6a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravata