red_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/08ad9b5867d1a0174452034ce27f1eaf96b87525/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T10:07:53Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T10:38:16Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Wire every embedded API to the agent-observability collector\n\nPlan phase P4 (journey-portal half). hex-service-kit v0.0.11 makes a gcp tracer refuse to\nbuild without OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT (decision D1), and no deployed service set it.\n\n- otel_collector_url (DEPLOY_OTEL_COLLECTOR_URL, required, exact HTTPS origin): Terraform\n  injects it into every embedded API as OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT and as\n  OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_AUDIENCE. Both names are Terraform-owned, so no app''s api_env can\n  repoint its spans, and an app added later cannot be missed by a hand-kept map.\n- The embedded APIs now route all egress through the VPC, on their own /24 subnet with\n  Cloud NAT. The collector''s ingress is internal-only, so without this every export would\n  be refused before IAM is consulted, however valid the token. The BFF''s /26 is sized for\n  the BFF alone; Direct VPC egress holds addresses per instance.\n- The renderer''s origin checks are one helper instead of two copies.","tree":{"sha":"3c3a556f58086c60609b558042271aafed046bb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/3c3a556f58086c60609b558042271aafed046bb4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/08ad9b5867d1a0174452034ce27f1eaf96b87525","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verif