thi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T13:40:49Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Say what the model probe saw, not that the model is unserved\n\nA server busy with other requests times out the probe while still serving\nthe model; the readiness row now repeats the kit''s own first line.","tree":{"sha":"8da2b4b483a3f63a0e4a3b391883ece60fd5f903","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/8da2b4b483a3f63a0e4a3b391883ece60fd5f903"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/1dbd7b00d2f646ba0b9db559fa7c0e00d090f968","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/1dbd7b00d2f646ba0b9db559fa7c0e00d090f968","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDFkYmQ3YjAwZDJmNjQ2YmEwYjlkYjU1OWZhN2MwZTAwZDA5MGY5Njg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/977fb29e495ca9e1c10805917356eeba19ac8bfa","sha":"977fb29e495ca9e1c10805917356eeba19ac8bfa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/977fb29e495ca9e1c10805917356eeba19ac8bfa"}],"sha":"1dbd7b00d2f646ba0b9db559fa7c0e00d090f968","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/1dbd7b00d2f646ba0b9db559fa7c0e00d090f968"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/977fb29e495ca9e1c10805917356eeba19ac8bfa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T13:29:08Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T13:40:49Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Serve the live lane from one local model, and set a damaged laptop ledger aside\n\nrun_journeys.py --live now forces the live profile on every app without a\ncore online search tool and hands them all one LOCAL_MODEL_URL (plus\nLOCAL_MODEL when the operator names one), read through the kit''s own\nsettings. The per-app model URL variables and the launcher-started model\nserver are gone: the launcher probes the server with the kit client, and\nwhen nothing answers it prints the kit''s start recipe and launches anyway.\nA live sibling that cannot start is shown UNAVAILABLE in the readiness\ntable instead of stopping the launch. loan-document-intelligence runs its\nlive profile rather than gcp.\n\nThe laptop access ledger follows the laptop rule: a database, key and\ncheckpoint set that is incomplete, damaged or rolled back behind its\ncheckpoint is moved aside with hex_service_kit.audit.set_aside, never\ndeleted, and a fresh chained ledger starts with a warning, at startup and\nunder a running portal. The managed adapters keep failing closed.\n\nBumps hex-service-kit to v0.0.9 for the local-model client and set_aside.","tree":{"sha":"cd1e3244a943b42cdf3cf2fff7d84869ce39b425","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/cd1e3244a943b42cdf3cf2fff7d84869ce39b425"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/977fb29e495ca9e1c10805917356eeba19ac8bfa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/977fb29e495ca9e1c10805917356eeba19ac8bfa","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDk3N2ZiMjllNDk1Y2E5ZTFjMTA4MDU5MTczNTZlZWJhMTlhYzhiZmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/9c4aa38809d64383ee7d52891ad9f4a0a3a7d376","sha":"9c4aa38809d64383ee7d52891ad9f4a0a3a7d376","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/9c4aa38809d64383ee7d52891ad9f4a0a3a7d376"}],"sha":"977fb29e495ca9e1c10805917356eeba19ac8bfa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/977fb29e495ca9e1c10805917356eeba19ac8bfa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/9c4aa38809d64383ee7d52891ad9f4a0a3a7d376/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T03:11:30Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T03:13:59Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Refuse a deployment whose producers neither name the console nor state routing off\n\nEvery producer''s review routing is now on by default and refuses to boot under gcp without\nHUMAN_REVIEW_URL and HUMAN_REVIEW_IAP_AUDIENCE. A deployment that forgot both used to find\nout at the service''s first start; now the plan and the renderer refuse it first.\n\n- The one embedded-app map, in Terraform and in the renderer, names each producer''s routing\n  switch (empty for the console, which routes nothing), and the contract test holds the two\n  copies and the prefix rule equal.\n- A precondition on the embedded-app contract, and the same rule in deployment_config.py,\n  require each producer''s api_env to name the console or state its switch false. A new plan\n  test fails without the precondition and passes with it.\n- The pairing fixture carries cdd-sow-research''s new review_routing field, which had turned\n  the wire-shape test red on main, and the pair exempts it with its reason: what happened\n  to the hand-off is the deployment''s routing posture, while requires_human_review, the\n  decision, stays compared.","tree":{"sha":"78124b0771388cb9e6c010bb764b09fc39c98d48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/78124b0771388cb9e6c010bb764b09fc39c98d48"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/9c4aa38809d64383ee7d52891ad9f4a0a3a7d376","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/9c4aa38809d64383ee7d52891ad9f4a0a3a7d376","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDljNGFhMzg4MDlkNjQzODNlZTdkNTI4OTFhZDlmNGEwYTNhN2QzNzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/78a076de778b0f5c034f817315449f1c282aec88","sha":"78a076de778b0f5c034f817315449f1c282aec88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/78a076de778b0f5c034f817315449f1c282aec88"}],"sha":"9c4aa38809d64383ee7d52891ad9f4a0a3a7d376","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/9c4aa38809d64383ee7d52891ad9f4a0a3a7d376"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/78a076de778b0f5c034f817315449f1c282aec88/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T09:59:16Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T01:32:43Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Switch the access audit, and prove it before the portal reports ready\n\nThe portal''s cheap runtime control under the fleet''s runtime-control contract.\n\n- PORTAL_ACCESS_AUDIT is read at settings load in three states: unset is on, a boolean\n  wins, emptied or unrecognised refuses at boot. Off binds a disabled audit that records\n  nothing and whose integrity view says so, and the portal logs one warning at startup.\n- On, /healthz and /v1/healthz append one content-free startup-probe event (and verify the\n  ledger where it is verifiable in process) and answer 503 until that succeeds, retrying on\n  each probe. The portal already failed every forwarded request closed on an audit outage;\n  now it also never reports ready while it could not audit, which is what the Cloud Run\n  startup probe and make demo-warm read.\n- Terraform gains access_audit_enabled and states PORTAL_ACCESS_AUDIT on the portal service.","tree":{"sha":"5c2061d16fd94f4724e34adf5a5bcda5bb412ca0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/5c2061d16fd94f4724e34adf5a5bcda5bb412ca0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/78a076de778b0f5c034f817315449f1c282aec88","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/78a076de778b0f5c034f817315449f1c282aec88","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDc4YTA3NmRlNzc4YjBmNWMwMzRmODE3MzE1NDQ5ZjFjMjgyYWVjODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/2b4560f28ec871d754035bc12f2c2d57c9b2d7eb","sha":"2b4560f28ec871d754035bc12f2c2d57c9b2d7eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/2b4560f28ec871d754035bc12f2c2d57c9b2d7eb"}],"sha":"78a076de778b0f5c034f817315449f1c282aec88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/78a076de778b0f5c034f817315449f1c282aec88"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/2b4560f28ec871d754035bc12f2c2d57c9b2d7eb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T04:18:56Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T04:24:48Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Give the audit bucket lock the fleet''s name and no default\n\nlock_audit_bucket defaulted to false, so the stack gave the control up by\nsilence whenever a deployment did not mention it. The fleet decided on\n2026-09-12 that an irreversible control takes no default and one name,\nworm_locked; this stack was never swept.\n\nThe Terraform variable is now worm_locked with no default. The reviewed\nrunner still reads the operator''s required DEPLOY_LOCK_AUDIT_BUCKET key and\nnow passes it as worm_locked, so the deployment env does not change and its\nnext plan is unaffected. The contract test states the declined posture once\nand gains a run proving a stated lock reaches the bucket; both it and the\nrunner test were observed failing on the rename before they were updated.","tree":{"sha":"c8b5f8ad2737bf893b46f896e3491aa617fb30cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/c8b5f8ad2737bf893b46f896e3491aa617fb30cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/2b4560f28ec871d754035bc12f2c2d57c9b2d7eb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/2b4560f28ec871d754035bc12f2c2d57c9b2d7eb","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDJiNDU2MGYyOGVjODcxZDc1NDAzNWJjMTJmMmMyZDU3YzliMmQ3ZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/34f9c8deef2951f48ba09ea8d933e880e2cc9a8c","sha":"34f9c8deef2951f48ba09ea8d933e880e2cc9a8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/34f9c8deef2951f48ba09ea8d933e880e2cc9a8c"}],"sha":"2b4560f28ec871d754035bc12f2c2d57c9b2d7eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/2b4560f28ec871d754035bc12f2c2d57c9b2d7eb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/34f9c8deef2951f48ba09ea8d933e880e2cc9a8c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T14:38:50Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T14:55:39Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Start compliance-advisory with a live flagship, and point the flagship at it\n\nSince cdd-sow-research#87 (2026-09-13) every networked profile of the flagship, `live`\nincluded, answers the dossier''s compliance check by asking compliance-advisory''s /ask. The\naddress is required with no default and the port is bound at boot, so a live flagship with no\nRSK_COMPLIANCE_URL refuses to start. The rm journey lists no compliance-advisory and the\nlauncher named no URL, so `run_journeys.py --journey rm --live` -- the laptop leg of the paired\ndemonstration -- could not bring the flagship up at all. Nothing reported it, because the only\nplace the refusal surfaced was the flagship''s own boot log.\n\n`_LIVE_SIBLINGS` now declares which live app asks which sibling over which variable. Under\n`--live` a sibling the selected journeys do not show is started as a backend only (nothing\nembeds it, so its console is not built), started first, and the variable is pointed at its\nloopback API. Loopback runs no IAP, so the adapter sends no token and compliance-advisory''s\nlive profile resolves its seeded persona, which is what the adapter''s own docstring already\nsaid the launcher arranged. An operator export still wins, an emptied export is refused rather\nthan replaced, and a live flagship this launch has no sibling for is refused before it spawns,\nnaming the variable, instead of dying in a log nobody is watching. The offline profile answers\nin-process and launches nothing extra.\n\nFalsified before trusting it: with the sibling map emptied and the wiring removed, six of the\nnew and updated tests fail.","tree":{"sha":"b1b0ae120adc8ba155d55d1e504e397edd35f35a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/b1b0ae120adc8ba155d55d1e504e397edd35f35a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/34f9c8deef2951f48ba09ea8d933e880e2cc9a8c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/34f9c8deef2951f48ba09ea8d933e880e2cc9a8c","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDM0ZjljOGRlZWYyOTUxZjQ4YmEwOWVhOGQ5MzNlODgwZTJjYzlhOGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/6667564b038733c3bf4b9483029cb12499d76229","sha":"6667564b038733c3bf4b9483029cb12499d76229","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/6667564b038733c3bf4b9483029cb12499d76229"}],"sha":"34f9c8deef2951f48ba09ea8d933e880e2cc9a8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/34f9c8deef2951f48ba09ea8d933e880e2cc9a8c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/6667564b038733c3bf4b9483029cb12499d76229/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T14:46:24Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T14:48:57Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Mock google-beta in the deployment contract suite, so it needs no credentials\n\nThe suite mocked `google` only. The IAP and Artifact Registry service identities are asked for\non the google-beta surface, so that provider stayed real and every run configured it by loading\napplication default credentials. It passed on any machine that had some, which is every\nmaintainer laptop, and the first CI run that named the suite, with none, failed its first run\nand skipped the other 37.\n\nReproduced locally before the fix with no ambient credentials (an empty HOME, no GOOGLE_*\nvariables): 0 passed, 1 failed, 37 skipped. With `mock_provider \"google-beta\" {}` the same\ncommand reports 38 passed, and the run with credentials is unchanged at 38 passed.","tree":{"sha":"cf7d555c16c93c1a937231200aa9366c00f3ceca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/cf7d555c16c93c1a937231200aa9366c00f3ceca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/6667564b038733c3bf4b9483029cb12499d76229","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/6667564b038733c3bf4b9483029cb12499d76229","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDY2Njc1NjRiMDM4NzMzYzNiZjRiOTQ4MzAyOWNiMTI0OTlkNzYyMjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/288976b7a697c0f70a5692508cdb91e52fc4e591","sha":"288976b7a697c0f70a5692508cdb91e52fc4e591","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/288976b7a697c0f70a5692508cdb91e52fc4e591"}],"sha":"6667564b038733c3bf4b9483029cb12499d76229","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/6667564b038733c3bf4b9483029cb12499d76229"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/288976b7a697c0f70a5692508cdb91e52fc4e591/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T14:40:08Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T14:48:57Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Run the Terraform test suite in CI\n\nThe offline-gate job now carries terraform_directory and terraform_test,\nre-rendered from the reviewed contract in portable-genai/org-metadata@9030354,\nso run-grc-ci runs fmt -check, init -backend=false, validate and test against\ninfra/terraform on every pull request and every push to main.\n\nThe suite proves this stack''s plan-level refusals with mock providers and no\ncredentials, and until now it ran only when somebody remembered\n`make tf-validate`: no job named it, so a pull request could break a refusal\nand merge green. Run locally before declaring it (terraform 1.15.6; the\nrunner has 1.16.0): fmt and validate green, 38 passed, 0 failed.","tree":{"sha":"b3a0cdaed7ea6bfe3dd11a8cc6fb9b9c9166fb91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/b3a0cdaed7ea6bfe3dd11a8cc6fb9b9c9166fb91"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/288976b7a697c0f70a5692508cdb91e52fc4e591","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/288976b7a697c0f70a5692508cdb91e52fc4e591","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDI4ODk3NmI3YTY5N2MwZjcwYTU2OTI1MDhjZGI5MWU1MmZjNGU1OTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/0d8a8926529a381e2d8fd500507497e451fa7d50","sha":"0d8a8926529a381e2d8fd500507497e451fa7d50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/0d8a8926529a381e2d8fd500507497e451fa7d50"}],"sha":"288976b7a697c0f70a5692508cdb91e52fc4e591","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/288976b7a697c0f70a5692508cdb91e52fc4e591"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/0d8a8926529a381e2d8fd500507497e451fa7d50/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T08:44:32Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T12:12:19Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Make customer-managed encryption optional, and off by default\n\nEvery binding to the stack''s Cloud KMS key now sits behind cmek_enabled,\ndefault false: the key ring, the key, every grant to a service agent, and\nevery store, log bucket, registry and revision that took the key. Block\nbindings became dynamic blocks; scalar bindings read the key through one(),\nwhich is null when the key does not exist and omits the attribute rather\nthan pointing it at nothing. The Terraform tests that assert on key material\nturn the gate on to keep meaning what they meant.\n\nWhy the default is off: a key ring can never be deleted, a log bucket that\nhas CMEK can never drop it, and registries and document stores take their\nkey at creation. None of that changes an answer or a screen, and everything\nis encrypted at rest with Google-managed keys regardless. A deployment with\na customer whose data it must shred, whose key access must be audited or\nwhose keys must live in an HSM sets it true in its own tfvars BEFORE the\nfirst apply. Where a stack already applied it, the key''s prevent_destroy\nrefuses a plan that omits the line, which is the right answer: the stores it\nbound stay bound.\n\nThe vendored deploy-and-residency-hardening skill says the same.","tree":{"sha":"39ac3b605b922051d4652e14e8573975743a6542","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/39ac3b605b922051d4652e14e8573975743a6542"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/0d8a8926529a381e2d8fd500507497e451fa7d50","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/0d8a8926529a381e2d8fd500507497e451fa7d50","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDBkOGE4OTI2NTI5YTM4MWUyZDhmZDUwMDUwNzQ5N2U0NTFmYTdkNTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/79f7f7763a9b7201b6440ee527adc95abdadad80","sha":"79f7f7763a9b7201b6440ee527adc95abdadad80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/79f7f7763a9b7201b6440ee527adc95abdadad80"}],"sha":"0d8a8926529a381e2d8fd500507497e451fa7d50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/0d8a8926529a381e2d8fd500507497e451fa7d50"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/79f7f7763a9b7201b6440ee527adc95abdadad80/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:20:49Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:22:56Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Prove the logging adoption in a subprocess, not in the suite''s own process\n\nThe first version of this guard re-imported the served module in-process under a chosen\nprofile. CI found two things wrong with that, neither of which shows up when the file runs\nalone. It left a differently-configured module in `sys.modules` for the rest of the session,\nso `test_standalone_flag.py` failed with `ImportError: module ... not in sys.modules`. And\nimporting under `gcp` installed that profile''s middleware, so suites that assert HSTS is\nabsent under `local` started seeing it.\n\nA subprocess is not a workaround for either. What ships is a fresh interpreter importing the\nserved module under a profile, which is exactly what this now runs, and it cannot leak into\nthe session because it is not the session. The formatter-output assertion builds the formatter\ndirectly, since what it is about is the shape this service''s errors take once it is installed.\n\nProved red against a mutated copy with the module-scope call removed and the CLI hook\nunregistered: four of the five assertions fail.","tree":{"sha":"8a03db8d0fe9912a479b654499f57dd2f1196421","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/8a03db8d0fe9912a479b654499f57dd2f1196421"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/79f7f7763a9b7201b6440ee527adc95abdadad80","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/79f7f7763a9b7201b6440ee527adc95abdadad80","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDc5ZjdmNzc2M2E5YjcyMDFiNjQ0MGVlNTI3YWRjOTVhYmRhZGFkODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/141113556a212dcab0e8326ecf2948c001cfdbdb","sha":"141113556a212dcab0e8326ecf2948c001cfdbdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/141113556a212dcab0e8326ecf2948c001cfdbdb"}],"sha":"79f7f7763a9b7201b6440ee527adc95abdadad80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/79f7f7763a9b7201b6440ee527adc95abdadad80"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/141113556a212dcab0e8326ecf2948c001cfdbdb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:13:09Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:22:56Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Emit structured logs from the process that actually ships\n\nThe deployed service wrote unparsed text to stdout. Read live against the reference deployment on 2026-09-15: of roughly 60 `severity>=ERROR` entries on `cloud_run_revision` in thirty days, not one came from an application. They were the platform''s own request log, or raw stderr in which a Python traceback arrived as several `textPayload` fragments with no severity, no logger name and no trace field.\n\n`hex_service_kit.logging.configure_logging` has existed since the convention was written and is called in 75 files across the workspace. It was called in none of the seven deployed stacks.\n\nWhat was missing is specific rather than cosmetic. Cloud Logging reads `severity` from the payload, so an application error was indistinguishable from an info line and could not drive a log-based metric. `logging.googleapis.com/trace` is what puts a log line inside the request it came from. And a traceback split across N entries has no single entry carrying the exception, which is what Error Reporting groups on.\n\nBoth entry points, and the placement matters in each. The API configures at module scope and before the app object is built, because the Dockerfile CMD serves the app object: anything inside a function never runs in a shipped process. The CLI uses its own installed entry point rather than a call under `if __name__ == \"__main__\"`, which never executes for a console script.\n\nThe profile comes from `resolve_profile`, the one reader of the profile variable the drift guard permits, and the CLI path refuses to be where a bad profile surfaces: it falls back to the text formatter so the command''s own clean exit is not replaced by a traceback.\n\nWhat was observed failing. Against a mutated copy of the tree with the module-scope call removed and the CLI hook unregistered, every new assertion fails, including that an exception renders as one JSON object carrying `severity`, `service` and a complete traceback in `message`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","tree":{"sha":"8b9ebcb5e49eac64e93d4a6771c744808a24e2ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/8b9ebcb5e49eac64e93d4a6771c744808a24e2ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/141113556a212dcab0e8326ecf2948c001cfdbdb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/141113556a212dcab0e8326ecf2948c001cfdbdb","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDE0MTExMzU1NmEyMTJkY2FiMGU4MzI2ZWNmMjk0OGMwMDFjZmRiZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/c3b00189eb8d71088ea6b0d8c15e048bae58ed60","sha":"c3b00189eb8d71088ea6b0d8c15e048bae58ed60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/c3b00189eb8d71088ea6b0d8c15e048bae58ed60"}],"sha":"141113556a212dcab0e8326ecf2948c001cfdbdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/141113556a212dcab0e8326ecf2948c001cfdbdb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/c3b00189eb8d71088ea6b0d8c15e048bae58ed60/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:23:02Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:33:28Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Resync the embeddable-UI skill: both assertion header names\n\nThe canonical skill told the next repository to verify \"the injected\n`x-goog-iap-jwt-assertion`\" and nothing else. That is the instruction, not a\nmistake somebody made: an app reading the reserved name alone answers 401 to\nevery authenticated caller the day it is embedded, because the serverless\nfrontend strips the whole reserved namespace from a request entering a service\nand the embedding host therefore forwards the assertion under a second name.\n\nThis repository''s own adapter does not carry the defect. The vendored skill\ndid, so this is the doc half of the same fix, resynced from org-metadata.\n\nOnly this one skill is resynced rather than the whole set, because\ndeploy-and-residency-hardening is in flight on another branch and a blanket\n`sync-skills.sh` would pull that unmerged work in with it.","tree":{"sha":"17920fad983859243880ee7db3a32a0849d47ba2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/17920fad983859243880ee7db3a32a0849d47ba2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/c3b00189eb8d71088ea6b0d8c15e048bae58ed60","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/c3b00189eb8d71088ea6b0d8c15e048bae58ed60","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKGMzYjAwMTg5ZWI4ZDcxMDg4ZWE2YjBkOGMxNWUwNDhiYWU1OGVkNjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/423510ce3078007dab954dbd4f58329cc79741ee","sha":"423510ce3078007dab954dbd4f58329cc79741ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/423510ce3078007dab954dbd4f58329cc79741ee"}],"sha":"c3b00189eb8d71088ea6b0d8c15e048bae58ed60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/c3b00189eb8d71088ea6b0d8c15e048bae58ed60"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/423510ce3078007dab954dbd4f58329cc79741ee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T23:40:50Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T23:49:26Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Gate the posture alerts, and stop copying every audit log into this bucket\n\nTwo changes the deployed stacks already carry, brought to the rest of the\nfleet so a fork does not inherit either on its first apply.\n\nThe posture alert policies and the log-based metrics behind them now sit\nbehind posture_alerts_enabled, default false. Cloud Monitoring bills every\nmetric-based alert condition, and a deployment with nobody on call buys\nnothing with them; the signals still land in Cloud Logging, where an operator\ncan read them.\n\nThe audit sink routes only this application''s own ledger into its bucket. It\nused to copy every Cloud Audit Log entry as well, which is a second\nCMEK-encrypted ingestion of what _Default already keeps for thirty days.\n\nNothing here is applied anywhere, so neither change moves a live resource.\nWhat they remove is the trap a fork inherits the day it applies.","tree":{"sha":"fa5b98a0b2e7e9aceadfbd8df36dc29e328502d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/fa5b98a0b2e7e9aceadfbd8df36dc29e328502d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/423510ce3078007dab954dbd4f58329cc79741ee","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/423510ce3078007dab954dbd4f58329cc79741ee","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDQyMzUxMGNlMzA3ODAwN2RhYjk1NGRiZDRmNTgzMjljYzc5NzQxZWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/d0e271a11d8da1edf7402f87e7ce380c88a6b64b","sha":"d0e271a11d8da1edf7402f87e7ce380c88a6b64b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/d0e271a11d8da1edf7402f87e7ce380c88a6b64b"}],"sha":"423510ce3078007dab954dbd4f58329cc79741ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/423510ce3078007dab954dbd4f58329cc79741ee"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/d0e271a11d8da1edf7402f87e7ce380c88a6b64b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T13:43:17Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T13:46:23Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Take the posture paging off the portal and keep its evidence for thirty days\n\nThe four posture alert policies (IAP denials, service-account key creation,\nVPC-SC denials, CMEK changes) now sit behind posture_alerts_enabled, default\nfalse: Cloud Monitoring bills alert conditions and a reference deployment\npages nobody, while the signals land in Cloud Logging regardless. The edge\nevidence bucket keeps thirty days rather than 180, the window _Default keeps\nanyway; the floor moved with it in the variable, the runner and the tests.\n\nApplied live to portable-genai-sg through the reviewed runner on 2026-09-13.","tree":{"sha":"2f568fb71746dc04407e22ec3bd8c0f1e3b210d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/2f568fb71746dc04407e22ec3bd8c0f1e3b210d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/d0e271a11d8da1edf7402f87e7ce380c88a6b64b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/d0e271a11d8da1edf7402f87e7ce380c88a6b64b","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKGQwZTI3MWExMWQ4ZGExZWRmNzQwMmY4N2U3Y2UzODBjODhhNmI2NGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/d7b22002e38b58b406b3ec6c3fae2d913bd6fb8d","sha":"d7b22002e38b58b406b3ec6c3fae2d913bd6fb8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/d7b22002e38b58b406b3ec6c3fae2d913bd6fb8d"}],"sha":"d0e271a11d8da1edf7402f87e7ce380c88a6b64b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/d0e271a11d8da1edf7402f87e7ce380c88a6b64b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/d7b22002e38b58b406b3ec6c3fae2d913bd6fb8d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T10:07:56Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T10:14:27Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Vendor the reduced required-artifact set\n\nThe portfolio gate stopped requiring `docs/practices-audit.md`,\n`docs/onprem-migration.md` and a fleet-wide `COMPLIANCE.md` on 2026-09-13, and the\ncanonical skills README was updated to match. This is the vendored copy following, so\nthe convention this repository carries is the one actually in force.\n\nThe scorecard shipped PRE-FILLED from a template render, so requiring it fleet-wide\nmeant every repository asserting a per-check verdict nobody had reached. The exit guide\ndocumented a migration for a profile that is a deliberate fail-fast placeholder. The\nprinciple-to-control mapping is now a launch-set expectation, because it is what a\nbuyer is shown.\n\nRetiring a requirement does not delete a file this repository already has. Nothing is\nremoved here; only the statement of what is required changes.\n\nVendored by `sync-skills.sh` from the canonical copy in org-metadata, never edited in\nplace, so the drift check stays green.","tree":{"sha":"0c59331076f604011dfe9a18c3bce597349fff30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/0c59331076f604011dfe9a18c3bce597349fff30"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/d7b22002e38b58b406b3ec6c3fae2d913bd6fb8d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/d7b22002e38b58b406b3ec6c3fae2d913bd6fb8d","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKGQ3YjIyMDAyZTM4YjU4YjQwNmIzZWM2YzNmYWUyZDkxM2JkNmZiOGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/6cc217be8d604487ff02e43c08799b43f882a46d","sha":"6cc217be8d604487ff02e43c08799b43f882a46d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/6cc217be8d604487ff02e43c08799b43f882a46d"}],"sha":"d7b22002e38b58b406b3ec6c3fae2d913bd6fb8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/d7b22002e38b58b406b3ec6c3fae2d913bd6fb8d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/6cc217be8d604487ff02e43c08799b43f882a46d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T06:44:38Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T11:42:59Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Pair the compliance answer, and capture whether the check ran\n\ncdd-sow-research added `CddCaseResponse.compliance` (f9d4362, still open as its PR #87) and\nthis repository''s pairing fixture, comparator and evidence had not followed. `make e2e-pair`\nwould have carried a whole section of the dossier past the comparison in silence, which is the\ndrift `test_the_fixture_is_the_wire` exists to make loud: it failed locally with\n`missing [''compliance'']`. Closed rather than suppressed.\n\nThe fixture gains the `compliance` object with exactly the five fields\n`ComplianceAnswerModel` publishes, valued as the laptop profile answers: an in-process answer\nciting nothing, because the offline adapter has no policy corpus.\n\nWhat the comparator compares, and why\n\nA local and a frontier model may differ in prose but not in a determination, so:\n\n- `compliance.present` is compared in BOTH directions. An absent answer is NOT CHECKED --\n  compliance-advisory was asked and did not answer -- which the dossier records rather than\n  fails on. The laptop answers in-process and cannot fail to, so the usual\n  left-is-the-reduced-profile asymmetry does not apply and there is nothing to tolerate: a\n  managed dossier reporting NOT CHECKED beside a laptop one that was answered is a regression.\n- `compliance.question` is compared. The service builds it from the subject''s type and\n  jurisdiction and the risk band -- inputs and a compared figure, never model prose -- so two\n  profiles asking different questions asked about different dossiers.\n- `compliance.requires_human_review` is compared. It is the ONLY determination the model\n  publishes: there is no allow/deny verdict and no policy-breach list on the wire, because the\n  answer is advisory and never an outcome, so this single bit is the whole of what it decides.\n  It is an escalation reason, the class the published claim names explicitly.\n- `compliance.grounded` -- whether ANY policy source stands behind the answer -- is compared in\n  ONE direction. The laptop cites nothing by construction while the networked profiles cite the\n  policy they read, so a plain comparison would be red on every run for a reason that is a\n  property of the profile. Tolerated left-to-right and RECORDED; the managed profile answering\n  with no policy behind it diverges. The same shape and the same reasoning as\n  `adverse_media.searched`.\n- The answer''s prose and its confidence are EXEMPT, the class of rating.rationale and\n  sow.confidence, and for a stronger reason than either: the rating is settled before the\n  question is asked, so nothing in the dossier is downstream of the wording.\n- WHICH policy passages ground it, how many and their titles are EXEMPT. The local stand-in\n  carries no corpus at all, so these are citations of two different sources of truth in exactly\n  the way ownership.citations are, and comparing them would demand the laptop invent a policy\n  library it does not ship.\n\nEvidence\n\n`dossier.json` is the wire body verbatim, so the answer was already captured. The evidence\nrecord beside it was not: it now states `compliance_checked` and `compliance_grounded` in three\nstates -- null for NOT CHECKED, false for answered from a stand-in, true for grounded -- so a\nservice outage is legible without reading the raw dossier. Answering every dossier from a\nstand-in unnoticed is the defect that produced the field in the first place.\n\nEach of the nine assertions was observed failing against a mutated copy of the tree, never\nagainst the committed one: dropping each of the four compared keys, taking `compliance.grounded`\nout of ONE_WAY, comparing the citations, emitting the answer''s fields when no answer arrived,\nand comparing the prose and the confidence.\n\n`test_the_fixture_is_the_wire` also resolves each model by name now, so a sibling checkout that\npredates a model reports which side is behind instead of an AttributeError raised while the\npairs list is still being built. No relaxation: an unresolvable model still fails.\n\n`PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make check` green (824 passed, 2 skipped, eval GATE PASS) with\nDOC1_REPO_PATH on a checkout of cdd-sow-research''s compliance branch. Against that repository''s\ncurrent main the fixture correctly reports the inverse, `invented [''compliance'']`, until #87\nlands; CI is a single-repo checkout and skips the comparison either way.","tree":{"sha":"8b7c8d4e9107adaa46cb85845b6bc8b45c71a5c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/8b7c8d4e9107adaa46cb85845b6bc8b45c71a5c2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/6cc217be8d604487ff02e43c08799b43f882a46d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/6cc217be8d604487ff02e43c08799b43f882a46d","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDZjYzIxN2JlOGQ2MDQ0ODdmZjAyZTQzYzA4Nzk5YjQzZjg4MmE0NmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/a822a98f446ceef3626b9b9dac7e546fae1ba631","sha":"a822a98f446ceef3626b9b9dac7e546fae1ba631","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/a822a98f446ceef3626b9b9dac7e546fae1ba631"}],"sha":"6cc217be8d604487ff02e43c08799b43f882a46d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/6cc217be8d604487ff02e43c08799b43f882a46d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/a822a98f446ceef3626b9b9dac7e546fae1ba631/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T06:16:23Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T06:18:58Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Make the shells a deployment names, so Marketing gets a host\n\nEvery persona shell was written out twice, once as `rm_shell` and once as\n`ops_shell`: five resources, the IAP backend map, the url map''s host rules and\npath matchers, the certificate''s domain list and its `random_id` keeper, the DNS\nset, four outputs, the rollback component list, four DEPLOY_* variables and the\nrenderer that reads them. Thirteen places. The Marketing journey has been in\n`config/journeys.yaml` since the persona journeys landed and no deployment could\npublish it, because the contract took exactly two shell images and two domains.\n\nA shell is now an entry in one ordered list. `var.shells` /\n`DEPLOY_SHELLS_JSON` is `{journey, image, domain}` per published host, the way\n`embedded_apps` names the subset of apps, and `shells.tf` derives the rest. No\n`.tf` file outside it names a journey, and a contract test holds that true so the\nenumeration cannot grow a second home.\n\nThe list is a list, not a map, and the order is load-bearing in one place: the\nmanaged certificate''s domain list. The provider treats it as ordered and\nForceNew, so a map would have sorted today''s two hosts into [ops, rm] and\nrotated the reference deployment''s certificate for nothing. The first entry is\nalso the url map''s default backend.\n\nFour refusals at plan, each with a test that fails when the guard is removed:\na journey the catalog does not define; two shells on one hostname; one journey\nserved by two shells; and a shell none of whose journey''s apps are in\n`embedded_apps` -- the BFF drops a journey with no mounted app and the React\nshell falls back to the FIRST journey in the catalog, so that host would serve\nanother persona''s journey and look perfectly healthy.\n\nThe two existing shells move in state rather than being replaced: `shells.tf`\ncarries a `moved` block per address and the certificate keeper is the same\nstring the hand-written pair produced, so a deployment naming the same two\nshells in the same order plans no shell create or destroy. One in-place change\nis expected -- the RM shell''s probes move from `/` to `/healthz`, which the\nstatic server both images ship already answers, because one `for_each` resource\ncannot probe two paths.\n\nAlso:\n- `ui-rm` takes a `JOURNEY` build argument. The journey is compiled in (Next.js\n  inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_*), so Terraform cannot read it back out of a digest: the\n  `journey` field is the operator''s claim and `e2e/app_coverage.py` is what holds\n  a hostname to the journey it renders.\n- `live_profile_check.py` takes `--shell <journey>=<url>`, repeatable, and checks\n  the feed against the shells it was given. A journey whose contents it cannot\n  state is refused rather than checked against nothing.\n- `.env.example` was missing `DEPLOY_PRODUCTION_EDGE_ENABLED`, so a `.env`\n  copied from it was refused for a key the example never named. Added, with a\n  test comparing the example to the loader''s own required set.\n- `infra/terraform/README.md` gains the add-a-shell-host procedure and what the\n  certificate replacement costs the hosts that were already live: it is\n  create-before-destroy onto a fresh name, so not the\n  `resourceInUseByAnotherResource` failure of 2026-08-29, but the replacement\n  starts PROVISIONING on every domain including the live ones.","tree":{"sha":"b60e92e252a5ccc17085b28574d74b1a2e81331a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/b60e92e252a5ccc17085b28574d74b1a2e81331a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/a822a98f446ceef3626b9b9dac7e546fae1ba631","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/a822a98f446ceef3626b9b9dac7e546fae1ba631","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKGE4MjJhOThmNDQ2Y2VlZjM2MjZiOWI5ZGFjN2U1NDZmYWUxYmE2MzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/57fafcc9302a3e260ffa9db7d085d259d3e2e34f","sha":"57fafcc9302a3e260ffa9db7d085d259d3e2e34f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/57fafcc9302a3e260ffa9db7d085d259d3e2e34f"}],"sha":"a822a98f446ceef3626b9b9dac7e546fae1ba631","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/a822a98f446ceef3626b9b9dac7e546fae1ba631"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/57fafcc9302a3e260ffa9db7d085d259d3e2e34f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T13:32:34Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T13:36:59Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump shared kits: hex-service-kit v0.0.8","tree":{"sha":"13b9a738bafa01277ab27d3d4d5151ae1daaf8d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/13b9a738bafa01277ab27d3d4d5151ae1daaf8d3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/57fafcc9302a3e260ffa9db7d085d259d3e2e34f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/57fafcc9302a3e260ffa9db7d085d259d3e2e34f","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDU3ZmFmY2M5MzAyYTNlMjYwZmZhOWRiN2QwODVkMjU5ZDNlMmUzNGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/9b7b3e531497507a235544853a6bb300da240fd2","sha":"9b7b3e531497507a235544853a6bb300da240fd2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/9b7b3e531497507a235544853a6bb300da240fd2"}],"sha":"57fafcc9302a3e260ffa9db7d085d259d3e2e34f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/57fafcc9302a3e260ffa9db7d085d259d3e2e34f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/9b7b3e531497507a235544853a6bb300da240fd2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T13:13:26Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T13:18:35Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Derive the deployable embedded apps from the one map that names their env\n\nvariables.tf allowed sixteen embedded app ids, but the managed-profile\nvalidation looked each one up in a seven-entry map and fell back to \"\".\nThe nine allowed-but-unmapped ids, marketing-compliance-gate among them,\nfailed the \"must use gcp or platform\" check by construction, so Track C\nrunbook C1 would refuse at plan. The reserved-env lists, the IAP audience\ninjection in cloud_run.tf, the error message and the renderer in\ndeployment_config.py each carried their own copy of the set.\n\ninfra/terraform/embedded_apps.tf now holds local.embedded_app_managed_env,\nid -> {profile, iap_audience}. The deployable ids, the managed-profile\ncheck, the Terraform-owned env names and the audience injection all derive\nfrom it, and the error messages name the ids from it. The checks are\npreconditions on terraform_data.embedded_app_contract because the stack\ndeclares Terraform >= 1.7, where a validation block cannot read a local.\nThe audience injection indexes the map directly: the old membership guard\nlet an unmapped app deploy with no audience at all.\n\nmarketing-compliance-gate joins with MKT_GOV_PROFILE and\nMKT_GOV_IAP_AUDIENCE, the names its config.py and gcp/iap_identity.py\nread. The other eight ids that were allowed but never mapped drop out\nuntil someone maps them. A new precondition refuses a Cloud Run service\nname over 49 characters at plan instead of mid-apply.\n\nThe renderer derives its known ids from one _MANAGED_ENV_BY_APP and the\n/apps/<id> mount rule. test_terraform_source_contract.py holds the two\nmaps equal, checks each profile against the launcher and each audience\nagainst the <PREFIX>_IAP_AUDIENCE convention, and fails if an app id or\nmanaged variable name reappears in any other .tf file. New terraform test\nruns accept marketing-compliance-gate on its managed profile and reject it\nwithout one, on local, overriding its audience, with an unmapped id, and\nover the name limit. Each guard was proven red on a mutated copy.","tree":{"sha":"5b907561a085b83c1b1797ea3bdfcb9a4cb0cca0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/5b907561a085b83c1b1797ea3bdfcb9a4cb0cca0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/9b7b3e531497507a235544853a6bb300da240fd2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{