T18:29:30Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T18:35:55Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump shared kits: agent-eval-kit v0.0.3","tree":{"sha":"201bc84e58b05b71068e6e484e5bb23a8865bcf5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/201bc84e58b05b71068e6e484e5bb23a8865bcf5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/e9772ec8e3308ff98d1c73529ce4d28b2a37438c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/e9772ec8e3308ff98d1c73529ce4d28b2a37438c","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKGU5NzcyZWM4ZTMzMDhmZjk4ZDFjNzM1MjljZTRkMjhiMmEzNzQzOGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/7baa8c465c68b2db0e3708c9a99cb17ca42c325f","sha":"7baa8c465c68b2db0e3708c9a99cb17ca42c325f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/7baa8c465c68b2db0e3708c9a99cb17ca42c325f"}],"sha":"e9772ec8e3308ff98d1c73529ce4d28b2a37438c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/e9772ec8e3308ff98d1c73529ce4d28b2a37438c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/7baa8c465c68b2db0e3708c9a99cb17ca42c325f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T16:39:21Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T16:41:59Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Score the two invariants that guard a grant, and give every bar a rubric\n\nThis repository had no rubric directory at all: every bar was an unlabelled\nmodule constant, which is exactly what practice E1 asks a repository not to do.\nSeven rubric files now carry each number beside the argument for it, the runner\nreads them, and assert_covers fails the build in both directions.\n\nTwo invariants moved from unit tests into the gate. The CSRF token and the\nbrowser-provenance proof are the two things standing between a hostile page and\na grant made in a signed-in user''s name, and both were covered only by tests. A\nunit test can be deleted in the same commit as the thing it guards, and a\npromotion that regressed either should not be certifiable. csrf_token_integrity\nand host_proof_integrity score the shipped verify_csrf_token and\nassess_browser_provenance over fifteen new golden cases.\n\nBoth corpora carry refusals as well as acceptances, and the refusals are the\ninteresting half: a token from another session, for another action, expired,\ntampered with or absent; a look-alike origin (portal.example.attacker.test), an\nunlabelled fetch site, a same-site rather than same-origin call, and a\nnavigation request. A one-directional corpus would score a verifier that accepts\neverything at a perfect 1.000, which is indistinguishable from having no check.\n\nFour bars said less than they meant. journey_integrity, identity_isolation,\nrouting_correctness and tenant_policy_isolation at 0.99 over corpora of four and\nsix cases were arithmetically identical to 1.0: five of six is 0.833. They now\nsay 1.0, which is also what the properties mean, since a trust boundary that\nholds 99% of the time is a boundary with a hole in it.\n\nThe promotion bundle default was \"local\", a name the authority does not\nregister, so an unset PORTAL_BUNDLE_ID sent a name that fails closed on\nUnknownMetricError: not a loose gate, no gate. Nothing reported it, because the\noffline smoke path never touches that line. It is now the registered\njourney-portal bundle.\n\nF4 and F5 are recorded as n/a with a reason rather than left blank. Nothing here\ngenerates text, so there is no model to judge and no model output to replay; the\neval harness is re-purposed to score security and composition invariants, which\nis the right reading of an eval for a trust boundary.\n\ndocs/evals.md is generated from the rubrics and the corpus, with --check in\n`make check`. Pin: agent-eval-kit v0.0.2.\n\nVerified: `make check` green end to end (779 passed, eval PASS over 35 cases and\n7 metrics).","tree":{"sha":"a17a8de72070a9c5fe04ac7392aea8d4d89ba04a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/a17a8de72070a9c5fe04ac7392aea8d4d89ba04a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/7baa8c465c68b2db0e3708c9a99cb17ca42c325f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/7baa8c465c68b2db0e3708c9a99cb17ca42c325f","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDdiYWE4YzQ2NWM2OGIyZGIwZTM3MDhjOWE5OWNiMTdjYTQyYzMyNWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/522fc99389079879fc8e688c4d33ce3e0de5e5df","sha":"522fc99389079879fc8e688c4d33ce3e0de5e5df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/522fc99389079879fc8e688c4d33ce3e0de5e5df"}],"sha":"7baa8c465c68b2db0e3708c9a99cb17ca42c325f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/7baa8c465c68b2db0e3708c9a99cb17ca42c325f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/522fc99389079879fc8e688c4d33ce3e0de5e5df/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T14:53:41Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T15:32:06Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump shared kits: hex-service-kit v0.0.7","tree":{"sha":"43cf5b37b36db3afc5087a44c2444640c0661dbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/43cf5b37b36db3afc5087a44c2444640c0661dbf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/522fc99389079879fc8e688c4d33ce3e0de5e5df","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/522fc99389079879fc8e688c4d33ce3e0de5e5df","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDUyMmZjOTkzODkwNzk4NzlmYzhlNjg4YzRkMzNjZTNlMGRlNWU1ZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/5c8bed33400a8473f1cc28a9656b89844fa4fa41","sha":"5c8bed33400a8473f1cc28a9656b89844fa4fa41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/5c8bed33400a8473f1cc28a9656b89844fa4fa41"}],"sha":"522fc99389079879fc8e688c4d33ce3e0de5e5df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/522fc99389079879fc8e688c4d33ce3e0de5e5df"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/5c8bed33400a8473f1cc28a9656b89844fa4fa41/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T13:48:12Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T13:54:56Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Compose the second line into a journey of its own\n\nThe four wave-3 systems (credit-portfolio-early-warning, soc-fraud-fusion,\ncontrol-room-handover, issue-remediation-capa) appeared nowhere in this repository. Their\ndemo books have nothing to be shown on and the plan''s own note that they \"need a journey\nbefore they need rows\" was true.\n\nA `risk` journey composes all four plus the review console the other persona journeys\nalready end in. Journeys are config, so the change is the config, the launcher''s two app\nmaps, the shell port and the CORS origin that goes with it. The four repositories all\ndefault to the template''s own :8099 and cannot be launched side by side on their own\ndefaults, so the portal assigns 8106 to 8109 and the launcher passes each as --port.\n\nFive walkthrough steps, and every one asserts a FIGURE or an absence rather than a\nheading: a heading renders whether or not anything was computed, which is how the\nmarketing walkthrough spent a wave reporting on an account no seed contained.\n\n  risk-early-warning  waits for the composite score beside the floor\n  risk-fraud-fusion   waits for the correlated alert ids and FAILS if another tenant''s\n                      alert appears in the same scope, which is the only way to show an\n                      authorisation control: by what it withholds\n  risk-handover       waits for a queue depth and fails on an empty scorecard, which is\n                      what a wall-clock window produced before the window was made to end\n                      at the shift being handed over\n  risk-issue          fails if either malformed intake record was admitted rather than\n                      dropped\n\nThe CORS origin matters more than it looks: a journey whose shell port is missing from\nthe local allowlist is a shell the BFF refuses, and the first place to meet that is a\ndemo.\n\nGate green: 765 tests, 135 subtests, eval 1.000 on all five metrics. The launcher\nresolves the journey end to end (--dry-run --journey risk).","tree":{"sha":"033fcd48ca5875fcf4872f5be5483ed61d9d666f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/033fcd48ca5875fcf4872f5be5483ed61d9d666f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/5c8bed33400a8473f1cc28a9656b89844fa4fa41","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/5c8bed33400a8473f1cc28a9656b89844fa4fa41","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDVjOGJlZDMzNDAwYTg0NzNmMWNjMjhhOTY1NmI4OTg0NGZhNGZhNDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/0d0525e6186e28771e760bbd225278b54b955b42","sha":"0d0525e6186e28771e760bbd225278b54b955b42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/0d0525e6186e28771e760bbd225278b54b955b42"}],"sha":"5c8bed33400a8473f1cc28a9656b89844fa4fa41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/5c8bed33400a8473f1cc28a9656b89844fa4fa41"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/0d0525e6186e28771e760bbd225278b54b955b42/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T14:02:09Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T14:04:33Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Report on an account that exists, and assert a figure rather than a heading\n\nThe marketing journey''s performance step submitted acct-sg-001, which exists in\nno seed and no BigQuery table. It passed because the local metrics adapter\nignored the account entirely and returned the same rows for any string, while the\nmanaged adapter has always filtered on it: the demo was showing a report the\ndeployment could not produce. That adapter now filters, so this step would have\nstarted failing, correctly, and it names a real account instead.\n\nBoth of its assertions were also satisfiable by an empty report. The two headings\nrender whenever the page lays out, so waiting for them proved the console drew\nrather than that anything was measured. The step now requires the report to name\nthe account back and to carry a rate, neither of which an empty one has. The\ncampaign step gains the same kind of assertion: a plan that allocated nothing\nstill renders its calendar, so the budget submitted has to appear in what came\nback.\n\nThe fake console the negative-control tests drive now models body text, because\nthree steps assert on a figure rather than an element and none of those\nassertions was being exercised. Its performance screen is a real report rather\nthan two bare headings, and a new case pins the shape the step was actually in:\nlayout present, headings present, nothing underneath.\n\nmake check passes: lint, typecheck, 30 walkthrough tests, five eval metrics.","tree":{"sha":"65f3c35d3aac361cd71b7a8c4012b99148420269","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/65f3c35d3aac361cd71b7a8c4012b99148420269"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/0d0525e6186e28771e760bbd225278b54b955b42","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/0d0525e6186e28771e760bbd225278b54b955b42","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDBkMDUyNWU2MTg2ZTI4NzcxZTc2MGJiZDIyNTI3OGI1NGI5NTViNDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/dc198b40d4c2c1f4387dce7ef24db750479fa413","sha":"dc198b40d4c2c1f4387dce7ef24db750479fa413","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/dc198b40d4c2c1f4387dce7ef24db750479fa413"}],"sha":"0d0525e6186e28771e760bbd225278b54b955b42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/0d0525e6186e28771e760bbd225278b54b955b42"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/dc198b40d4c2c1f4387dce7ef24db750479fa413/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T00:19:36Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T00:27:36Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Read the client''s portfolio before reading the house view\n\nThe RM journey''s advisory step registered a portfolio, built a briefing and\nasserted that its citations were real. It never showed the portfolio, so an\naudience saw recommendations with nothing to judge relevance against, and the\nstep would have passed just as well on a client whose holdings the briefing said\nnothing about.\n\nSplits it in two. The first step reads the portfolio against the allocation the\nbank publishes for that risk profile, and asserts a computed status and the named\nmodel portfolio rather than a heading: a panel that rendered the client and no\ngaps would look almost identical from the back of a room. It submits nothing and\nreturns instantly, because deciding what a portfolio is short of needs no model,\nand the note says so while it is on screen.\n\nThe second step then reads the day''s research against those gaps, and gains one\nassertion: that the briefing set the house view against this portfolio at all,\nwhich a briefing losing its report panel would fail while still passing every\ncitation check above.\n\nThe presenter notes carry the pair of claims the steps exist to make, and the\ntests pin both: the shortfalls are arithmetic, and a gap never overrides the\nsuitability check. Deleting either phrase fails the build, which was proved by\ndeleting one.\n\nmake check passes: lint, typecheck, 30 walkthrough tests, five eval metrics.","tree":{"sha":"50388b11ccabfffc2bc9192bf393994a495138ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/50388b11ccabfffc2bc9192bf393994a495138ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/dc198b40d4c2c1f4387dce7ef24db750479fa413","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/dc198b40d4c2c1f4387dce7ef24db750479fa413","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKGRjMTk4YjQwZDRjMmMxZjQzODdkY2U3ZWYyNGRiNzUwNDc5ZmE0MTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/6c249085052807927d4c307e772286855d5b3838","sha":"6c249085052807927d4c307e772286855d5b3838","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/6c249085052807927d4c307e772286855d5b3838"}],"sha":"dc198b40d4c2c1f4387dce7ef24db750479fa413","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/dc198b40d4c2c1f4387dce7ef24db750479fa413"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","id":49699333,"login":"dependabot[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/6c249085052807927d4c307e772286855d5b3838/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T05:35:41Z","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dependabot[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T22:22:52Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump next from 16.3.3 to 16.3.4 in /ui-rm\n\nBumps [next](https://github.com/vercel/next.js) from 16.3.3 to 16.3.4.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/compare/v16.3.3...v16.3.4)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: next\n  dependency-version: 16.3.4\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a19ed3e4a740ac98b6689596741ec39bdcd9e48e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/a19ed3e4a740ac98b6689596741ec39bdcd9e48e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/6c249085052807927d4c307e772286855d5b3838","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/6c249085052807927d4c307e772286855d5b3838","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDZjMjQ5MDg1MDUyODA3OTI3ZDRjMzA3ZTc3MjI4Njg1NWQ1YjM4Mzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/c216d29f4996ec823f20b3a5933288e281390853","sha":"c216d29f4996ec823f20b3a5933288e281390853","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/c216d29f4996ec823f20b3a5933288e281390853"}],"sha":"6c249085052807927d4c307e772286855d5b3838","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/6c249085052807927d4c307e772286855d5b3838"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/c216d29f4996ec823f20b3a5933288e281390853/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-06T05:33:07Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T05:33:07Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Name systems by repository, and make the hosted walkthrough reach credit-memo\n\n* Name the systems this repo depends on, instead of their catalog ids\n\nRepository names are unique across the organization, so a reader no longer has\nto resolve a code through a table to learn which system is meant. The catalog\ndropped its ID column, and this repository follows.\n\nBeyond prose, four identifier changes:\n\n- The review payload''s source_key prefix is the repository name. It is a dedup\n  key -- human-review-console queries on it and the local store makes it a\n  PRIMARY KEY -- so producers and the console have to agree, and the branch\n  carries the migration for rows written under the old prefix.\n- Terraform''s local.render_catalog_id becomes local.render_repository. It feeds\n  display names and descriptions, which update in place.\n- scripts/demo.py''s catalog id is deleted rather than renamed: a REPOSITORY\n  constant and a \"repository\" state key were already there beside it.\n- scripts/rename_fork.py loses --catalog-id, which had nothing left to rewrite.\n\nLines that outgrew the 100-column limit because a name is longer than an id are\nrewrapped rather than shortened by dropping the name. `ruff check`,\n`ruff format --check` and the offline tests are clean.\n\nDeployed resource identifiers are deliberately NOT changed: the Terraform\nname_prefix stems and the Secret Manager secret ids still carry the old\nlowercase id. Those name resources that exist in the deployment, and renaming a\nname_prefix destroys and recreates them, so they are an infrastructure\nmigration rather than a rename.\n\n* Unrot the hosted walkthrough so --iap-impersonate can run at all\n\nFour independent faults, each of which stopped the script before the one after\nit could be seen. Found by running it against the deployment rather than by\nreading it.\n\nThe dynamic load of e2e/targets.py never registered the module in sys.modules.\nOn 3.12 the dataclasses machinery resolves a class''s defining module through\nsys.modules, so building targets.py''s frozen dataclass raised AttributeError on\na None module and no token could be minted at all.\n\ntargets._setting no longer exists; it is targets.setting. The caller was left\nbehind by the rename. _mint_iap_token is still private and still correct.\n\nThe health probe asked <apiBase>/healthz, but the API mounts its routes under\n/v1, so it 404''d and the preflight refused every profile. Two identical copies\nof that probe existed, in _require_profile and _require_live; both are fixed,\nand both now try the versioned path and fall back, so one probe fits a\ndeployment and a laptop alike.\n\nFiling a document waited a bare 30s -- the only long wait in this file without a\nnamed budget, against 300s and 900s elsewhere. Against a deployment the file\ncrosses the edge to an API at minScale=0 and a PDF is parsed in another region,\nso it expired mid-upload. Now _UPLOAD_TIMEOUT_MS.\n\nWith these, the hosted rehearsal reaches step 03 and its first two steps pass.\nStep 03 still fails: the Build CDD dossier click issues no request at all -- the\nAPI log for the whole window carries only liveness probes, where a green\nmake e2e-gcp shows POST /v1/cdd. That is a separate fault, still open.\n\n* Guard the ops persona-picker wait the way the rm one already is\n\n_rm_open skips the \"Demo identity\" wait when _HOSTED, because the picker is a\nlocal-profile affordance and the deployment renders none -- identity there is\nwhoever signed in through IAP. _ops_open was left behind by that fix and waits\nunconditionally, so the first hosted ops run would hang on text that never\nappears.\n\nLatent today: no ops step is marked hosted=True, so the hosted rehearsal never\nreaches it. It would bite the moment one is enabled, which is exactly what\nadding the credit-memo use case to hosted testing requires.\n\n* Reach the credit-memo step on the deployment, and stop three stale asserts\n\ncredit-memo-drafting is now deployed and served by the Ops shell, so the hosted\nwalkthrough can include it. Four things stood in the way, each hiding the next.\n\nThe hosted branch forced ops_origin = rm_origin with the comment \"hosted steps\nare the RM subset; one origin drives them all\". That stopped being true: the Ops\nshell answers on its own host and _open_shell waits on that shell''s heading, so\nthe step opened the wrong shell. The ops host is now named through\nPORTAL_E2E_SHELL_OPS_BASE_URL, falling back to the RM origin so an RM-only\ndeployment behaves exactly as before.\n\nops-open and ops-credit-memo-drafting-credit-memo are marked hosted, with the\nhosted notes the RM steps already carry.\n\n_require_live could not verify this app at all: no health route is reachable\nthrough the portal proxy (/v1/healthz reaches the API and 404s; bare /healthz\nnever arrives). It now falls back to the OpenAPI document, which every one of\nthese FastAPI apps serves, and says out loud that it verified reachability\nrather than the gcp profile. That is a weaker promise than the one made for\ncdd-sow-research, and the fix belongs in the app.\n\nTwo locators had gone stale against the richer form: get_by_label(\"Borrower\")\nresolves to two textboxes, and get_by_text(\"Credit memo\") matches the submit\nbutton and the layout''s provenance banner, so the result wait could pass before\nanything was built. Both are now unambiguous.\n\nStill open, and out of scope here: the build itself submits nothing. The API log\nfor the whole step carries only the preflight probes -- no memo request arrives.\nThe app has grown a multi-step flow (label, extract, adjust, confirm the spread,\nthen build) and _ops_doc2 still drives the single-form shape it had before.\n\n* Format the credit-memo result wait the way ruff wants it\n\nThe multi-line get_by_role(...).first.wait_for(...) I wrote fails\nruff format --check, which is the offline gate''s second command, so the PR was\nblocked on formatting rather than on anything it asserts.\n\n* Make the ops narration prose, and update the test premise the deployment changed\n\nTwo guards in this repo caught the credit-memo change, and both were right.\n\nThe presenter notes must read as spoken prose of at least two sentences; the\nhosted note I added for the credit-memo step was one sentence joined by a colon,\nso it failed the narration guard rather than the step.\n\ntest_hosted_selection_excludes_apps_the_deployment_does_not_embed asserted that\na hosted ops run is only the close, on the stated premise that the Ops journey''s\napps are not deployed. credit-memo-drafting was deployed on 2026-09-05 and is\nserved by the Ops shell, so that premise is now false. The exclusion the test\nactually guards -- that a step which is not hosted cannot be named on a hosted\nrun -- is unchanged and still asserted.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"911031421be7003901368ff5285e919c82bc60b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/911031421be7003901368ff5285e919c82bc60b9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/c216d29f4996ec823f20b3a5933288e281390853","verification":{"payload":"tree 911031421be7003901368ff5285e919c82bc60b9\nparent 12169d01f748841e20ad65a6546c790ffc389744\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1788672787 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788672787 +0800\n\nName systems by repository, and make the hosted walkthrough reach credit-memo\n\n* Name the systems this repo depends on, instead of their catalog ids\n\nRepository names are unique across the organization, so a reader no longer has\nto resolve a code through a table to learn which system is meant. The catalog\ndropped its ID column, and this repository follows.\n\nBeyond prose, four identifier changes:\n\n- The review payload''s source_key prefix is the repository name. It is a dedup\n  key -- human-review-console queries on it and the local store makes it a\n  PRIMARY KEY -- so producers and the console have to agree, and the branch\n  carries the migration for rows written under the old prefix.\n- Terraform''s local.render_catalog_id becomes local.render_repository. It feeds\n  display names and descriptions, which update in place.\n- scripts/demo.py''s catalog id is deleted rather than renamed: a REPOSITORY\n  constant and a \"repository\" state key were already there beside it.\n- scripts/rename_fork.py loses --catalog-id, which had nothing left to rewrite.\n\nLines that outgrew the 100-column limit because a name is longer than an id are\nrewrapped rather than shortened by dropping the name. `ruff check`,\n`ruff format --check` and the offline tests are clean.\n\nDeployed resource identifiers are deliberately NOT changed: the Terraform\nname_prefix stems and the Secret Manager secret ids still carry the old\nlowercase id. Those name resources that exist in the deployment, and renaming a\nname_prefix destroys and recreates them, so they are an infrastructure\nmigration rather than a rename.\n\n* Unrot the hosted walkthrough so --iap-impersonate can run at all\n\nFour independent faults, each of which stopped the script before the one after\nit could be seen. Found by running it against the deployment rather than by\nreading it.\n\nThe dynamic load of e2e/targets.py never registered the module in sys.modules.\nOn 3.12 the dataclasses machinery resolves a class''s defining module through\nsys.modules, so building targets.py''s frozen dataclass raised AttributeError on\na None module and no token could be minted at all.\n\ntargets._setting no longer exists; it is targets.setting. The caller was left\nbehind by the rename. _mint_iap_token is still private and still correct.\n\nThe health probe asked <apiBase>/healthz, but the API mounts its routes under\n/v1, so it 404''d and the preflight refused every profile. Two identical copies\nof that probe existed, in _require_profile and _require_live; both are fixed,\nand both now try the versioned path and fall back, so one probe fits a\ndeployment and a laptop alike.\n\nFiling a document waited a bare 30s -- the only long wait in this file without a\nnamed budget, against 300s and 900s elsewhere. Against a deployment the file\ncrosses the edge to an API at minScale=0 and a PDF is parsed in another region,\nso it expired mid-upload. Now _UPLOAD_TIMEOUT_MS.\n\nWith these, the hosted rehearsal reaches step 03 and its first two steps pass.\nStep 03 still fails: the Build CDD dossier click issues no request at all -- the\nAPI log for the whole window carries only liveness probes, where a green\nmake e2e-gcp shows POST /v1/cdd. That is a separate fault, still open.\n\n* Guard the ops persona-picker wait the way the rm one already is\n\n_rm_open skips the \"Demo identity\" wait when _HOSTED, because the picker is a\nlocal-profile affordance and the deployment renders none -- identity there is\nwhoever signed in through IAP. _ops_open was left behind by that fix and waits\nunconditionally, so the first hosted ops run would hang on text that never\nappears.\n\nLatent today: no ops step is marked hosted=True, so the hosted rehearsal never\nreaches it. It would bite the moment one is enabled, which is exactly what\nadding the credit-memo use case to hosted testing requires.\n\n* Reach the credit-memo step on the deployment, and stop three stale asserts\n\ncredit-memo-drafting is now deployed and served by the Ops shell, so the hosted\nwalkthrough can include it. Four things stood in the way, each hiding the next.\n\nThe hosted branch forced ops_origin = rm_origin with the comment \"hosted steps\nare the RM subset; one origin drives them all\". That stopped being true: the Ops\nshell answers on its own host and _open_shell waits on that shell''s heading, so\nthe step opened the wrong shell. The ops host is now named through\nPORTAL_E2E_SHELL_OPS_BASE_URL, falling back to the RM origin so an RM-only\ndeployment behaves exactly as before.\n\nops-open and ops-credit-memo-drafting-credit-memo are marked hosted, with the\nhosted notes the RM steps already carry.\n\n_require_live could not verify this app at all: no health route is reachable\nthrough the portal proxy (/v1/healthz reaches the API and 404s; bare /healthz\nnever arrives). It now falls back to the OpenAPI document, which every one of\nthese FastAPI apps serves, and says out loud that it verified reachability\nrather than the gcp profile. That is a weaker promise than the one made for\ncdd-sow-research, and the fix belongs in the app.\n\nTwo locators had gone stale against the richer form: get_by_label(\"Borrower\")\nresolves to two textboxes, and get_by_text(\"Credit memo\") matches the submit\nbutton and the layout''s provenance banner, so the result wait could pass before\nanything was built. Both are now unambiguous.\n\nStill open, and out of scope here: the build itself submits nothing. The API log\nfor the whole step carries only the preflight probes -- no memo request arrives.\nThe app has grown a multi-step flow (label, extract, adjust, confirm the spread,\nthen build) and _ops_doc2 still drives the single-form shape it had before.\n\n* Format the credit-memo result wait the way ruff wants it\n\nThe multi-line get_by_role(...).first.wait_for(...) I wrote fails\nruff format --check, which is the offline gate''s second command, so the PR was\nblocked on formatting rather than on anything it asserts.\n\n* Make the ops narration prose, and update the test premise the deployment changed\n\nTwo guards in this repo caught the credit-memo change, and both were right.\n\nThe presenter notes must read as spoken prose of at least two sentences; the\nhosted note I added for the credit-memo step was one sentence joined by a colon,\nso it failed the narration guard rather than the step.\n\ntest_hosted_selection_excludes_apps_the_deployment_does_not_embed asserted that\na hosted ops run is only the close, on the stated premise that the Ops journey''s\napps are not deployed. credit-memo-drafting was deployed on 2026-09-05 and is\nserved by the Ops shell, so that premise is now false. The exclusion the test\nactually guards -- that a step which is not hosted cannot be named on a hosted\nrun -- is unchanged and still asserted.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnPsTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZyUQAJ1WsAQ10w+slpSFIdJoWCbu\n+PtSg96wd9YGyzm3bv9eB81dNZcZ8/vFOO9j52mbntG094pHbyvpdD7GjvpDdoIH\naBuBVzVe5mpe/bX5raKZJUACE4vS1NyP1QKh+OKgbrJFFL7QgJqLpfUBuCA7D7cX\nXLUO/zXo5N6mErlpozF/7vgVtZHyafq55o8r+oPKxxC18JC1gRBM59JHnj9YD6S2\n6UzqBKRfqV6qkgw596pWbiJFzZlCpDhj21yDIdXD03uJ/dD1V3rv3LucMLLY9vDM\nFdzJ1E9XXNpQbmK/ctW32v+ynSRpsKSPQMVmQkxfS5+15DdA596ob4bjHXKixe4c\nZhhdpFBfRbOVlL/87FGy99CyMBpSHTX8GGpA1R7YNVaelsQ/9aqO2ZPBS48xrXSX\nZSLGQ2+kiTnOfweV7CqraD6K3vfUpHv25QazFmZaBy858c+jEcZgWwMJBTAZ6hZ6\nJVqP2YkZ0uI97YBr8qzACcBJsiN7++/u9NKJM5ShFLvzE3p/syx25TX66N/pSMO0\naaXGDe8AJApwcHGpwRqsUjEdqKp4JbwL2vWxFW+4EELXg5PF/5XafdaT0UagnFIm\nzdOu8TozbH76kLwHyNEi4WaJFkPV+W0DDV7jJxNaJmt8cIxEPrhtGqdAMrFUpx6t\n+M1+hJ2IFKMsgc4raha7\n=6HOY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-06T05:33:08Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/c216d29f4996ec823f20b3a5933288e281390853","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKGMyMTZkMjlmNDk5NmVjODIzZjIwYjNhNTkzMzI4OGUyODEzOTA4NTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/12169d01f748841e20ad65a6546c790ffc389744","sha":"12169d01f748841e20ad65a6546c790ffc389744","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/12169d01f748841e20ad65a6546c790ffc389744"}],"sha":"c216d29f4996ec823f20b3a5933288e281390853","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/c216d29f4996ec823f20b3a5933288e281390853"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/12169d01f748841e20ad65a6546c790ffc389744/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T22:55:05Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T22:57:25Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Drive every mounted app in a browser, on both targets\n\nThe portal mounts sixteen apps across five journeys, and until now exactly one of\nthem had ever been opened by a test. `rm_journey.py` proves one journey deeply --\na real dossier, captured off the wire and paired across profiles -- and nothing\ncovered the other half of the claim this repository makes, which is that all of\nthem compose. A portal is not a link page; that difference is only visible in a\nbrowser, and it was unmeasured on both the laptop and the deployment.\n\n`e2e/app_coverage.py` sweeps it. Per app, and every assertion is a property of the\nPORTAL rather than of the app: the shell renders the journey it was built for with\nexactly the apps the BFF catalog declares, the UI is framed from the portal''s own\norigin under this app''s mount, the frame holds a document rather than a proxy error,\nand the app''s own API call reached its backend through `<mount>/api/`. It presses no\nbuttons: sixteen workflows behind one name would be sixteen brittle specs, and the\ndeep journey is where a workflow is proved.\n\nThe app list is never written down here. It comes from the target''s own\n`/v1/journeys`, so the same command sweeps twenty mounts on a laptop and one on the\ndeployment, and `coverage.json` records the fifteen apps this checkout knows that\nthe deployment does not serve rather than reporting a green sweep of one app as if\nit were the portfolio. A journey the portal serves but this run has no origin for is\nreported as never opened, because \"we did not open the ops shell\" and \"the ops shell\nis fine\" must not print the same.\n\nMeasured on both targets: 20/20 mounts compose across five shells locally, and\n1/1 on the deployment behind IAP, which is the first time the embedding at `/agent`\nhas been driven since the edge was rebuilt on the new address.\n\nTwo of the three bugs found writing it were mine, and are worth naming because they\nboth read exactly like product faults. The Angular shell mutates one iframe''s `src`\nin place, so reading the frame URL straight after a tab click reports every app as\nframed from its predecessor; and Playwright''s sync API dispatches events only inside\nPlaywright calls, so a `time.sleep` poll starves the response listener it is waiting\non -- that one reported \"the console never called its API\" about a console that had\ncalled it twice. The wait now pumps.\n\nThe third is real and is left standing red: eight embedded consoles request\n`/api/agent/healthz` at the shell''s origin root, because `ProvenanceBanner` hardcodes\nan origin-relative path that is not basePath-aware. Embedded, it 404s and the banner\nrenders nothing -- so the strip naming runtime and model, which an org decision put on\nevery page, is silently absent in every embedded view. The fix belongs in the app\nrepositories, not here.\n\n`e2e/` also joins LINT_PATHS. It was outside them, so the specs that produce this\nrepository''s deployment evidence were the one body of code the gate never checked.","tree":{"sha":"1e76655da9cc4f0216e52678e712cb95620c5068","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/1e76655da9cc4f0216e52678e712cb95620c5068"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/12169d01f748841e20ad65a6546c790ffc389744","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/12169d01f748841e20ad65a6546c790ffc389744","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDEyMTY5ZDAxZjc0ODg0MWUyMGFkNjVhNjU0NmM3OTBmZmMzODk3NDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/b880995f79c84e44f62b59539a038f7a891b0b48","sha":"b880995f79c84e44f62b59539a038f7a891b0b48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/b880995f79c84e44f62b59539a038f7a891b0b48"}],"sha":"12169d01f748841e20ad65a6546c790ffc389744","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/12169d01f748841e20ad65a6546c790ffc389744"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/b880995f79c84e44f62b59539a038f7a891b0b48/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T00:59:01Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T01:08:26Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Drop the CDD_TRIAGE_MODEL override, now that it duplicates the default\n\nThe launcher forced `CDD_TRIAGE_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash` for a `--live` Doc1,\nexplaining that \"the default triage model (gemini-3.1-flash-lite) is not served\nin the pinned asia-southeast1 region\".\n\nNeither half holds any more. cdd-sow-research defaults\n`triage: ${CDD_TRIAGE_MODEL:-gemini-3.5-flash}`, so the override set exactly the\ndefault; and gemini-3.5-flash is served in asia-southeast1, so there is no\nin-region gap left to paper over. An operator export won over this default\nanyway, so it guarded nothing.\n\nThe launch plan drops the triage-model line with it: it cannot report a value it\nno longer sets. `_live_doc1_environment` keeps CDD_MAX_BODY_BYTES, which still\ncovers the export-wins-the-default behaviour in the tests.","tree":{"sha":"193c2b178a034fa19ededd33e54c4bf8e89af648","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/193c2b178a034fa19ededd33e54c4bf8e89af648"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/b880995f79c84e44f62b59539a038f7a891b0b48","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/b880995f79c84e44f62b59539a038f7a891b0b48","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKGI4ODA5OTVmNzljODRlNDRmNjJiNTk1MzlhMDM4ZjdhODkxYjBiNDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/b82625fff27b8399004bf2dce69879e6096763fd","sha":"b82625fff27b8399004bf2dce69879e6096763fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/b82625fff27b8399004bf2dce69879e6096763fd"}],"sha":"b880995f79c84e44f62b59539a038f7a891b0b48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/b880995f79c84e44f62b59539a038f7a891b0b48"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/b82625fff27b8399004bf2dce69879e6096763fd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T14:20:08Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T21:35:40Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Let a deployment decline the load-balancer edge\n\nThe edge -- url map, managed certificate, HTTPS proxy, global address and forwarding rule --\nwas declared unconditionally, so it was standing spend no deployment could decline and none of\nthem recorded. The reference deployment tore it down by hand on 2026-09-02 for ~$40/month,\nwhich left the config still declaring an edge that no longer existed: any later apply, for any\nunrelated reason, would have rebuilt it silently.\n\nGuard all five behind production_edge_enabled, defaulting false to match the fleet''s existing\nname for this in production_edge.tf. The three backend services and their serverless NEGs stay\nunconditional: they are free without a forwarding rule in front and are what a rebuild reuses.\n\nMake it a REQUIRED deployment key rather than an optional one, for the reason already written\nabove the other three cost-posture keys -- a default that a deployment never states is a\ndecision nobody made. It is now the largest of the four.\n\nThe contract test asserts the guard in BOTH directions. Asserting only the declined side would\npass with no wiring at all, because the declining value and the Terraform default are the same\nliteral; only a stated true proves the input is actually carried.\n\nAlso formats variables.tf and the contract test, which have been failing `terraform fmt -check`\nat HEAD independently of this change.","tree":{"sha":"fbd9c02b8571360e1e50355a3cfc7cec24a3de44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/fbd9c02b8571360e1e50355a3cfc7cec24a3de44"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/b82625fff27b8399004bf2dce69879e6096763fd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/b82625fff27b8399004bf2dce69879e6096763fd","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKGI4MjYyNWZmZjI3YjgzOTkwMDRiZjJkY2U2OTg3OWU2MDk2NzYzZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/11c4fc859ae18d57004c538849f832a22316ce74","sha":"11c4fc859ae18d57004c538849f832a22316ce74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/11c4fc859ae18d57004c538849f832a22316ce74"}],"sha":"b82625fff27b8399004bf2dce69879e6096763fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/b82625fff27b8399004bf2dce69879e6096763fd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/11c4fc859ae18d57004c538849f832a22316ce74/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T15:21:46Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T15:44:35Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Adopt the fleet''s GitHub Actions gate, alongside the Cloud Build one\n\nPart of the fleet''s move off paid Cloud Build, which bills SGD ~3.94/day for work that calls no\nGoogle Cloud API, reads no secret and holds no deploy authority. Actions runs the same work free\non a public repository. Proved on account-takeover-investigator first: both jobs green, 138s of\nwall clock against Cloud Build''s 266s, running the same run-grc-ci in the same reviewed image.\n\nNothing about branch protection changes here. `pr-<repo> (portable-genai-ci-sg)` remains the\nonly REQUIRED check, so this reports alongside it and cannot block a merge while it is proved.\n\nGENERATED, not written: org-metadata/scripts/render-actions-callers.py emits this from the same\nci/gcp/repository-policy.json entry the Cloud Build trigger is built from, and its --check mode\nfails on drift. The 196 workflow files retired on 2026-09-01 rotted because each was maintained\nby hand; this one has no hand to rot by.","tree":{"sha":"2f4320af484487abe6e993823f59e691a61b3a4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/2f4320af484487abe6e993823f59e691a61b3a4e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/11c4fc859ae18d57004c538849f832a22316ce74","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/11c4fc859ae18d57004c538849f832a22316ce74","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDExYzRmYzg1OWFlMThkNTcwMDRjNTM4ODQ5ZjgzMmEyMjMxNmNlNzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/2579c60bfed5c7e56c92e4adcfcd2cb4c6c81120","sha":"2579c60bfed5c7e56c92e4adcfcd2cb4c6c81120","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/2579c60bfed5c7e56c92e4adcfcd2cb4c6c81120"}],"sha":"11c4fc859ae18d57004c538849f832a22316ce74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/11c4fc859ae18d57004c538849f832a22316ce74"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/2579c60bfed5c7e56c92e4adcfcd2cb4c6c81120/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T10:08:21Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T10:18:43Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Unfreeze two demo scripts that had rotted against the service they demonstrate\n\nBoth offline demo scripts failed, and nothing reported it. They are named in no\nCI job, and the only assertion anyone ran about them was that the files exist.\n\n`scripts/demo_selftest.py` was refused with a 503 before it asserted anything.\nThe app-object exposure guard refuses the unauthenticated `local` posture to any\nnon-loopback peer, and TestClient''s default peer is the literal host\n`testclient`. The suite already solved this in `tests/conftest.py` and says so in\na comment; the demo script never got the same fix.\n\nPast that, both scripts asserted the journey catalog was exactly `{\"rm\", \"ops\"}`.\nThe configured catalog carries five journeys. The catalog is CONFIG, so both now\nread the expectation from the same file the app reads, and assert it is not\nempty. A literal set meant a green demo depended on nobody adding a journey,\nwhich is the opposite of what a portability claim should depend on.\n\nBoth scripts now run in the hosted Cloud Build check via this repository''s job\ncontract, so they fail a build rather than a meeting.","tree":{"sha":"bfe32a8f692515cd00928c9f862efb14130e189a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/bfe32a8f692515cd00928c9f862efb14130e189a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-porta