s://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/2fdf18fda41933ff8a4b982ced59059e5c33985b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T10:45:47Z","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dependabot[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T07:58:28Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump @types/node from 26.2.0 to 26.4.0 in /ui-rm\n\nBumps [@types/node](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/node) from 26.2.0 to 26.4.0.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/node)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: \"@types/node\"\n  dependency-version: 26.4.0\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d74da394544d0e00a91ac28b1d80760225cd9fa6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/d74da394544d0e00a91ac28b1d80760225cd9fa6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/2fdf18fda41933ff8a4b982ced59059e5c33985b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/2fdf18fda41933ff8a4b982ced59059e5c33985b","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDJmZGYxOGZkYTQxOTMzZmY4YTRiOTgyY2VkNTkwNTllNWMzMzk4NWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/62c4e8335b105b25bf041f4bdd77f5bbf3ffc01b","sha":"62c4e8335b105b25bf041f4bdd77f5bbf3ffc01b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/62c4e8335b105b25bf041f4bdd77f5bbf3ffc01b"}],"sha":"2fdf18fda41933ff8a4b982ced59059e5c33985b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/2fdf18fda41933ff8a4b982ced59059e5c33985b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/62c4e8335b105b25bf041f4bdd77f5bbf3ffc01b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T06:43:51Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T06:50:14Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Let mypy see the Google SDKs it had been resolving to nothing\n\nThe hosted `lint_gcp` job type-checks this tree against its RUNTIME lock, which is the only\ncheck in the fleet that can see the cloud adapters at all: the offline gate installs the dev\nlock, which carries no Google Cloud SDK, so mypy resolved `google.*` to nothing and reported\nnothing about the code that talks to the cloud. That job has been **non-blocking** since\n2026-08-30 while its findings were worked through. It is blocking now, and this is the\nrepository half of that promotion.\n\n**What was left before this could happen was upstream typing, and the answer is MORE type\nchecking rather than a suppression.** Two settings, in this repository''s own `pyproject.toml`\nrather than in the CI runner:\n\n* **`follow_untyped_imports = true`, scoped to `google.*`.** mypy now ANALYSES a dependency\n  that ships no `py.typed` instead of skipping it. Measured rather than argued: a bogus method\n  planted on a `google.cloud.storage` client is reported by **nothing** under the old\n  configuration and is an `attr-defined` error under this one -- the same defect class that\n  turned out to be real in `disputes-chargebacks-manager`, which called a `SessionsClient`\n  method that does not exist.\n* **`untyped_calls_exclude = [\"google\"]`.** This drops one complaint -- *\"this callee has no\n  annotations\"* -- and nothing else. `disallow_untyped_calls` exists to stop typed code calling\n  OUR untyped code; aimed at a third-party release it is a demand no work in this repository can\n  satisfy, and proto-plus generates every message `__init__` without annotations. Falsified\n  before it was trusted: with the exclusion in place, a planted nonexistent method still reports\n  `attr-defined` and a planted wrong argument type still reports `arg-type` naming the real\n  expected type.\n\n**They live here and not in the runner on purpose.** Two checks reading different configuration\nis what produced the one-line contradiction that blocked this promotion for a day: in\n`human-review-console` a `# type: ignore` was REQUIRED by the offline gate and reported UNUSED by\nlint-gcp. The offline gate and the hosted job now read the same `[tool.mypy]` and differ only in\nwhich packages are installed, which is the property the SDK declaration in this file already\nexisted to hold.\n\n**The scope on `follow_untyped_imports` is not tidiness.** Set globally it also follows the 3.14\nstandard library, where mypy 2.3.1 cannot parse CPython''s own `annotationlib.py`: `agent-registry`\nreported `Invalid syntax` in a standard-library file and **checked nothing at all**. That was\nfound by running all fifty-two trees rather than the three the shape had been validated on.\n`google.protobuf.*` is then excluded from following INSIDE that scope, because a generated `_pb2`\nmodule builds its classes at import time through a descriptor builder, so mypy reading the source\nreports `Module has no attribute \"Timestamp\"` for a class that plainly exists.\n\n**The mypy floor was legacy and is raised to `>=2.3.1`.** `>=1.10` was not neutral: both settings\nabove arrived in mypy 1.14, so the floor permitted a resolution that would not understand the\nfile configuring it. The lock already pins `mypy==2.3.1`, so this was latent rather than live.\n\nWhat this tree reports now, both checks, cold cache:\n\n| check | environment | result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `lint_gcp` | runtime lock (`requirements-gcp.lock`) | `Success: no issues found in 55 source files` |\n| offline gate | dev lock (`requirements-dev.lock`) | `Success: no issues found in 55 source files` |\n\nGate:  766 passed, 6 deselected.","tree":{"sha":"080569683b1891deba43064e7770269d0ff3bcdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/080569683b1891deba43064e7770269d0ff3bcdd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/62c4e8335b105b25bf041f4bdd77f5bbf3ffc01b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/62c4e8335b105b25bf041f4bdd77f5bbf3ffc01b","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDYyYzRlODMzNWIxMDViMjViZjA0MWY0YmRkNzdmNWJiZjNmZmMwMWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/1eab70f00d47d32e9b5640fde3d366cfa15397e4","sha":"1eab70f00d47d32e9b5640fde3d366cfa15397e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/1eab70f00d47d32e9b5640fde3d366cfa15397e4"}],"sha":"62c4e8335b105b25bf041f4bdd77f5bbf3ffc01b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/62c4e8335b105b25bf041f4bdd77f5bbf3ffc01b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/1eab70f00d47d32e9b5640fde3d366cfa15397e4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T22:17:52Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T22:21:34Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Declare the client libraries the bound cloud adapters import\n\nThe `lint-gcp` job was widened from its four pilot trees to every tree carrying a\n`requirements-gcp.lock`, and run locally against each. This repository was one of **thirty of\nfifty-three** where it found the same defect: a Google Cloud client library that a bound adapter\nimports and that is declared **nowhere** — not in the `gcp` extra, not in the lock.\n\nNothing noticed because the imports are lazy. The module imports clean and the port fails only on\nuse, so the adapter is DEAD on the managed profile while every gate stays green. That is precisely\nthe blindness this job exists to remove: `make lint` installs the dev lock alone, so mypy resolves\n`google.cloud.*` to `Any` and reports nothing about the code that talks to the cloud.\n\nThe fix is a declaration, not a suppression. Each distribution is added to the `gcp` extra with a\nfloor equal to the major that actually resolved — written after resolving rather than guessed\nbefore it, because a floor invented in advance either guesses or permits a resolution predating\neverything the adapter was written against.\n\n**The lock change is purely additive: zero existing pins changed**, checked across all thirty\ntrees. `requirements-dev.lock` is untouched, so the offline gate installs exactly what it did.\n\nVerified by re-running the job against a runtime venv built from the new lock: the findings this\ncloses are gone. What remains fleet-wide is upstream untypedness in `google-cloud-logging` and\n`google.auth` (`Call to untyped function`), which is a property of those libraries rather than of\nthis tree, and is why the job stays non-blocking for now.\n\nGate: this repository''s own CI-declared target passes.","tree":{"sha":"da327ed39c54d5d64026a5f2f03f1bc3bf13d113","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/da327ed39c54d5d64026a5f2f03f1bc3bf13d113"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/1eab70f00d47d32e9b5640fde3d366cfa15397e4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/1eab70f00d47d32e9b5640fde3d366cfa15397e4","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDFlYWI3MGYwMGQ0N2QzMmU5YjU2NDBmZGUzZDM2NmNmYTE1Mzk3ZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/43a07f65256798164a8c38927e8f40ac91ab819c","sha":"43a07f65256798164a8c38927e8f40ac91ab819c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/43a07f65256798164a8c38927e8f40ac91ab819c"}],"sha":"1eab70f00d47d32e9b5640fde3d366cfa15397e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/1eab70f00d47d32e9b5640fde3d366cfa15397e4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/43a07f65256798164a8c38927e8f40ac91ab819c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T14:26:27Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T14:39:23Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Both shells state where they run; the launcher stops a server nothing calls\n\nTwo halves of the org decision of 2026-08-30, and the launcher half is the one with a\ndefect in it.\n\nTHE LAUNCHER. Four apps held an entry in _LIVE_APP_PROFILES, and each entry mirrored\nthe shared local model server''s endpoint into that app''s own URL variable. Three of\nthem -- cio-advisory, compliance-advisory, credit-memo-drafting -- went Gemini-only\ntoday and no longer have such a variable to mirror into. The roster''s value is now\n(profile env, model-server URL env OR None), and _LOCAL_MODEL_APPS is DERIVED from it\nrather than hand-listed, so a future conversion cannot leave the launcher starting a\nmodel server nothing calls. Only trade-finance-checker is left on it; on-prem is its\npoint.\n\nThe three that converted now get GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT mirrored in, the way Doc1\nalready did, and --live warns by name when it is unset: without it they start clean\nand fail at the first generation, which is the worst moment to discover it.\n\nA defect found while restructuring, and it is the reason the derived set matters:\nRsk1''s real-corpus refresh was NESTED UNDER the model-server launch. That was only\never correct while Rsk1 needed a model server. The refresh is about the regulator\ncorpus, not about generation, so folding it under the server would have silently\nstopped refreshing the corpus the moment Rsk1 went Gemini-only -- a live demo quietly\nserving a stale corpus, with nothing red anywhere. It is now its own condition.\n\nTHE BANNER. Every served UI states, at the top of every page, where it runs and which\nmodel answers. /healthz and /v1/healthz both answer `runtime` and `generator_model`,\nand a test asserts BOTH are wired: they exist for different reasons (the serverless\nfrontend answers /healthz without reaching this container, which is why /v1/healthz\nexists at all) and a shell pointed at either has to get the same story.\n\nThe portal answers `no-model`, and that is the interesting part rather than a\nformality. It is a launcher and a BFF: it generates nothing, and every page that shows\ngenerated content is an embedded app rendering its own banner from its own healthz,\ninside its own frame. The two answers can legitimately DIFFER -- a portal on GCP\nmounting an app on a laptop, or the reverse -- and a reviewer reading a dossier in a\nframe needs both facts, not whichever one happened to be on screen. `no-model` is also\ndeliberately not `deterministic-offline-stub`: that string would claim a model-shaped\nport bound to a stub, and there is no port here to bind.\n\nBoth shells carry it, React and Angular, because a two-framework demo where only one\nshell states its provenance is a demo that teaches the wrong lesson. In the Angular\nshell it sits ABOVE the error branch: a screenshot of a failed console is still a\nscreenshot somebody has to be able to place.\n\nBoth shells sized their workbench at `height: 100vh`, which claims a full viewport\nwhether or not anything sits above it, so the naive mount pushed the bottom off\nscreen. Both now make the parent the column and let the shell claim what is left --\nno magic number to go stale when the banner''s font or padding changes, and the layout\nis identical when the banner has not rendered.\n\nGates: make check green (756 passed + 113 subtests, eval GATE: PASS), both shells\nbuild clean, and both banners verified rendering in a browser against the running BFF\n-- \"running locally · model no-model\" -- with the workbench correctly sized beneath.","tree":{"sha":"c4c33e8988c13497d67f1e814d18b5c7bbcd6e84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/c4c33e8988c13497d67f1e814d18b5c7bbcd6e84"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/43a07f65256798164a8c38927e8f40ac91ab819c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/43a07f65256798164a8c38927e8f40ac91ab819c","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDQzYTA3ZjY1MjU2Nzk4MTY0YThjMzg5MjdlOGY0MGFjOTFhYjgxOWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/3fa15891bb21696952fa81ce1a30a9e79665c83e","sha":"3fa15891bb21696952fa81ce1a30a9e79665c83e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/3fa15891bb21696952fa81ce1a30a9e79665c83e"}],"sha":"43a07f65256798164a8c38927e8f40ac91ab819c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/43a07f65256798164a8c38927e8f40ac91ab819c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/3fa15891bb21696952fa81ce1a30a9e79665c83e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T12:58:32Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T12:58:56Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"F4 row: PASS at 17/17, measured 2026-08-30; the superseded FAIL stays as the route","tree":{"sha":"e58ea95032a0b2b5efc155cc56430a5f1dceaa86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/e58ea95032a0b2b5efc155cc56430a5f1dceaa86"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/3fa15891bb21696952fa81ce1a30a9e79665c83e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/3fa15891bb21696952fa81ce1a30a9e79665c83e","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDNmYTE1ODkxYmIyMTY5Njk1MmZhODFjZTFhMzBhOWU3OTY2NWM4M2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/40ac1ba6cbc70f9f01a0250f34d91491f4748453","sha":"40ac1ba6cbc70f9f01a0250f34d91491f4748453","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/40ac1ba6cbc70f9f01a0250f34d91491f4748453"}],"sha":"3fa15891bb21696952fa81ce1a30a9e79665c83e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/3fa15891bb21696952fa81ce1a30a9e79665c83e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/40ac1ba6cbc70f9f01a0250f34d91491f4748453/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T11:50:36Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T11:52:44Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Give the dossier build timeout headroom: runtime 900s, BFF upstream 600s\n\nA live CDD dossier build against the real watchlist measured 5m13s-5m40s on the\ndeployment (2026-08-30, twice, warm instance with the snapshot cached), so the\n300s Cloud Run request timeout made the edge answer 504 while the build completed\nuselessly behind it. 900s covers the observed worst case with headroom, and the\nBFF upstream timeout rises to 600s, matching what the laptop launcher already\ngrants the same build and what the e2e''s own dossier wait allows: the three\nsurfaces that time one dossier build now agree.\n\nterraform validate green; make check green. Why the deployed build takes ~5m\nwhere a laptop takes ~50s is a separate open question (screening was measured at\n1.5s over the full 20,813-entry snapshot and is NOT the gap).","tree":{"sha":"779c6f5d642e9e4182e0b3cf62fcdc5921690c45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/779c6f5d642e9e4182e0b3cf62fcdc5921690c45"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/40ac1ba6cbc70f9f01a0250f34d91491f4748453","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/40ac1ba6cbc70f9f01a0250f34d91491f4748453","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDQwYWMxYmE2Y2JjNzBmOWYwMWEwMjUwZjM0ZDkxNDkxZjQ3NDg0NTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/3d52eb4a041c9b9131b48a1ca15dab6db6a29207","sha":"3d52eb4a041c9b9131b48a1ca15dab6db6a29207","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/3d52eb4a041c9b9131b48a1ca15dab6db6a29207"}],"sha":"40ac1ba6cbc70f9f01a0250f34d91491f4748453","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/40ac1ba6cbc70f9f01a0250f34d91491f4748453"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/3d52eb4a041c9b9131b48a1ca15dab6db6a29207/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T09:29:33Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T09:32:22Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Doc1''s live leg is Gemini-API-only: model server scoped to the apps still on a local model\n\nDoc1 left the local model server (org decision, 2026-08-30): its live profile now\nmakes every model call on the Gemini API, so the launcher no longer starts or\nwarns about the model server on Doc1''s behalf. The server starts only when an app\nfrom the _LIVE_APP_PROFILES roster is in the launch plan, the live plan prints\nonly the live apps actually selected, and the GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT warning now\nsays what is true: without it Doc1''s live profile is entirely dead, not just its\ngrounded lookups.\n\nmake check green; --live --dry-run for the rm journey verified by execution.","tree":{"sha":"d2716bf9f43545d102c7add86736ac4a680aa0bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/d2716bf9f43545d102c7add86736ac4a680aa0bc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/3d52eb4a041c9b9131b48a1ca15dab6db6a29207","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/3d52eb4a041c9b9131b48a1ca15dab6db6a29207","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDNkNTJlYjRhMDQxYzliOTEzMWI0OGExY2ExNWRhYjZkYjZhMjkyMDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/8b8980ba3554ad825adae7e0bc6d45531dc64865","sha":"8b8980ba3554ad825adae7e0bc6d45531dc64865","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/8b8980ba3554ad825adae7e0bc6d45531dc64865"}],"sha":"3d52eb4a041c9b9131b48a1ca15dab6db6a29207","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/3d52eb4a041c9b9131b48a1ca15dab6db6a29207"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/8b8980ba3554ad825adae7e0bc6d45531dc64865/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T23:06:35Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T23:15:59Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Say --built in the file an operator has open, and score F4 as FAIL\n\nTwo docs were telling operators the wrong thing, and one was telling a buyer the wrong\nthing.\n\ne2e/README.md said `make e2e-local` needs `make journeys`, so the plain dev launch is what\nanyone following it ran. Behind the portal''s reverse proxy a `next dev` embed never\nhydrates -- markup served, chunks loaded, React never attached -- and the console sits on\n\"Connecting to the CDD agent\" until the step times out against an API answering 200 in\nmilliseconds. The Track C runbook had been carrying that warning on this file''s behalf;\nthe warning belongs here, next to the command, and the runbook now links down instead.\n`next start` is also the shape the deployment runs, so the laptop leg of a pair should not\nhave been measuring a dev server in the first place.\n\nThe F4 row read PASS with a paragraph underneath explaining that the score was withdrawn.\nA verdict and its own retraction cannot both stand in the same cell. It is FAIL, measured\n2026-08-29: both legs pass all nine steps at band medium and score 0.25, and the pair\nexits non-zero on three of seventeen fields with the exemption list untouched. The three\nare one cause -- the laptop answers partly from the fictional corpus it seeds for an\noffline demo while the deployment reads the case''s own uploaded evidence -- and closing it\nis a product decision rather than a comparator fix.\n\nThe withdrawn 16-field pass stays in the row, because it is the reason this FAIL is the\nstronger result: three of those sixteen read keys the wire model does not carry, so they\ncompared null to null and could never have failed.","tree":{"sha":"a738ceff06c7a7933aea0c334b34712f4ad0cbc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/a738ceff06c7a7933aea0c334b34712f4ad0cbc1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/8b8980ba3554ad825adae7e0bc6d45531dc64865","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/8b8980ba3554ad825adae7e0bc6d45531dc64865","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDhiODk4MGJhMzU1NGFkODI1YWRhZTdlMGJjNmQ0NTUzMWRjNjQ4NjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/7da6b60f753a9ca692c16c57b75141c61597b147","sha":"7da6b60f753a9ca692c16c57b75141c61597b147","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/7da6b60f753a9ca692c16c57b75141c61597b147"}],"sha":"8b8980ba3554ad825adae7e0bc6d45531dc64865","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/8b8980ba3554ad825adae7e0bc6d45531dc64865"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/7da6b60f753a9ca692c16c57b75141c61597b147/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T14:41:48Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T14:45:35Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Adopt hex-service-kit v0.0.6\n\nThe 0.0.6 identity knobs -- machine_tenants, subject_from, refuse_unmapped_tenant and a\nhuman-subject allowlist -- have been released and unadopted since 2026-08-28. Every one\ndefaults to what this repository already does, so this bump is the version move and\nnothing else: no behaviour changes until an adopter says so.\n\nThe lockfiles pin the 40-character commit the tag resolved to, not the tag, so what\ninstalls cannot change without a diff.","tree":{"sha":"5f0212d7e955dec70773e0cd2338bcf544c42cb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/5f0212d7e955dec70773e0cd2338bcf544c42cb0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/7da6b60f753a9ca692c16c57b75141c61597b147","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/7da6b60f753a9ca692c16c57b75141c61597b147","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDdkYTZiNjBmNzUzYTljYTY5MmMxNmM1N2I3NTE0MWM2MTU5N2IxNDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/a744a350a115bf80275b3c30f317b669d0765a72","sha":"a744a350a115bf80275b3c30f317b669d0765a72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/a744a350a115bf80275b3c30f317b669d0765a72"}],"sha":"7da6b60f753a9ca692c16c57b75141c61597b147","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/7da6b60f753a9ca692c16c57b75141c61597b147"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/a744a350a115bf80275b3c30f317b669d0765a72/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T14:21:50Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T14:24:01Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Apply security updates to the two shell images, as the BFF already did\n\nThe BFF image learned on 2026-08-26 that a digest pin freezes the base image and\ntherefore also freezes its unpatched packages. The RM and Ops shells carry the same\n`python:3.14-slim` runtime and never got the same layer, so both shipped the same 39\nfixable HIGH Debian advisories -- every one with a released fix -- plus the two findings\npip VENDORS inside `pip/_vendor` (msgpack, setuptools). Neither vendored package is a\ndependency of a static file server, neither appears in any lockfile, and no constraint\ncould have reached them, because they were never resolved.\n\nA serving container installs nothing, so the package manager goes with the updates.\n\nFound by a blocking promotion scan refusing to push, which is the argument for the scan\nbeing blocking rather than advisory: the images had been built and deployed twice with\nthese findings present and nothing said so.","tree":{"sha":"2bdb59eae3735288c937ff7d7ab5c18bbb470323","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/2bdb59eae3735288c937ff7d7ab5c18bbb470323"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/a744a350a115bf80275b3c30f317b669d0765a72","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/a744a350a115bf80275b3c30f317b669d0765a72","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKGE3NDRhMzUwYTExNWJmODAyNzViM2MzMGYzMTdiNjY5ZDA3NjVhNzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/1efce2d35bf79b494555e0c99ae7d5ae5345bde5","sha":"1efce2d35bf79b494555e0c99ae7d5ae5345bde5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/1efce2d35bf79b494555e0c99ae7d5ae5345bde5"}],"sha":"a744a350a115bf80275b3c30f317b669d0765a72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/a744a350a115bf80275b3c30f317b669d0765a72"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/1efce2d35bf79b494555e0c99ae7d5ae5345bde5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T12:54:57Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T13:00:13Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Wait on the case file''s markup, not on one of its two sentences\n\n`make e2e-local` timed out at step 5 for sixty seconds against a panel that had\nsettled almost immediately. The wait accepted either a document list or the text\n\"No documents yet\", and the CDD console prints that sentence only when it has no\nseeded corpus: with one, uploads are optional and it says so differently. The local\nprofile seeds a corpus, so the condition could never become true there.\n\nKeying on `data-demo=\"document-list-empty\"` (added beside the list in\ncdd-sow-research) makes both empty states settle the wait, and leaves the prose free\nto say what each profile actually means without breaking the journey that reads it.\n\nProved by execution: all nine steps now pass on the local target, comparable_fields=17.","tree":{"sha":"bd36e4ab4b9a87380aafdfa67a962849e76c2613","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/bd36e4ab4b9a87380aafdfa67a962849e76c2613"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/1efce2d35bf79b494555e0c99ae7d5ae5345bde5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/1efce2d35bf79b494555e0c99ae7d5ae5345bde5","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDFlZmNlMmQzNWJmNzliNDk0NTU1ZTBjOTlhZTdkNWFlNTM0NWJkZTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/cecdb823bf348cdc12b3ba52e74b2099f2d4016a","sha":"cecdb823bf348cdc12b3ba52e74b2099f2d4016a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/cecdb823bf348cdc12b3ba52e74b2099f2d4016a"}],"sha":"1efce2d35bf79b494555e0c99ae7d5ae5345bde5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/1efce2d35bf79b494555e0c99ae7d5ae5345bde5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/cecdb823bf348cdc12b3ba52e74b2099f2d4016a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T10:06:57Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T10:08:59Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Key the deployed apps on repository names, restoring a plan that could not run\n\n`terraform plan` on this stack FAILED on main, and had since the app-id rename landed\nhalf-done:\n\n    Error: Invalid value for variable\n      embedded_apps must be a non-empty subset of doc1, doc2, ..., hrz7\n      This was checked by the validation rule at variables.tf:183\n\n`variables.tf` had been moved to validate repository names, but everything that FEEDS it\nhad not: `deployment_config.py` still emitted `{\"doc1\": ...}` with `/apps/doc1` mount\npaths, and the second validation still looked the profile env var up in a map keyed on the\nold ids. The two halves could not both be satisfied, so the stack was unplannable.\n\nBoth halves now use repository names, and `terraform plan` runs again.\n\n**Image paths are deliberately NOT renamed.** `.../cdd-sow/doc1-api@sha256:...` is a\ndeployed artifact name, not an app id; rewriting it would point the deployment at an image\nthat does not exist. Only a rebuild can move those, and the digests stay pinned meanwhile.\n\nTwo latent bugs of the same shape as the one already fixed in `domain/catalog.py`, both\nfound by running this rather than reading it:\n\n- `deployment_config.py` capped app ids at 21 characters -- fine for `doc1`, refusing\n  `loan-document-intelligence` outright. Now 63, the Cloud Run service-name label limit,\n  matching `catalog.py`.\n- The readiness readout padded its label column to 22, so repository names ran into the\n  status column and destroyed the alignment the readout exists for. Now 34.\n\n`hrz5_audit.py` is renamed to `observability_audit.py` in the same pass, and a comment in\n`catalog.py` that EXPLAINED the old codes is restored -- the sweep had rewritten the very\nexample it was making.","tree":{"sha":"40dfda634c0b89532c04d16ee0c9332f0b97d6af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/40dfda634c0b89532c04d16ee0c9332f0b97d6af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/cecdb823bf348cdc12b3ba52e74b2099f2d4016a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/cecdb823bf348cdc12b3ba52e74b2099f2d4016a","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKGNlY2RiODIzYmYzNDhjZGMxMmIzYmE1MmU3NGIyMDk5ZjJkNDAxNmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/3211c8a80f25c8287dcdbc6a2e786a2080bd69aa","sha":"3211c8a80f25c8287dcdbc6a2e786a2080bd69aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/3211c8a80f25c8287dcdbc6a2e786a2080bd69aa"}],"sha":"cecdb823bf348cdc12b3ba52e74b2099f2d4016a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/cecdb823bf348cdc12b3ba52e74b2099f2d4016a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/3211c8a80f25c8287dcdbc6a2e786a2080bd69aa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T10:02:12Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T10:05:05Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Lint the scripts directory, not eight files inside it\n\n`make lint` named eight of the fifteen files in `scripts/`, so seven were unchecked, among\nthem the three this session edited most and the two presenter-runner suites CI had just been\nwired to execute. The default for a newly added script was to go unlinted forever, which is\nthe wrong direction for a gate: a file should have to be excluded on purpose, never included\non purpose.\n\nFound the expensive way. A backgrounded `make decks` hung in `marp --pptx` for 101 minutes,\nand the command chain it belonged to ended in a `cp` that restored\n`scripts/demo_walkthrough.py` from a snapshot predating a formatting fix. The `cp` ran, the\nfile went stale, and `make lint` reported success, because that file was one of the seven.\n`git status` caught it; the gate did not.\n\n`ci.yaml` also carried its own copy of the path list, and the two had already drifted: CI\nomitted `scripts/journey_ui_smoke.py` that the Makefile checked, so they disagreed about what\n\"lint passes\" means. The step now runs `make lint`, and the Makefile is the one home for the\nlist.\n\nAll seven newly covered files passed unchanged, which is exactly what made the enumerated\nlist look harmless for as long as it did. Proved closed by replaying the original corruption\nand watching `make lint` exit non-zero on it.","tree":{"sha":"e0d4414ead6e163c98ed7c13514433a6c7c24568","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/e0d4414ead6e163c98ed7c13514433a6c7c24568"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/3211c8a80f25c8287dcdbc6a2e786a2080bd69aa","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/3211c8a80f25c8287dcdbc6a2e786a2080bd69aa","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDMyMTFjOGE4MGYyNWM4Mjg3ZGNkYmM2YTJlNzg2YTIwODBiZDY5YWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/8f90c33d29cebdf128ba784350e61a542b740622","sha":"8f90c33d29cebdf128ba784350e61a542b740622","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/8f90c33d29cebdf128ba784350e61a542b740622"}],"sha":"3211c8a80f25c8287dcdbc6a2e786a2080bd69aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/3211c8a80f25c8287dcdbc6a2e786a2080bd69aa"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/8f90c33d29cebdf128ba784350e61a542b740622/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T09:52:14Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T09:57:58Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Name the platform environment variables for what they are\n\nThe HRZ_ prefix is a retired catalog code. It named nothing an operator could look up:\nHRZ_HUMAN_REVIEW_URL, HRZ7_S2S_TOKEN and HRZ_REGISTRY_* say which internal identifier a\nservice used to carry, not which service they address. The names now say that directly --\nHUMAN_REVIEW_URL, HUMAN_REVIEW_S2S_TOKEN, AGENT_REGISTRY_*, KNOWLEDGE_BASE_URL,\nGUARDRAIL_GATEWAY_URL, QUALITY_GATE_URL, OBSERVABILITY_URL, AUDIT_URL -- so a `.env` file\ncan be read without the catalog open beside it.\n\nThis is the remainder of a change that landed across 49 repositories earlier today; these\nwere held back because their trees carried unmerged work at the time.\n\nAlso here, and only landable now that both sides are on main: DEPLOY_HRZ5_URL and\nDEPLOY_HRZ5_AUDIENCE become DEPLOY_OBSERVABILITY_URL and DEPLOY_OBSERVABILITY_AUDIENCE.\nThat pair spans journey-portal''s deployment_config.py and org-metadata''s deployment env\nfile, so renaming either side alone would have broken the deployment configuration; it was\ndeliberately left until the two could move together. `hrz5_audit.py` and its test are\nrenamed to `observability_audit.py`, and `to_hrz5_audit_event` to\n`to_observability_audit_event`, so the module no longer names the code either.\n\nNothing about the wire contract changes; these are the names of the values, not the values.","tree":{"sha":"1be30f6892889b6b114640836f44842d3af3a7d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/1be30f6892889b6b114640836f44842d3af3a7d4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/8f90c33d29cebdf128ba784350e61a542b740622","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/8f90c33d29cebdf128ba784350e61a542b740622","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDhmOTBjMzNkMjljZWJkZjEyOGJhNzg0MzUwZTYxYTU0MmI3NDA2MjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/01d24fd0449b2947c3a0e6db68dbd3a4414cf98e","sha":"01d24fd0449b2947c3a0e6db68dbd3a4414cf98e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/01d24fd0449b2947c3a0e6db68dbd3a4414cf98e"}],"sha":"8f90c33d29cebdf128ba784350e61a542b740622","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/8f90c33d29cebdf128ba784350e61a542b740622"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/01d24fd0449b2947c3a0e6db68dbd3a4414cf98e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T08:28:32Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T08:40:30Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Declare a step''s pair beside the step, not in the deck that draws it\n\nWhich walkthrough steps are the counterpart of which is a fact about the walkthrough, and it\nwas living in org-metadata''s deck renderer. Before that the renderer inferred it from the word\n\"pair\" appearing in the narration, which both missed a declared pair and would have marked any\nstep that happened to use the word. Both are the same mistake at different sizes: the deck\nguessing at something the source owns.\n\nStep.pair_with carries it now, beside the steps it describes, so a step renamed or moved cannot\nleave a stale copy behind. The renderer reads it and still refuses to render when a partner names\na step the journey does not run; that refusal was proved by pointing a pair at a step id that\ndoes not exist and watching the render exit non-zero.","tree":{"sha":"42a53c3fc565afdc849b1b5ce33536236d8d97fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/42a53c3fc565afdc849b1b5ce33536236d8d97fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/01d24fd0449b2947c3a0e6db68dbd3a4414cf98e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/01d24fd0449b2947c3a0e6db68dbd3a4414cf98e","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDAxZDI0ZmQwNDQ5YjI5NDdjM2EwZTZkYjY4ZGJkM2E0NDE0Y2Y5OGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/5e1e86a2a0fad5a8855854353487886e209caa0f","sha":"5e1e86a2a0fad5a8855854353487886e209caa0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/5e1e86a2a0fad5a8855854353487886e209caa0f"}],"sha":"01d24fd0449b2947c3a0e6db68dbd3a4414cf98e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/01d24fd0449b2947c3a0e6db68dbd3a4414cf98e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/5e1e86a2a0fad5a8855854353487886e209caa0f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T07:40:12Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T07:42:36Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Move the launcher and walkthrough to the renamed app ids\n\nThe CI gate caught what the local run missed: scripts/ carries its own test\nfiles, and the walkthrough that drives the demo decks keys on app ids too.","tree":{"sha":"c0c884e7dc21b887a26df10ff4c625f68e73b182","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/c0c884e7dc21b887a26df10ff4c625f68e73b182"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/5e1e86a2a0fad5a8855854353487886e209caa0f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/5e1e86a2a0fad5a8855854353487886e209caa0f","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDVlMWU4NmEyYTBmYWQ1YTg4NTU4NTQzNTM0ODc4ODZlMjA5Y2FhMGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/7d58530749ba1de18e2873cd4066c0e8b8cf5a57","sha":"7d58530749ba1de18e2873cd4066c0e8b8cf5a57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/7d58530749ba1de18e2873cd4066c0e8b8cf5a57"}],"sha":"5e1e86a2a0fad5a8855854353487886e209caa0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/5e1e86a2a0fad5a8855854353487886e209caa0f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/7d58530749ba1de18e2873cd4066c0e8b8cf5a57/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T07:34:21Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T07:42:36Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Wrap two lines the longer app ids pushed past the limit","tree":{"sha":"9afcd6aad058b2ccf9d5926b3d20cf2815e86b09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/9afcd6aad058b2ccf9d5926b3d20cf2815e86b09"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/7d58530749ba1de18e2873cd4066c0e8b8cf5a57","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/7d58530749ba1de18e2873cd4066c0e8b8cf5a57","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDdkNTg1MzA3NDliYTFkZTE4ZTI4NzNjZDQwNjZjMGU4YjhjZjVhNTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/f01aca601b24e320039d5e65d7a425467c338c8c","sha":"f01aca601b24e320039d5e65d7a425467c338c8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/f01aca601b24e320039d5e65d7a425467c338c8c"}],"sha":"7d58530749ba1de18e2873cd4066c0e8b8cf5a57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/7d58530749ba1de18e2873cd4066c0e8b8cf5a57"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/f01aca601b24e320039d5e65d7a425467c338c8c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T07:29:44Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T07:42:36Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Key deployed names on repositories, not catalog codes\n\nA resource name is the one place a rename costs a rebuild: Cloud Run URLs\nand KMS ring names cannot be changed in place. These were all codes.\n\n- name_prefix hrz9 -> journey, so service names, service accounts, the CMEK\n  ring and the VPC-SC perimeter title carry the repository''s own name.\n- Five service-account display names read ''Hrz9 ...''.\n- App ids become repository names, so the embedded services are\n  journey-cdd-sow-research-{api,ui} rather than journey-doc1-*, and a user\n  lands on /apps/credit-memo-drafting/ rather than /apps/doc2/.\n\nTwo defects the rename exposed, both of which would have bitten any id\nlonger than four characters:\n\n- The app-id pattern was ^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,30}$, sized for ''doc1'' and\n  ''mkt6''. ''performance-marketing-optimisation'' is 34 characters and was\n  refused outright. Widened to 63, the label limit these ids must satisfy\n  as Cloud Run service-name components.\n- The canonical /agent mount resolved a hardcoded ''doc1'', so every request\n  to it 404''d once the id moved. It now resolves the app by name.","tree":{"sha":"eda9bafe04ee233491f5c7e02ba6a8c7edcc72ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/eda9bafe04ee233491f5c7e02ba6a8c7edcc72ad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/f01aca601b24e320039d5e65d7a425467c338c8c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/f01aca601b24e320039d5e65d7a425467c338c8c","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKGYwMWFjYTYwMWIyNGUzMjAwMzlkNWU2NWQ3YTQyNTQ2N2MzMzhjOGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/6d4108d148ec54c619d9f3166351730d7c4f083a","sha":"6d4108d148ec54c619d9f3166351730d7c4f083a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/6d4108d148ec54c619d9f3166351730d7c4f083a"}],"sha":"f01aca601b24e320039d5e65d7a425467c338c8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/f01aca601b24e320039d5e65d7a425467c338c8c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/6d4108d148ec54c619d9f3166351730d7c4f083a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T06:01:41Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T06:08:56Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Make the walkthrough''s negative controls able to fail, and the pair compare the money\n\nSix of the demo''s own assertions could not fail, and the pair comparison was reading fields the\nwire does not send. Both are the same defect in different clothes: a check that cannot go red is a\nslideshow with extra steps.\n\nThe walkthrough:\n- mkt-gate-refused waited for text a PASSING review also renders, so the compliance gate wrongly\n  APPROVING the guaranteed-returns copy would have sailed through. It is the demo''s flagship\n  negative control and persona-journeys.md promises in writing that it fails the run.\n- gov-architecture, mkt-performance and gov-promotion-gate waited on static page chrome or\n  pass/fail-agnostic text; mkt-creative''s guard missed WARN variants.\n- svc-rules told the room the answer comes from the regulators'' published instruments. Under the\n  profile that step enforces it comes from a deliberately fictional corpus.\n- smoke_journeys parked a permanent fictional item in the review queue the demo presents. It now\n  raises as the analyst and withdraws as the approver, which leaves the queue as it found it and\n  is a second identity proof, since the console refuses a self-approval.\n- smoke gained --journey, because the portal serves its whole catalog whatever was launched, so\n  the inventory''s own six-command order failed at step 4 after a single-journey launch.\n\nThe pair:\n- sow.amounts compared amount, currency and period against a source object carrying only kind,\n  description, est_value_band and citations. It extracted null on both sides, so the flagship\n  ''the two profiles must agree about the money'' check compared nothing and degenerated to a\n  source count. rating.factors and screening.alerts had the same dead-field bug.\n- tests/test_pairing.py certified the comparator against a fixture shaped like the comparator''s\n  imagination rather than the wire, which is why every dead comparison passed its own can-fail\n  test.\n- pair_report exited 0 against stale artifacts left by a failed run, which today would have\n  reported agreement against the deleted deployment''s dossier.\n- The evidence writer recorded a citations figure that was the key count of two dicts, constant 8\n  on every run of either target.\n\nCI ran none of the tests that enforce the step-order contract: the bare pytest collected only\ntestpaths=[tests], so scripts/test_demo_walkthrough.py and scripts/test_run_journeys.py never ran\non a pull request. The eval fabricated a perfect 1.0 for any metric whose case kind had no rows,\nwhich is the E4 fail-open shape.\n\nExcludes infra/terraform and config/journeys.yaml, which a concurrent repo-code rename owns.","tree":{"sha":"dde0719ff7b2741e191b18f70e1da99e61ed6481","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/dde0719ff7b2741e191b18f70e1da99e61ed6481"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/6d4108d148ec54c619d9f3166351730d7c4f083a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/6d4108d148ec54c619d9f3166351730d7c4f083a","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDZkNDEwOGQxNDhlYzU0YzYxOWQ5ZjMxNjYzNTE3MzBkN2M0ZjA4M2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/9b27e1fdeea3b8355ff3444ff883acdabbe40369","sha":"9b27e1fdeea3b8355ff3444ff883acdabbe40369","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/9b27e1fdeea3b8355ff3444ff883acdabbe40369"}],"sha":"6d4108d148ec54c619d9f3166351730d7c4f083a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/6d4108d148ec54c619d9f3166351730d7c4f083a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/9b27e1fdeea3b8355ff3444ff883acdabbe40369/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T00:48:00Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T00:51:41Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Fix cert rotation and cross-arch shell builds\n\n- The managed certificate could never survive a domain change: replacement is\n  create-before-destroy now, with the name keyed to the domain set via\n  random_id, because the old cert cannot be deleted while the HTTPS proxy\n  references it (resourceInUseByAnotherResource, observed swapping the\n  bootstrap domains for the minted LB address).\n- ui-rm/ui-ops gain .dockerignore: without one, the host''s native\n  node_modules is COPY''d over the image''s install and the build crashes\n  under cross-arch emulation.\n- Shell builder stages run on the build host''s own architecture\n  (--platform=$BUILDPLATFORM): they emit only static files, and emulating\n  them crashed the Angular CLI''s lmdb cache.","tree":{"sha":"1b3d6ddf252378d922e4b5cbe348046531e64575","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/1b3d6ddf252378d922e4b5cbe348046531e64575"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/9b27e1fdeea3b8355ff3444ff883acdabbe40369","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/9b27e1fdeea3b8355ff3444ff883acdabbe40369","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDliMjdlMWZkZWVhM2I4MzU1ZmYzNDQ0ZmY4ODNhY2RhYmJlNDAzNjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/b386f37cbe72826d4089f5f3763c420af3461aa8","sha":"b386f37cbe72826d4089f5f3763c420af3461aa8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/b386f37cbe72826d4089f5f3763c420af3461aa8"}],"sha":"9b27e1fdeea3b8355ff3444ff883acdabbe40369","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/9b27e1fdeea3b8355ff3444ff883acdabbe40369"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/b386f37cbe72826d4089f5f3763c420af3461aa8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T23:31:28Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T23:35:05Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Declare the portal image registry in terraform\n\nEvery image variable in this stack must be pinned by sha256 digest, yet the\nrepository those digests live in was created by hand during the reference\ndeployment and existed in no Terraform, so a clean checkout could not\nrebuild the stack it describes. Declared CMEK-bound, with the Artifact\nRegistry service agent asked for rather than spelled out, and immutable\ntags to close the same tag-moving gap the digest validation closes.","tree":{"sha":"732e0d05e488cba6f09c15b2795d986756d06f5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/732e0d05e488cba6f09c15b2795d986756d06f5e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/b386f37cbe72826d4089f5f3763c420af3461aa8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/b386f37cbe72826d4089f5f3763c420af3461aa8","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKGIzODZmMzdjYmU3MjgyNmQ0MDg5ZjVmMzc2M2M0MjBhZjM0NjFhYTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/2585805ca734966c60efcc7d528cfa77f2f19c5f","sha":"2585805ca734966c60efcc7d528cfa77f2f19c5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/2585805ca734966c60efcc7d528cfa77f2f19c5f"}],"sha":"b386f37cbe72826d4089f5f3763c420af3461aa8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/b386f37cbe72826d4089f5f3763c420af3461aa8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/2585805ca734966c60efcc7d528cfa77f2f19c5f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T21:57:40Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T22:00:32Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Wait for the briefing, not for the header above it\n\nThe step waited first on a sentence that is part of the console''s static header. That\nmatched the instant the page rendered, spent none of the long timeout it was given, and\nleft the real assertion below it with the default thirty seconds while a grounded research\npass was still running. The step then failed on a briefing that was about to arrive.\n\nThe same assertion would have passed on a page where nothing had happened at all, which is\nthe worse half of the defect: a wait that matches chrome measures nothing. The wait is now\non the briefing itself, carrying the timeout the work actually needs.","tree":{"sha":"320188849a4227db548fb72c78acc80ed6a9e856","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/320188849a4227db548fb72c78acc80ed6a9e856"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/2585805ca734966c60efcc7d528cfa77f2f19c5f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/2585805ca734966c60efcc7d528cfa77f2f19c5f","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDI1ODU4MDVjYTczNDk2NmM2MGVmY2M3ZDUyOGNmYTc3ZjJmMTljNWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/06c1674da5fcddf8a3a2ba2f5fba01f12c52d423","sha":"06c1674da5fcddf8a3a2ba2f5fba01f12c52d423","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/06c1674da5fcddf8a3a2ba2f5fba01f12c52d423"}],"sha":"2585805ca734966c60efcc7d528cfa77f2f19c5f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/2585805ca734966c60efcc7d528cfa77f2f19c5f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/06c1674da5fcddf8a3a2ba2f5fba01f12c52d423/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T21:54:46Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T22:00:32Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Photograph the result, not the form that produced it\n\nEvery captured image was a picture of the workbench with a filled-in form. The console sits\nin a frame with its own scrollbar, so a full-page capture of the page around it stops at the\nfold and the result the step just produced never appears: the evidence recorded the least\ninteresting half of each step, and the committed walkthrough images show exactly that.\n\nThe frame is now grown to its own content height for the capture and restored afterwards. A\nstep with no embedded console captures unchanged, and a failure to resize falls back to the\nprevious behaviour rather than costing the demonstration its evidence.","tree":{"sha":"3fed771d1556158654624f6067faa6de129729ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/3fed771d1556158654624f6067faa6de129729ba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/06c1674da5fcddf8a3a2ba2f5fba01f12c52d423","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/06c1674da5fcddf8a3a2ba2f5fba01f12c52d423","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDA2YzE2NzRkYTVmY2RkZjhhM2EyYmEyZjVmYmEwMWYxMmM1MmQ0MjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/59b4ab0b8c7e91ebf2b9ce6d25c6114e684dda64","sha":"59b4ab0b8c7e91ebf2b9ce6d25c6114e684dda64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/59b4ab0b8c7e91ebf2b9ce6d25c6114e684dda64"}],"sha":"06c1674da5fcddf8a3a2ba2f5fba01f12c52d423","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/06c1674da5fcddf8a3a2ba2f5fba01f12c52d423"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/59b4ab0b8c7e91ebf2b9ce6d25c6114e684dda64/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T21:42:23Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T21:52:07Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Find a filed document by what the console actually renders\n\nA document filed against a case is a BUTTON that opens it, not a link. This waited for a\nlink, so the check for an already-filed document never matched and the confirmation after\nuploading never matched either: every live run uploaded the evidence and then failed thirty\nseconds later looking for something that could not exist.\n\nThe console had changed and the step had not, which no offline test could catch, because\nthe only thing that knows the difference is the running interface.","tree":{"sha":"445b74e3b700693721aeb6594f4c59c4ced80aea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/445b74e3b700693721aeb6594f4c59c4ced80aea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/59b4ab0b8c7e91ebf2b9ce6d25c6114e684dda64","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/59b4ab0b8c7e91ebf2b9ce6d25c6114e684dda64","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDU5YjRhYjBiOGM3ZTkxZWJmMmI5Y2U2ZDI1YzYxMTRlNjg0ZGRhNjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/e5aa191d42fe25960b4fc40f6644630352751581","sha":"e5aa191d42fe25960b4fc40f6644630352751581","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/e5aa191d42fe25960b4fc40f6644630352751581"}],"sha":"59b4ab0b8c7e91ebf2b9ce6d25c6114e684dda64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/59b4ab0b8c7e91ebf2b9ce6d25c6114e684dda64"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/e5aa191d42fe25960b4fc40f6644630352751581/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T21:39:17Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T21:52:07Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Wait for every console to be interactive, not only the new ones\n\nSelecting a console and filling its form immediately puts the values into the document\nrather than into the console''s own state, so the form submits as if it were empty. The\npersona workbenches were given a wait for the console''s first call to its API; the\nrelationship manager''s and the operations analyst''s steps were left waiting only for the\nframe''s body to exist, which is true long before the page can accept input.\n\nUnder the live profile that raced the very first upload: the step filed a document, the\nconsole never saw it, and the run failed thirty seconds later looking for a document that\nwas never there. Both helpers now share one readiness rule, so a console is interactive\nbefore any step types into it, in every journey.\n\nThe fifth argument to the older helper was the frame title repeated, which the frame is\nalready located by; it is now the app id the readiness check needs.","tree":{"sha":"8bb412cca82a75220280646f6ed6220732eef5cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/8bb412cca82a75220280646f6ed6220732eef5cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/e5aa191d42fe25960b4fc40f6644630352751581","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/e5aa191d42fe25960b4fc40f6644630352751581","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKGU1YWExOTFkNDJmZTI1OTYwYjRmYzQwZjY2NDQ2MzAzNTI3NTE1ODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/6bee5e280742bfaff33369f5fb2764275b6623a7","sha":"6bee5e280742bfaff33369f5fb2764275b6623a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/6bee5e280742bfaff33369f5fb2764275b6623a7"}],"sha":"e5aa191d42fe25960b4fc40f6644630352751581","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/e5aa191d42fe25960b4fc40f6644630352751581"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/6bee5e280742bfaff33369f5fb2764275b6623a7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T17:28:18Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T18:48:46Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Give each persona workbench its own opening\n\nThe opening spoken before the first screen frames a demonstration ACROSS two workbenches:\ntwo front-end stacks, one identity, the same capabilities composed twice. A single persona\nworkbench cannot show any of that, so borrowing it promised the room something the next\neight minutes would not deliver.\n\nThe persona journeys now open on what they actually demonstrate: one person''s work, in\norder, assembled from applications that were built separately, with the figures computed in\nplain code and at least one control refusing something and naming the rule. It also states\nup front that these capabilities run on the data each ships with, which is the honest thing\nto say before the first screen rather than when somebody asks.\n\nFound by generating a deck from the walkthrough, which put the wrong opening on a slide\nwhere it was obvious.","tree":{"sha":"5e8f725a7d6b34db3ded51201b2359b4b5d57c03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/5e8f725a7d6b34db3ded51201b2359b4b5d57c03"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/6bee5e280742bfaff33369f5fb2764275b6623a7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/6bee5e280742bfaff33369f5fb2764275b6623a7","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDZiZWU1ZTI4MDc0MmJmYWZmMzMzNjlmNWZiMjc2NDI3NWI2NjIzYTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/9f8fd125bd8bde041301e34c0e0228eec873f14b","sha":"9f8fd125bd8bde041301e34c0e0228eec873f14b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/9f8fd125bd8bde041301e34c0e0228eec873f14b"}],"sha":"6bee5e280742bfaff33369f5fb2764275b6623a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/6bee5e280742bfaff33369f5fb2764275b6623a7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/9f8fd125bd8bde041301e34c0e0228eec873f14b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T17:09:06Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T18:48:46Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Say which command starts the workbench that is not answering\n\nA refused connection when opening a journey means it was never launched, which is the most\nlikely thing to be wrong a minute before a demo. Playwright''s stack trace is a poor way to\nlearn that, so the failure now names the workbench and the exact command that starts it.","tree":{"sha":"f0caab313194e8b9ddbe7ba59b6e7ea5b73357a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/f0caab313194e8b9ddbe7ba59b6e7ea5b73357a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/9f8fd125bd8bde041301e34c0e0228eec873f14b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/9f8fd125bd8bde041301e34c0e0228eec873f14b","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDlmOGZkMTI1YmQ4YmRlMDQxMzAxZTM0YzBlMDIyOGVlYzg3M2YxNGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/5f9ced9cd5261c40d06bffcabdc36afdafe51484","sha":"5f9ced9cd5261c40d06bffcabdc36afdafe51484","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/5f9ced9cd5261c40d06bffcabdc36afdafe51484"}],"sha":"9f8fd125bd8bde041301e34c0e0228eec873f14b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/9f8fd125bd8bde041301e34c0e0228eec873f14b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/5f9ced9cd5261c40d06bffcabdc36afdafe51484/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T17:04:42Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T18:48:46Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Make the promotion gate''s refusal the point of that step\n\nThe gate returns FAIL while every quality measure passes and every attack is blocked, and\nit names why: the evidence it was handed is not attested. That is the most interesting\nresult on the screen and the narration walked past it, so the step now says it out loud and\nasserts it. Passing the tests is not the same as having proof the tests were run against\nthe thing being shipped, and a gate that approved here would be measuring a model and\ncalling it a control.\n\nAsserting the verdict also keeps the narration honest: if the fixture ever changes to one\nthat promotes, this step fails rather than describing a refusal that no longer happens.","tree":{"sha":"e3d38780d06e85e6ddf1d78b202a7741e7433f03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/e3d38780d06e85e6ddf1d78b202a7741e7433f03"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/5f9ced9cd5261c40d06bffcabdc36afdafe51484","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/5f9ced9cd5261c40d06bffcabdc36afdafe51484","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDVmOWNlZDljZDUyNjFjNDBkMDZiZmZjYWJkYzM2YWZkYWZlNTE0ODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/294a31810da05fe12bd8137a1b3beb5ea45afe1d","sha":"294a31810da05fe12bd8137a1b3beb5ea45afe1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/294a31810da05fe12bd8137a1b3beb5ea45afe1d"}],"sha":"5f9ced9cd5261c40d06bffcabdc36afdafe51484","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/5f9ced9cd5261c40d06bffcabdc36afdafe51484"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/294a31810da05fe12bd8137a1b3beb5ea45afe1d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T17:02:33Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T18:48:46Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Give each persona journey a narrated walkthrough that can fail\n\nComposing the journeys proved the consoles were alive. It did not prove the work they\nexist for, so each journey now has its own script in the same runner the other two use:\nthe campaign manager researches, plans, makes advertising, has a claim refused, measures\nand personalises; the model-risk owner judges a proposal and runs a release gate; the\ncomplaints handler assesses a complaint and asks what the rules require.\n\nEvery step asserts its own claim rather than waiting for a heading. The refusal step fails\nthe run unless the gate names the rule that was broken, the creative step fails unless the\nvariants passed their checks, the gate step fails unless the probes reported, and the\ncomplaint step fails unless the drafted reply is visibly held for a person.\n\nThree things had to be fixed to make any of it run, and each was a real trap.\n\nSelecting a console and typing into it immediately put the text into the document rather\nthan into the console''s own state, so the form submitted as if it were empty and the\napplication appeared to ignore the presenter. Steps now wait for the console''s first call\nto its own API, which is the earliest honest proof it is running rather than rendered, and\nrecording starts before the workbench opens because the first console is already loading\nby the time its tab could be clicked.\n\nThe preflight resolved each app''s workbench from a table keyed by app, so a system mounted\nin two journeys sent the service journey''s checks at the operations workbench, which was\nnot running. It now resolves the workbench from the step''s own journey.\n\nAnd configuring the origins rewrote every app that was not the relationship manager''s onto\nthe operations origin, which pointed the marketing steps at a shell that does not serve\nthem.","tree":{"sha":"16416010808ff423c3c06c8964cfcd73082f1edc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/16416010808ff423c3c06c8964cfcd73082f1edc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/294a31810da05fe12bd8137a1b3beb5ea45afe1d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/294a31810da05fe12bd8137a1b3beb5ea45afe1d","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDI5NGEzMTgxMGRhMDVmZTEyYmQ4MTM3YTFiM2JlYjVlYTQ1YWZlMWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/58dbc70b525683bcdfcc35e34cbebf8e6b941d2e","sha":"58dbc70b525683bcdfcc35e34cbebf8e6b941d2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/58dbc70b525683bcdfcc35e34cbebf8e6b941d2e"}],"sha":"294a31810da05fe12bd8137a1b3beb5ea45afe1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/294a31810da05fe12bd8137a1b3beb5ea45afe1d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/58dbc70b525683bcdfcc35e34cbebf8e6b941d2e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T16:00:37Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T16:05:56Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Compose three more persona workbenches, and prove their consoles are alive\n\nThe portal served two journeys. It now serves five: the marketing manager''s, the\nmodel-risk owner''s and the complaints handler''s, alongside the relationship manager''s and\nthe operations analyst''s. Each is an ordered walk through systems that already existed, so\nthe change is a journey entry naming apps plus the mounts they answer on.\n\nOne shell serves them all. The React shell renders whichever journey it is named, so a new\npersona workbench is that shell started again with a different journey and port rather than\na second front end; Ops keeps its Angular shell, so two front-end stacks against one portal\ncontract stays demonstrable. Serving several at once needs a build directory each, because\nthe journey name is baked in at build time and concurrent instances would otherwise\noverwrite one another''s output. The shell''s title and mark follow the journey, which a\nfixed \"RM\" did not.\n\nThree defects were found by running it, and each was invisible to a health check.\n\nThe local tenant policy knew only the two original shell origins, so a new journey''s shell\nwas refused, and the refusal reached the browser as a 403 on the embedded app''s own assets:\nthe app rendered and reported its backend unreachable.\n\nEvery backend is now told its profile rather than left to inherit one. Only some of them\nrefuse an inherited profile today and relying on that is what made the review console\nanswer 401 to every write while its health check stayed green.\n\nAnd `scripts/journey_ui_smoke.py` exists because nothing asked the question that catches\nany of this: for every app in every journey, does the console the audience will look at\nactually call its own API? It opens each workbench, selects every tab, and fails by name\notherwise. It also recognises the development-server case, where the console''s own\nContent-Security-Policy refuses the `eval` a dev build compiles with, so React never starts\nand the whole page is dead markup: the demo runs built, and now says so when it is not.","tree":{"sha":"b0d179eab4d7796fd9b73457e6af4e773c605dd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/b0d179eab4d7796fd9b73457e6af4e773c605dd8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/58dbc70b525683bcdfcc35e34cbebf8e6b941d2e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/58dbc70b525683bcdfcc35e34cbebf8e6b941d2e","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDU4ZGJjNzBiNTI1NjgzYmNkZmNjMzVlMzRjYmViZjhlNmI5NDFkMmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/b21d2fe5eaed5d01cbf4bc7040ff70057df21ff4","sha":"b21d2fe5eaed5d01cbf4bc7040ff70057df21ff4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/b21d2fe5eaed5d01cbf4bc7040ff70057df21ff4"}],"sha":"58dbc70b525683bcdfcc35e34cbebf8e6b941d2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/58dbc70b525683bcdfcc35e34cbebf8e6b941d2e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/b21d2fe5eaed5d01cbf4bc7040ff70057df21ff4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T14:48:09Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T14:51:30Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Drive the same walkthrough against the deployment, and hold before each submission\n\nThree changes, all in service of presenting this system on a laptop and on the\ndeployment in one session.\n\nThe walkthrough gains a target. `--target gcp` selects the subset of steps the\ndeployment can honestly serve, narrates them with hosted variants that name the\nmanaged services and disclose the labelled screening stand-in, expects each app to\nreport the managed profile rather than a local one, and either waits for the\npresenter to sign in through IAP or mints the same service-account token the e2e\nsuite uses. Steps the deployment does not embed are not offered rather than\ndegraded, and app API bases are read from the portal''s own journey catalog so one\nscript is correct on both targets.\n\n`--confirm-inputs` holds once each form is filled and before it is submitted, so\nthe audience can read what is about to be sent while the presenter narrates it.\nIt is ignored under --no-pause, because an unattended capture must not block.\n\nThe launcher now names Hrz7''s profile. Without it the review service refused every\nreview with 401 while its health check still read green, so the queue listed and\ndisposed of nothing and the maker-checker steps could not run at all. The test that\ncovers it was observed failing before the fix, and the presenter runners'' own\nsuites are now named in the test target: they sat outside testpaths and nothing\ninvoked them.","tree":{"sha":"d387db1787c6432f0155b81d84f69ea77f2b0035","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/d387db1787c6432f0155b81d84f69ea77f2b0035"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/b21d2fe5eaed5d01cbf4bc7040ff70057df21ff4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/b21d2fe5eaed5d01cbf4bc7040ff70057df21ff4","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKGIyMWQyZmU1ZWFlZDVkMDFjYmY0YmM3MDQwZmY3MDA1N2RmMjFmZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/a6f90c00c60025d2ef29a8da540de0b93e33b7be","sha":"a6f90c00c60025d2ef29a8da540de0b93e33b7be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/a6f90c00c60025d2ef29a8da540de0b93e33b7be"}],"sha":"b21d2fe5eaed5d01cbf4bc7040ff70057df21ff4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/b21d2fe5eaed5d01cbf4bc7040ff70057df21ff4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/a6f90c00c60025d2ef29a8da540de0b93e33b7be/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T12:13:53Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T12:18:00Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Let the deployment state its own cost posture, and score F4 as it now stands\n\nThree standing charges in this stack had no deployment surface at all. The\ninstance floor sat inside the reviewed `runtime` object, load-balancer\nsampling and the NAT log filter were literals, and the sanctioned Terraform\nrunner forbids -var and -var-file on purpose. So the only way to decline any\nof them was to edit the default every adopter inherits, which is not\ndeclining a control, it is changing the product.\n\nThat is the same shape that locked a sibling stack''s audit bucket for seven\nyears: the tfvars named neither the lock nor the retention, the code default\nsaid true, and the irreversible thing happened because nobody could say\notherwise. A control with no surface is a control nobody chooses.\n\n  runtime_min_instances, split out of the runtime object. Five services run\n  from it, so the default is five instances billed around the clock whether\n  or not anyone calls them. Splitting it cost the paired validation that\n  held the floor against the ceiling -- a validation block may not read a\n  second variable on the Terraform floor this stack declares -- so that\n  check moved to a lifecycle precondition, where it still refuses at plan\n  time rather than becoming a comment.\n\n  lb_log_sample_rate and nat_log_filter, both defaulting to what they\n  already did. Kept as variables rather than lowered in place: on a stack\n  whose access log is evidence, full sampling is correct, and on one whose\n  egress claim needs defending, the translations ARE the evidence.\n\nAll three are REQUIRED deployment keys rather than optional ones, and that\nis the whole point. An optional key with a default is how a deployment ends\nup never having decided. `check` now refuses an .env that does not state\nthem, which is the refusal this change exists to produce.\n\ntest_internal_only_upstreams_are_paired_with_direct_vpc_egress asserted\n`filter = \"ALL\"` as a literal and had to change. It was asserting the\nspelling rather than the control: the durable statement is that NAT logging\nis enabled, that its filter is bound to a reviewed variable, and that the\nvariable defaults to full capture. It now asserts those three.\n\nF4 moves to PASS. `make e2e-pair` exits zero on 16 compared fields, twice on\nindependent runs, with the exemption list not edited to get there. The row\nkeeps the whole route rather than the verdict: the first run''s 12\ndivergences over 18 fields, and that closing them took repository fixes,\ndeployment fixes and two data repairs -- including taking the risk band away\nfrom the model, and pinning a shared request builder that defaulted to\ntemperature 0.2 and made the managed profile disagree with itself run to\nrun. A green pair before that pin would have been luck. Two exemptions\nremain, both narrowed and both with written reasons, and audit correlation\nis still not compared.","tree":{"sha":"6a5d57053dce62618d26b9252bb74b10f7a78d22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/6a5d57053dce62618d26b9252bb74b10f7a78d22"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/a6f90c00c60025d2ef29a8da540de0b93e33b7be","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/a6f90c00c60025d2ef29a8da540de0b93e33b7be","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKGE2ZjkwYzAwYzYwMDI1ZDJlZjI5YThkYTU0MGRlMGI5M2UzM2I3YmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/3d9c717e5a14af985c276e93eb107109e1c26207","sha":"3d9c717e5a14af985c276e93eb107109e1c26207","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/3d9c717e5a14af985c276e93eb107109e1c26207"}],"sha":"a6f90c00c60025d2ef29a8da540de0b93e33b7be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/a6f90c00c60025d2ef29a8da540de0b93e33b7be"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/3d9c717e5a14af985c276e93eb107109e1c26207/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T06:54:37Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T06:59:53Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump shared kits: hex-service-kit v0.0.5","tree":{"sha":"1ecff2a14039d8afaca56a8d079cb4f91948cf22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/1ecff2a14039d8afaca56a8d079cb4f91948cf22"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/3d9c717e5a14af985c276e93eb107109e1c26207","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/3d9c717e5a14af985c276e93eb107109e1c26207","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDNkOWM3MTdlNWExNGFmOTg1YzI3NmU5M2ViMTA3MTA5ZTFjMjYyMDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/3e5eb14fad7413b8be006217f262c9d1b36c1f0d","sha":"3e5eb14fad7413b8be006217f262c9d1b36c1f0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/3e5eb14fad7413b8be006217f262c9d1b36c1f0d"}],"sha":"3d9c717e5a14af985c276e93eb107109e1c26207","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/3d9c717e5a14af985c276e93eb107109e1c26207"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/3e5eb14fad7413b8be006217f262c9d1b36c1f0d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T06:06:07Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T06:19:25Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Follow the 2026-08-27 region revision, and say where the deployment still runs\n\nThe Terraform region and the runtime preflight default to asia-southeast1 again. The\nallowlist deliberately carries TWO members while the migration is in flight: dropping the\ntarget region would fail a bare terraform plan, and dropping the one the reference\ndeployment runs in would make that deployment fail its own residency validation.\n\nThe dossier now cites the 2026-08-27 revision rather than the 2026-08-24 one it\nsuperseded, and separates the target region from where the stack actually runs. The\nper-service availability check that revision retired was run after all; it is what\nreversed the decision, so the dossier records it as discharged rather than moot.","tree":{"sha":"4ae51877190dc6b29a1868363339c62b910d7b66","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/4ae51877190dc6b29a1868363339c62b910d7b66"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/3e5eb14fad7413b8be006217f262c9d1b36c1f0d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/3e5eb14fad7413b8be006217f262c9d1b36c1f0d","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDNlNWViMTRmYWQ3NDEzYjhiZTAwNjIxN2YyNjJjOWQxYjM2YzFmMGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/3b3a18c3733e648411fe7749768cf9ea8ec6609f","sha":"3b3a18c3733e648411fe7749768cf9ea8ec6609f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/3b3a18c3733e648411fe7749768cf9ea8ec6609f"}],"sha":"3e5eb14fad7413b8be006217f262c9d1b36c1f0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/3e5eb14fad7413b8be006217f262c9d1b36c1f0d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/3b3a18c3733e648411fe7749768cf9ea8ec6609f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T19:48:20Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T19:48:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Exempt the SoW classification, compare the money, and add a presence check (#44)\n\nTwo models reading one page of prose classify the wealth it describes\ndifferently -- asset_sale and business_ownership against business_ownership and\nother -- and each assigns its own reading a confidence. That is the declared\nquality reduction the published invariant already permits, in the same class as\nthe adverse_media and ownership exemptions beside it.\n\nOnly the classification and the confidence are exempt. The first attempt at this\nentry exempted sow.sources wholesale, which quietly took the AMOUNTS with it,\nand a guard in tests/test_pairing.py caught exactly that: an amount, a currency\nand a period are consequential figures a reviewer acts on, so two profiles\nreading one statement must agree about the money even when they disagree about\nwhat to call it. sow.amounts is compared in its own right now, and sow.present\nanswers the question exempting a subtree would otherwise bury -- did this\nprofile extract a source of wealth at all.\n\nWhat makes this honest rather than convenient is what changed underneath it: the\nband and score are no longer downstream of the classification, because they now\ncome from the deterministic scorecard. Exempting these two while the score still\ndepended on them would have exempted the score too, silently.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"483d46c9b6e2e8cab5eaa5d3ffae077bdef14423","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/483d46c9b6e2e8cab5eaa5d3ffae077bdef14423"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/3b3a18c3733e648411fe7749768cf9ea8ec6609f","verification":{"payload":"tree 483d46c9b6e2e8cab5eaa5d3ffae077bdef14423\nparent bd00382492eecf30116627da50b9e2ee54bd3fa0\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787773700 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787773700 +0800\n\nExempt the SoW classification, compare the money, and add a presence check (#44)\n\nTwo models reading one page of prose classify the wealth it describes\ndifferently -- asset_sale and business_ownership against business_ownership and\nother -- and each assigns its own reading a confidence. That is the declared\nquality reduction the published invariant already permits, in the same class as\nthe adverse_media and ownership exemptions beside it.\n\nOnly the classification and the confidence are exempt. The first attempt at this\nentry exempted sow.sources wholesale, which quietly took the AMOUNTS with it,\nand a guard in tests/test_pairing.py caught exactly that: an amount, a currency\nand a period are consequential figures a reviewer acts on, so two profiles\nreading one statement must agree about the money even when they disagree about\nwhat to call it. sow.amounts is compared in its own right now, and sow.present\nanswers the question exempting a subtree would otherwise bury -- did this\nprofile extract a source of wealth at all.\n\nWhat makes this honest rather than convenient is what changed underneath it: the\nband and score are no longer downstream of the classification, because they now\ncome from the deterministic scorecard. Exempting these two while the score still\ndepended on them would have exempted the score too, silently.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqj0MECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0Y8QAFdB+qqp3iBRj0NYtmTsNSqC\nHH0c9YU50AzokxwwEKKpgOXqWZzxnFCADdwnxTFsy0vG117mBHNoP9pW1I20/CmR\n01HHQtrEy4Z3EEnD+n/snFRfoKYGmTBYNlC/tK+aflOplFxpxtbdY3G81nbXdhij\n1/dQ6eST7GgwX3L0WwjkNLPNWlPJp4bNZJSqPX4gFqMfjuRfv2hzP55UiOiyrGlx\n300IspoM7U22DTqaQjgFeyCD11k0+A9NNfS44o7qsuL0Q8Q3Wg1g7BitmrsrzqIN\nyt6W02E9sQf6T3hR/cxSYmNwHvOm+K1PrvM+n6lmb+jGsP34p/yI7pCKkVr8E+X2\n/bmAbxAmtOaljfOAwWseikv8NeQHc3TqmsMsZ+Dj2TLVxywBxNr/yMj0O4QjDy92\nNwPoeiEBQNaQ//jPlAiAiST4Td6lU2mbtBbHn5BDjYekFnTAGbYLDrN6pzxYAfw6\n1Fq8S1P7WXW1McsPRnbb9Mop27kXXAwpZuL0SeCUkoAhZ3FLSJcpEw6xVer8wcGB\nDsR0Tk7J0zdY9CRkKcErsX+1s0iBJ3yQ48nVb/JcsSw5uYYRTZsBkjvPAorKLtcW\nlcUH5+lc7mUYWIiifDUhIZDkHShEiiDULqTOKVaI3whlQ0o4/WjdThZA7uy6Wsa0\n3bRH685YksIE2qGY64nU\n=wcwj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T19:48:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/3b3a18c3733e648411fe7749768cf9ea8ec6609f","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDNiM2ExOGMzNzMzZTY0ODQxMWZlNzc0OTc2OGNmOWVhOGVjNjYwOWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/bd00382492eecf30116627da50b9e2ee54bd3fa0","sha":"bd00382492eecf30116627da50b9e2ee54bd3fa0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/bd00382492eecf30116627da50b9e2ee54bd3fa0"}],"sha":"3b3a18c3733e648411fe7749768cf9ea8ec6609f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/3b3a18c3733e648411fe7749768cf9ea8ec6609f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/bd00382492eecf30116627da50b9e2ee54bd3fa0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T14:07:16Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T14:07:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Apply Debian security updates and drop pip from the portal serving image (#43)\n\n* Apply Debian security updates and drop pip from the portal serving image\n\nFound by running the managed trust-boundary suite against the deployment, which\nis what Track C item 4 asks for and what nothing had re-run.\n\nThe suite failed on a real gap: the deployment exposes no /v1/healthz, so a\nreadiness probe against /healthz is answered by the serverless frontend and\nnever reaches the container -- it measures the platform, not the application.\nThe route has existed in this repository since 5dd1a51; the deployed image was\nbuilt before it. Same staleness class as the Doc1 image, in the portal itself.\n\nRebuilding it surfaced two more, both of which the promotion scan refused:\n\nA digest pin freezes the base image, which means it also freezes its unpatched\npackages. Reproducible and vulnerable are not opposites, and the pin is\notherwise cited as evidence of the first while quietly guaranteeing the second:\nthis image carried 39 fixable HIGH Debian advisories, every one with a released\nfix, because nothing here ever applied one. Doc1''s Dockerfile has carried that\nreasoning and that layer for some time; the portal had not.\n\nThat left two findings, both pip''s VENDORED copies -- msgpack and setuptools\nlive inside pip/_vendor, so a scanner reports them as installed packages.\nNeither is a dependency of this application and no constraint could reach them,\nbecause they were never resolved. A serving container installs nothing, so pip\ngoes, exactly as it does in Doc1.\n\nThe image now scans clean on the blocking pass, and /v1/healthz answers 200 from\nthe container on the deployment.\n\n* Ignore the agent-rule files the Next.js build generates\n\nNext.js 16 writes AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md into each UI directory during a build.\nThey are generated, not authored here, so after every --built run the tree was\ndirty for a change nobody made and the portfolio gate reported it as a finding.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4646dbc32c6b4c87f33f1ebdc3c2d0ef1c63f861","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/4646dbc32c6b4c87f33f1ebdc3c2d0ef1c63f861"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/bd00382492eecf30116627da50b9e2ee54bd3fa0","verification":{"payload":"tree 4646dbc32c6b4c87f33f1ebdc3c2d0ef1c63f861\nparent bb8ad5f14606e2543b914ea6d2347d74647178de\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787753236 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787753236 +0800\n\nApply Debian security updates and drop pip from the portal serving image (#43)\n\n* Apply Debian security updates and drop pip from the portal serving image\n\nFound by running the managed trust-boundary suite against the deployment, which\nis what Track C item 4 asks for and what nothing had re-run.\n\nThe suite failed on a real gap: the deployment exposes no /v1/healthz, so a\nreadiness probe against /healthz is answered by the serverless frontend and\nnever reaches the container -- it measures the platform, not the application.\nThe route has existed in this repository since 5dd1a51; the deployed image was\nbuilt before it. Same staleness class as the Doc1 image, in the portal itself.\n\nRebuilding it surfaced two more, both of which the promotion scan refused:\n\nA digest pin freezes the base image, which means it also freezes its unpatched\npackages. Reproducible and vulnerable are not opposites, and the pin is\notherwise cited as evidence of the first while quietly guaranteeing the second:\nthis image carried 39 fixable HIGH Debian advisories, every one with a released\nfix, because nothing here ever applied one. Doc1''s Dockerfile has carried that\nreasoning and that layer for some time; the portal had not.\n\nThat left two findings, both pip''s VENDORED copies -- msgpack and setuptools\nlive inside pip/_vendor, so a scanner reports them as installed packages.\nNeither is a dependency of this application and no constraint could reach them,\nbecause they were never resolved. A serving container installs nothing, so pip\ngoes, exactly as it does in Doc1.\n\nThe image now scans clean on the blocking pass, and /v1/healthz answers 200 from\nthe container on the deployment.\n\n* Ignore the agent-rule files the Next.js build generates\n\nNext.js 16 writes AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md into each UI directory during a build.\nThey are generated, not authored here, so after every --built run the tree was\ndirty for a change nobody made and the portfolio gate reported it as a finding.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjvMUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAU4MQAIKl1kUNqT27fzAvytGC0zC5\no8gQVEapj6CzJQl3XDFmIzzDyKTTOzUtKJwW/E0iuEc68o9S9n03oJUZZfQGV+Vl\n/9y/SiPeh0jBISoaZvY7oeIL8KQbJJeLJc0HR7yOKBO1/Pi2lYhepXgmR55StjU3\n876N08sgl0CmFC3khs6sOPjHXvILTGZW74cHXTrr1xavmK90B7lxzuFtYpwmMABN\nnFLbSV5ynQTLOjyemJxiwdyLB/HnnwiSsLdAmojGvokNae+8HlQUNirD9MiZcakC\nk5Muse3nlrG7ML3vzfYE7T2SkIr2HoJh5Ve0mTUIBgfNlpCbKlO8rLNPtydus6ee\n3z8d4/572chHsWnYUZKZVeKlqwZbDNWSNIxEqCfW3j1PZsTf/vz0PytrXFl/r3iO\n7gFa/bhOU2ihbu+VWf/qUZV51D5uuPWn7AJOvztmI/oRjAARl4+WNR74/xdq2dAE\nvkuVF4VTGYLms4VsHFh74ZZSEBOxdTZt8Y0FLmkg2HgSV5A/A6MwQUDBcIEaoM4o\ntPiFEx4W8U2PV9eRTQ0i2nbezt+S5vV23U+CTnmpYduNjGxgAxF/x/Fm/W1FmaJi\nr7cped8T/YdcOq5/WSdFwoDelU96GkD4ucBoJKyuL7J72dcPfkDDEMGQ8mbQl1Uk\nrM7+HS75SzP6d2A3oRE3\n=i+Ao\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T14:07:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/bd00382492eecf30116627da50b9e2ee54bd3fa0","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKGJkMDAzODI0OTJlZWNmMzAxMTY2MjdkYTUwYjllMmVlNTRiZDNmYTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/bb8ad5f14606e2543b914ea6d2347d74647178de","sha":"bb8ad5f14606e2543b914ea6d2347d74647178de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/bb8ad5f14606e2543b914ea6d2347d74647178de"}],"sha":"bd00382492eecf30116627da50b9e2ee54bd3fa0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/bd00382492eecf30116627da50b9e2ee54bd3fa0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/bb8ad5f14606e2543b914ea6d2347d74647178de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T01:25:53Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T01:25:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Rebind the transport facts, and record why the claim half is not adopted (#42)\n\nTwo findings, both from executing the commons against this adapter rather than\nreading it.\n\nThe transport half was missing in adapters/gcp/identity.py. It carried its own\nliterals for the assertion header, the issuer and the key set while\ndomain/identity_injection.py has taken them from the commons since tier 3\nlanded. Nothing could notice, because a literal always agrees with itself, and\ntwo modules in one repository disagreeing about which header carries identity\nis the exact drift the kit exists to make impossible. They are rebound, and\nthe guard asserts the source rather than the value, because an equality\nassertion is what a fresh copy satisfies.\n\nThe claim half is deliberately not adopted, and the blocker empties a\nload-bearing tenant. FederationPolicy.tenant_for short circuits on\nmachine=True and returns machine_tenant, one string for every machine caller,\nbefore domain_tenants is consulted at all. This deployment maps a service\naccount''s own project domain onto a reviewed tenant, so under the commons\nevery mapped machine caller resolves to no tenant: fail-closed and closed for\na whole population, and invisible to an offline gate because the local profile\nnever constructs this adapter. Filling machine_tenant in is not the fix, since\none string would give an unreviewed project the same tenant as a reviewed one.\n\nA second disagreement runs the other way: tenant_for consults the map for the\nasserted domain and the mail domain and takes the first mapped, where this\nadapter consults hd if present and otherwise the mail domain. Both belong in\nthe kit''s backlog as a missing machine_tenants map rather than in a change\nthat quietly moves who this service serves.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"15ce16e47a6c9edd6a2197d39772d9bb31acfb87","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/15ce16e47a6c9edd6a2197d39772d9bb31acfb87"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/bb8ad5f14606e2543b914ea6d2347d74647178de","verification":{"payload":"tree 15ce16e47a6c9edd6a2197d39772d9bb31acfb87\nparent f1b9fbdda1d9529f6e50e5b78d61cc0bbb28657c\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787707553 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787707553 +0800\n\nRebind the transport facts, and record why the claim half is not adopted (#42)\n\nTwo findings, both from executing the commons against this adapter rather than\nreading it.\n\nThe transport half was missing in adapters/gcp/identity.py. It carried its own\nliterals for the assertion header, the issuer and the key set while\ndomain/identity_injection.py has taken them from the commons since tier 3\nlanded. Nothing could notice, because a literal always agrees with itself, and\ntwo modules in one repository disagreeing about which header carries identity\nis the exact drift the kit exists to make impossible. They are rebound, and\nthe guard asserts the source rather than the value, because an equality\nassertion is what a fresh copy satisfies.\n\nThe claim half is deliberately not adopted, and the blocker empties a\nload-bearing tenant. FederationPolicy.tenant_for short circuits on\nmachine=True and returns machine_tenant, one string for every machine caller,\nbefore domain_tenants is consulted at all. This deployment maps a service\naccount''s own project domain onto a reviewed tenant, so under the commons\nevery mapped machine caller resolves to no tenant: fail-closed and closed for\na whole population, and invisible to an offline gate because the local profile\nnever constructs this adapter. Filling machine_tenant in is not the fix, since\none string would give an unreviewed project the same tenant as a reviewed one.\n\nA second disagreement runs the other way: tenant_for consults the map for the\nasserted domain and the mail domain and takes the first mapped, where this\nadapter consults hd if present and otherwise the mail domain. Both belong in\nthe kit''s backlog as a missing machine_tenants map rather than in a change\nthat quietly moves who this service serves.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjkChCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqicQAEYFLD7VI4uozJ8lcFSzNOWB\nlMOO+NZaXOOBpNQMZdrkgmkFyl8+8dVysEAKFKV6BHPGklBbkQTtRwUqgLB1+Mjs\nRh9IwqunoS9vxSUeKtKWeRmuT8+Ty1YLtuTVF+0MFBX6jbkDgAWWjoDjRnQ+oID2\nBhq52/xRbMi0ImmPTKHsqSCDiik97aypqX71adQ09FAdVNdp1cSrKfaj0eEm8pKL\n4cZaiVokhLTuZD7oPB64DMSMEa1vrGNbygokDBzBnIgOXLo+kULZ9jJEmiRaWhY9\n42DpKEQiG5KL1BEL5Z0HJ/pFiDY9wC3aUBnzbZmHi2z5KibH6UpQep4btKpKpLn1\niIIDUieIr4pwLU6Pg0uveWN5ckXDzWhnU2Vs6aZh/R7z/GK+mRn/MubP+A9/ZWl5\n/Nn0nwrxsaRTX+42gVrCQMd8jTGyXMlXrPv1unmeoYEtdkByrCTW272WtsTP8PaQ\nc+9Lv9R4CEMhmp9X0vFSkaijOU+a2CXY59cRjilYc1EkHclId5TLdJkDFs4gNbI+\n05AVmv2BInGXQef0NQlT+f6XQPlejl7F7aUqcaolh1z6ijORXAkACOTJLMnclVBV\nAQceer6gYZCwyF0THGI2Iet7VVFK23Hgp+zvOurw//LJgPak6bMjP8U0Wsb8xHHk\nrk5VKGHBcJY6Xr7HizDF\n=hLpW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T01:25:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/bb8ad5f14606e2543b914ea6d2347d74647178de","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKGJiOGFkNWYxNDYwNmUyNTQzYjkxNGVhNmQyMzQ3ZDc0NjQ3MTc4ZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/f1b9fbdda1d9529f6e50e5b78d61cc0bbb28657c","sha":"f1b9fbdda1d9529f6e50e5b78d61cc0bbb28657c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/f1b9fbdda1d9529f6e50e5b78d61cc0bbb28657c"}],"sha":"bb8ad5f14606e2543b914ea6d2347d74647178de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/bb8ad5f14606e2543b914ea6d2347d74647178de"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/f1b9fbdda1d9529f6e50e5b78d61cc0bbb28657c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T00:27:43Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T00:27:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Exempt ownership resolution, and keep presence compared (#41)\n\nRunbook C2 said this needed a written decision rather than a code change, and this is it.\nThe laptop resolves the demo subject from a seeded registry fixture; the managed profile\nasks a grounded web search, which correctly finds nothing for an entity that does not\nexist. Comparing them would demand the managed side invent an owner for a fictional\ncompany, which is the same defect the adverse_media exemption exists to prevent.\n\nOnly `ownership.owners` and `ownership.citations` are exempt. `ownership.present` and\n`ownership.root_entity` stay compared, deliberately: whether a profile resolved ownership\nat all is exactly the silent omission the pair exists to catch, and exempting the subtree\nwholesale would have hidden it. The citations follow the owners because they are citations\nOF those two different sources, not because citation comparison is unreliable.\n\nBoth halves move together, since a field is excluded by not being emitted in `comparable`\nand EXEMPT is the declaration that says why.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"555f6847bb573d1c00733df41e42e4608ec5caec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/555f6847bb573d1c00733df41e42e4608ec5caec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/f1b9fbdda1d9529f6e50e5b78d61cc0bbb28657c","verification":{"payload":"tree 555f6847bb573d1c00733df41e42e4608ec5caec\nparent 5dd1a511a926b7e4de625b9aaeb5242717fb4c08\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787704063 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787704063 +0800\n\nExempt ownership resolution, and keep presence compared (#41)\n\nRunbook C2 said this needed a written decision rather than a code change, and this is it.\nThe laptop resolves the demo subject from a seeded registry fixture; the managed profile\nasks a grounded web search, which correctly finds nothing for an entity that does not\nexist. Comparing them would demand the managed side invent an owner for a fictional\ncompany, which is the same defect the adverse_media exemption exists to prevent.\n\nOnly `ownership.owners` and `ownership.citations` are exempt. `ownership.present` and\n`ownership.root_entity` stay compared, deliberately: whether a profile resolved ownership\nat all is exactly the silent omission the pair exists to catch, and exempting the subtree\nwholesale would have hidden it. The citations follow the owners because they are citations\nOF those two different sources, not because citation comparison is unreliable.\n\nBoth halves move together, since a field is excluded by not being emitted in `comparable`\nand EXEMPT is the declaration that says why.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjjL/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd1YQAI6kd2/DgoEKWSquljtqguFY\nfMkt+6dcJni/I9X5IgA9DFpH/09nWldiPZCdbfO0ALvx8XCXtI5lxG7njYx4akB4\n3EUP7eKrfYsKwwazNGIz6K1BB2gLMC3m6itOLBO6YV6KmfQHVIl6VbMR1mIoVsCg\nWgi61B38mRKZhi5G+OKHImZY4hlQyFmYesFBB0nRE3zw52k3nO1eZvmvp6SAcH2i\nbO/dMiSXSZItQXNYpUoyrFOdii5pZSSjGu94DKClNDrZaxse1gmL5qecTEAvPFBj\niJhFeCVnur1yZs7cDAod+s6AECASjaqxKoCSiRxiZvIIlDhIpfi55+R12+o6kbB2\nHiGJqPIgQe/M6TZeD3ELSPexoeO3OrBSb7u+A54+UpwJBCCArRuPyovpytMjGT4w\n5PBgpmOEy1yQYqZDiCXKgXVOCvzZNWuWCiMNpajIlc/3Mwr+W2mSevsNcWUXfR95\n4T07rR/kc1bIwzuoht0Xe/dRlc8zw9rGpsChilMhz/8+lrFQ4+Lhwush6FGF2zn4\nAWacuXXGDTeZolqEyZYHxbftJ7pFg5+8aILbrmgGmK/7ZYPG9Z0SqrnuQCXY8sOh\n0xblQ/iwk3Wi8LF1NBZ/gElagpHgrJKTwwqALCn61W8hCSq9miRSPCXSS+uHh8Q5\nn2k7QtdmxiRohMEajy9f\n=iYAW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T00:27:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/f1b9fbdda1d9529f6e50e5b78d61cc0bbb28657c","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKGYxYjlmYmRkYTFkOTUyOWY2ZTUwZTViNzhkNjFjYzBiYmIyODY1N2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/5dd1a511a926b7e4de625b9aaeb5242717fb4c08","sha":"5dd1a511a926b7e4de625b9aaeb5242717fb4c08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/5dd1a511a926b7e4de625b9aaeb5242717fb4c08"}],"sha":"f1b9fbdda1d9529f6e50e5b78d61cc0bbb28657c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/f1b9fbdda1d9529f6e50e5b78d61cc0bbb28657c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/5dd1a511a926b7e4de625b9aaeb5242717fb4c08/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T00:22:13Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T00:22:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Stop the trust-boundary suite reporting a bypass that is not there, and serve the readiness path it asks for (#40)\n\nThe managed trust-boundary suite had never been run against a deployment. Running it\nfailed both edge tests, and the forged-header one failed saying the serverless frontend\nwas not stripping the reserved namespace: in other words, it reported a live\nauthentication bypass.\n\nThere is no bypass. `urlopen` follows redirects by default. IAP refuses by answering 302\ntowards Google sign-in, the test followed that redirect, and the sign-in page answered\n200, which the assertion read as the app having served an unauthenticated caller. The\nsame two requests through `curl -I` returned 302 both times. A guard that cannot pass\nagainst a correctly behaving system is worse than an absent one, and this one accused the\ndeployment of the most serious defect it could have. The opener no longer follows\nredirects, so the refusal is observed rather than fetched.\n\nWith that corrected the suite got far enough to find something real. `/healthz` is\nanswered by the serverless frontend and never reaches this container, so a proxied\nreadiness probe reports healthy whether or not the application is running. The versioned\npath the suite asks for did not exist, so there was no path a proxied probe could honestly\nuse. `/v1/healthz` now answers from the loaded settings, beside `/healthz` and reporting\nidentically, and joins the unauthenticated set for the same reason `/healthz` is in it:\nit carries no tenant data and a probe holds no session.\n\nRed first: the new readiness guard was run with the route renamed away and failed, then\npassed once restored. Offline `make check` is green.\n\nFive of the six managed tests now pass against the named deployment. The sixth still\nreports 404 for the versioned path, correctly: the running revision carries an image built\nbefore this change, and rolling a new image is not in scope here.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"63fb69e127235a5e9534f5aa34a733c7cd0a108a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/63fb69e127235a5e9534f5aa34a733c7cd0a108a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/5dd1a511a926b7e4de625b9aaeb5242717fb4c08","verification":{"payload":"tree 63fb69e127235a5e9534f5aa34a733c7cd0a108a\nparent 225608c45d154e9b2e4b26700f196c0271d112f5\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787703733 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787703733 +0800\n\nStop the trust-boundary suite reporting a bypass that is not there, and serve the readiness path it asks for (#40)\n\nThe managed trust-boundary suite had never been run against a deployment. Running it\nfailed both edge tests, and the forged-header one failed saying the serverless frontend\nwas not stripping the reserved namespace: in other words, it reported a live\nauthentication bypass.\n\nThere is no bypass. `urlopen` follows redirects by default. IAP refuses by answering 302\ntowards Google sign-in, the test followed that redirect, and the sign-in page answered\n200, which the assertion read as the app having served an unauthenticated caller. The\nsame two requests through `curl -I` returned 302 both times. A guard that cannot pass\nagainst a correctly behaving system is worse than an absent one, and this one accused the\ndeployment of the most serious defect it could have. The opener no longer follows\nredirects, so the refusal is observed rather than fetched.\n\nWith that corrected the suite got far enough to find something real. `/healthz` is\nanswered by the serverless frontend and never reaches this container, so a proxied\nreadiness probe reports healthy whether or not the application is running. The versioned\npath the suite asks for did not exist, so there was no path a proxied probe could honestly\nuse. `/v1/healthz` now answers from the loaded settings, beside `/healthz` and reporting\nidentically, and joins the unauthenticated set for the same reason `/healthz` is in it:\nit carries no tenant data and a probe holds no session.\n\nRed first: the new readiness guard was run with the route renamed away and failed, then\npassed once restored. Offline `make check` is green.\n\nFive of the six managed tests now pass against the named deployment. The sixth still\nreports 404 for the versioned path, correctly: the running revision carries an image built\nbefore this change, and rolling a new image is not in scope here.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjjG1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaTsQAFzW3fht0Gpimx7efc6zER21\nx5FZsC8yO+LD9r5jRKGQHLHV+t0zu/I/FEDFzKhHU+0IuKR9PayjcqdYQPVDJh5R\nxeJL1gsQiPBEW0fA0fQTbLG0epWCGhd//UdKE1C78ilg4c1kGwQpIqhT8l/5Yy3f\nlHeFSqgsFoN41foHBiIQD4dQfwdw4AxdxRegXulvrXxRd+xroEIKPKxVO7IwyCVh\nGVcvKS79zOddeYzc9FeYlr7EeiEIKZxFQ5GbqJbNHLL/Wrg6UHYWonbLyFcxUND+\nv04YKteYEDLAgEnAHYquBEF4FXVRs55ql5AZ7sHCOcX8UrqPGeFlBgFk4X8iRYh1\n8DpWGUuxtQyP226t7bxwczRDHWTHBIWRPhRaFryc9XNk+9fSzRd31BVLPaoocYh/\noMhx5/7pH1cLeSr30zJORIIyvEPHVE4E0yOc9zJFwPRYA4Xv/wHqH9oNwdjWPNtI\nBO5yT0Nx8xHMhy+5p1t5R9eexoPPlfqpMK3+Uvbj1sW1c/WoBgxzFEini+NSxf+x\n4fTahYlXjWtSU3vL5op8r4aRyuTHZgaKnEbppiLwDTidoG3Fshr3gulF1Cz2OR+q\n2LKrSu7X54B1lNg/gKokIw4Y7QYxXaM+maE+XLTnXNXA/FxlRFTmhK/HGdHUXd1k\nsuDxv6V7DvweZUWmYl+N\n=Dye3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T00:22:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/5dd1a511a926b7e4de625b9aaeb5242717fb4c08","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDVkZDFhNTExYTkyNmI3ZTRkZTYyNWI5YWFlYjUyNDI3MTdmYjRjMDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/225608c45d154e9b2e4b26700f196c0271d112f5","sha":"225608c45d154e9b2e4b26700f196c0271d112f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/225608c45d154e9b2e4b26700f196c0271d112f5"}],"sha":"5dd1a511a926b7e4de625b9aaeb5242717fb4c08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/5dd1a511a926b7e4de625b9aaeb5242717fb4c08"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/225608c45d154e9b2e4b26700f196c0271d112f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:54:15Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:54:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Pin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#39)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","tree":{"sha":"bb1e49997a5fe1dd8be71a6975c48ace2a789574","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/bb1e49997a5fe1dd8be71a6975c48ace2a789574"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/225608c45d154e9b2e4b26700f196c0271d112f5","verification":{"payload":"tree bb1e49997a5fe1dd8be71a6975c48ace2a789574\nparent e471f7a17224cbc2c5f89f2700dbb0a16d86f017\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787673255 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787673255 +0800\n\nPin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#39)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbqnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqLgQACmvCMUryCSkwHfmJnxqgG2U\nAvcK5q5zhyIMgIrsEJP5SzhMaWcENGofgwgBXisrpJkGL4aH5hMD8QMIuoR+8gqz\nJ70kxmZdi+s8kHhZO4TrhShLh+p+7yRJBMIqC4F5TcLN8s+N6cu7ZAS56OW4QSOr\nsegFonO4qgOSUcL2kbS2zH6YfUOEKSyeki7lvL+jOBvSp9DYQvFBbufHxwB5DRj/\njzfUb67QqEix2jveWzkH/MHC4AR+Hdq5ziddMtbyV5ASFqyO7ti8KBl5pNZdgrvo\nJuKghvghatKEAFkfjcZpoz51xO/OGbK4bCiUObh7urrX8kz8Fx1255ayeiFrPViD\nwH+jgoCIdB3bPuTaK+HQH+FZVYDC/hy1TSQER25lsdNeevXi1vT7VHWoTAs9zA7S\neiEvHed6kMpyJAKFR6h8w+GhlRW3qyl67s/MOlrP/1ZFvzr2N2M/NpoJu6VjWVj0\nv1ZpWgwLuD+gcntItdeQtB25WDKiDNCFZoSfED76qHVidRpLnkLddsLD7OCmOfYr\nTGsPOtjp3QwssTL7LZG2LyPTRDyiEJSIX5iOi+TpUJfQN91jeMXfsvIbIjKn4rdf\nSJaGeDGyOq3wMzMMVfgxzyVu5ljJpINqxYsPZYQwjBkMIPGbxp9F2nkbv87+v95c\nN0VSwLbkjATf75tehm/y\n=ZURx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T15:54:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/225608c45d154e9b2e4b26700f196c0271d112f5","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDIyNTYwOGM0NWQxNTRlOWIyZTRiMjY3MDBmMTk2YzAyNzFkMTEyZjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/e471f7a17224cbc2c5f89f2700dbb0a16d86f017","sha":"e471f7a17224cbc2c5f89f2700dbb0a16d86f017","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/e471f7a17224cbc2c5f89f2700dbb0a16d86f017"}],"sha":"225608c45d154e9b2e4b26700f196c0271d112f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/225608c45d154e9b2e4b26700f196c0271d112f5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/e471f7a17224cbc2c5f89f2700dbb0a16d86f017/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T14:33:15Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T14:33:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"A managed suite for the properties only a real edge can show (#38)\n\nTrack C item 4. Hrz9 was exercised against the real services by running it, which\nfound defects no offline profile can reach; that proves those paths worked at the\nmoment they were run, and nothing re-runs them.\n\nThe offline suite already asserts the header-rewrite plan thoroughly, and it cannot\nassert the part that actually broke, because every defect the first deployment\nfound was a property of the HOP rather than of the plan. x-goog-* is stripped by\nthe serverless frontend entering a service, so the portal could not hand an\nembedded app the assertion IAP had given it -- the plan was correct and the app\nanswered ''missing IAP assertion header'' about a request that had passed through IAP\none hop earlier. x-serverless-authorization is INJECTED by the platform, so nothing\nin an offline fixture contains it and no offline test can forget to strip it.\n/healthz is answered by the frontend and never reaches the container, so a proxied\nreadiness probe reports healthy either way.\n\nThree states, never two: unset skips so the offline gate is unaffected, named and\nreachable runs, named and NOT usable FAILS. A managed suite that skips on bad\nconfiguration reports the same green as one that ran. All three proved by execution\nbefore committing, including the refusal of an http:// origin, since an identity\ntoken handed to a plaintext origin is a credential on the wire.\n\nToken minting reuses e2e/targets.py rather than reimplementing it, so this suite and\nthe browser journey cannot silently diverge on how they authenticate.\n\nGate: 648 passed, eval GATE PASS.","tree":{"sha":"fe95fe1eea9dfe6a254d0bf5432beadad1a3d41a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/fe95fe1eea9dfe6a254d0bf5432beadad1a3d41a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portab