zAwZGJiMGExNmQ4NmYwMTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/3eee3f7ef0c79f61c32335b85359912da99e8186","sha":"3eee3f7ef0c79f61c32335b85359912da99e8186","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/3eee3f7ef0c79f61c32335b85359912da99e8186"}],"sha":"e471f7a17224cbc2c5f89f2700dbb0a16d86f017","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/e471f7a17224cbc2c5f89f2700dbb0a16d86f017"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/3eee3f7ef0c79f61c32335b85359912da99e8186/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T14:11:33Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T14:11:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Compare which documents ground a claim, and adopt the federation kit (#37)\n\n* Compare which documents ground a claim, not how a store chunked them\n\nThe first live pair reported citation counts of 3 against 8 and stopped there,\nwhich reads as a policy divergence and was two different things wearing one\nnumber: a store returning one document as eight extractive segments, and eight\ntitles that had each decayed into their own document id. Neither is a count of\nsources.\n\n_citations now groups by source_id first, so the compared count is of distinct\nDOCUMENTS and no re-chunking can make the pair red. That tolerance is not a\nweakening: the comparison also now carries the titles themselves, as a sorted\nmultiset, which it did not before -- which is how eight citations that had all\nlost their names still differed only in a count. Two distinct documents sharing a\ntitle stay two. The passage count is added to EXEMPT with its reason, beside the\nsnippet and page entries that exempt the same parser fidelity for the same cause.\n\nAdopt hex_service_kit.federation for the trust boundary. The rules were only ever\nimplemented here while fifty-four repositories carried their own copy of the\nreceiving half and had already drifted on it; a trust boundary described in two\nplaces will be described differently in two places. What stays here is the\nportal''s vocabulary -- its profile names and its InjectionPlan type. What moved is\nevery security decision: which headers a browser may never assert, which\ncredential a proxy must not forward, and the two names one assertion travels\nunder. The header constants are rebound from the kit rather than re-declared, so\ndrift is impossible rather than merely unlikely.\n\nGate: 648 passed, eval GATE PASS.\n\n* Pin hex-service-kit v0.0.2 for the federation module","tree":{"sha":"c52de46665c8de6c127e70b126fec78949590a1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/c52de46665c8de6c127e70b126fec78949590a1f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/3eee3f7ef0c79f61c32335b85359912da99e8186","verification":{"payload":"tree c52de46665c8de6c127e70b126fec78949590a1f\nparent 9a722f9ed34ce91c4449ae4c28ad5f6c07e103d2\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787667093 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787667093 +0800\n\nCompare which documents ground a claim, and adopt the federation kit (#37)\n\n* Compare which documents ground a claim, not how a store chunked them\n\nThe first live pair reported citation counts of 3 against 8 and stopped there,\nwhich reads as a policy divergence and was two different things wearing one\nnumber: a store returning one document as eight extractive segments, and eight\ntitles that had each decayed into their own document id. Neither is a count of\nsources.\n\n_citations now groups by source_id first, so the compared count is of distinct\nDOCUMENTS and no re-chunking can make the pair red. That tolerance is not a\nweakening: the comparison also now carries the titles themselves, as a sorted\nmultiset, which it did not before -- which is how eight citations that had all\nlost their names still differed only in a count. Two distinct documents sharing a\ntitle stay two. The passage count is added to EXEMPT with its reason, beside the\nsnippet and page entries that exempt the same parser fidelity for the same cause.\n\nAdopt hex_service_kit.federation for the trust boundary. The rules were only ever\nimplemented here while fifty-four repositories carried their own copy of the\nreceiving half and had already drifted on it; a trust boundary described in two\nplaces will be described differently in two places. What stays here is the\nportal''s vocabulary -- its profile names and its InjectionPlan type. What moved is\nevery security decision: which headers a browser may never assert, which\ncredential a proxy must not forward, and the two names one assertion travels\nunder. The header constants are rebound from the kit rather than re-declared, so\ndrift is impossible rather than merely unlikely.\n\nGate: 648 passed, eval GATE PASS.\n\n* Pin hex-service-kit v0.0.2 for the federation module","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjaKVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAu18QAHL6CQnBosgKTOkk+MgB8LNG\nw9vgLQmXp1kepyT7fT/kv8u/qeNL+y4m4JCOePBgky9uP7haZlgpq4FdCxZ+A4ps\nYUDLRKMSrCT99gyMA+hzz1hP//S6Qxg74T2u2zyaihIXZ6MfEFsphMLrqnzho4Li\nipEMvmKoXHGDPwx+I1hJzSGVbKFErVTpzA1yJylyU7Ldz5rxOQXKOHRD6JQ4GFmH\nDxbrWB8R66EeZmck9Uzpor7M2aaF5X75WG8gnthAlt3FebW4/8YdH84XYmvPhkiY\ndnODuaA3lGvPZNyo3DRjCsIDsQ7hI9alLycz/ChLPySokQkPkMvkIjZjAD0D1sK6\nNFmkqnTfuGjjZhJIS+i+dJndWdNTwARcfHkZyM8FPwZ7BFNBi3e9ka2zjGx0NBrs\nlbsmY3aULKiyP/HPvSv2kG7trTJngIeRt5bY34iH5Qs/4pD9PrSMqxYoCuvJUOFd\n6P3Bs/zXFCyCiRQqBoDgKFTQSMlrLpDfOzhC+ZOBQ8/OoVLDXpN57W89mLCdIqOY\neHatuvl+Hxd8K0XKj1dTF00O0dnl3l84DoDXFtL77Xb7LlRDVIknm9gjtVfzVHaN\nCd2kIz9nEcMQO45jXE9zhWRzXJLsn8gURVomrs9p6Qxoel3CxYm62Woz4nB3Ww36\nWBbmu+tpsE8DCLZ4tLNG\n=DAdw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T14:11:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/3eee3f7ef0c79f61c32335b85359912da99e8186","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDNlZWUzZjdlZjBjNzlmNjFjMzIzMzViODUzNTk5MTJkYTk5ZTgxODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/9a722f9ed34ce91c4449ae4c28ad5f6c07e103d2","sha":"9a722f9ed34ce91c4449ae4c28ad5f6c07e103d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/9a722f9ed34ce91c4449ae4c28ad5f6c07e103d2"}],"sha":"3eee3f7ef0c79f61c32335b85359912da99e8186","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/3eee3f7ef0c79f61c32335b85359912da99e8186"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/9a722f9ed34ce91c4449ae4c28ad5f6c07e103d2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T13:19:44Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T13:19:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Compare the two profiles instead of running them twice, and score F4 (#36)\n\nThe demo ran the same journey on a laptop and on the deployment and both passed.\nThat is not a pair. The invariant this catalog publishes is stronger: the same\ninput produces the same consequential figures, checks, escalation reasons and\ncitation relationships in every profile, and what may differ is quality, scale\nand durability.\n\nThe old evidence recorded risk_rating_chars and source_of_wealth_chars, 275\nagainst 1613, and asserted len(sow) > 40. Character counts of the NARRATION are\nthe one quantity the invariant explicitly permits to differ, so the evidence\nmeasured the only thing allowed to move and asserted nothing about the four that\nmust not.\n\nmake e2e-pair compares the deterministic dossier captured from each target''s own\nPOST /v1/cdd -- the artifact the surface actually rendered, not a second request\n-- and exits non-zero on divergence. pairing.py is the specification: what it\ncompares is policy, and every exemption carries the reason it is a declared\nreduction. tests/test_pairing.py gates it offline and proves it can fail, one\ncase per class of divergence and one per tolerated reduction.\n\nIt is RED on its first live run, and that is the finding: 12 divergences over 18\ncompared fields. The deployment performed no sanctions or PEP screening at all\nwhile the laptop screened six lists, and neither surface said so. The same\nsubject and evidence produced a different verdict, band medium against low and\nscore 0.45 against 0.1, off entirely different scorecard factors. UBO resolution\nreturned an owner locally and none on the deployment. Every managed citation\ntitle decayed into its own document id, so a cited source reads as an opaque id\nrather than as the bank statement it is. The two profiles are not running the\nsame case, which two runs recorded side by side had been concealing.\n\nF4 is scored here as FAIL. Closing it is managed-profile work, not comparison\nwork; adding a field to the exemption list to reach green is the one thing that\nmust not happen.\n\nTwo defects the work surfaced on the way:\n\n- comparable() always returns its key set, so testing the dict for truthiness\n  passed two EMPTY dossiers as agreeing. all(()) in a different costume, in the\n  module written to refuse exactly that. It now tests the values that carry the\n  verdict. Its own test caught it.\n- e2e/README.md claimed e2e-local joins the repository gate. It does not, and\n  never did. That is the same class the catalog''s re-audit hunts: evidence cited\n  but not run. The claim now matches reality, and the offline pairing tests are\n  what actually gates.\n\nRegion: the defaults shipped asia-southeast1 against a stack running us-central1\nsince the portfolio decision was revised, so a default terraform plan failed its\nown residency validation -- looking like a working guard rather than a stale\ndefault, which is the more expensive kind of wrong. Terraform, the runtime\nallowlist and the dossier now follow the revision. A served OpenAPI description\nhardcoding a region it cannot read went with it. The four tests that pinned the\nold region are updated without weakening a guard: the unapproved-region test now\nuses europe-west1 and asserts it really is outside the allowlist.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f652b4615f94687fd4739b441bba4c8178261d19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/f652b4615f94687fd4739b441bba4c8178261d19"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/9a722f9ed34ce91c4449ae4c28ad5f6c07e103d2","verification":{"payload":"tree f652b4615f94687fd4739b441bba4c8178261d19\nparent 9d7f40daf080a296874ad4c20e15a0e107f69be9\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787663984 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787663984 +0800\n\nCompare the two profiles instead of running them twice, and score F4 (#36)\n\nThe demo ran the same journey on a laptop and on the deployment and both passed.\nThat is not a pair. The invariant this catalog publishes is stronger: the same\ninput produces the same consequential figures, checks, escalation reasons and\ncitation relationships in every profile, and what may differ is quality, scale\nand durability.\n\nThe old evidence recorded risk_rating_chars and source_of_wealth_chars, 275\nagainst 1613, and asserted len(sow) > 40. Character counts of the NARRATION are\nthe one quantity the invariant explicitly permits to differ, so the evidence\nmeasured the only thing allowed to move and asserted nothing about the four that\nmust not.\n\nmake e2e-pair compares the deterministic dossier captured from each target''s own\nPOST /v1/cdd -- the artifact the surface actually rendered, not a second request\n-- and exits non-zero on divergence. pairing.py is the specification: what it\ncompares is policy, and every exemption carries the reason it is a declared\nreduction. tests/test_pairing.py gates it offline and proves it can fail, one\ncase per class of divergence and one per tolerated reduction.\n\nIt is RED on its first live run, and that is the finding: 12 divergences over 18\ncompared fields. The deployment performed no sanctions or PEP screening at all\nwhile the laptop screened six lists, and neither surface said so. The same\nsubject and evidence produced a different verdict, band medium against low and\nscore 0.45 against 0.1, off entirely different scorecard factors. UBO resolution\nreturned an owner locally and none on the deployment. Every managed citation\ntitle decayed into its own document id, so a cited source reads as an opaque id\nrather than as the bank statement it is. The two profiles are not running the\nsame case, which two runs recorded side by side had been concealing.\n\nF4 is scored here as FAIL. Closing it is managed-profile work, not comparison\nwork; adding a field to the exemption list to reach green is the one thing that\nmust not happen.\n\nTwo defects the work surfaced on the way:\n\n- comparable() always returns its key set, so testing the dict for truthiness\n  passed two EMPTY dossiers as agreeing. all(()) in a different costume, in the\n  module written to refuse exactly that. It now tests the values that carry the\n  verdict. Its own test caught it.\n- e2e/README.md claimed e2e-local joins the repository gate. It does not, and\n  never did. That is the same class the catalog''s re-audit hunts: evidence cited\n  but not run. The claim now matches reality, and the offline pairing tests are\n  what actually gates.\n\nRegion: the defaults shipped asia-southeast1 against a stack running us-central1\nsince the portfolio decision was revised, so a default terraform plan failed its\nown residency validation -- looking like a working guard rather than a stale\ndefault, which is the more expensive kind of wrong. Terraform, the runtime\nallowlist and the dossier now follow the revision. A served OpenAPI description\nhardcoding a region it cannot read went with it. The four tests that pinned the\nold region are updated without weakening a guard: the unapproved-region test now\nuses europe-west1 and asserts it really is outside the allowlist.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjZZwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8y4QAGjQLlR5FIUHuv96MHnEuRSw\nxm/e0WaBtjtpDiloR7sbXoFwX7US6ejGZt87Wi4dfPNi3kNnpz+akjk+4jcrxNQ9\nt/8wBX59jMJV53vJ99uq/vdk44c+dQs5Xbawj/hGSpolEt72WR7qS8dHmZtfzDDh\nt6bMd+RQZqDRQZ/t1cSwCwFe5OFos6qY1+QRu6Uqe1IM+a+lPcF+1KPqKZkctOzv\n3jjB0jmKdXawXZXZ7vTDv7HRJIMzay+sEIFixSJkx6StXdacS/M+8p5127jcFjXS\nONiByttmS1TioiXxRUAK4bX1/55S23vfsYhavdFSjPxGlYTbLvuoSDVhyAxfcCG8\ndRAn1508+EJfs7SpNhWenA03udWJarsvL4dXckHdlyCD0jF7wSRlxG7uOqc9MvEP\nVpN5GNA7Fqig7/ro7WAmVENEc2pcPGDpA16csUMQxWU1oeD4PpnOjW62lvK5RU1Q\nl/T+kdZZuUTAeumoUL3j/Ii3JP226+2e3LO0QImdj7CWpV+duX+s62yXah9UGkfQ\n5e8F6gv+uHROknonZi467dv3JY2s4JKmpXoQSwdyUUoO1NOINddWEskLz/fUPdOk\nH5k+0um63F45uBoDNjUh8onKyyb1H3ug6MApDFPGBmN1tdb5KRY7MBbNyNB2hABh\noa+98nk803Ze66c3Ac+T\n=SL/K\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T13:19:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/9a722f9ed34ce91c4449ae4c28ad5f6c07e103d2","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDlhNzIyZjllZDM0Y2U5MWM0NDQ5YWU0YzI4YWQ1ZjZjMDdlMTAzZDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/9d7f40daf080a296874ad4c20e15a0e107f69be9","sha":"9d7f40daf080a296874ad4c20e15a0e107f69be9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/9d7f40daf080a296874ad4c20e15a0e107f69be9"}],"sha":"9a722f9ed34ce91c4449ae4c28ad5f6c07e103d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/9a722f9ed34ce91c4449ae4c28ad5f6c07e103d2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/9d7f40daf080a296874ad4c20e15a0e107f69be9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T07:56:15Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T07:56:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Managed-profile fixes and the guards that catch them (3 commits) (#35)\n\n* Make the deployed portal serve: hop-scoped credentials, tenant mapping, same-origin CORS, e2e\n\nThe managed portal answered 503 on every route and, once that cleared, 401 on every\nembedded request. Four defects, all invisible offline, plus the browser demo that would\nhave caught them.\n\n- x-serverless-authorization is INJECTED by the serverless frontend and holds a token for\n  THIS service. Forwarded verbatim it reaches the next Cloud Run service, whose frontend\n  prefers it over authorization and refuses it, because its audience names the previous\n  hop. Now hop-by-hop, with the decoded IAP identity headers stripped alongside.\n\n- The assertion is injected under x-portal-iap-assertion as well, because x-goog-* is a\n  reserved namespace the frontend removes: the portal was injecting a header the platform\n  then dropped, and the embedded app reported \"did not pass through IAP\" about a request\n  that had.\n\n- tenant came off the hd claim while the embed registry declared a tenant LABEL. Two\n  strings that can never match, so the host/tenant check denied every request.\n  tenant_by_identity_domain relates them, and Terraform validates that every mapped tenant\n  has a reviewed embed policy.\n\n- A same-origin request that carries Origin was judged a cross-origin caller and denied.\n  Browsers send Origin on crossorigin script fetches, so the embedded console''s own chunks\n  came back 403 as JSON, the browser refused to execute them, and it never hydrated.\n\nEvery fail-closed refusal now says WHY in the log while the response stays uniform: the\naudit sink, the identity resolver, and the upstream proxy each had none, which is why a\ndeployed service that was refusing everything looked healthy.\n\nDeployment inputs are reviewed inputs: cloud_run_deletion_protection and the identity\ndomain list were hand-edited into a generated file that render overwrites. Embedded\nservices are now told their own project and region, and their runtime identities get the\nobservability roles any service needs to run.\n\ne2e/ drives the RM journey in a real browser against BOTH targets from one script, with\nprogrammatic IAP access so no password is ever typed. It passes end to end locally:\njourney, verified identity, same-origin embedding, a real dossier with a risk rating and\nsource-of-wealth narrative, and no console errors.\n\n* Let the proxy wait as long as the embedded app actually takes\n\nThe BFF''s default upstream timeout is tuned for an API call, and an embedded app doing real\nwork is not one: a CDD dossier reads documents, retrieves grounded passages and makes\nseveral model calls, and took 76 seconds on the deployment. The proxy gave up first, so the\nbrowser was shown a 500 for a request the app went on to answer 200 -- the worst shape of\nfailure, because both halves look correct from their own logs and only a third observer\nsees the disagreement.\n\nThe application already documented the knob (\"raise the configured upstream-timeout env for\nthat\"); the deployment simply had no way to express it, so the managed portal ran on a\ndefault nobody chose. Now a reviewed input, validated to stay strictly below the Cloud Run\nrequest timeout: a proxy timeout longer than the platform''s own is a timeout that never\nfires, and the caller gets the platform''s opaque termination instead of the proxy''s error.\n\n* Assert the case HAS its evidence, rather than that this run uploaded it\n\nThe case is deliberately stable across runs: an analyst returns to a case, and on the\nmanaged target the retrieval index only holds what has already been ingested. Uploading\nunconditionally therefore piled a fresh copy of the same document into the case on every\nrun, which is demo litter rather than a property worth asserting.\n\nThe assertion is now that the evidence is present, uploading it only when it is not.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"7e48e3a8e79d3c505d408ca45d6b3c215ea12d7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/7e48e3a8e79d3c505d408ca45d6b3c215ea12d7f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/9d7f40daf080a296874ad4c20e15a0e107f69be9","verification":{"payload":"tree 7e48e3a8e79d3c505d408ca45d6b3c215ea12d7f\nparent ea83fc3457635a70091022af4953a1a22742f6bb\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787644575 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787644575 +0800\n\nManaged-profile fixes and the guards that catch them (3 commits) (#35)\n\n* Make the deployed portal serve: hop-scoped credentials, tenant mapping, same-origin CORS, e2e\n\nThe managed portal answered 503 on every route and, once that cleared, 401 on every\nembedded request. Four defects, all invisible offline, plus the browser demo that would\nhave caught them.\n\n- x-serverless-authorization is INJECTED by the serverless frontend and holds a token for\n  THIS service. Forwarded verbatim it reaches the next Cloud Run service, whose frontend\n  prefers it over authorization and refuses it, because its audience names the previous\n  hop. Now hop-by-hop, with the decoded IAP identity headers stripped alongside.\n\n- The assertion is injected under x-portal-iap-assertion as well, because x-goog-* is a\n  reserved namespace the frontend removes: the portal was injecting a header the platform\n  then dropped, and the embedded app reported \"did not pass through IAP\" about a request\n  that had.\n\n- tenant came off the hd claim while the embed registry declared a tenant LABEL. Two\n  strings that can never match, so the host/tenant check denied every request.\n  tenant_by_identity_domain relates them, and Terraform validates that every mapped tenant\n  has a reviewed embed policy.\n\n- A same-origin request that carries Origin was judged a cross-origin caller and denied.\n  Browsers send Origin on crossorigin script fetches, so the embedded console''s own chunks\n  came back 403 as JSON, the browser refused to execute them, and it never hydrated.\n\nEvery fail-closed refusal now says WHY in the log while the response stays uniform: the\naudit sink, the identity resolver, and the upstream proxy each had none, which is why a\ndeployed service that was refusing everything looked healthy.\n\nDeployment inputs are reviewed inputs: cloud_run_deletion_protection and the identity\ndomain list were hand-edited into a generated file that render overwrites. Embedded\nservices are now told their own project and region, and their runtime identities get the\nobservability roles any service needs to run.\n\ne2e/ drives the RM journey in a real browser against BOTH targets from one script, with\nprogrammatic IAP access so no password is ever typed. It passes end to end locally:\njourney, verified identity, same-origin embedding, a real dossier with a risk rating and\nsource-of-wealth narrative, and no console errors.\n\n* Let the proxy wait as long as the embedded app actually takes\n\nThe BFF''s default upstream timeout is tuned for an API call, and an embedded app doing real\nwork is not one: a CDD dossier reads documents, retrieves grounded passages and makes\nseveral model calls, and took 76 seconds on the deployment. The proxy gave up first, so the\nbrowser was shown a 500 for a request the app went on to answer 200 -- the worst shape of\nfailure, because both halves look correct from their own logs and only a third observer\nsees the disagreement.\n\nThe application already documented the knob (\"raise the configured upstream-timeout env for\nthat\"); the deployment simply had no way to express it, so the managed portal ran on a\ndefault nobody chose. Now a reviewed input, validated to stay strictly below the Cloud Run\nrequest timeout: a proxy timeout longer than the platform''s own is a timeout that never\nfires, and the caller gets the platform''s opaque termination instead of the proxy''s error.\n\n* Assert the case HAS its evidence, rather than that this run uploaded it\n\nThe case is deliberately stable across runs: an analyst returns to a case, and on the\nmanaged target the retrieval index only holds what has already been ingested. Uploading\nunconditionally therefore piled a fresh copy of the same document into the case on every\nrun, which is demo litter rather than a property worth asserting.\n\nThe assertion is now that the evidence is present, uploading it only when it is not.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjUqfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUR4QABvw9JHwkQ+6YYLqj0LJpgSQ\nxM6Wp16ka7VEB7gugO6JfZjaKTdJp6TWBWfffwixwrocuhqabmL7oNqA5t3aAMOT\n+nYgayklH0w7sEi0iHviUW3OrUcxVrQ/N4avu+fEuE2d7MjNHtgQiZPSKlKo8/7s\nQyhTCTtoiCT6f9Qsd+d1g/BVPZl4pLsiZz3SREdxJ8ZTLpBiklBbeqj6WqIoPrLZ\nEP0b5QWUTupvA7zFwcNystc8kULcntwneYAQvEUqsdUo+Yu8C3eN97fTbLE93Nj2\nduc1HifrAoXKzACoX3l56kSpzEywS7/prRikPdtQ1V+QWE0csQH50M1AJSaic9iv\n+7/YNONfKiGJe4pTqj2Vbxqf3/VtAT7kekBWqu9APEtFZFzwsdBaObp/KvxBhEKZ\nXbzzhSql+SNioIQceVnXclVYDxP+bsA/7ey9dEtQk9UlROYihCJXHo3ROGm2twKQ\nkLb7+SZNMFVnu/3DdeU5i92CUGy0j6dXZQm0tN/K17Y7XLUdTOYIc38LErP9o8pM\nT/5usuApSaR2p+0ew7q9BRbJqG6ocSE3RAvp69aJ/NBiJfjtKlwc9ZO1KYUEXzc3\namj4e3FSjqWG90eHZbEwhywr2Kp9oW3+QBPfdqROO8ByqMsK7ydiajHpBk/4PWvQ\n5DjGGQqsz6FoO4vjRE4b\n=KiH6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T07:56:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/9d7f40daf080a296874ad4c20e15a0e107f69be9","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9WNoAKDlkN2Y0MGRhZjA4MGEyOTY4NzRhZDRjMjBlMTVhMGUxMDdmNjliZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/journey-portal/commit/ea83fc3457635a70091022af4953a1a22742f6bb","sha":"ea83fc3457635a70091022af4953a1a22742f6bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/ea83fc3457635a70091022af4953a1a22742f6bb"}],"sha":"9d7f40daf080a296874ad4c20e15a0e107f69be9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/9d7f40daf080a296874ad4c20e15a0e107f69be9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/commits/ea83fc3457635a70091022af4953a1a22742f6bb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T16:14:49Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T16:24:58Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Deploy a subset of journeys, and fix the eight defects that blocked the first apply\n\nHrz9 had never been applied. Applying it into portable-genai-prod on 2026-08-24\nfound eight defects, and two of the shells could not be BUILT at all.\n\nThe RM shell pinned react 19.2.7 against react-dom 19.2.8, whose peer requires\n^19.2.8, so `npm ci` failed and the image could not be produced. The Ops shell\nhad @angular/compiler at 22.1.2 against @angular/compiler-cli at 22.1.0, which\npins its peer to an exact version; Angular framework packages move as a set, so\nthey are aligned on the highest already present. Neither was reachable from any\ntest: nothing in the suite builds these images.\n\nThe portal could not deploy a subset of journeys. embedded_apps required exactly\nseven, in the Python validator AND in two Terraform validations, which coupled\nseven independently-released repositories into one atomic deployment and made a\nsingle-journey installation inexpressible -- the opposite of the incremental\nadoption this architecture argues for. Five of those seven repositories ship no\nUI Dockerfile at all, so the rule could not be satisfied by anyone. The safety\nproperties are kept exactly: non-empty, known ids only, digest-pinned images,\ncanonical mount path, and a rollback map that covers what is actually being\ndeployed rather than a constant.\n\nThe runtime was coupled the same way. journeys.yaml is the CATALOGUE of what the\nportal can serve, so a deployment that mounted one app still loaded all seven and\nrefused to start on the six carrying ${VAR:-http://127.0.0.1:...} defaults --\ncorrectly, since a managed profile must not proxy plaintext. PORTAL_APPS now\nnames what this installation mounts. Silently dropping unconfigured apps would\nhave been worse: a genuinely misconfigured upstream would vanish instead of\nbeing reported, so anything named must exist in the config, and a journey whose\nevery app belongs to another installation is dropped rather than shown as an\nempty dead end.\n\nRegion was hardcoded to exactly asia-southeast1 in the deployment validator and\nto a fixed APAC set at runtime, making the portal the one component that could\nnot follow a portfolio region decision without a code change -- and it did not\nmatch the region the launch set settled on. Both are deploy-time inputs now, and\nTerraform passes its allowlist to the runtime so the two cannot disagree, which\nis precisely how the first startup failed.\n\nFour smaller ones, each fatal on its own. A TCP liveness probe, which Cloud Run\nrejects outright. The IAP service agent spelled out rather than asked for, so it\ndid not exist. The logging CMEK member missing its serviceAccount: prefix. And a\nbucketWriter grant to an empty string: a sink routing to a bucket in its own\nproject is given no writer identity, so the grant could never apply and cannot\nbe made conditional either.\n\nTwo shared-project findings worth keeping. A project may belong to exactly one\nregular VPC-SC perimeter, so co-located stacks name which one owns it rather\nthan each asserting its own. And PORTAL_IAP_AUDIENCE was set unconditionally,\nbut set-but-empty is a REJECTED input by design -- so the documented two-pass\nbootstrap, where the audience does not exist until the first apply creates the\nbackend service, could never complete its first pass.\n\n603 tests pass. All seven Cloud Run services are live and healthy.","tree":{"sha":"9ea98fef3e1415a85d2864d10d56dde9eeb41168","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/trees/9ea98fef3e1415a85d2864d10d56dde9eeb41168"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/journey-portal/git/commits/ea83fc3457635a70091022af4953a1a22742f6bb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https:/