"type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/53cb14e73a555849eb74f9b6f168a023c0c9f83d","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDUzY2IxNGU3M2E1NTU4NDllYjc0ZjliNmYxNjhhMDIzYzBjOWY4M2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/e8c84f151fe7ada3e83b14f92dc03454ef5c7a59","sha":"e8c84f151fe7ada3e83b14f92dc03454ef5c7a59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/e8c84f151fe7ada3e83b14f92dc03454ef5c7a59"}],"sha":"53cb14e73a555849eb74f9b6f168a023c0c9f83d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/53cb14e73a555849eb74f9b6f168a023c0c9f83d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/e8c84f151fe7ada3e83b14f92dc03454ef5c7a59/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T15:14:59Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T15:43:00Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Screen the asset title with the body on INPUT\n\nReviewService.review and SubstantiationService.assess both INPUT-screened\n`asset.body or asset.title`, so any asset with a non-empty body left its\ntitle unscreened. Both narration prompts quote `''{asset.title}''` to the\nmodel verbatim (services.py _narrate, substantiation.py _narrate), so a\ncaller-supplied title reached the model without passing the guardrail.\n\nBoth services now render title and body into one string with a static\n_request_text helper and pass it to the existing _guard, which audits\nBLOCKED and raises GuardrailBlockedError on a block.\n\ntests/unit/test_screening_covers_model_text.py drives both services through\nthe local container with an asset whose body is non-empty:\n- test_review_input_screen_sees_the_title and\n  test_substantiation_input_screen_sees_the_title wrap the bound guardrail\n  in a spy and assert the title and the body are in the INPUT-screened text.\n- test_injection_in_the_review_title_is_blocked and\n  test_injection_in_the_substantiation_title_is_blocked put \"ignore all\n  previous instructions\" in the title and assert GuardrailBlockedError.\n\nFalsified: with src stashed back to origin/main all four fail (the screened\ntext was the body alone, and DID NOT RAISE GuardrailBlockedError); with the\nfix all four pass. make gate passes.","tree":{"sha":"ef81551ad447225c22e30a081cc81ce745764857","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/ef81551ad447225c22e30a081cc81ce745764857"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/e8c84f151fe7ada3e83b14f92dc03454ef5c7a59","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.github