80a6a78a71d7ccd428f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/e2eb652002da0cda3f1434d2f50563cdd6dbdcf1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T14:33:48Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T14:53:10Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump next to 16.3.8: critical RCE in next/og (GHSA-vcvr-r3jv-pc5j)\n\nnext 16.2.0 to 16.3.5 carries a critical remote code execution in\nnext/og ImageResponse, and the gate''s npm audit (--audit-level=high) now\nfails every pull request on it. The pin moves to 16.3.8, the first release\npast the advisory''s range on this line, and `npm audit fix` takes\nbaseline-browser-mapping past GHSA-w5vr-8v7q-w6rv (moderate). Lock-only\nchange; npm audit reports no vulnerabilities.","tree":{"sha":"4c849ee3ab09becee9c62c86a54574c5d293ab11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/4c849ee3ab09becee9c62c86a54574c5d293ab11"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/e2eb652002da0cda3f1434d2f50563cdd6dbdcf1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/e2eb652002da0cda3f1434d2f50563cdd6dbdcf1","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKGUyZWI2NTIwMDJkYTBjZGEzZjE0MzRkMmY1MDU2M2NkZDZkYmRjZjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/b1ca03b63da9e9c9c4f7e78b9e5b86f1e9528442","sha":"b1ca03b63da9e9c9c4f7e78b9e5b86f1e9528442","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/b1ca03b63da9e9c9c4f7e78b9e5b86f1e9528442"}],"sha":"e2eb652002da0cda3f1434d2f50563cdd6dbdcf1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/e2eb652002da0cda3f1434d2f50563cdd6dbdcf1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/b1ca03b63da9e9c9c4f7e78b9e5b86f1e9528442/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:21:28Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:25:35Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Fail the Model Armor verdict closed: allow only NO_MATCH_FOUND with SUCCESS\n\nThe REST verdict mapping was `allowed = state != \"MATCH_FOUND\"`, falling back to\n\"no per-filter findings\" when the state was absent. That allowed\nFILTER_MATCH_STATE_UNSPECIFIED, an empty or missing sanitizationResult, and any\nPARTIAL or FAILURE screen, which arrives WITH NO_MATCH_FOUND because a skipped\nfilter reports no match: a prompt padded past the prompt-injection filter''s\ntoken limit went through unscreened. invocationResult was never read.\n\nThe verdict is now allowed only when filterMatchState is the literal string\nNO_MATCH_FOUND and invocationResult is the literal string SUCCESS; anything\nelse, including a non-object body or numeric enums, blocks with a finding that\nsays why. The 30s deadline and HTTP error propagation are unchanged.\n\ntests/unit/test_model_armor_verdict_mapping.py drives screen() through a fake\nHTTP client at two levels: an SDK-free half on mirror enums (runs in the\noffline gate) and a real-SDK half that serializes real modelarmor_v1 messages\nto the REST wire JSON with the SDK''s own to_json and pins the mirror enums to\nthe real ones (skips where google-cloud-modelarmor is absent). Against the old\nmapping 34 of the 55 cases fail.","tree":{"sha":"9e1dfb5466b7ea8dfe6ae93a254326a824234792","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/9e1dfb5466b7ea8dfe6ae93a254326a824234792"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/b1ca03b63da9e9c9c4f7e78b9e5b86f1e9528442","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/b1ca03b63da9e9c9c4f7e78b9e5b86f1e9528442","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKGIxY2EwM2I2M2RhOWU5YzljNGY3ZTc4YjllNWI4NmYxZTk1Mjg0NDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/b1dfa54e3f1d84b73f97f2e5358e7ddf9f852c07","sha":"b1dfa54e3f1d84b73f97f2e5358e7ddf9f852c07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/b1dfa54e3f1d84b73f97f2e5358e7ddf9f852c07"}],"sha":"b1ca03b63da9e9c9c4f7e78b9e5b86f1e9528442","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/b1ca03b63da9e9c9c4f7e78b9e5b86f1e9528442"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/b1dfa54e3f1d84b73f97f2e5358e7ddf9f852c07/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T10:20:10Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T10:38:42Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Name the collector to the standalone service, and refuse one without it\n\nWith the Cloud Trace tracer retired, a standalone service under MKT_GOV_PROFILE=gcp refuses\nits first traced request unless OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT names the agent-observability\ncollector. otlp_endpoint sets it and OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_AUDIENCE, and is required with\nstandalone_service_enabled, so the omission is refused at plan. The standalone service is\noff in the reference deployment; the portal-embedded API gets both variables from\njourney-portal.","tree":{"sha":"3e701188258d0951c20de53aa7f18105cd79229e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/3e701188258d0951c20de53aa7f18105cd79229e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/b1dfa54e3f1d84b73f97f2e5358e7ddf9f852c07","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/b1dfa54e3f1d84b73f97f2e5358e7ddf9f852c07","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKGIxZGZhNTRlM2YxZDg0YjczZjk3ZjJlNTM1OGU3ZGRmOWY4NTJjMDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/ec7fb534961bdc2fb5c014175adc3c2af40f2338","sha":"ec7fb534961bdc2fb5c014175adc3c2af40f2338","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/ec7fb534961bdc2fb5c014175adc3c2af40f2338"}],"sha":"b1dfa54e3f1d84b73f97f2e5358e7ddf9f852c07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/b1dfa54e3f1d84b73f97f2e5358e7ddf9f852c07"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/ec7fb534961bdc2fb5c014175adc3c2af40f2338/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T10:16:07Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T10:38:42Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Trace only through the collector: retire the Cloud Trace tracer onto build_tracer\n\nPlan phase P4, decision D1. The gcp and platform profiles bound a hand-written tracer that\nexported straight to Cloud Trace, around the agent-observability collector that deletes GenAI\ncontent attributes, and fell back to OTel metrics or a Cloud Logging FinOps log for token\nusage. They now bind CloudTracerAdapter, the template''s thin adapter over\nhex_service_kit.tracing.build_tracer, which exports OTLP to OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT only,\nrecords token usage as gen_ai.* span attributes, and refuses the first span when the endpoint\nis unset. journey-portal injects the endpoint into every embedded API; spans carry\nservice.name marketing-compliance-gate.\n\n- hex-service-kit v0.0.10 -> v0.0.11 (build_tracer(service=...), no direct path).\n- The gcp extra drops opentelemetry-exporter-gcp-trace and names the tracer''s OTLP\n  dependencies directly: the kit''s otel extra floors opentelemetry-sdk at 1.44, above the\n  <=1.42.1 ceiling google-adk declares, so naming the extra is unresolvable.\n- Relocked with scripts/lock.py (no --upgrade): only the kit pin moves, and the Cloud Trace\n  exporter and google-cloud-trace leave the gcp lock.\n- SPEC names the new path; a test holds the binding and the refusal.\n\nDeploy order: the portal apply that injects the endpoint, and the collector''s invoker grant,\nland before an image built from this commit. Neither is applied yet.","tree":{"sha":"321fbc77fd812d9a75800b2fac4d7e27db87a225","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/321fbc77fd812d9a75800b2fac4d7e27db87a225"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/ec7fb534961bdc2fb5c014175adc3c2af40f2338","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/ec7fb534961bdc2fb5c014175adc3c2af40f2338","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKGVjN2ZiNTM0OTYxYmRjMmZiNWMwMTQxNzVhZGMzYzJhZjQwZjIzMzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/05ccc06ab7f2b60565f712f342086b0b521b5953","sha":"05ccc06ab7f2b60565f712f342086b0b521b5953","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/05ccc06ab7f2b60565f712f342086b0b521b5953"}],"sha":"ec7fb534961bdc2fb5c014175adc3c2af40f2338","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/ec7fb534961bdc2fb5c014175adc3c2af40f2338"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/05ccc06ab7f2b60565f712f342086b0b521b5953/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T22:20:16Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T22:34:33Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Sync the canonical skills: model pills and the live profile","tree":{"sha":"280ad1b8fb9893c881f798598b04c5b324b536af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/280ad1b8fb9893c881f798598b04c5b324b536af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/05ccc06ab7f2b60565f712f342086b0b521b5953","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/05ccc06ab7f2b60565f712f342086b0b521b5953","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDA1Y2NjMDZhYjdmMmI2MDU2NWY3MTJmMzQyMDg2YjBiNTIxYjU5NTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/be34e1d430fea8180d3976506c63ebf8d6aa9f44","sha":"be34e1d430fea8180d3976506c63ebf8d6aa9f44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/be34e1d430fea8180d3976506c63ebf8d6aa9f44"}],"sha":"05ccc06ab7f2b60565f712f342086b0b521b5953","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/05ccc06ab7f2b60565f712f342086b0b521b5953"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/be34e1d430fea8180d3976506c63ebf8d6aa9f44/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T22:08:14Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T22:16:13Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Answer pills: name the model that answered, drop the provenance banner\n\n- Bump hex-service-kit to v0.0.10 (only the kit pin moved in the three locks).\n- install_answer_provenance(app) emits X-Answered-By / X-Search-Used; the CORS\n  middleware exposes both, since the console calls the service cross-origin.\n- Gemini adapter notes the model it called (generate and classify); the offline\n  stub notes deterministic-offline-stub; the live kit client notes itself. No\n  call attaches an online search tool, so nothing notes a search.\n- LlmRequest.temperature is optional (None = not sent). Review summary and\n  green-claim narrative are free; classify stays pinned at 0.0; the ADK agent\n  no longer pins 0.2.\n- Delete use_hard_reasoning and the unused hard_reasoning model;\n  generator_model is models.reasoning, the model the adapter calls.\n- UI: ModelPills replaces ProvenanceBanner (fixed top right, light-only), one\n  window.fetch wrapper reads both headers off API_BASE responses.","tree":{"sha":"14bc78b969889a0f97ee6bef54b4ff6108e31390","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/14bc78b969889a0f97ee6bef54b4ff6108e31390"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/be34e1d430fea8180d3976506c63ebf8d6aa9f44","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/be34e1d430fea8180d3976506c63ebf8d6aa9f44","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKGJlMzRlMWQ0MzBmZWE4MTgwZDM5NzY1MDZjNjNlYmY4ZDZhYTlmNDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/c6707e78d0e1c596e229a929836670a5a9e5f858","sha":"c6707e78d0e1c596e229a929836670a5a9e5f858","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/c6707e78d0e1c596e229a929836670a5a9e5f858"}],"sha":"be34e1d430fea8180d3976506c63ebf8d6aa9f44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/be34e1d430fea8180d3976506c63ebf8d6aa9f44"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/c6707e78d0e1c596e229a929836670a5a9e5f858/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T13:38:34Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T13:42:28Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Add the live laptop profile: the llm port on the shared local model\n\nMKT_GOV_PROFILE=live binds every port to the same offline adapter local\ndoes, except llm, which now calls the fleet''s one local open-weight\nmodel through hex_service_kit.localmodel (kit v0.0.9). The narration\nschema goes in the prompt, the answer is validated and retried, and the\nresponse records the model id that answered.\n\nlive keeps the laptop posture: seeded personas, localhost CORS origins,\nthe loopback exposure guard, in-process stores and human-readable logs.\nThe banner names the local model. Narration stays best-effort as it is\nfor Gemini: a down server or an answer that never validates raises a\nnamed domain error, the services keep the deterministic fallback\nnarrative, and the findings and verdicts are unchanged. local stays the\nprofile tests, CI and make demo use.","tree":{"sha":"d7bfde725d1d552e90dae5b3002bec542985297d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/d7bfde725d1d552e90dae5b3002bec542985297d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/c6707e78d0e1c596e229a929836670a5a9e5f858","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/c6707e78d0e1c596e229a929836670a5a9e5f858","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKGM2NzA3ZTc4ZDBlMWM1OTZlMjI5YTkyOTgzNjY3MGE1YTllNWY4NTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/8123f0d5c599a111c5fffe2bc4166a9393ad1cc2","sha":"8123f0d5c599a111c5fffe2bc4166a9393ad1cc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/8123f0d5c599a111c5fffe2bc4166a9393ad1cc2"}],"sha":"c6707e78d0e1c596e229a929836670a5a9e5f858","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/c6707e78d0e1c596e229a929836670a5a9e5f858"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/8123f0d5c599a111c5fffe2bc4166a9393ad1cc2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T03:35:15Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T03:39:21Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Mint the console bearer for the portal''s IAP edge\n\nThe deployed human-review-console is an embedded app behind journey-portal''s\nIAP edge, which accepts only a Google-signed ID token minted for the IAP OAuth\nclient id. The static S2S_TOKEN bearer cannot pass that edge, so under gcp\nevery review, assessment and consent-grant hand-off would be refused.\n\nBump review-kit to v0.0.2 for its per-submission bearer_provider. The managed\nreview router reads HUMAN_REVIEW_IAP_AUDIENCE in three states and, when set,\nmints a fresh ID token per submission through a new lazy-import helper in\n_s2s; unset keeps the static token. Under gcp, routing on now refuses at boot\nunless both HUMAN_REVIEW_URL and HUMAN_REVIEW_IAP_AUDIENCE are named, and a\nbackend-service path pasted as the audience is refused by name.\n\nThe standalone Cloud Run service sets HUMAN_REVIEW_URL from Terraform, so it\ngains human_review_iap_audience, validated as an OAuth client id while routing\nis on, or its next gcp revision would refuse to boot.","tree":{"sha":"b7883f3db454ff00da18e1c59cc4b71f757ed33d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/b7883f3db454ff00da18e1c59cc4b71f757ed33d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/8123f0d5c599a111c5fffe2bc4166a9393ad1cc2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/8123f0d5c599a111c5fffe2bc4166a9393ad1cc2","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDgxMjNmMGQ1YzU5OWExMTFjNWZmZmUyYmM0MTY2YTkzOTNhZDFjYzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/b3575a50e76690d1d28f2b0163e678ee08e01d69","sha":"b3575a50e76690d1d28f2b0163e678ee08e01d69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/b3575a50e76690d1d28f2b0163e678ee08e01d69"}],"sha":"8123f0d5c599a111c5fffe2bc4166a9393ad1cc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/8123f0d5c599a111c5fffe2bc4166a9393ad1cc2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/b3575a50e76690d1d28f2b0163e678ee08e01d69/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T10:20:16Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T10:24:09Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Switch the guardrail and review routing, and report every hand-off\n\nmarketing-compliance-gate joins the fleet''s runtime-control contract for the two cheap\ncontrols it has: the guardrail and review routing. It has no PII-redaction port, so it gets\nno redaction switch.\n\n- MKT_GOV_GUARDRAIL and MKT_GOV_REVIEW_ROUTING are read once at settings load in three\n  states: unset is on, a boolean wins, emptied or unrecognised refuses at boot. Off binds a\n  disabled adapter from adapters/controls.py and logs one warning per process.\n- Under gcp or platform, routing on with no HUMAN_REVIEW_URL refuses at boot. Before, the\n  platform router discovered the missing console on each hand-off and the domain swallowed\n  the error, so every escalation was silently dropped. A Model Armor guardrail with an\n  empty template also refuses at boot.\n- /v1/review, /v1/substantiation and /v1/consent/records, the review agent tool, the CLI\n  review and substantiate commands and the MCP review tool hand off through\n  RecordingReviewRouter. Each result carries review_routing (routed, failed, off,\n  not_required), and a failure is logged by exception type. The console says it in plain\n  words.\n- Terraform gains guardrail_enabled, review_routing_enabled and human_review_url on the\n  standalone service, validated so routing on needs an https console; two plan tests hold\n  that.\n- The runbook documents the switches and the boot refusal, and SPEC no longer calls the\n  hand-off merely best effort.","tree":{"sha":"2ad24b4e137e162ca3a7bbb0502e5df1fc7596f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/2ad24b4e137e162ca3a7bbb0502e5df1fc7596f8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/b3575a50e76690d1d28f2b0163e678ee08e01d69","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/b3575a50e76690d1d28f2b0163e678ee08e01d69","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKGIzNTc1YTUwZTc2NjkwZDFkMjhmMmIwMTYzZTY3OGVlMDhlMDFkNjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/26e9735a611c90d11b83369bee7ce223231a5c00","sha":"26e9735a611c90d11b83369bee7ce223231a5c00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/26e9735a611c90d11b83369bee7ce223231a5c00"}],"sha":"b3575a50e76690d1d28f2b0163e678ee08e01d69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/b3575a50e76690d1d28f2b0163e678ee08e01d69"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/26e9735a611c90d11b83369bee7ce223231a5c00/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T15:00:52Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T15:07:20Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Run the real IAP verifier against a negative matrix, on both headers\n\nThis service is embedded behind the journey portal''s IAP edge, so it is one\nof the few that receives a forwarded assertion in production, and nothing\nhere proved that google-auth actually refuses a bad one: the transport suite\nstubs _verify and the refusal-split suite blocks the google-auth import.\n\ntests/unit/test_iap_crypto_matrix.py mints a P-256 key, signs ES256\nassertions as IAP does, serves the key set in IAP''s {kid: PEM} shape from an\nin-process transport that asserts IAP''s URL, and runs the real verify_token\nthrough the adapter exactly as the gcp profile builds it. 74 cells, every\nrefusal under both x-goog-iap-jwt-assertion and x-portal-iap-assertion:\nwrong and absent audience, expired, not yet valid, no exp or iat, three\nimpostor keys and a tampered payload, malformed tokens, alg none, the HS256\nconfusion, wrong and absent issuer, no email or sub, blank headers, the\nprecedence between the two names, and an unconfigured or emptied audience.\n\nMachine callers: a service account mapped by exact address in\nMKT_GOV_IAP_MACHINE_TENANTS_JSON resolves to its tenant. An unmapped one in\nthe same project authenticates with no tenant, which fails closed at every\ntenant-scoped read (refuse_unmapped_tenant is left off). A domain-map entry\nfor the project''s domain tenants no machine, and a forged assertion for a\nmapped one is refused by the verifier.\n\n.env.example is new. The hosted runner reads its <PREFIX>_PROFILE= line to\nname the require-flag, and this repository never had the file, so the\nmatrix step would have died before running anything. The .gitignore and\n.dockerignore already exempt it by name. It documents only variables the\ncode reads: the profile, the project and the three IAP settings.\n\nProved red against broken copies of the adapter, one mutant each: audience=\ndropped (6 cells red), a wrong issuer accepted (4), the forwarded header\nskipping the verifier (18, every one of them host-forwarded), certs_url=\ndropped (49), the machine map ignored (2), the algorithm pin removed (12),\nan unconfigured audience verified anyway (6), and the emptied audience\nreported as unset (4).\n\nThe caller is re-rendered from portable-genai/org-metadata@3980637, which\ngives offline-gate iap_matrix_path and requirements-gcp.lock as its runtime\nlockfile, so this pull request''s own gate installs google-auth, sets\nMKT_GOV_REQUIRE_IAP_MATRIX=1 and fails if the matrix skips. Locally,\nCI-shaped on Python 3.14.6: 74 passed; make gate, ui-check, demo-selftest\nand portability all exit 0.","tree":{"sha":"79efef03c2c32842b917e1f2762678e4fe17833d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/79efef03c2c32842b917e1f2762678e4fe17833d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/26e9735a611c90d11b83369bee7ce223231a5c00","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/26e9735a611c90d11b83369bee7ce223231a5c00","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDI2ZTk3MzVhNjExYzkwZDExYjgzMzY5YmVlN2NlMjIzMjMxYTVjMDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/1b33859cea82bb9cf80bbc5ecabc7cf130ea8a05","sha":"1b33859cea82bb9cf80bbc5ecabc7cf130ea8a05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/1b33859cea82bb9cf80bbc5ecabc7cf130ea8a05"}],"sha":"26e9735a611c90d11b83369bee7ce223231a5c00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/26e9735a611c90d11b83369bee7ce223231a5c00"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/1b33859cea82bb9cf80bbc5ecabc7cf130ea8a05/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T14:40:10Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T14:46:59Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Run the Terraform test suite in CI\n\nThe offline-gate job now carries terraform_directory and terraform_test,\nre-rendered from the reviewed contract in portable-genai/org-metadata@9030354,\nso run-grc-ci runs fmt -check, init -backend=false, validate and test against\ninfra/terraform on every pull request and every push to main.\n\nThe suite proves this stack''s plan-level refusals with mock providers and no\ncredentials, and until now it ran only when somebody remembered\n`make tf-validate`: no job named it, so a pull request could break a refusal\nand merge green. Run locally before declaring it (terraform 1.15.6; the\nrunner has 1.16.0): fmt and validate green, 12 passed, 0 failed.\n\nThe security FAQ''s residual-risk list said there was no CI terraform fmt or\nvalidate job and that provider binaries were committed under\ninfra/terraform/.terraform/. The first half stops being true with this\nchange and the second was already untrue (only .terraform.lock.hcl is\ntracked), so the bullet is removed.","tree":{"sha":"8108790124525edd96ca1ff0928354a05b9a003b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/8108790124525edd96ca1ff0928354a05b9a003b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/1b33859cea82bb9cf80bbc5ecabc7cf130ea8a05","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/1b33859cea82bb9cf80bbc5ecabc7cf130ea8a05","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDFiMzM4NTljZWE4MmJiOWNmODBiYmM1ZWNhYmM3Y2YxMzBlYThhMDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/1d422d4666c4a8c7a417b5dfbad96a7c43b5f577","sha":"1d422d4666c4a8c7a417b5dfbad96a7c43b5f577","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/1d422d4666c4a8c7a417b5dfbad96a7c43b5f577"}],"sha":"1b33859cea82bb9cf80bbc5ecabc7cf130ea8a05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/1b33859cea82bb9cf80bbc5ecabc7cf130ea8a05"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/1d422d4666c4a8c7a417b5dfbad96a7c43b5f577/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T08:44:37Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T12:12:35Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Make customer-managed encryption optional, and off by default\n\nEvery binding to the stack''s Cloud KMS key now sits behind cmek_enabled,\ndefault false: the key ring, the key, every grant to a service agent, and\nevery store, log bucket, registry and revision that took the key. Block\nbindings became dynamic blocks; scalar bindings read the key through one(),\nwhich is null when the key does not exist and omits the attribute rather\nthan pointing it at nothing. The Terraform tests that assert on key material\nturn the gate on to keep meaning what they meant.\n\nWhy the default is off: a key ring can never be deleted, a log bucket that\nhas CMEK can never drop it, and registries and document stores take their\nkey at creation. None of that changes an answer or a screen, and everything\nis encrypted at rest with Google-managed keys regardless. A deployment with\na customer whose data it must shred, whose key access must be audited or\nwhose keys must live in an HSM sets it true in its own tfvars BEFORE the\nfirst apply. Where a stack already applied it, the key''s prevent_destroy\nrefuses a plan that omits the line, which is the right answer: the stores it\nbound stay bound.\n\nThe vendored deploy-and-residency-hardening skill says the same.","tree":{"sha":"c7a551ca410acbc9380e634e5f744910257dfc95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/c7a551ca410acbc9380e634e5f744910257dfc95"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/1d422d4666c4a8c7a417b5dfbad96a7c43b5f577","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/1d422d4666c4a8c7a417b5dfbad96a7c43b5f577","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDFkNDIyZDQ2NjZjNGE4YzdhNDE3YjVkZmJhZDk2YTdjNDNiNWY1Nzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/884ffc58d98214a0d90a563038c0a66e9535b254","sha":"884ffc58d98214a0d90a563038c0a66e9535b254","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/884ffc58d98214a0d90a563038c0a66e9535b254"}],"sha":"1d422d4666c4a8c7a417b5dfbad96a7c43b5f577","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/1d422d4666c4a8c7a417b5dfbad96a7c43b5f577"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/884ffc58d98214a0d90a563038c0a66e9535b254/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:20:47Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:23:55Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Prove the logging adoption in a subprocess, not in the suite''s own process\n\nThe first version of this guard re-imported the served module in-process under a chosen\nprofile. CI found two things wrong with that, neither of which shows up when the file runs\nalone. It left a differently-configured module in `sys.modules` for the rest of the session,\nso `test_standalone_flag.py` failed with `ImportError: module ... not in sys.modules`. And\nimporting under `gcp` installed that profile''s middleware, so suites that assert HSTS is\nabsent under `local` started seeing it.\n\nA subprocess is not a workaround for either. What ships is a fresh interpreter importing the\nserved module under a profile, which is exactly what this now runs, and it cannot leak into\nthe session because it is not the session. The formatter-output assertion builds the formatter\ndirectly, since what it is about is the shape this service''s errors take once it is installed.\n\nProved red against a mutated copy with the module-scope call removed and the CLI hook\nunregistered: four of the five assertions fail.","tree":{"sha":"6a670d1da0d5e59a942ad14d98c016d7d17c2791","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/6a670d1da0d5e59a942ad14d98c016d7d17c2791"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/884ffc58d98214a0d90a563038c0a66e9535b254","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/884ffc58d98214a0d90a563038c0a66e9535b254","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDg4NGZmYzU4ZDk4MjE0YTBkOTBhNTYzMDM4YzBhNjZlOTUzNWIyNTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/9f571d263626fb228d459bf3bd2fd2f50bf3347c","sha":"9f571d263626fb228d459bf3bd2fd2f50bf3347c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/9f571d263626fb228d459bf3bd2fd2f50bf3347c"}],"sha":"884ffc58d98214a0d90a563038c0a66e9535b254","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/884ffc58d98214a0d90a563038c0a66e9535b254"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/9f571d263626fb228d459bf3bd2fd2f50bf3347c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:13:04Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T12:23:55Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Emit structured logs from the process that actually ships\n\nThe deployed service wrote unparsed text to stdout. Read live against the reference deployment on 2026-09-15: of roughly 60 `severity>=ERROR` entries on `cloud_run_revision` in thirty days, not one came from an application. They were the platform''s own request log, or raw stderr in which a Python traceback arrived as several `textPayload` fragments with no severity, no logger name and no trace field.\n\n`hex_service_kit.logging.configure_logging` has existed since the convention was written and is called in 75 files across the workspace. It was called in none of the seven deployed stacks.\n\nWhat was missing is specific rather than cosmetic. Cloud Logging reads `severity` from the payload, so an application error was indistinguishable from an info line and could not drive a log-based metric. `logging.googleapis.com/trace` is what puts a log line inside the request it came from. And a traceback split across N entries has no single entry carrying the exception, which is what Error Reporting groups on.\n\nBoth entry points, and the placement matters in each. The API configures at module scope and before the app object is built, because the Dockerfile CMD serves the app object: anything inside a function never runs in a shipped process. The CLI uses its own installed entry point rather than a call under `if __name__ == \"__main__\"`, which never executes for a console script.\n\nThe profile comes from `resolve_profile`, the one reader of the profile variable the drift guard permits, and the CLI path refuses to be where a bad profile surfaces: it falls back to the text formatter so the command''s own clean exit is not replaced by a traceback.\n\nWhat was observed failing. Against a mutated copy of the tree with the module-scope call removed and the CLI hook unregistered, every new assertion fails, including that an exception renders as one JSON object carrying `severity`, `service` and a complete traceback in `message`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","tree":{"sha":"945f06d58b5b8ca8070122746b54fae061a42ee1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/945f06d58b5b8ca8070122746b54fae061a42ee1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/9f571d263626fb228d459bf3bd2fd2f50bf3347c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/9f571d263626fb228d459bf3bd2fd2f50bf3347c","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDlmNTcxZDI2MzYyNmZiMjI4ZDQ1OWJmM2JkMmZkMmY1MGJmMzM0N2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/f15f98bfac2bebdcc5423c691c2b4040ba53c51d","sha":"f15f98bfac2bebdcc5423c691c2b4040ba53c51d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/f15f98bfac2bebdcc5423c691c2b4040ba53c51d"}],"sha":"9f571d263626fb228d459bf3bd2fd2f50bf3347c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/9f571d263626fb228d459bf3bd2fd2f50bf3347c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/f15f98bfac2bebdcc5423c691c2b4040ba53c51d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:23:28Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:33:47Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Resync the embeddable-UI skill: both assertion header names\n\nThe canonical skill told the next repository to verify \"the injected\n`x-goog-iap-jwt-assertion`\" and nothing else. That is the instruction, not a\nmistake somebody made: an app reading the reserved name alone answers 401 to\nevery authenticated caller the day it is embedded, because the serverless\nfrontend strips the whole reserved namespace from a request entering a service\nand the embedding host therefore forwards the assertion under a second name.\n\nThis repository''s own adapter does not carry the defect. The vendored skill\ndid, so this is the doc half of the same fix, resynced from org-metadata.\n\nOnly this one skill is resynced rather than the whole set, because\ndeploy-and-residency-hardening is in flight on another branch and a blanket\n`sync-skills.sh` would pull that unmerged work in with it.","tree":{"sha":"7f2705aa988016a44eea59216df5964cb16829da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/7f2705aa988016a44eea59216df5964cb16829da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/f15f98bfac2bebdcc5423c691c2b4040ba53c51d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/f15f98bfac2bebdcc5423c691c2b4040ba53c51d","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKGYxNWY5OGJmYWMyYmViZGNjNTQyM2M2OTFjMmI0MDQwYmE1M2M1MWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/44091b740534f943989a40f34da458248c9abaef","sha":"44091b740534f943989a40f34da458248c9abaef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/44091b740534f943989a40f34da458248c9abaef"}],"sha":"f15f98bfac2bebdcc5423c691c2b4040ba53c51d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/f15f98bfac2bebdcc5423c691c2b4040ba53c51d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/44091b740534f943989a40f34da458248c9abaef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T13:42:29Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T13:45:25Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Take the posture paging and the audit-log copy off the reference deployment\n\nThe posture alert policies and their log-based metrics now sit behind\nposture_alerts_enabled, default false. Cloud Monitoring bills every\nmetric-based alert condition, and a reference deployment that pages nobody\nbuys nothing with them; the signals land in Cloud Logging regardless. The\naudit sink routes only this application''s own ledger into its bucket rather\nthan a copy of every Cloud Audit Log entry, which _Default already keeps for\nthirty days. The deployment var file states both decisions.\n\nApplied live to portable-genai-sg by targeted apply on 2026-09-13.","tree":{"sha":"b1ac0394e2185b69d5c1a46de973fdfff592f335","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/b1ac0394e2185b69d5c1a46de973fdfff592f335"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/44091b740534f943989a40f34da458248c9abaef","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/44091b740534f943989a40f34da458248c9abaef","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDQ0MDkxYjc0MDUzNGY5NDM5ODlhNDBmMzRkYTQ1ODI0OGM5YWJhZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/987af550cc7cccc1af203b8788d577eb3178ce71","sha":"987af550cc7cccc1af203b8788d577eb3178ce71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/987af550cc7cccc1af203b8788d577eb3178ce71"}],"sha":"44091b740534f943989a40f34da458248c9abaef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/44091b740534f943989a40f34da458248c9abaef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/987af550cc7cccc1af203b8788d577eb3178ce71/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T12:03:40Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T12:10:30Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Let an unpassed build argument stay unset, so the console can be built at all\n\nThis console reads its base path and API base THREE-STATE: unset takes the documented\ndefault, and set-and-empty is a refusal. The image declared both as build arguments\ndefaulting to the empty string and then set them as environment variables\nunconditionally, which turned \"not passed\" into \"passed as empty\". So `docker build ui`\nwith no arguments could not build this image, and failed with an error about an emptied\nvariable rather than about a missing argument. The default shape the Dockerfile appeared\nto offer was unreachable, and the deployment''s own build command was the only one that\nworked.\n\nThe empty defaults and the ENV assignment are both removed. A bare ARG reaches the\nbuild''s RUN steps as a real environment variable when it is passed and stays UNSET when\nit is not, so the three states the application distinguishes survive the image boundary.\n\nVerified by execution rather than by reading the reference: a probe image reports UNSET\nwith no `--build-arg` and the value when one is given. Then, against the real console,\nthe SHIPPED Dockerfile fails with no build arguments (exit 1), and this one builds with\nnone (exit 0) and builds again with the deployment''s own arguments (exit 0).","tree":{"sha":"2ffb38b87e00285dcd9a3278a0b963d6f9d490b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/2ffb38b87e00285dcd9a3278a0b963d6f9d490b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/987af550cc7cccc1af203b8788d577eb3178ce71","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/987af550cc7cccc1af203b8788d577eb3178ce71","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDk4N2FmNTUwY2M3Y2NjYzFhZjIwM2I4Nzg4ZDU3N2ViMzE3OGNlNzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/ba12784f508887b6ed6056efcabc44970c8548fe","sha":"ba12784f508887b6ed6056efcabc44970c8548fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/ba12784f508887b6ed6056efcabc44970c8548fe"}],"sha":"987af550cc7cccc1af203b8788d577eb3178ce71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/987af550cc7cccc1af203b8788d577eb3178ce71"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/ba12784f508887b6ed6056efcabc44970c8548fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T10:05:51Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T10:14:52Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Vendor the reduced required-artifact set\n\nThe portfolio gate stopped requiring `docs/practices-audit.md`,\n`docs/onprem-migration.md` and a fleet-wide `COMPLIANCE.md` on 2026-09-13, and the\ncanonical skills README was updated to match. This is the vendored copy following, so\nthe convention this repository carries is the one actually in force.\n\nThe scorecard shipped PRE-FILLED from a template render, so requiring it fleet-wide\nmeant every repository asserting a per-check verdict nobody had reached. The exit guide\ndocumented a migration for a profile that is a deliberate fail-fast placeholder. The\nprinciple-to-control mapping is now a launch-set expectation, because it is what a\nbuyer is shown.\n\nRetiring a requirement does not delete a file this repository already has. Nothing is\nremoved here; only the statement of what is required changes.\n\nVendored by `sync-skills.sh` from the canonical copy in org-metadata, never edited in\nplace, so the drift check stays green.","tree":{"sha":"b30e1446b2a070f6e5ec869ae6e19d0a714b5ebc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/b30e1446b2a070f6e5ec869ae6e19d0a714b5ebc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/ba12784f508887b6ed6056efcabc44970c8548fe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/ba12784f508887b6ed6056efcabc44970c8548fe","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKGJhMTI3ODRmNTA4ODg3YjZlZDYwNTZlZmNhYmM0NDk3MGM4NTQ4ZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/a947122fa79a111cebc0ca3e7003668125af5e5c","sha":"a947122fa79a111cebc0ca3e7003668125af5e5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/a947122fa79a111cebc0ca3e7003668125af5e5c"}],"sha":"ba12784f508887b6ed6056efcabc44970c8548fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/ba12784f508887b6ed6056efcabc44970c8548fe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/a947122fa79a111cebc0ca3e7003668125af5e5c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T09:28:07Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T09:55:18Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Gate the project audit config, and default it off\n\n`google_project_iam_audit_config` is AUTHORITATIVE for the service it names, so a\nstack declaring `allServices` does not add to the project''s audit configuration,\nit REPLACES it. Forty-eight stacks in this fleet declared it unconditionally and\nfour gated it, which is the collision the posture record already documents as the\nreason those four decline: a stack asking for DATA_READ and DATA_WRITE removes an\nADMIN_READ a sibling enabled, and Terraform reports it as a create rather than a\nchange, because the stack holds no prior state for a resource that is already live.\n\nThis stack now carries `manage_audit_config`, defaulted false. A deployment that\nwants data-access logging names it in its own tfvars, in exactly one stack per\nproject. Data-access logs are also the highest-volume class Cloud Logging ingests,\nand nothing in the reference deployment reads them.\n\nVerified: terraform fmt is clean and terraform validate passes on every touched\ntree; the three Terraform test suites asserting plan-level refusals pass.","tree":{"sha":"acbb582d9719cd55d9e9473284d464b96bbc8985","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/acbb582d9719cd55d9e9473284d464b96bbc8985"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/a947122fa79a111cebc0ca3e7003668125af5e5c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/a947122fa79a111cebc0ca3e7003668125af5e5c","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKGE5NDcxMjJmYTc5YTExMWNlYmMwY2EzZTcwMDM2NjgxMjVhZjVlNWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/01823051db10c5fbe2df17fb0270edba7fd2083d","sha":"01823051db10c5fbe2df17fb0270edba7fd2083d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/01823051db10c5fbe2df17fb0270edba7fd2083d"}],"sha":"a947122fa79a111cebc0ca3e7003668125af5e5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/a947122fa79a111cebc0ca3e7003668125af5e5c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/01823051db10c5fbe2df17fb0270edba7fd2083d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T14:43:41Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T14:47:21Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Read the IAP assertion from either name it travels under, not just the reserved one\n\nx-goog-* is Google''s reserved namespace, and the serverless frontend strips it from\nevery request entering a Cloud Run service, so an embedding host can never forward\nthe x-goog-iap-jwt-assertion header its own edge received. This is the identical\ndefect that made compliance-advisory and cio-advisory answer 401 to every\nauthenticated caller the day they were deployed as embedded apps\n(org-metadata/docs/plans/open-backlog.md, \"forty-six repositories read the one\nassertion header an embedding host can never forward\", opened 2026-09-12).\nmarketing-compliance-gate carried the same bug and is about to be embedded under\njourney-portal, so it is fixed here before that rather than after a live 401.\n\nresolve() now reads either name through the kit''s select_assertion, preferring the\nedge-injected one, with both taking the identical verification path.","tree":{"sha":"9cdb6c85658ba435585b1e493baa32321c41faa4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/9cdb6c85658ba435585b1e493baa32321c41faa4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/01823051db10c5fbe2df17fb0270edba7fd2083d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/01823051db10c5fbe2df17fb0270edba7fd2083d","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDAxODIzMDUxZGIxMGM1ZmJlMmRmMTdmYjAyNzBlZGJhN2ZkMjA4M2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/18bcf867241ef541d2702db4694feb36a5cb9452","sha":"18bcf867241ef541d2702db4694feb36a5cb9452","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/18bcf867241ef541d2702db4694feb36a5cb9452"}],"sha":"01823051db10c5fbe2df17fb0270edba7fd2083d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/01823051db10c5fbe2df17fb0270edba7fd2083d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/18bcf867241ef541d2702db4694feb36a5cb9452/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T11:45:34Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T11:49:31Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Restrict resource.type on every posture alert, so the API stops refusing them\n\nCloud Monitoring refuses a threshold condition filter that names only\nmetric.type: it requires a restriction on resource.type as well. This\nstack''s four alert policies never carried one, so they had never been\ncreatable in any project. Found only by the first real apply of this\nstack on 2026-09-12, after 21 of its 25 resources had already landed\nand the remaining four failed with:\n\n  Error 400: ... must specify a restriction on \"resource.type\" in\n  the filter\n\nNeither terraform validate nor a schema check can see this, because\nthe API refused the value, not the shape.\n\nWhich resource type to restrict on is not free either: a log-based\nmetric''s time series carry the monitored resource of the log entries\nit counted, and several Cloud Logging resource types have no\nMonitoring equivalent and collapse to `global`. Naming the wrong\ntype is quieter and worse than naming none, since the API accepts it\nand the policy then matches nothing forever. Each of the four\nsignals'' resource types is derived here from what its own filter\nactually selects, one condition per resource type the signal can\narrive under (guardrail_blocks spans two), with the policy''s existing\nOR combiner doing the union.\n\ninfra/terraform/tests/alert_policy_filters.tftest.hcl pins the\nresolved filter values with mock providers and no credentials, and\nwas observed failing without the resource.type restriction.\n\ndocs/practices-audit.md''s D5 row now records the finding and the\nguard.","tree":{"sha":"c4f91983be8adc96b61df2574c4ba5262186ee85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/c4f91983be8adc96b61df2574c4ba5262186ee85"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/18bcf867241ef541d2702db4694feb36a5cb9452","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/18bcf867241ef541d2702db4694feb36a5cb9452","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDE4YmNmODY3MjQxZWY1NDFkMjcwMmRiNDY5NGZlYjM2YTVjYjk0NTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/64bc4c51f9f90eb8764cd8fb7f6f916e5766abb1","sha":"64bc4c51f9f90eb8764cd8fb7f6f916e5766abb1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/64bc4c51f9f90eb8764cd8fb7f6f916e5766abb1"}],"sha":"18bcf867241ef541d2702db4694feb36a5cb9452","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/18bcf867241ef541d2702db4694feb36a5cb9452"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/64bc4c51f9f90eb8764cd8fb7f6f916e5766abb1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T09:35:59Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T09:49:58Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Patch the API image this stack promotes, rather than only pinning it\n\n`trivy image --exit-code 1 --ignore-unfixed --severity HIGH,CRITICAL` on the\nbuilt API image reports 30 fixable HIGH from the pinned Debian 13.6 base and 2\nfrom Python packages. Hosted CI never runs `docker build` and nothing else in\nthis repository read the root Dockerfile, so both were invisible to every check\nhere. Both sibling stacks beside this deployment reported the same two numbers\nearlier today and were fixed the same way.\n\nA digest pin freezes the base image, which freezes its unpatched packages too.\nReproducible and patched are independent properties: the pin buys the first and\nwas then standing as this image''s supply-chain evidence for both. The 30 base\nfindings are the util-linux family (CVE-2026-53612, CVE-2026-53613,\nCVE-2026-53614) plus openssl (CVE-2026-14456), every one of them fixable by the\ndistribution, so the runtime stage now applies the security updates on top.\n\nThe 2 Python findings are not a stale lock and no lock move reaches them.\nmsgpack and setuptools are vendored INSIDE pip, pinned by pip/_vendor/vendor.txt,\nand appear in no lockfile here because they were never resolved. A serving\ncontainer installs nothing, so pip leaves the runtime image in both the system\nprefix and the copied venv, which removes the findings and the install capability\ntogether.\n\ntests/unit/test_api_image.py holds the upgrade, the absent package manager, the\nnon-root user and the digest pins, reading the RUNTIME stage only: the builder\nlegitimately carries a compiler, git and pip and none of it is copied forward.\nEach assertion was watched go red first: the upgrade layer deleted, the base\ndigest dropped, USER set to root, and the pip removal reduced to its\npip-*.dist-info lines. That last one is why the paths are matched as whole paths\nrather than as substrings: a substring check stays GREEN on a Dockerfile that\ndeletes only the metadata directory and ships the package, with both vendored\nfindings still in the image.","tree":{"sha":"443d5437ceed899f76524d8231d64d94159d6570","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/443d5437ceed899f76524d8231d64d94159d6570"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/64bc4c51f9f90eb8764cd8fb7f6f916e5766abb1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/64bc4c51f9f90eb8764cd8fb7f6f916e5766abb1","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDY0YmM0YzUxZjlmOTBlYjg3NjRjZDhmYjdmNmY5MTZlNTc2NmFiYjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/b5c81e77cdfd6542a197214513a04aa1a7063026","sha":"b5c81e77cdfd6542a197214513a04aa1a7063026","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/b5c81e77cdfd6542a197214513a04aa1a7063026"}],"sha":"64bc4c51f9f90eb8764cd8fb7f6f916e5766abb1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/64bc4c51f9f90eb8764cd8fb7f6f916e5766abb1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/b5c81e77cdfd6542a197214513a04aa1a7063026/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T09:38:06Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T09:41:42Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Prove the console in the shape the portal actually runs it\n\n`make ui-check` built the console once, in the default shape, and the default\nshape is not what ships. The base path and the API base are BUILD-time inputs to\nNext.js, so the embedded console is a different artefact: a green default build\nsays nothing about it. A sibling console proved that the expensive way earlier\ntoday, when `docker build ui --build-arg NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH=/apps/...` failed\nsix CSP assertions on a commit whose own ui-check was green.\n\nui-check now builds and probes both shapes, with the portal''s prefix in\nUI_BASE_PATH and UI_API_BASE. This repository already carried the fix that\nsibling needed in `ui/scripts/assert-hydratable.mjs`, which derives the base path\nfrom NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH instead of probing the site root, and the fix is\nload-bearing: reverting it and running the probe against the embedded build\nreproduces exactly those six failures, five absent CSP directives and a missing\nnonce, because a base-path build answers 404 at `/` and 308s the base path with a\ntrailing slash, and neither response carries a CSP at all.\n\nObserved: both shapes now build and both report every one of their 9 script tags\ncarrying the CSP nonce, and the target exits 0.\n\ntests/unit/test_ui_image.py holds the two-shape gate, the base-path probe, the\nstandalone output the image copies, the two build ARGs, the digest pins, and a\nruntime stage that is non-root with no package manager and its distribution\npatches applied. Each assertion was watched go red first: the second build and\nprobe removed from ui-check, UI_BASE_PATH emptied, the probe pointed back at the\nsite root, and ui/Dockerfile''s `apk upgrade` and npm removal reverted.","tree":{"sha":"2744b4c3f4a0c646f9f6d25350dbf5504aba60de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/2744b4c3f4a0c646f9f6d25350dbf5504aba60de"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/b5c81e77cdfd6542a197214513a04aa1a7063026","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/b5c81e77cdfd6542a197214513a04aa1a7063026","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKGI1YzgxZTc3Y2RmZDY1NDJhMTk3MjE0NTEzYTA0YWExYTcwNjMwMjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/7708a7ff8542335b80f5840d322ed4b5735c4dd6","sha":"7708a7ff8542335b80f5840d322ed4b5735c4dd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/7708a7ff8542335b80f5840d322ed4b5735c4dd6"}],"sha":"b5c81e77cdfd6542a197214513a04aa1a7063026","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/b5c81e77cdfd6542a197214513a04aa1a7063026"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/7708a7ff8542335b80f5840d322ed4b5735c4dd6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T09:30:54Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T09:34:39Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Create the registry this stack''s own images are promoted into\n\nEvery sibling stack in the deployment project owns the Artifact Registry\nrepository its images live in, because the repository is where residency, CMEK\nand tag immutability are decided. This one owned none, so the API and console\nimages had nowhere to be promoted to and the deployment stopped before the\nportal apply. Two siblings closed the same gap earlier today, and all three were\nfound the same way: by trying to deploy. Nothing in this repository noticed,\nbecause no check asserted that the path infra/terraform/README.md tells an\noperator to push to is a path this Terraform creates. It was not: the README\nnamed a `mkt` repository that exists in no stack here.\n\nartifact_registry.tf adds the regional Docker repository\n`marketing-compliance-gate`, bound to this stack''s own key with its own service\nagent grant, because CMEK does not cascade and Artifact Registry encrypts as its\nown service agent rather than as the caller. Tags are immutable, so a promoted\nrelease tag always names the same bytes rather than being re-pointed under a\nreviewer who checked the tag instead of the digest.\n\nNo cleanup policy, deliberately, and the same choice the siblings made: the\ndeployment pins digests, so a policy that deleted an untagged or older version\nwould be the only resource in this stack able to delete a RUNNING deployment''s\nimage, and it would do it on a timer rather than in a plan anybody read.\n\nPull access is repository-scoped and named per identity rather than inherited\nfrom the project-wide reader that a shared project''s owner can tighten without\nthis stack noticing: the serving identity this stack creates, plus every\nadditional_serving_service_accounts entry, which is what the deployed API and\nconsole containers actually authenticate as under the portal. The pull set is\nkeyed by a label, not by the email, because a for_each over computed\nservice-account emails is refused before a plan exists.\n\nartifactregistry.googleapis.com was already enabled in apis.tf. The new\nimage_registry output names the path the README push step and container_image\nboth build on, and the README, the tfvars example and the existing plan test now\nname a digest in that registry rather than in the repository nobody created.\n\ntests/image_registry.tftest.hcl proves residency, format, the key, the service\nagent grant, tag immutability, the absent cleanup policy, the enabled API, and\nthat pull access covers exactly those identities with reader scoped to this\nrepository. Each assertion was watched go red first, on a copy in a scratch\ndirectory: immutable_tags false, a dropped kms_key_name, the repository renamed\nto `mkt`, the host identities removed from the pull set, a cleanup policy added,\nthe API line deleted, the location moved to us-central1, reader widened to\nwriter, and the service agent grant downgraded to cloudkms.viewer.","tree":{"sha":"7f781aa8688c191d2b740e5f66b82907fd011bf2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/7f781aa8688c191d2b740e5f66b82907fd011bf2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/7708a7ff8542335b80f5840d322ed4b5735c4dd6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/7708a7ff8542335b80f5840d322ed4b5735c4dd6","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDc3MDhhN2ZmODU0MjMzNWI4MGY1ODQwZDMyMmVkNGI1NzM1YzRkZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/69cad516266faa080dccbc72675c3718c9a8ff27","sha":"69cad516266faa080dccbc72675c3718c9a8ff27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/69cad516266faa080dccbc72675c3718c9a8ff27"}],"sha":"7708a7ff8542335b80f5840d322ed4b5735c4dd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/7708a7ff8542335b80f5840d322ed4b5735c4dd6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/69cad516266faa080dccbc72675c3718c9a8ff27/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T09:18:55Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T09:22:25Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Say that the consent bridge is the only way consent reaches the rule engine\n\ndomain/consent.py still described the asset-review path as deriving its granted\npurposes from MarketingAsset.granted_consents. That field is gone: the review\nresolves the records of the subject its audience_subject_id names, through this\nsame module. The module that owns the bridge was the one place still describing\nthe hole it closed, and SPEC outranks a docstring only when they agree.","tree":{"sha":"223f64bf6729f073fcbce4e9ee7a48ae773abff6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/223f64bf6729f073fcbce4e9ee7a48ae773abff6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/69cad516266faa080dccbc72675c3718c9a8ff27","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/69cad516266faa080dccbc72675c3718c9a8ff27","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDY5Y2FkNTE2MjY2ZmFhMDgwZGNjYmM3MjY3NWMzNzE4YzlhOGZmMjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/332198fdfb8a3f87ca11a7152a754a650e59d61e","sha":"332198fdfb8a3f87ca11a7152a754a650e59d61e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/332198fdfb8a3f87ca11a7152a754a650e59d61e"}],"sha":"69cad516266faa080dccbc72675c3718c9a8ff27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/69cad516266faa080dccbc72675c3718c9a8ff27"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/332198fdfb8a3f87ca11a7152a754a650e59d61e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T09:13:28Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T09:18:03Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Read the audience subject''s stored consent instead of accepting a typed one\n\nThe console''s review form took consent as free text. MarketingAsset carried a\ngranted_consents tuple the caller filled in, the form had a \"Granted consents\n(comma-separated)\" box wired straight to it, and the deterministic\nCONSENT_REQUIRED rules read nothing else. So the gate could be told any consent\nby typing it, and the seeded regional consent and preference store this same\nservice maintains, with its withdrawals, expiries, suppressions and four-eyes\npending grants, was never consulted on the review path. Every check stayed green\nthroughout: the rule fired, the finding was cited, the audit event was written,\nthe eval scored 1.0. None of them asked where the consent came from, because the\nrequest was allowed to say.\n\nThe asset now carries audience_subject_id and no consent at all. ReviewService\nresolves that subject''s stored records through ConsentStorePort under the\nVERIFIED tenant, ConsentEngine.granted_purposes reduces them to the purposes\nthey grant at an instant, and that set is what reaches the rule engine. The\nbridge already existed for the consent routes; the review path is now its second\ncaller, so \"granted\" means one thing in this service. RuleEngine.consent_checks\nis deleted rather than left as a wrapper over the asset''s own claim, and a\nCONSENT_REQUIRED check reaching the per-rule evaluator fails closed saying it\ncannot be decided from the asset.\n\nFour states, and three grant nothing: a grant on file, a record that grants\nnothing, a subject the store holds no record for, and no subject named. The last\ntwo stay distinguishable on purpose, because \"checked and absent\" and \"never\nchecked\" are different facts about a compliance verdict and neither is consent.\nReview.consent_source records which, the console, the CLI and the demo console\nprint it, and the audit event names the records read, the purposes granted and\nwhy none were. A store that raises is not caught: a review cannot honestly\nreport \"consent not granted\" when it could not look.\n\nA caller still sending granted_consents is REFUSED with the field named, not\nsilently given a different answer, so AssetModel forbids extras. subject_ref\nmoves to domain/consent.py because the review audits a subject too, and a second\nspelling of the pseudonym would be a second chance to leak. as_of is a\ndomain-level argument the demo and the eval pin for reproducibility and is\ndeliberately absent from POST /v1/review: a caller able to choose the instant\ncould age a review back to when an expired grant was live.\n\nThe golden review rows name subjects described in golden_consent.jsonl and the\neval seeds the real store from that one file, so the stored state the reviews\nrest on is written down once rather than re-asserted in a second dataset. The\ndemo walkthrough points its four assets at a granted, a withdrawn and an unknown\nsubject, so the refusals are on screen.\n\nTests, each observed failing first against a planted defect: the route and audit\nlevel in test_review_reads_consent_from_the_store.py (an absent record treated as\na grant, 2 red; an untenanted store read, 1 red; a raw subject id in the audit,\n2 red), the console level in ui/tests/consent-is-read-not-typed.test.mjs (the\ntyped field restored, 1 red), and the browser level through the existing\ndemo-browser job plus demo_selftest (a served page claiming a read that never\nhappened, red in both). The route tests also prove a MAPPED MACHINE CALLER\nreaches the consent read, because a sibling deployment''s authorized surface\nrefused every machine caller by resolving tenancy from a human''s hosted domain\nalone.","tree":{"sha":"3ede207c25ce431068a5b36ea610c27353a60acf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/3ede207c25ce431068a5b36ea610c27353a60acf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/332198fdfb8a3f87ca11a7152a754a650e59d61e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/332198fdfb8a3f87ca11a7152a754a650e59d61e","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDMzMjE5OGZkZmI4YTNmODdjYTExYTcxNTJhNzU0YTY1MGU1OWQ2MWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/2fc624518b7c7b5a7624afd4d0642364bf88b322","sha":"2fc624518b7c7b5a7624afd4d0642364bf88b322","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/2fc624518b7c7b5a7624afd4d0642364bf88b322"}],"sha":"332198fdfb8a3f87ca11a7152a754a650e59d61e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/332198fdfb8a3f87ca11a7152a754a650e59d61e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/2fc624518b7c7b5a7624afd4d0642364bf88b322/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T08:48:14Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T08:51:41Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Serve the gcp profile''s rules from the versioned pack bundled in the repository\n\nThe gcp profile bound rule_provider to a Gemini File Search store named\nmkt-gov-rule-kb that nothing in infra/terraform provisioned. Every guard on that\nbinding was green: the adapter constructed, it satisfied the Protocol, its module\nimported no SDK. None of them asked whether a deployed review would have any rules,\nand it would not have: an unprovisioned store serves an empty rule set and\nReviewService raises RuleSetEmptyError, so every review on the deployment would\nhave refused.\n\nThe rule source under gcp is now the versioned pack already bundled in the package,\nthe same rules the local profile indexes, held in an in-memory FTS5 index. The\ndeployment provisions no rule store, so the rules a deployed review fires are the\nrules the offline gate and the eval set proved, a rule change arrives through review\nrather than a console edit against a managed index, and no operator can leave the\nservice pointing at an empty one. The File Search adapter is deleted rather than\nleft selectable: platform already reaches a rule store over HTTP through\nremote_rules, so File Search had no remaining role.\n\nRuleSet now carries the pack version. The provider stamps it, mkt-gov rules prints\nit, and the review''s audit event records it as rule_pack_version, so a finding is\ntraceable to the revision that produced it. A store re-seeded with rules of unstated\nprovenance reports an empty version rather than claiming the current one, so a test\ndouble cannot pass for the bundled pack. knowledge_base loses data_store_id,\nlocation and top_k, which only the deleted adapter read, and local loses the\nseed_path nothing ever read.\n\ntest_gcp_rule_source_is_the_bundled_pack.py asks the missing question: it resolves\nthe provider from the real settings binding, asserts every (market, vertical) scope\nis non-empty AND date-versioned, and proves a review under gcp fails on named rules\nfrom the pack with the version on its audit event. Observed failing first against\ntwo planted defects: rebinding the profile to the onprem provider (9 of 10 red) and\nblanking RULE_PACK_VERSION (6 of 10 red).","tree":{"sha":"521d2b248dc0cc515753e241b609cb6c9a352076","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/521d2b248dc0cc515753e241b609cb6c9a352076"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/2fc624518b7c7b5a7624afd4d0642364bf88b322","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/2fc624518b7c7b5a7624afd4d0642364bf88b322","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDJmYzYyNDUxOGI3YzdiNWE3NjI0YWZkNGQwNjQyMzY0YmY4OGIzMjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/4321a6fd89ad9bc1592b22525a17d480696e43d9","sha":"4321a6fd89ad9bc1592b22525a17d480696e43d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/4321a6fd89ad9bc1592b22525a17d480696e43d9"}],"sha":"2fc624518b7c7b5a7624afd4d0642364bf88b322","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/2fc624518b7c7b5a7624afd4d0642364bf88b322"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/a