e,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/b3e7f7b6bdd0cc7e3036d14cec600c70e252565b","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKGIzZTdmN2I2YmRkMGNjN2UzMDM2ZDE0Y2VjNjAwYzcwZTI1MjU2NWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/9c4a253cb2a16d945afec127c5358297f61660ba","sha":"9c4a253cb2a16d945afec127c5358297f61660ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/9c4a253cb2a16d945afec127c5358297f61660ba"}],"sha":"b3e7f7b6bdd0cc7e3036d14cec600c70e252565b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/b3e7f7b6bdd0cc7e3036d14cec600c70e252565b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/9c4a253cb2a16d945afec127c5358297f61660ba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T16:34:13Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T16:41:44Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Score the one generative output, and give every bar one home\n\nThis service is deliberately almost all deterministic code: the verdict, the\ncoverage and every rule finding are computed. The substantiation NARRATIVE is\nthe one thing a model contributes, and nothing measured it. That is an odd shape\nfor a service whose whole purpose is to stop an unsubstantiated claim reaching\nthe public: the single generative output was the one thing the gate did not\nscore. A narrative can sit under a correct verdict and still assert an absolute\nthe evidence does not carry, read as a publishing decision rather than an\nassessment, or claim completeness over evidence that has an age. Those are the\nthree things a marketing reviewer overrides a verdict on, and they are what the\njudged half now grades, against a model-risk floor in config/quality-floors.toml.\n\nThresholds now have one home. The THRESHOLDS dict is gone; every bar is read\nfrom eval/rubrics/*.yaml where the argument for it lives, and assert_covers\nfails the build in both directions. What was here before was a dict AND a loader\nthat overlaid four rubric files on top of it and fell back to the dict when\nPyYAML was missing.\n\nThe denominator rule is asserted against the corpus that actually divides each\nrate, which is not the example count for any of them: finding_accuracy at 0.90\nover the thirteen expected failing rule ids rather than eight golden assets,\nwhich would not have supported it; rule_coverage at 0.95 over the applicable\nrules; consent_decision_accuracy over its own seventeen subjects.\n\nThe falsification ordering this repository invented keeps its place and gains\nits name: assert_metrics_not_falsely_green is still the first statement of the\nscored run, now through prove_before_scoring, which is the same statement with\nthe commons behind it.\n\ndocs/evals.md is generated from the rubrics, the three corpora and the floors,\nwith --check in `make gate`. Pin: agent-eval-kit v0.0.2. practices-audit gains\nE4 and E5; the D3 row and the adoption FAQ stop citing ci.yaml and\neval-gate.yaml, both deleted on 2026-09-01.\n\nVerified: `make gate` green end to end (605 passed, eval PASS, narrative PASS).","tree":{"sha":"338d92a9a6a3ba951783282bd3b38ec7317c0141","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/338d92a9a6a3ba951783282bd3b38ec7317c0141"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/9c4a253cb2a16d945afec127c5358297f61660ba","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/9c4a253cb2a16d945afec127c5358297f61660ba","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDljNGEyNTNjYjJhMTZkOTQ1YWZlYzEyN2M1MzU4Mjk3ZjYxNjYwYmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/6c020b9c061c46b1a050e66f4460d8d0816d6009","sha":"6c020b9c061c46b1a050e66f4460d8d0816d6009","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/6c020b9c061c46b1a050e66f4460d8d0816d6009"}],"sha":"9c4a253cb2a16d945afec127c5358297f61660ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/9c4a253cb2a16d945afec127c5358297f61660ba"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/6c020b9c061c46b1a050e66f4460d8d0816d6009/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T14:53:53Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T15:36:28Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump shared kits: hex-service-kit v0.0.7","tree":{"sha":"196d5ddf5659f657b7e26e57177231749090dba7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/196d5ddf5659f657b7e26e57177231749090dba7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/6c020b9c061c46b1a050e66f4460d8d0816d6009","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/6c020b9c061c46b1a050e66f4460d8d0816d6009","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDZjMDIwYjljMDYxYzQ2YjFhMDUwZTY2ZjQ0NjBkOGQwODE2ZDYwMDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/d5ee3b8f71b0816f6021cc968756d24bb08be5c7","sha":"d5ee3b8f71b0816f6021cc968756d24bb08be5c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/d5ee3b8f71b0816f6021cc968756d24bb08be5c7"}],"sha":"6c020b9c061c46b1a050e66f4460d8d0816d6009","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/6c020b9c061c46b1a050e66f4460d8d0816d6009"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/d5ee3b8f71b0816f6021cc968756d24bb08be5c7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T14:38:01Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T14:41:20Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Replace the market FIELD, not the property, when the loader is told a market\n\nSettings.active_market is a property over the market field, so\ndataclasses.replace(settings, active_market=...) raised. Found by running the loader\nagainst the real store rather than by any test: the dry run does not exercise the branch\nbecause it takes --market and the default path never replaces anything.\n\nIt raised rather than silently writing to the wrong region''s database, which is the\nfailure mode worth having here.\n\nVerified by loading: 18 documents into portable-genai-sg/mkt6-asia-southeast1 under\ntenant reference-bank, with the second tenant kept separate, and the adapter''s own\ncomposite query (tenant AND subject_id) answering 1 record for this tenant''s subject and\n0 for the other tenant''s. Those queries returning at all is the proof the five composite\nindexes are the right ones: without them Firestore fails with FAILED_PRECONDITION.","tree":{"sha":"8c89ba51769e4774640bc9b3cfe48de0292d918d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/8c89ba51769e4774640bc9b3cfe48de0292d918d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/d5ee3b8f71b0816f6021cc968756d24bb08be5c7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/d5ee3b8f71b0816f6021cc968756d24bb08be5c7","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKGQ1ZWUzYjhmNzFiMDgxNmY2MDIxY2M5Njg3NTZkMjRiYjA4YmU1Yzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/9d870b577f73993aa166918ee134294e055db2fe","sha":"9d870b577f73993aa166918ee134294e055db2fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/9d870b577f73993aa166918ee134294e055db2fe"}],"sha":"d5ee3b8f71b0816f6021cc968756d24bb08be5c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/d5ee3b8f71b0816f6021cc968756d24bb08be5c7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/9d870b577f73993aa166918ee134294e055db2fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T14:15:16Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T14:22:07Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Format the CMEK guard the way ruff wants it","tree":{"sha":"f0209df75adec11a05971974798d94db5c31e3b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/f0209df75adec11a05971974798d94db5c31e3b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/9d870b577f73993aa166918ee134294e055db2fe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/9d870b577f73993aa166918ee134294e055db2fe","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDlkODcwYjU3N2Y3Mzk5M2FhMTY2OTE4ZWUxMzQyOTRlMDU1ZGIyZmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/b7c2a80f2ced334c4a3ca49717fedfacd2c21042","sha":"b7c2a80f2ced334c4a3ca49717fedfacd2c21042","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/b7c2a80f2ced334c4a3ca49717fedfacd2c21042"}],"sha":"9d870b577f73993aa166918ee134294e055db2fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/9d870b577f73993aa166918ee134294e055db2fe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/b7c2a80f2ced334c4a3ca49717fedfacd2c21042/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T14:02:28Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T14:22:07Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Make Firestore CMEK conditional: it is allowlist-gated, so an unconditional block fails the apply\n\nThe recorded posture (org-metadata/docs/deployment-posture.md) says Firestore CMEK is\nexternally blocked, allowlist-gated by Google. An unconditional cmek_config block does\nnot degrade on a project that has not been admitted: the apply fails outright. So the\nkey is a variable defaulting to empty, the service-agent binding stays in kms.tf so\nturning it on is one variable, and the runbook says why the one non-strict default in\nthis file is not a preference. A test pins it.","tree":{"sha":"c78081e3b4783fd4f741ff93c38f370beb49c5ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/c78081e3b4783fd4f741ff93c38f370beb49c5ba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/b7c2a80f2ced334c4a3ca49717fedfacd2c21042","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/b7c2a80f2ced334c4a3ca49717fedfacd2c21042","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKGI3YzJhODBmMmNlZDMzNGM0YTNjYTQ5NzE3ZmVkZmFjZDJjMjEwNDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/f3a80dfe5005a6e85146543d6904dbb46d90c9ad","sha":"f3a80dfe5005a6e85146543d6904dbb46d90c9ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/f3a80dfe5005a6e85146543d6904dbb46d90c9ad"}],"sha":"b7c2a80f2ced334c4a3ca49717fedfacd2c21042","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/b7c2a80f2ced334c4a3ca49717fedfacd2c21042"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/f3a80dfe5005a6e85146543d6904dbb46d90c9ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T13:54:08Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T14:22:07Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Provision the two Firestore stores, route them by residency, and seed the consent leg\n\nBoth managed adapters have been bound as the implementations of their ports since the\nrepository was written, and infra/terraform/ created no database, enabled no API,\ngranted no role and bound no key. The consent leg of the marketing journey would have\nfailed at its first request on a deployment, and the substantiation evidence a compliance\nofficer is meant to pull up months later had nowhere to be. Loading the three marketing\nBigQuery books left that leg empty for exactly this reason.\n\nThe residency validation reached nothing. Both adapters called resolve_region(...) and\nDISCARDED the result, then built firestore.Client(project=...) against the project''s\nDEFAULT database. A database''s location is fixed at creation and a project has one\ndefault, so a JP request passed the residency check and then read and wrote whichever\nsingle region that database sat in. The check was real and the wire was not. There is\none NAMED database per residency region now, mkt6-<region>, built from the same region\nlist on both sides, and the adapters select it from the region they resolved. An\nunresolved region refuses rather than falling back, because a fallback is how a\nvalidated boundary becomes a comment.\n\nvar.residency_regions defaults to [var.region]: a single-market install provisions one\nstore. A database in a country nobody is serving is standing cost and a residency\nsurface with no user.\n\nComposite indexes are declared for every multi-field query the two adapters run, and\ndeliberately not for the single-field one. Firestore maintains single-field indexes\nitself; a composite query with no index fails at REQUEST time with FAILED_PRECONDITION,\nthe first time a compliance officer opens a subject, on the deployment and nowhere else.\nThe indexes are per database, so three regions get three sets rather than one that\nserves the first.\n\nscripts/load_consent_seed.py writes the same seven subjects the offline profile serves,\nthrough the managed adapter''s OWN write methods rather than a second serializer: a\nloader with its own document shape is a second description of the store, and the one\nthat drifts is the one nobody reads. --tenant is required, other-brand is kept separate\nso a cross-tenant read that \"worked\" is visibly wrong rather than merely empty, and it\nrefuses unless the store is empty or its manifest says what it holds is fictional.\n\nThe evidence store is provisioned and NOT seeded: created, indexed, keyed and\nregion-routed, with whatever an institution ingests.\n\nGate green: 602 tests, eval, terraform validate, portability. The region guard was\nwatched failing against the shipped client construction and the index guard against a\ndropped index.","tree":{"sha":"12eb35df3fc87458e0bc3913db73f87971041a32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/12eb35df3fc87458e0bc3913db73f87971041a32"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/f3a80dfe5005a6e85146543d6904dbb46d90c9ad","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/f3a80dfe5005a6e85146543d6904dbb46d90c9ad","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKGYzYTgwZGZlNTAwNWE2ZTg1MTQ2NTQzZDY5MDRkYmI0NmQ5MGM5YWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/5863ec8d001b3699e9a7c8acf75fe7613c184f05","sha":"5863ec8d001b3699e9a7c8acf75fe7613c184f05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/5863ec8d001b3699e9a7c8acf75fe7613c184f05"}],"sha":"f3a80dfe5005a6e85146543d6904dbb46d90c9ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/f3a80dfe5005a6e85146543d6904dbb46d90c9ad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/5863ec8d001b3699e9a7c8acf75fe7613c184f05/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T10:01:17Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-06T22:39:02Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Name the systems this repo depends on, instead of their catalog ids\n\nRepository names are unique across the organization, so a reader no longer has\nto resolve a code through a table to learn which system is meant. The catalog\ndropped its ID column, and this repository follows.\n\nBeyond prose, four identifier changes:\n\n- The review payload''s source_key prefix is the repository name. It is a dedup\n  key -- human-review-console queries on it and the local store makes it a\n  PRIMARY KEY -- so producers and the console have to agree, and the branch\n  carries the migration for rows written under the old prefix.\n- Terraform''s local.render_catalog_id becomes local.render_repository. It feeds\n  display names and descriptions, which update in place.\n- scripts/demo.py''s catalog id is deleted rather than renamed: a REPOSITORY\n  constant and a \"repository\" state key were already there beside it.\n- scripts/rename_fork.py loses --catalog-id, which had nothing left to rewrite.\n\nLines that outgrew the 100-column limit because a name is longer than an id are\nrewrapped rather than shortened by dropping the name. `ruff check`,\n`ruff format --check` and the offline tests are clean.\n\nDeployed resource identifiers are deliberately NOT changed: the Terraform\nname_prefix stems and the Secret Manager secret ids still carry the old\nlowercase id. Those name resources that exist in the deployment, and renaming a\nname_prefix destroys and recreates them, so they are an infrastructure\nmigration rather than a rename.","tree":{"sha":"2f65b629f43286d85263e0b801f95c68ad23117b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/2f65b629f43286d85263e0b801f95c68ad23117b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/5863ec8d001b3699e9a7c8acf75fe7613c184f05","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https