gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/f5c53468c3bc1a3f87fb13b644d2881ee118d643/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-03T00:58:49Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-03T01:07:58Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Name the triage model the settings actually pin\n\nThe module docstrings said triage/classification uses `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`.\nThat was false on two counts:\n\n- `config/settings.yaml` pins `triage: gemini-3.5-flash`. The prose described a\n  pin that no longer exists: the 2026-08-27 in-region sweep changed the settings\n  and left the docstrings behind.\n- `gemini-3.1-flash-lite` commits ML processing to the `us` and `eu`\n  multi-regions only (verified against the publisher 2026-09-03), so it cannot\n  serve a deployment whose `models.location` defaults to `asia-southeast1`.\n  See org-metadata/docs/gcp-service-region-availability.md for the region table.","tree":{"sha":"228c0dc4147254d1675a16f20db0817f0b12b2b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/228c0dc4147254d1675a16f20db0817f0b12b2b9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/f5c53468c3bc1a3f87fb13b644d2881ee118d643","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/f5c53468c3bc1a3f87fb13b644d2881ee118d643","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKGY1YzUzNDY4YzNiYzFhM2Y4N2ZiMTNiNjQ0ZDI4ODFlZTExOGQ2NDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/1e36e0b3d995d8b4b530d59de76ab9099f708ce1","sha":"1e36e0b3d995d8b4b530d59de76ab9099f708ce1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/1e36e0b3d995d8b4b530d59de76ab9099f708ce1"}],"sha":"f5c53468c3bc1a3f87fb13b644d2881ee118d643","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/f5c53468c3bc1a3f87fb13b644d2881ee118d643"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/1e36e0b3d995d8b4b530d59de76ab9099f708ce1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T15:22:02Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T15:44:52Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Adopt the fleet''s GitHub Actions gate, alongside the Cloud Build one\n\nPart of the fleet''s move off paid Cloud Build, which bills SGD ~3.94/day for work that calls no\nGoogle Cloud API, reads no secret and holds no deploy authority. Actions runs the same work free\non a public repository. Proved on account-takeover-investigator first: both jobs green, 138s of\nwall clock against Cloud Build''s 266s, running the same run-grc-ci in the same reviewed image.\n\nNothing about branch protection changes here. `pr-<repo> (portable-genai-ci-sg)` remains the\nonly REQUIRED check, so this reports alongside it and cannot block a merge while it is proved.\n\nGENERATED, not written: org-metadata/scripts/render-actions-callers.py emits this from the same\nci/gcp/repository-policy.json entry the Cloud Build trigger is built from, and its --check mode\nfails on drift. The 196 workflow files retired on 2026-09-01 rotted because each was maintained\nby hand; this one has no hand to rot by.","tree":{"sha":"719b5210736a2a99d9eb2dc1e7d08c82d7acba65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/719b5210736a2a99d9eb2dc1e7d08c82d7acba65"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/1e36e0b3d995d8b4b530d59de76ab9099f708ce1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/1e36e0b3d995d8b4b530d59de76ab9099f708ce1","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDFlMzZlMGIzZDk5NWQ4YjRiNTMwZDU5ZGU3NmFiOTA5OWY3MDhjZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/55e535108e27826b835406cadb73459966d9101e","sha":"55e535108e27826b835406cadb73459966d9101e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/55e535108e27826b835406cadb73459966d9101e"}],"sha":"1e36e0b3d995d8b4b530d59de76ab9099f708ce1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/1e36e0b3d995d8b4b530d59de76ab9099f708ce1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/55e535108e27826b835406cadb73459966d9101e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-01T09:17:51Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T09:34:22Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Retire the GitHub Actions workflows, which had never run\n\nGitHub Actions are disabled for the whole organization\n(`enabled_repositories: \"none\"`), so every workflow file in this repository had\nnever executed and could not. The required check is the hosted Cloud Build\ntrigger, which already runs this repository''s gate, its ui-check where it has a\nUI, its terraform test, lint-gcp, and the IAP negative matrix against the\nruntime lockfile.\n\nUnrunnable configuration rots unobserved, and this had. The workflows still\npinned python 3.12 and 3.13 long after the fleet moved to 3.14, and the shared\nhard gate derived its environment prefix with a pattern that could not match any\nrepository whose prefix contains an underscore.\n\nRemoved:\n- .github/workflows/\n- the tests that asserted the contents of those files, and the test modules that\n  existed only to guard them\n- the github-actions dependabot ecosystem, which now has nothing left to pin\n\nKept, and repointed rather than deleted: every assertion that guarded something\nstill enforced. Where a test checked several things and only some were about a\nworkflow, the workflow lines were removed and the rest left standing.\n\nControl claims that cited a workflow as their evidence now name what actually\nenforces them. Where nothing does, they say so: the scheduled corpus refresh,\nthe managed release path and the promotion gate have no automated runner, which\nwas already true and is now written down.","tree":{"sha":"568cb242ec6dd955d8dab3f39fd09a298507a33a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/568cb242ec6dd955d8dab3f39fd09a298507a33a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/55e535108e27826b835406cadb73459966d9101e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/55e535108e27826b835406cadb73459966d9101e","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDU1ZTUzNTEwOGUyNzgyNmI4MzU0MDZjYWRiNzM0NTk5NjZkOTEwMWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/3e96f16befeeef31ad12a404b8dd3ae59b62c77c","sha":"3e96f16befeeef31ad12a404b8dd3ae59b62c77c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/3e96f16befeeef31ad12a404b8dd3ae59b62c77c"}],"sha":"55e535108e27826b835406cadb73459966d9101e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/55e535108e27826b835406cadb73459966d9101e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","id":49699333,"login":"dependabot[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/3e96f16befeeef31ad12a404b8dd3ae59b62c77c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T06:53:25Z","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dependabot[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T07:59:28Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump the python-minor-patch group across 1 directory with 2 updates\n\nBumps the python-minor-patch group with 2 updates in the / directory: [google-adk](https://github.com/google/adk-python) and [ruff](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff).\n\n\nUpdates `google-adk` from 2.7.1 to 2.8.0\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/google/adk-python/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/google/adk-python/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/google/adk-python/compare/v2.7.1...v2.8.0)\n\nUpdates `ruff` from 0.16.3 to 0.16.5\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff/compare/0.16.3...0.16.5)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: google-adk\n  dependency-version: 2.8.0\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n  dependency-group: python-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: ruff\n  dependency-version: 0.16.5\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: python-minor-patch\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>","tree":{"sha":"c112239db30825cd73c855840093fae312c933f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/c112239db30825cd73c855840093fae312c933f8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/3e96f16befeeef31ad12a404b8dd3ae59b62c77c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/3e96f16befeeef31ad12a404b8dd3ae59b62c77c","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDNlOTZmMTZiZWZlZWVmMzFhZDEyYTQwNGI4ZGQzYWU1OWI2MmM3N2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/1400822e4ef8ac0a78cd698b709b14a289bc805b","sha":"1400822e4ef8ac0a78cd698b709b14a289bc805b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/1400822e4ef8ac0a78cd698b709b14a289bc805b"}],"sha":"3e96f16befeeef31ad12a404b8dd3ae59b62c77c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/3e96f16befeeef31ad12a404b8dd3ae59b62c77c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","id":49699333,"login":"dependabot[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/1400822e4ef8ac0a78cd698b709b14a289bc805b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T15:36:46Z","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dependabot[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T07:59:20Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump the npm-minor-patch group across 1 directory with 7 updates\n\nBumps the npm-minor-patch group with 7 updates in the /ui directory:\n\n| Package | From | To |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [next](https://github.com/vercel/next.js) | `16.3.0` | `16.3.3` |\n| [react](https://github.com/react/react/tree/HEAD/packages/react) | `19.2.7` | `19.2.8` |\n| [@types/react](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/react) | `19.2.17` | `19.2.18` |\n| [react-dom](https://github.com/react/react/tree/HEAD/packages/react-dom) | `19.2.7` | `19.2.8` |\n| [@types/react-dom](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/react-dom) | `19.2.3` | `19.2.5` |\n| [@types/node](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/node) | `26.2.0` | `26.4.0` |\n| [typescript](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript) | `5.5.3` | `5.9.3` |\n\n\n\nUpdates `next` from 16.3.0 to 16.3.3\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/compare/v16.3.0...v16.3.3)\n\nUpdates `react` from 19.2.7 to 19.2.8\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/react/react/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/react/react/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/react/react/commits/v19.2.8/packages/react)\n\nUpdates `@types/react` from 19.2.17 to 19.2.18\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/react)\n\nUpdates `react-dom` from 19.2.7 to 19.2.8\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/react/react/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/react/react/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/react/react/commits/v19.2.8/packages/react-dom)\n\nUpdates `@types/react-dom` from 19.2.3 to 19.2.5\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/react-dom)\n\nUpdates `@types/node` from 26.2.0 to 26.4.0\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/node)\n\nUpdates `@types/react` from 19.2.17 to 19.2.18\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/react)\n\nUpdates `@types/react-dom` from 19.2.3 to 19.2.5\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/react-dom)\n\nUpdates `typescript` from 5.5.3 to 5.9.3\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/compare/v5.5.3...v5.9.3)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: \"@types/node\"\n  dependency-version: 26.3.0\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: \"@types/react\"\n  dependency-version: 19.2.18\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: \"@types/react\"\n  dependency-version: 19.2.18\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: \"@types/react-dom\"\n  dependency-version: 19.2.5\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: \"@types/react-dom\"\n  dependency-version: 19.2.5\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: next\n  dependency-version: 16.3.3\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: react\n  dependency-version: 19.2.8\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: react-dom\n  dependency-version: 19.2.8\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: typescript\n  dependency-version: 5.9.3\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>","tree":{"sha":"5f9dfdaccf89842a253444c7dbbc78a0a172b71e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/5f9dfdaccf89842a253444c7dbbc78a0a172b71e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/1400822e4ef8ac0a78cd698b709b14a289bc805b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/1400822e4ef8ac0a78cd698b709b14a289bc805b","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDE0MDA4MjJlNGVmOGFjMGE3OGNkNjk4YjcwOWIxNGEyODliYzgwNWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/4bb11578be10bbec470eeaaabc0cdb8778eca075","sha":"4bb11578be10bbec470eeaaabc0cdb8778eca075","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/4bb11578be10bbec470eeaaabc0cdb8778eca075"}],"sha":"1400822e4ef8ac0a78cd698b709b14a289bc805b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/1400822e4ef8ac0a78cd698b709b14a289bc805b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/4bb11578be10bbec470eeaaabc0cdb8778eca075/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T22:16:55Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T05:16:56Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Stop next dev writing a second working agreement into ui/\n\n`next dev` generates `ui/AGENTS.md` and `ui/CLAUDE.md` and leaves them behind.\nThe catalog''s convention is that AGENTS.md is the working agreement and it is\nthe ONLY one, with no tool-specific alias, and this repo already carries its own\nat the root: the generated pair is a second agreement plus exactly the alias\nthe convention forbids. The generated prose also contains an em-dash, which\nthe catalog''s house style forbids in shipped markdown.\n\nBoth files were already on disk here, kept out of sight by a .gitignore entry\nthat this removes. Hiding a generated file is not the same as not generating\none, and an ignored file is precisely the file that cannot show up in\n`git status` on the day the flag stops working.\nDeleting them by hand does not hold either, because the next `next dev` writes\nthem again. This is a template defect, not a per-repo one.\n\n`agentRules` is a top-level NextConfig option in the pinned next 16.3.x, not an\nexperimental one (config-shared.d.ts, default true; the writer is\nserver/lib/generate-agent-files.js, called behind an isDev check, which is why\nthe CI production build never surfaced it). Setting it false in\nui/next.config.mjs turns the generation off at the source.\n\nThe guard lives in\ntests/unit/test_ui_agent_documents.py, a new module,\nand has two halves. Asserting the flag catches its removal; asserting both\nfiles are ABSENT catches a framework bump that renames or drops the option,\nwhich the flag assertion alone would sail straight through.\n\nSame change as hex-service-template PR 15, which carries the proof: a repo\nrendered, installed and started on the same next version with agent detection\non, before and after. Before, both files and the generation line in the log;\nafter, neither. Verified here by this repo''s own offline gate.","tree":{"sha":"98e2e40932e985f9b24bbaedd17ab71b2019de43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/98e2e40932e985f9b24bbaedd17ab71b2019de43"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/4bb11578be10bbec470eeaaabc0cdb8778eca075","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/4bb11578be10bbec470eeaaabc0cdb8778eca075","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDRiYjExNTc4YmUxMGJiZWM0NzBlZWFhYWJjMGNkYjg3NzhlY2EwNzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/de95c79c8b080ba1ae0388184337105f087eb65b","sha":"de95c79c8b080ba1ae0388184337105f087eb65b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/de95c79c8b080ba1ae0388184337105f087eb65b"}],"sha":"4bb11578be10bbec470eeaaabc0cdb8778eca075","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/4bb11578be10bbec470eeaaabc0cdb8778eca075"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/de95c79c8b080ba1ae0388184337105f087eb65b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T06:44:05Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T06:50:40Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Let mypy see the Google SDKs it had been resolving to nothing\n\nThe hosted `lint_gcp` job type-checks this tree against its RUNTIME lock, which is the only\ncheck in the fleet that can see the cloud adapters at all: the offline gate installs the dev\nlock, which carries no Google Cloud SDK, so mypy resolved `google.*` to nothing and reported\nnothing about the code that talks to the cloud. That job has been **non-blocking** since\n2026-08-30 while its findings were worked through. It is blocking now, and this is the\nrepository half of that promotion.\n\n**What was left before this could happen was upstream typing, and the answer is MORE type\nchecking rather than a suppression.** Two settings, in this repository''s own `pyproject.toml`\nrather than in the CI runner:\n\n* **`follow_untyped_imports = true`, scoped to `google.*`.** mypy now ANALYSES a dependency\n  that ships no `py.typed` instead of skipping it. Measured rather than argued: a bogus method\n  planted on a `google.cloud.storage` client is reported by **nothing** under the old\n  configuration and is an `attr-defined` error under this one -- the same defect class that\n  turned out to be real in `disputes-chargebacks-manager`, which called a `SessionsClient`\n  method that does not exist.\n* **`untyped_calls_exclude = [\"google\"]`.** This drops one complaint -- *\"this callee has no\n  annotations\"* -- and nothing else. `disallow_untyped_calls` exists to stop typed code calling\n  OUR untyped code; aimed at a third-party release it is a demand no work in this repository can\n  satisfy, and proto-plus generates every message `__init__` without annotations. Falsified\n  before it was trusted: with the exclusion in place, a planted nonexistent method still reports\n  `attr-defined` and a planted wrong argument type still reports `arg-type` naming the real\n  expected type.\n\n**They live here and not in the runner on purpose.** Two checks reading different configuration\nis what produced the one-line contradiction that blocked this promotion for a day: in\n`human-review-console` a `# type: ignore` was REQUIRED by the offline gate and reported UNUSED by\nlint-gcp. The offline gate and the hosted job now read the same `[tool.mypy]` and differ only in\nwhich packages are installed, which is the property the SDK declaration in this file already\nexisted to hold.\n\n**The scope on `follow_untyped_imports` is not tidiness.** Set globally it also follows the 3.14\nstandard library, where mypy 2.3.1 cannot parse CPython''s own `annotationlib.py`: `agent-registry`\nreported `Invalid syntax` in a standard-library file and **checked nothing at all**. That was\nfound by running all fifty-two trees rather than the three the shape had been validated on.\n`google.protobuf.*` is then excluded from following INSIDE that scope, because a generated `_pb2`\nmodule builds its classes at import time through a descriptor builder, so mypy reading the source\nreports `Module has no attribute \"Timestamp\"` for a class that plainly exists.\n\n**The mypy floor was legacy and is raised to `>=2.3.1`.** `>=1.10` was not neutral: both settings\nabove arrived in mypy 1.14, so the floor permitted a resolution that would not understand the\nfile configuring it. The lock already pins `mypy==2.3.1`, so this was latent rather than live.\n\nWhat this tree reports now, both checks, cold cache:\n\n| check | environment | result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `lint_gcp` | runtime lock (`requirements-gcp.lock`) | `Success: no issues found in 92 source files` |\n| offline gate | dev lock (`requirements-dev.lock`) | `Success: no issues found in 92 source files` |\n\nGate:  589 passed, 1 deselected.","tree":{"sha":"a6941419e76a295f5b8b9a9034931f38d0d337ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/a6941419e76a295f5b8b9a9034931f38d0d337ee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/de95c79c8b080ba1ae0388184337105f087eb65b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/de95c79c8b080ba1ae0388184337105f087eb65b","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKGRlOTVjNzljOGIwODBiYTFhZTAzODgxODQzMzcxMDVmMDg3ZWI2NWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/0cb1d7a13dac4ec716ad86028fadb95425932a26","sha":"0cb1d7a13dac4ec716ad86028fadb95425932a26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/0cb1d7a13dac4ec716ad86028fadb95425932a26"}],"sha":"de95c79c8b080ba1ae0388184337105f087eb65b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/de95c79c8b080ba1ae0388184337105f087eb65b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/0cb1d7a13dac4ec716ad86028fadb95425932a26/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T01:41:01Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T01:52:32Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Compare each declared MCP schema against the arguments its handler reads\n\n`test_mcp_surface_is_served_and_packaged.py` already pins the tool NAMES in both\ndirections, and `hex_service_kit.mcpserve.bind` refuses to start on a name mismatch.\nNeither says anything about the PAYLOAD. A tool can be declared, bound, served and still\ndescribe arguments its handler never reads, or read arguments the caller was never told\nto send.\n\nThat is the defect the portfolio backlog recorded twice about one tool in\n`loan-document-intelligence`: `cross_validate` was narrowed once from an unresolvable\n`extract_ids` to a REQUIRED `documents` array, and the callable ignored `documents`\nentirely. Both narrowings were done by READING, and reading is what missed it the second\ntime. So the new test compares the two sides mechanically.\n\nThe handlers take `**arguments`, so there is no signature to check a schema against. What\nthere is, and what decides the outcome of a call, is which keys the handler actually reads\nout of that bag. That is read from the AST rather than by calling anything, because the\nhandlers are closures over a live container and this has to hold under the offline gate.\nKeys reached through a helper taking `arguments` count as read by every handler that calls\nit, transitively; a handler declaring its bag `**_` reads nothing on purpose and its schema\nmust declare no properties.\n\nRun across the fourteen trees that serve a catalog, it reported findings in seven. This is\none of them.\n\nThis tree was already clean: the check is added as a regression guard, not because\nanything here was wrong.\n\nFalsified rather than assumed. Restoring the pre-fix narrow declaration on\n`credit-memo-drafting`''s `peer_compare` makes the check fail with the exact sentence above,\nand putting it back clears it, so a passing run is evidence rather than silence. The\n`test_the_ast_walk_finds_the_handlers_it_is_supposed_to_check` case guards the other way: if\nthe walk and the served handler roster ever disagree, every remaining assertion would be\nchecking a different set of tools than the one served, and it says so instead.\n\nGate: 589 passed, 1 deselected.","tree":{"sha":"af9b1bc5a988462c6fac8fa2d872c34aced2efdf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/af9b1bc5a988462c6fac8fa2d872c34aced2efdf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/0cb1d7a13dac4ec716ad86028fadb95425932a26","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/0cb1d7a13dac4ec716ad86028fadb95425932a26","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDBjYjFkN2ExM2RhYzRlYzcxNmFkODYwMjhmYWRiOTU0MjU5MzJhMjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/a0988ba854fe785547bc187be9d08667eede2d9d","sha":"a0988ba854fe785547bc187be9d08667eede2d9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/a0988ba854fe785547bc187be9d08667eede2d9d"}],"sha":"0cb1d7a13dac4ec716ad86028fadb95425932a26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/0cb1d7a13dac4ec716ad86028fadb95425932a26"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/a0988ba854fe785547bc187be9d08667eede2d9d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T14:20:42Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T14:28:00Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Every page states where it runs and which model answers\n\nThe companion half of the org decision of 2026-08-30. This gate is demonstrated on a laptop\nand on the deployment, sometimes in the same hour, and a screenshot of one is\nindistinguishable from the other. A viewer who cannot tell which they are looking at\ncannot tell whether what they are reading came from a real managed service or a\ndeterministic offline stub, and that is exactly the confusion an audit-first pitch\ncannot afford. So the page says it, always, instead of the presenter saying it\nsometimes.\n\n/healthz now answers `runtime` and `generator_model`, and the console renders both at\nthe top of every page. The banner is mounted in the LAYOUT rather than in a page,\nbecause \"at the top of every page\" is a property of the console and a page that forgot\nit would be the one page a screenshot came from. It renders in EMBED mode too, and\nembedded is the mode that needs it most: a panel inside somebody else''s portal is\nwhere a viewer has least context about where the answer came from.\n\nNeither value is inferred in the browser. A console that read its runtime from\n`window.location` would be right until the deployment served through a proxy and wrong\nsilently after that, so the service is asked and the service answers. `runtime` is\nderived from the profile, and `onprem` reads `local` deliberately: it runs on the\nadopter''s own iron, and \"running on GCP\" is the one sentence that deployment must\nnever print.\n\nThe banner renders null until the service has answered, and null again if it never\ndoes. Defaulting to \"running locally\" during the fetch would state a falsehood on\nevery deployment page load; a failed health call is already reported by the console''s\nown error surface, and chrome that guessed would be asserting provenance it does not\nhave.\n\nThe canonical component and the healthz contract now ship in hex-service-template, so\na newly scaffolded repo gets both without this being re-derived.","tree":{"sha":"47b922a44e046b4b5661de413f24ec83b995c13e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/47b922a44e046b4b5661de413f24ec83b995c13e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/a0988ba854fe785547bc187be9d08667eede2d9d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/a0988ba854fe785547bc187be9d08667eede2d9d","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKGEwOTg4YmE4NTRmZTc4NTU0N2JjMTg3YmU5ZDA4NjY3ZWVkZTJkOWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/1e03ff392d567717f88fa9fcbe6d80ef98411f41","sha":"1e03ff392d567717f88fa9fcbe6d80ef98411f41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/1e03ff392d567717f88fa9fcbe6d80ef98411f41"}],"sha":"a0988ba854fe785547bc187be9d08667eede2d9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/a0988ba854fe785547bc187be9d08667eede2d9d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/1e03ff392d567717f88fa9fcbe6d80ef98411f41/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T01:25:57Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T01:34:25Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Name the MCP Tool field input_schema\n\nThe field is `input_schema`; `inputSchema` is its pydantic alias. Passing the alias\nworks at runtime and dumps identically on the wire, so this is drift against a compat\nshim rather than a live break -- but a type-checker that can see the `mcp` package\nrejects the keyword, and this tree''s dev lock cannot see it either.","tree":{"sha":"f959a1e1dd832937fe9d6dce0faa5acecf2c8dcb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/f959a1e1dd832937fe9d6dce0faa5acecf2c8dcb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/1e03ff392d567717f88fa9fcbe6d80ef98411f41","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/1e03ff392d567717f88fa9fcbe6d80ef98411f41","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDFlMDNmZjM5MmQ1Njc3MTdmODhmYTlmY2JlNmQ4MGVmOTg0MTFmNDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/59e26a57aca25798e8ffada23750f9735015a6e8","sha":"59e26a57aca25798e8ffada23750f9735015a6e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/59e26a57aca25798e8ffada23750f9735015a6e8"}],"sha":"1e03ff392d567717f88fa9fcbe6d80ef98411f41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/1e03ff392d567717f88fa9fcbe6d80ef98411f41"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/59e26a57aca25798e8ffada23750f9735015a6e8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T01:25:57Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T01:34:25Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Copy the verified IAP claims into a dict\n\n`id_token.verify_token` returns a `Mapping[str, Any]`, not a `dict`. The annotation\non this line claimed a dict, so a type-checker that can actually see `google.oauth2`\nreports an assignment error. This tree''s own gate never saw it: the dev lock carries\nno google-auth, so mypy resolved the module to `Any` and said nothing.\n\nCopying into a dict is what `hex-service-template` and the rest of the fleet already\ndo, and what `cdd-sow-research` documents in place: callers own a mutable snapshot of\nthe claims rather than the SDK''s view of them. Behaviour is unchanged.\n\nFalsified first: against the previous line the checker reports the error, against this\none it does not.","tree":{"sha":"126e26531d796a9309abcdab539aa6905f1ba7ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/126e26531d796a9309abcdab539aa6905f1ba7ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/59e26a57aca25798e8ffada23750f9735015a6e8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/59e26a57aca25798e8ffada23750f9735015a6e8","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDU5ZTI2YTU3YWNhMjU3OThlOGZmYWRhMjM3NTBmOTczNTAxNWE2ZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/8f7e49df8167b6093300808ad6ebb76938850911","sha":"8f7e49df8167b6093300808ad6ebb76938850911","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/8f7e49df8167b6093300808ad6ebb76938850911"}],"sha":"59e26a57aca25798e8ffada23750f9735015a6e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/59e26a57aca25798e8ffada23750f9735015a6e8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/8f7e49df8167b6093300808ad6ebb76938850911/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T14:17:42Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T14:38:24Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Adopt hex-service-kit v0.0.6\n\nThe 0.0.6 identity knobs -- machine_tenants, subject_from, refuse_unmapped_tenant and a\nhuman-subject allowlist -- have been released and unadopted since 2026-08-28. Every one\ndefaults to what this repository already does, so this bump is the version move and\nnothing else: no behaviour changes until an adopter says so.\n\nThe lockfiles pin the 40-character commit the tag resolved to, not the tag, so what\ninstalls cannot change without a diff.","tree":{