2812aa5970bf78d413f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/8db427ee0879fc726f2cbecddfe34f15ce8d58e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T22:51:00Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T22:57:33Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Move the MCP surface to the 2026-07-28 stateless era\n\nMCP 2026-07-28 removed the initialize handshake and protocol-level sessions,\nmade server/discover mandatory, and added required resultType, ttlMs and\ncacheScope fields. This repo declared 2025-11-25, the newest revision of the\nera that replaced, so it described a protocol the fleet no longer speaks.\n\n- Declare MCP_PROTOCOL_VERSION = \"2026-07-28\", added where the revision was\n  previously stated only in prose.\n- mcp>=1.2 becomes mcp>=2.1. The 1.x SDK predates the stateless era and cannot\n  speak it, so the old floor permitted a resolution that silently reinstates\n  the handshake this revision removed.\n- a2a-sdk>=0.2 becomes >=1.1. Not verified against a real 1.x install: it lives\n  in the gcp extra, which the offline gate deliberately does not install.","tree":{"sha":"fd46ed89ebfd3c6be182d83506749712e3ba90b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/fd46ed89ebfd3c6be182d83506749712e3ba90b0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/8db427ee0879fc726f2cbecddfe34f15ce8d58e1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/8db427ee0879fc726f2cbecddfe34f15ce8d58e1","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh9_9oAKDhkYjQyN2VlMDg3OWZjNzI2ZjJjYmVjZGRmZTM0ZjE1Y2U4ZDU4ZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commit/64d2386e30617e0ef74ce2e3068db16e0ebbc4d6","sha":"64d2386e30617e0ef74ce2e3068db16e0ebbc4d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/64d2386e30617e0ef74ce2e3068db16e0ebbc4d6"}],"sha":"8db427ee0879fc726f2cbecddfe34f15ce8d58e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/8db427ee0879fc726f2cbecddfe34f15ce8d58e1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/64d2386e30617e0ef74ce2e3068db16e0ebbc4d6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T16:03:53Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T16:03:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Record the IAP refusal-split evidence in the C1 audit row (#17)\n\nThe three IAP refusals closed in #15 were never written into\n`docs/practices-audit.md`, and the workspace rule is that a change which closes a practice\ncheck records its evidence there, saying what was observed failing first. This does that and\nnothing else. C1 keeps its PASS verdict: nothing regressed, the evidence behind it was simply\nmissing.\n\nThe row now names the refusal shapes an operator actually got, the exception types that\nreplaced them (`IapAudienceUnconfiguredError` and `IapVerifierUnavailableError`, both\n`EndUserAuthUnavailableError` subclasses carrying `http_status` 503), the subclass-ordering\nhazard in `api/security.py`, and `tests/unit/test_iap_refusal_split.py` as the guard.\n\n## Observed failing first\n\nReproduced offline in a throwaway worktree at `def8691^`, with no cloud SDK, no credential and\nno network:\n\n```\naudience unset, assertion present : IdentityError: MKT_GOV_IAP_AUDIENCE is not configured; cannot verify IAP assertion\naudience unset, bare curl         : IdentityError: MKT_GOV_IAP_AUDIENCE is not configured; cannot verify IAP assertion\nheader is ''   ''                   : IdentityError: assertion is not a compact JWS or JWE, so it carries no readable algorithm header\ngoogle-auth blocked               : ModuleNotFoundError: No module named ''google.auth.transport''\n```\n\nThe audience was already checked before the header here, so the bare curl did\nname the unset variable. What it did not do was carry a status that said the fault was the\ndeployment''s.\n\n`api/security.py` answered 401 \"authentication required\" for the first two alike, so an\noperator was told authentication had failed when no credential would have helped.\n\nThree further observations, same worktree method:\n\n* `tests/unit/test_iap_refusal_split.py` does not import against that tree at all: neither\n  `EndUserAuthUnavailableError` nor the two `Iap*Error` types existed.\n* With only those types injected and the pre-fix behaviour left standing: 8 failed, 3 passed.\n* On the fixed tree with the two `except` branches in `api/security.py` reordered: 1 failed,\n  10 passed, and the one failure is\n  `test_the_api_answers_a_deployment_failure_with_its_own_status_and_message`, answering 401\n  where 503 is owed. That is the subclass-ordering hazard, executed.\n\nDocumentation only. No source, test or lockfile is touched.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e5baf2912e71433e3c1652b9ffe467071e0bd14e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/e5baf2912e71433e3c1652b9ffe467071e0bd14e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/64d2386e30617e0ef74ce2e3068db16e0ebbc4d6","verification":{"payload":"tree e5baf2912e71433e3c1652b9ffe467071e0bd14e\nparent 333f604fa66ba5ac8d4463900e2673dfc44f5bb7\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787673833 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787673833 +0800\n\nRecord the IAP refusal-split evidence in the C1 audit row (#17)\n\nThe three IAP refusals closed in #15 were never written into\n`docs/practices-audit.md`, and the workspace rule is that a change which closes a practice\ncheck records its evidence there, saying what was observed failing first. This does that and\nnothing else. C1 keeps its PASS verdict: nothing regressed, the evidence behind it was simply\nmissing.\n\nThe row now names the refusal shapes an operator actually got, the exception types that\nreplaced them (`IapAudienceUnconfiguredError` and `IapVerifierUnavailableError`, both\n`EndUserAuthUnavailableError` subclasses carrying `http_status` 503), the subclass-ordering\nhazard in `api/security.py`, and `tests/unit/test_iap_refusal_split.py` as the guard.\n\n## Observed failing first\n\nReproduced offline in a throwaway worktree at `def8691^`, with no cloud SDK, no credential and\nno network:\n\n```\naudience unset, assertion present : IdentityError: MKT_GOV_IAP_AUDIENCE is not configured; cannot verify IAP assertion\naudience unset, bare curl         : IdentityError: MKT_GOV_IAP_AUDIENCE is not configured; cannot verify IAP assertion\nheader is ''   ''                   : IdentityError: assertion is not a compact JWS or JWE, so it carries no readable algorithm header\ngoogle-auth blocked               : ModuleNotFoundError: No module named ''google.auth.transport''\n```\n\nThe audience was already checked before the header here, so the bare curl did\nname the unset variable. What it did not do was carry a status that said the fault was the\ndeployment''s.\n\n`api/security.py` answered 401 \"authentication required\" for the first two alike, so an\noperator was told authentication had failed when no credential would have helped.\n\nThree further observations, same worktree method:\n\n* `tests/unit/test_iap_refusal_split.py` does not import against that tree at all: neither\n  `EndUserAuthUnavailableError` nor the two `Iap*Error` types existed.\n* With only those types injected and the pre-fix behaviour left standing: 8 failed, 3 passed.\n* On the fixed tree with the two `except` branches in `api/security.py` reordered: 1 failed,\n  10 passed, and the one failure is\n  `test_the_api_answers_a_deployment_failure_with_its_own_status_and_message`, answering 401\n  where 503 is owed. That is the subclass-ordering hazard, executed.\n\nDocumentation only. No source, test or lockfile is touched.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbzpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqj8QAGGs2QpyxIyBvvgrMi6EcRFJ\n4IvEsgSZdWW6Jrg8gDpNBOB78bwiroTXo02o+J7bffvKzd+fS8JqgS7Jw3CQ9fYt\n/xSs+px/cUC9+4LFUYZR8k917+G1HcXy738fZCvfGYAns/WfNu0bZgm5kSTUmGlm\nalMQPwKhi3K2cMWZ0WA7W7GfHfxLIriIqhzy963DLEaaZ8LCN8Hb/J1SUMp6rhXi\nca95Lxx4uJUH3ZCbpuiiAf+YD8cunmQxWQQHp4cVykBofffUEG+QxG5VbRcVMlbv\nxpmH0OngYiV5z5B3osS9il8FL0+is4e9tFpk2nVRpjH+91CWMHi+owLcFka4+2kZ\nf6zHK4QtYdWCgx7u6X74NcHLn1pwzlLaHO4SpX04S7+2absreDUF6tcYQfDSzngS\nIrvZax9f4thQZ/XqOwfCyKojPkO2tSuWy9FjTX0ocxbsCS1CVJWc3oR1O6TZLZrY\nX+L+CrsQHf3aR2QQqmT64tFUdMwZrsj3EFph4jMv4fZckOEswWNuAh+cwMVOytBm\nH1rXVzhnIWJqeaZptjqX