nts{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/333f604fa66ba5ac8d4463900e2673dfc44f5bb7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:51:20Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:51:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Pin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#16)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","tree":{"sha":"51f7ae106faf64027d4221f1497a0d1515b08485","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/51f7ae106faf64027d4221f1497a0d1515b08485"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/333f604fa66ba5ac8d4463900e2673dfc44f5bb7","verification":{"payload":"tree 51f7ae106faf64027d4221f1497a0d1515b08485\nparent def869130dcbf72f302b6dea921725717b1bb0d1\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787673080 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787673080 +0800\n\nPin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#16)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbn4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACUkQAI2/uvk2KVSVuuC9F6z9azGV\nSoi0BEP091z2m24KNJn5bk57bjIjkEJyjSxdMcEG7A0sAk7QP52KfNQVTbr7pQdE\nEj2+gZQQKKRkAd+sxyiv1jr7Wln5okUAA73NldzMQFXX7LQvv8NYnm/W4ZV/DdsW\nmGycfViVhqnnizjtA2zRd8Z02Q093hfJ0fDT86F24SttRbuCpWiY2k1uPDcaJXcZ\nJ8Cnd0eZHqn1P78eFpCdh/elssthk7uTOdd/0EijA+xBT8vRDzRysdM7ZOT57YNO\nT5pI7kr0Ic1S1Sx1uRMMB5rEI0tkVkZZon9nRS6phxyGBLiamgUhqTQ7pQsQr9eU\nijBucVG5iX50pYfYxNmhcsUKqgoQG4cR8wcAorOIgsfR4k+XIbdrqUPwK2l/rUkM\n30oMKw8HPTtR9C9k4vTBUCnmw3vJQUXS