ar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/commits/def869130dcbf72f302b6dea921725717b1bb0d1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:18:53Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:18:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Close the three IAP refusal gaps and bind the transport facts to v0.0.3 (#15)\n\nThis repository carries adapters/gcp/iap_identity.py, the earlier of the two IAP adapter shapes\nin this fleet. Measured against adapters/gcp/identity.py, which most of the fleet carries, it was\nweaker in three ways. All three were reachable with no cloud SDK, no credential and no network,\nand all three are closed here.\n\n**A configuration failure reported as an authentication failure.** An unconfigured audience\nraised a plain IdentityError, which api/security.py answers 401 \"authentication required\". An\noperator reads that and goes hunting for a missing credential; no credential would have helped.\nIt was also checked SECOND, after the assertion header, so the deployment-level failure was only\never reported to callers who already had an assertion. The operator probing with curl and no\nheader got \"missing IAP assertion header\" and learned nothing. The audience check now comes\nfirst and raises IapAudienceUnconfiguredError, an EndUserAuthUnavailableError carrying\nhttp_status 503, and api/security.py answers with that status and that message.\n\n**A whitespace-only header taking a different path.** ctx.header(...) was read without .strip().\nA header a proxy or a deployment template rendered blank is truthy, so it skipped the\nmissing-header refusal and was refused further down by the algorithm pin, which reports a\nmalformed token for what is actually an absent one.\n\n**A missing extra crashing rather than refusing.** The lazy google-auth import sat outside any\ntry. Without the [gcp] extra it raised ModuleNotFoundError out of resolve, past get_principal,\nand FastAPI answered a bare 500 per request. It now raises IapVerifierUnavailableError, also 503.\n\nThe three IAP transport facts are also rebound from hex_service_kit.federation rather than\nre-declared, and the pin moves to @v0.0.3, relocked with org-metadata scripts/fleet-deps.py\nrefresh (commit d28baa1c). No lockfile was hand-edited.\n\n## Observed failing first\n\nAgainst the adapter exactly as it shipped, offline:\n\n    (a) audience unconfigured\n      with an assertion header : IdentityError: <PREFIX>_IAP_AUDIENCE is not configured; cannot verify IAP assertion\n      with NO header (operator): IdentityError: missing IAP assertion header; request did not pass through IAP\n          both plain IdentityError, so api/security.py answers 401 for both\n    (b) header is ''   ''        : IdentityError: assertion is not a compact JWS or JWE, so it carries no readable algorithm header\n          refused as a malformed token, not as a missing one\n    (c) google-auth blocked    : ModuleNotFoundError: No module named ''google.auth.transport''\n          not an IdentityError, so it escapes get_principal: a bare 500\n\ntests/unit/test_iap_refusal_split.py is the same three paths as assertions, plus two that prove\napi/security.py answers the deployment failure 503 with the operator''s message while an ordinary\nrefusal is still a bare 401 that tells a caller nothing they could forge with.\n\n## What is NOT changed\n\nThe fourth difference between the two adapter families, the principals tuple, is deliberately\nleft alone. This adapter grants user:<subject>; the identity.py family grants nothing at all. It\nis THIS one that agrees with hex_service_kit.federation.principal_from_iap_claims, so changing it\ntoward the other family would remove a verified identity''s own principal. The divergence is\nrecorded in the test module rather than closed in the wrong direction.\n\nThis also does not adopt principal_from_iap_claims. Executing this adapter and the kit function\nagainst the same claim sets, with FederationPolicy(tenant_from_hosted_domain=True), shows four\nremaining disagreements, so the tenant and principal half stays local. Details in the wave-2 report.\n\n## Gate\n\nmake gate, exit 0, 544 passed 1 deselected 544 passed 1 deselected. Offline, with the v0.0.3 lock installed.","tree":{"sha":"e2d6a106abec813f22cb62f46dc5cfe92c7fbb97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/trees/e2d6a106abec813f22cb62f46dc5cfe92c7fbb97"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/marketing-compliance-gate/git/commits/def869130dcbf72f302b6dea921725717b1bb0d1","verification":{"payload":"tree e2d6a106abec813f22cb62f46dc5cfe92c7fbb97\nparent 7fb997435f12f05b7dff195f9fa8e2bbd567b419\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787671133 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787671133 +0800\n\nClose the three IAP refusal gaps and bind the transport facts to v0.0.3 (#15)\n\nThis repository carries adapters/gcp/iap_identity.py, the earlier of the two IAP adapter shapes\nin this fleet. Measured against adapters/gcp/identity.py, which most of the fleet carries, it was\nweaker in three ways. All three were reachable with no cloud SDK, no credential and no network,\nand all three are closed here.\n\n**A configuration failure reported as an authentication failure.** An unconfigured audience\nraised a plain IdentityError, which api/security.py answers 401 \"authentication required\". An\noperator reads that and goes hunting for a missing credential; no credential would have helped.\nIt was also checked SECOND, after the assertion header, so the deployment-level failure was only\never reported to callers who already had an assertion. The operator probing with curl and no\nheader got \"missing IAP assertion header\" and learned nothing. The audience check now comes\nfirst and raises IapAudienceUnconfiguredError, an EndUserAuthUnavailableError carrying\nhttp_status 503, and api/security.py answers with that status and that message.\n\n**A whitespace-only header taking a different path.** ctx.header(...) was read without .strip().\nA header a proxy or a deployment template rendered blank is truthy, so it skipped the\nmissing-header refusal and was refused further down by the algorithm pin, which reports a\nmalformed token for what is actually an absent one.\n\n**A missing extra crashing rather than refusing.** The lazy google-auth import sat outside any\ntry. Without the [gcp] extra it raised ModuleNotFoundError out of resolve, past get_principal,\nand FastAPI answered a bare 500 per request. It now raises IapVerifierUnavailableError, also 503.\n\nThe three IAP transport facts are also rebound from hex_service_kit.federation rather than\nre-declared, and the pin moves to @v0.0.3, relocked with org-metadata scripts/fleet-deps.py\nrefresh (commit d28baa1c). No lockfile was hand-edited.\n\n## Observed failing first\n\nAgainst the adapter exactly as it shipped, offline:\n\n    (a) audience unconfigured\n      with an assertion header : IdentityError: <PREFIX>_IAP_AUDIENCE is not configured; cannot verify IAP assertion\n      with NO header (operator): IdentityError: missing IAP assertion header; request did not pass through IAP\n          both plain IdentityError, so api/security.py answers 401 for both\n    (b) header is ''   ''        : IdentityError: assertion is not a compact JWS or JWE, so it carries no readable algorithm header\n          refused as a malformed token, not as a missing one\n    (c) google-auth blocked    : ModuleNotFoundError: No module named ''google.auth.transport''\n          not an IdentityError, so it escapes get_principal: a bare 500\n\ntests/unit/test_iap_refusal_split.py is the same three paths as assertions, plus two that prove\napi/security.py answers the deployment failure 503 with the operator''s message while an ordinary\nrefusal is still a bare 401 that tells a caller nothing they could forge with.\n\n## What is NOT changed\n\nThe fourth difference between the two adapter families, the principals tuple, is deliberately\nleft alone. This adapter grants user:<subject>; the identity.py family grants nothing at all. It\nis THIS one that agrees with hex_service_kit.federation.principal_from_iap_claims, so changing it\ntoward the other family would remove a verified identity''s own principal. The divergence is\nrecorded in the test module rather than closed in the wrong direction.\n\nThis also does not adopt principal_from_iap_claims. Executing this adapter and the kit function\nagainst the same claim sets, with FederationPolicy(tenant_from_hosted_domain=True), shows four\nremaining disagreements, so the tenant and principal half stays local. Details in the wave-2 report.\n\n## Gate\n\nmake gate, exit 0, 544 passed 1 deselected 544 passed 1 deselected. Offline, with the v0.0.3 lock installed.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbJeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcJMQACi6f1283kfO