m/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/e8673262361e454f49f069d71e538d59ecb3d472/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T04:13:44Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T04:23:28Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Make the audit bucket lock a stated choice, not a literal\n\nlogging_worm.tf hard-coded `locked = true` on a bucket whose retention\ndefaults to about seven years, so the first apply of this stack anywhere\nlocked it irreversibly, with no variable a deployment could set to decline.\nThat is the shape the fleet''s 2026-09-12 decision on irreversible controls\nwas written against, and this stack was never swept.\n\nThe lock now reads worm_locked, which has no default, so a plan refuses\nuntil the deployment states it; the tfvars example shows the production\nform. Comments, resource descriptions and docs that said the bucket is\nlocked, or locked by default, now say it is lockable and never defaulted.","tree":{"sha":"4493b918fdfbaf3ece1cdba98056ee467a6fc0b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/4493b918fdfbaf3ece1cdba98056ee467a6fc0b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/e8673262361e454f49f069d71e538d59ecb3d472","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/use