eceived_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/0de43d690918633f582c5b7751c3c5abb769e252/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T22:31:03Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T22:38:39Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Every bar this corpus cannot express is 1.0 now, and says so\n\nA threshold t tolerates a single failure only over at least 1/(1-t) scored\ndecisions. Every bar raised here is scored 0/1 once per case over a corpus far\nshort of that, so each one already required a perfect run while reading as though\nit priced one failure in. 0.99 was not a looser bar than 1.00 over these corpora.\nIt was the same bar with a friendlier face, which is worse than either: a\nreviewer reads it as headroom that does not exist.\n\nEach rubric now carries the arithmetic beside the number: how many decisions the\nmetric scores, what a single failure would give, and how many cases it would take\nbefore a bar below 1.0 meant anything. The last line is the useful one, because\nit says the number to move first is the corpus and not the bar.\n\nFor the safety family it is also what the property means. A leak gate that is\nright 99% of the time is a gate with a hole in it, and there is no acceptable\nlevel of one unredacted identifier reaching an audit record.\n\nFound by org-metadata''s new eval-governance check, which reads every launch-set\nrepository''s rubrics against the promotion authority and could see what no single\nrepository can see about itself.","tree":{"sha":"33c00b9ffd9a73a203c8027be03d7cc28f3cad4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/33c00b9ffd9a73a203c8027be03d7cc28f3cad4e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/0de43d690918633f582c5b7751c3c5abb769e252","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/0de43d690918633f582c5b7751c3c5abb769e252","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh-TdoAKDBkZTQzZDY5MDkxODYzM2Y1ODJjNWI3NzUxYzNjNWFiYjc2OWUyNTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/3e88438dcbfc9ce3a2b3ce3bef3d7c908d1e646e","sha":"3e88438dcbfc9ce3a2b3ce3bef3d7c908d1e646e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/3e88438dcbfc9ce3a2b3ce3bef3d7c908d1e646e"}],"sha":"0de43d690918633f582c5b7751c3c5abb769e252","url":"https