i.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/a0baf89d018282dbebf44262ca98f64902a4143a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T10:56:30Z","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dependabot[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T07:55:12Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Bump the npm-minor-patch group across 1 directory with 7 updates\n\nBumps the npm-minor-patch group with 7 updates in the /ui directory:\n\n| Package | From | To |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [next](https://github.com/vercel/next.js) | `16.3.0` | `16.3.3` |\n| [react](https://github.com/react/react/tree/HEAD/packages/react) | `19.2.7` | `19.2.8` |\n| [@types/react](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/react) | `19.2.17` | `19.2.18` |\n| [react-dom](https://github.com/react/react/tree/HEAD/packages/react-dom) | `19.2.7` | `19.2.8` |\n| [@types/react-dom](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/react-dom) | `19.2.3` | `19.2.5` |\n| [@types/node](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/tree/HEAD/types/node) | `26.2.0` | `26.4.0` |\n| [typescript](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript) | `5.5.3` | `5.9.3` |\n\n\n\nUpdates `next` from 16.3.0 to 16.3.3\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/vercel/next.js/compare/v16.3.0...v16.3.3)\n\nUpdates `react` from 19.2.7 to 19.2.8\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/react/react/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/react/react/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/react/react/commits/v19.2.8/packages/react)\n\nUpdates `@types/react` from 19.2.17 to 19.2.18\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/react)\n\nUpdates `react-dom` from 19.2.7 to 19.2.8\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/react/react/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/react/react/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/react/react/commits/v19.2.8/packages/react-dom)\n\nUpdates `@types/react-dom` from 19.2.3 to 19.2.5\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/react-dom)\n\nUpdates `@types/node` from 26.2.0 to 26.4.0\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/node)\n\nUpdates `@types/react` from 19.2.17 to 19.2.18\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/react)\n\nUpdates `@types/react-dom` from 19.2.3 to 19.2.5\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped/commits/HEAD/types/react-dom)\n\nUpdates `typescript` from 5.5.3 to 5.9.3\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/compare/v5.5.3...v5.9.3)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: \"@types/node\"\n  dependency-version: 26.3.0\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: \"@types/react\"\n  dependency-version: 19.2.18\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: \"@types/react\"\n  dependency-version: 19.2.18\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: \"@types/react-dom\"\n  dependency-version: 19.2.5\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: \"@types/react-dom\"\n  dependency-version: 19.2.5\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: next\n  dependency-version: 16.3.2\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: react\n  dependency-version: 19.2.8\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: react-dom\n  dependency-version: 19.2.8\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-patch\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n- dependency-name: typescript\n  dependency-version: 5.9.3\n  dependency-type: direct:development\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n  dependency-group: npm-minor-patch\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>","tree":{"sha":"3a5de7b3da2f1fb0f910011b32de794ef497b91a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/3a5de7b3da2f1fb0f910011b32de794ef497b91a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/a0baf89d018282dbebf44262ca98f64902a4143a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/a0baf89d018282dbebf44262ca98f64902a4143a","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh-TdoAKGEwYmFmODlkMDE4MjgyZGJlYmY0NDI2MmNhOThmNjQ5MDJhNDE0M2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/f346e6ea3a8473ac1198ffab435be2b92b0f9502","sha":"f346e6ea3a8473ac1198ffab435be2b92b0f9502","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/f346e6ea3a8473ac1198ffab435be2b92b0f9502"}],"sha":"a0baf89d018282dbebf44262ca98f64902a4143a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/a0baf89d018282dbebf44262ca98f64902a4143a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/f346e6ea3a8473ac1198ffab435be2b92b0f9502/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T22:15:49Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-01T05:15:33Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Stop next dev writing a second working agreement into ui/\n\n`next dev` generates `ui/AGENTS.md` and `ui/CLAUDE.md` and leaves them behind.\nThe catalog''s convention is that AGENTS.md is the working agreement and it is\nthe ONLY one, with no tool-specific alias, and this repo already carries its own\nat the root: the generated pair is a second agreement plus exactly the alias\nthe convention forbids. The generated prose also contains an em-dash, which\nthe catalog''s house style forbids in shipped markdown.\n\nBoth files were already on disk here, kept out of sight by a .gitignore entry\nthat this removes. Hiding a generated file is not the same as not generating\none, and an ignored file is precisely the file that cannot show up in\n`git status` on the day the flag stops working.\nDeleting them by hand does not hold either, because the next `next dev` writes\nthem again. This is a template defect, not a per-repo one.\n\n`agentRules` is a top-level NextConfig option in the pinned next 16.3.x, not an\nexperimental one (config-shared.d.ts, default true; the writer is\nserver/lib/generate-agent-files.js, called behind an isDev check, which is why\nthe CI production build never surfaced it). Setting it false in\nui/next.config.mjs turns the generation off at the source.\n\nThe guard lives in\ntests/unit/test_ui_agent_documents.py, a new module,\nand has two halves. Asserting the flag catches its removal; asserting both\nfiles are ABSENT catches a framework bump that renames or drops the option,\nwhich the flag assertion alone would sail straight through.\n\nSame change as hex-service-template PR 15, which carries the proof: a repo\nrendered, installed and started on the same next version with agent detection\non, before and after. Before, both files and the generation line in the log;\nafter, neither. Verified here by this repo''s own offline gate.","tree":{"sha":"55eb6f947158cecb90036e4a14d552f5a178e0dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/55eb6f947158cecb90036e4a14d552f5a178e0dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/f346e6ea3a8473ac1198ffab435be2b92b0f9502","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/f346e6ea3a8473ac1198ffab435be2b92b0f9502","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh-TdoAKGYzNDZlNmVhM2E4NDczYWMxMTk4ZmZhYjQzNWJlMmI5MmIwZjk1MDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/164c861cbdcd96924a82d9405ac6063944c0c997","sha":"164c861cbdcd96924a82d9405ac6063944c0c997","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/164c861cbdcd96924a82d9405ac6063944c0c997"}],"sha":"f346e6ea3a8473ac1198ffab435be2b92b0f9502","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/f346e6ea3a8473ac1198ffab435be2b92b0f9502"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/164c861cbdcd96924a82d9405ac6063944c0c997/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T06:43:05Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T06:48:54Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Let mypy see the Google SDKs it had been resolving to nothing\n\nThe hosted `lint_gcp` job type-checks this tree against its RUNTIME lock, which is the only\ncheck in the fleet that can see the cloud adapters at all: the offline gate installs the dev\nlock, which carries no Google Cloud SDK, so mypy resolved `google.*` to nothing and reported\nnothing about the code that talks to the cloud. That job has been **non-blocking** since\n2026-08-30 while its findings were worked through. It is blocking now, and this is the\nrepository half of that promotion.\n\n**What was left before this could happen was upstream typing, and the answer is MORE type\nchecking rather than a suppression.** Two settings, in this repository''s own `pyproject.toml`\nrather than in the CI runner:\n\n* **`follow_untyped_imports = true`, scoped to `google.*`.** mypy now ANALYSES a dependency\n  that ships no `py.typed` instead of skipping it. Measured rather than argued: a bogus method\n  planted on a `google.cloud.storage` client is reported by **nothing** under the old\n  configuration and is an `attr-defined` error under this one -- the same defect class that\n  turned out to be real in `disputes-chargebacks-manager`, which called a `SessionsClient`\n  method that does not exist.\n* **`untyped_calls_exclude = [\"google\"]`.** This drops one complaint -- *\"this callee has no\n  annotations\"* -- and nothing else. `disallow_untyped_calls` exists to stop typed code calling\n  OUR untyped code; aimed at a third-party release it is a demand no work in this repository can\n  satisfy, and proto-plus generates every message `__init__` without annotations. Falsified\n  before it was trusted: with the exclusion in place, a planted nonexistent method still reports\n  `attr-defined` and a planted wrong argument type still reports `arg-type` naming the real\n  expected type.\n\n**They live here and not in the runner on purpose.** Two checks reading different configuration\nis what produced the one-line contradiction that blocked this promotion for a day: in\n`human-review-console` a `# type: ignore` was REQUIRED by the offline gate and reported UNUSED by\nlint-gcp. The offline gate and the hosted job now read the same `[tool.mypy]` and differ only in\nwhich packages are installed, which is the property the SDK declaration in this file already\nexisted to hold.\n\n**The scope on `follow_untyped_imports` is not tidiness.** Set globally it also follows the 3.14\nstandard library, where mypy 2.3.1 cannot parse CPython''s own `annotationlib.py`: `agent-registry`\nreported `Invalid syntax` in a standard-library file and **checked nothing at all**. That was\nfound by running all fifty-two trees rather than the three the shape had been validated on.\n`google.protobuf.*` is then excluded from following INSIDE that scope, because a generated `_pb2`\nmodule builds its classes at import time through a descriptor builder, so mypy reading the source\nreports `Module has no attribute \"Timestamp\"` for a class that plainly exists.\n\n**The mypy floor was legacy and is raised to `>=2.3.1`.** `>=1.10` was not neutral: both settings\nabove arrived in mypy 1.14, so the floor permitted a resolution that would not understand the\nfile configuring it. The lock already pins `mypy==2.3.1`, so this was latent rather than live.\n\nWhat this tree reports now, both checks, cold cache:\n\n| check | environment | result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `lint_gcp` | runtime lock (`requirements-gcp.lock`) | `Success: no issues found in 87 source files` |\n| offline gate | dev lock (`requirements-dev.lock`) | `Success: no issues found in 87 source files` |\n\nGate:  415 passed, 1 deselected.","tree":{"sha":"ae34ab053f9667d7ec872eb266876e3dee10d7df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/ae34ab053f9667d7ec872eb266876e3dee10d7df"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/164c861cbdcd96924a82d9405ac6063944c0c997","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/164c861cbdcd96924a82d9405ac6063944c0c997","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh-TdoAKDE2NGM4NjFjYmRjZDk2OTI0YTgyZDk0MDVhYzYwNjM5NDRjMGM5OTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/853ea93cf040cad1ad7b6203733ba48a7a14eb6b","sha":"853ea93cf040cad1ad7b6203733ba48a7a14eb6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/853ea93cf040cad1ad7b6203733ba48a7a14eb6b"}],"sha":"164c861cbdcd96924a82d9405ac6063944c0c997","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/164c861cbdcd96924a82d9405ac6063944c0c997"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/853ea93cf040cad1ad7b6203733ba48a7a14eb6b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T03:54:51Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T04:03:53Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Read the managed model id from where each service actually keeps it\n\nThe provenance banner resolved the managed model id from a constant declared on the\nbound adapter, and **twenty-five of thirty-eight trees answered `managed-model-unnamed`**.\n\nReading them showed the resolver was looking in the wrong place rather than the trees being\nsilent. Most of the fleet pins the id in SETTINGS, under a name chosen per repository:\n`models.reasoning`, `narrator_model`, `generation_model`, `narration_model`, `drafting_model`.\nOne kept it as a literal inside the model call. Twelve bind a managed adapter that is a\ndeployment-wired placeholder and raises rather than generating, so there is no model to name.\n\n`_GENERATOR_MODEL_ATTR` now names that settings path once per tree, beside `_GENERATOR_PORT`,\nand the resolver reads it before falling back to an adapter constant. The banner reads the same\nvalue the adapter passes to the model call rather than a second copy that drifts.\n\nThis tree keeps its id at `Settings.models.reasoning`.\n\nWhat this tree now reports:\n\n| profile | `runtime` | `generator_model` |\n|---|---|---|\n| `local` | `local` | `deterministic-offline-stub` |\n| `gcp` | `gcp` | `gemini-3.5-flash` |\n| `onprem` | `local` | `onprem-not-implemented` |\n\n**Two answers replace the placeholder, because they say different things.**\n`managed-not-implemented` means the managed path refuses rather than generating.\n`managed-model-unset` means the settings field exists and this deployment has not pinned a\nmodel — actionable, and different from a repository that names none. `managed-model-unnamed`\nsurvives only as a defensive fallback and **no tree reaches it any more.**\n\n**`managed-not-implemented` is the only answer that is INFERRED rather than read, so it\nis the only one that can be wrong**, and it now has a guard: a tree claiming it must not call a\nmodel API. That guard took three attempts, and each failure was found by falsifying rather than\nby reading:\n\n1. Asserting the adapter \"raises\" passed a deliberately broken `soc-fraud-fusion`, which\n   generates and also raises on bad input. Too weak.\n2. It had already let a real mis-classification through. **`conversation-qa-scorecard` calls\n   `generate_content`** and raises only when its model is unconfigured; it had been grouped with\n   the placeholders on the strength of that raise. Its model is named now, and its banner reports\n   `gemini-3.5-flash` instead of claiming the path is unimplemented.\n3. The check read the DEFAULT profile, where the answer is the offline stub, so it returned\n   before checking anything and passed the broken tree again. It reads the managed profile now.\n\nFalsified in both directions at the end: clearing `soc-fraud-fusion`''s settings path makes it\nfail with *\"reports managed-not-implemented but calls ''generate_content''\"*, and restoring it\nclears it.\n\nGate: 415 passed, 1 deselected.","tree":{"sha":"3c53401da1a197bd718dea6ab329e94b558bafb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/3c53401da1a197bd718dea6ab329e94b558bafb0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/853ea93cf040cad1ad7b6203733ba48a7a14eb6b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/853ea93cf040cad1ad7b6203733ba48a7a14eb6b","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh-TdoAKDg1M2VhOTNjZjA0MGNhZDFhZDdiNjIwMzczM2JhNDhhN2ExNGViNmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/9c90154ee4cc6d739ed69842617f1d823b041f8d","sha":"9c90154ee4cc6d739ed69842617f1d823b041f8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/9c90154ee4cc6d739ed69842617f1d823b041f8d"}],"sha":"853ea93cf040cad1ad7b6203733ba48a7a14eb6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/853ea93cf040cad1ad7b6203733ba48a7a14eb6b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/9c90154ee4cc6d739ed69842617f1d823b041f8d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T02:27:39Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T02:33:57Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"State where this console runs and which model answers, on every page\n\nEvery served console now names, at the top of every page, WHERE it is running and\nWHICH model answers. That is the org decision of 2026-08-30, and this tree is one of the\nthirty-eight that had not adopted it.\n\n**Not cosmetic.** These systems are demonstrated on a laptop and on a deployment, sometimes\nin the same hour, and a screenshot of one is indistinguishable from the other. A viewer who\ncannot tell which they are looking at cannot tell whether what they are reading came from a\nmanaged model or from a deterministic offline stub, and that is exactly the confusion an\naudit-first pitch cannot afford. The page says it, always, instead of the presenter saying\nit sometimes.\n\n**Both halves come from the service, on `/healthz`.** Nothing in the browser infers either.\nA console that read its own runtime from `window.location` would be right until the day the\ndeployment served through a proxy, and wrong silently after that.\n\nWhat this tree now reports:\n\n| profile | `runtime` | `generator_model` |\n|---|---|---|\n| `local` | `local` | `deterministic-offline-stub` |\n| `gcp` | `gcp` | `managed-model-unnamed` |\n| `onprem` | `local` | `onprem-not-implemented` |\n\n**`generator_model` is read off the BINDING, not kept as a second settings string.** A\nsettings field would be a claim ABOUT the binding, and the two drift the first time somebody\nrebinds a profile without remembering the second field. `_GENERATOR_PORT` names the port\nwhose active binding decides the answer, so rebinding it changes the banner in the same edit.\n\nThis tree''s managed adapter pins no model id anywhere, so the managed profile answers\n`managed-model-unnamed`. That is not a placeholder for a nicer string: it truthfully says a\nmanaged generator is bound and this repository does not name which model it calls. Inventing\nan id would be exactly the fiction the banner exists to prevent, and the honest answer makes\nthe gap visible instead.\n\n**The vocabulary distinguishes four things that are genuinely different**, because a reviewer\napproving an escalation is entitled to know which one they are reading:\n`deterministic-offline-stub` (a model-shaped port bound to a stub), `no-model` (no such port\nexists at all), `onprem-not-implemented` (the port exists and refuses), and a real model id.\n`runtime` states where the PROCESS runs, so `onprem` reads `local` -- a managed model call\ndoes not make a process cloud-hosted.\n\n`tests/unit/test_provenance_banner_contract.py` asserts agreement with the profile rather\nthan mere presence, because a banner that is present and wrong is worse than none: it turns\n\"the viewer does not know\" into \"the viewer has been told the wrong thing\". Falsified rather\nthan assumed -- making an offline profile report a Gemini id fails it with *\"the ''local''\nprofile reports ''gemini-3.5-flash'', which reads as a managed model answering a request that\nnever left the machine\"*, and reverting clears it.\n\nThe component and the `.provenance-banner` style are copied from the render-verified\n`hex-service-template`, and it is mounted in the LAYOUT rather than in a page: \"at the top of\nevery page\" is a property of the console, and a page that forgot it would be the one a\nscreenshot came from.\n\nGate: 413 passed, 1 deselected.","tree":{"sha":"eccfc4a2345f3a87127aed6e380eb3b26d0694c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/eccfc4a2345f3a87127aed6e380eb3b26d0694c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/9c90154ee4cc6d739ed69842617f1d823b041f8d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/9c90154ee4cc6d739ed69842617f1d823b041f8d","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh-TdoAKDljOTAxNTRlZTRjYzZkNzM5ZWQ2OTg0MjYxN2YxZDgyM2IwNDFmOGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/d6470e30aff854c368188b54d2408464f931b6dd","sha":"d6470e30aff854c368188b54d2408464f931b6dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/d6470e30aff854c368188b54d2408464f931b6dd"}],"sha":"9c90154ee4cc6d739ed69842617f1d823b041f8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/9c90154ee4cc6d739ed69842617f1d823b041f8d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/d6470e30aff854c368188b54d2408464f931b6dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T01:40:43Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T01:52:06Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Compare each declared MCP schema against the arguments its handler reads\n\n`test_mcp_surface_is_served_and_packaged.py` already pins the tool NAMES in both\ndirections, and `hex_service_kit.mcpserve.bind` refuses to start on a name mismatch.\nNeither says anything about the PAYLOAD. A tool can be declared, bound, served and still\ndescribe arguments its handler never reads, or read arguments the caller was never told\nto send.\n\nThat is the defect the portfolio backlog recorded twice about one tool in\n`loan-document-intelligence`: `cross_validate` was narrowed once from an unresolvable\n`extract_ids` to a REQUIRED `documents` array, and the callable ignored `documents`\nentirely. Both narrowings were done by READING, and reading is what missed it the second\ntime. So the new test compares the two sides mechanically.\n\nThe handlers take `**arguments`, so there is no signature to check a schema against. What\nthere is, and what decides the outcome of a call, is which keys the handler actually reads\nout of that bag. That is read from the AST rather than by calling anything, because the\nhandlers are closures over a live container and this has to hold under the offline gate.\nKeys reached through a helper taking `arguments` count as read by every handler that calls\nit, transitively; a handler declaring its bag `**_` reads nothing on purpose and its schema\nmust declare no properties.\n\nRun across the fourteen trees that serve a catalog, it reported findings in seven. This is\none of them.\n\n**A channel that could not be used, and a reviewer reviewing against an\nempty brief.**\n\n`channel` lived in the scope fragment all three tools shared, so `search_brand_corpus`\nadvertised one: `RetrievalQuery` has no channel field and nothing downstream reads one. It\nalso declared `market` and `vertical` and then searched unscoped, the same hole as\n`market-intelligence`. Fixed by splitting `_CHANNEL_SCHEMA` out for the two tools that\nbuild a creative, and passing the market and vertical the corpus search genuinely supports.\n\n`review_variant` runs the checks with the SAME `_brief` as `generate_creative` -- a claim is\njudged against the campaign theme, the product and the offer -- and declared none of them.\nNow shared as `_BRIEF_SCHEMA`. `n_variants` is deliberately not in it: it is how many drafts\nto produce, meaningless when reviewing one supplied variant, and `_brief` now takes it as an\nargument so the review path cannot read it.\n\nFalsified rather than assumed. Restoring the pre-fix narrow declaration on\n`credit-memo-drafting`''s `peer_compare` makes the check fail with the exact sentence above,\nand putting it back clears it, so a passing run is evidence rather than silence. The\n`test_the_ast_walk_finds_the_handlers_it_is_supposed_to_check` case guards the other way: if\nthe walk and the served handler roster ever disagree, every remaining assertion would be\nchecking a different set of tools than the one served, and it says so instead.\n\nGate: 403 passed, 1 deselected.","tree":{"sha":"75d3a07560030c237c80ef65d7af905f6a0b2d76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/75d3a07560030c237c80ef65d7af905f6a0b2d76"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/d6470e30aff854c368188b54d2408464f931b6dd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/d6470e30aff854c368188b54d2408464f931b6dd","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh-TdoAKGQ2NDcwZTMwYWZmODU0YzM2ODE4OGI1NGQyNDA4NDY0ZjkzMWI2ZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/af88adea6c9363389cd1cba570ed6e60f06dd6c7","sha":"af88adea6c9363389cd1cba570ed6e60f06dd6c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/af88adea6c9363389cd1cba570ed6e60f06dd6c7"}],"sha":"d6470e30aff854c368188b54d2408464f931b6dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/d6470e30aff854c368188b54d2408464f931b6dd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/af88adea6c9363389cd1cba570ed6e60f06dd6c7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T01:25:56Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T01:34:02Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Name the MCP Tool field input_schema\n\nThe field is `input_schema`; `inputSchema` is its pydantic alias. Passing the alias\nworks at runtime and dumps identically on the wire, so this is drift against a compat\nshim rather than a live break -- but a type-checker that can see the `mcp` package\nrejects the keyword, and this tree''s dev lock cannot see it either.","tree":{"sha":"6feef5c22a691cabf5ceba534b2ab0668cdf1139","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/6feef5c22a691cabf5ceba534b2ab0668cdf1139"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/af88adea6c9363389cd1cba570ed6e60f06dd6c7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/af88adea6c9363389cd1cba570ed6e60f06dd6c7","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh-TdoAKGFmODhhZGVhNmM5MzYzMzg5Y2QxY2JhNTcwZWQ2ZTYwZjA2ZGQ2Yzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/05b4d30ff107543f685b01c9a609d8a0e9acb20a","sha":"05b4d30ff107543f685b01c9a609d8a0e9acb20a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/05b4d30ff107543f685b01c9a609d8a0e9acb20a"}],"sha":"af88adea6c9363389cd1cba570ed6e60f06dd6c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/af88adea6c9363389cd1cba570ed6e60f06dd6c7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/05b4d30ff107543f685b01c9a609d8a0e9acb20a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T01:25:56Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T01:34:02Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Copy the verified IAP claims into a dict\n\n`id_token.verify_token` returns a `Mapping[str, Any]`, not a `dict`. The annotation\non this line claimed a dict, so a type-checker that can actually see `google.oauth2`\nreports an assignment error. This tree''s own gate never saw it: the dev lock carries\nno google-auth, so mypy resolved the module to `Any` and said nothing.\n\nCopying into a dict is what `hex-service-template` and the rest of the fleet already\ndo, and what `cdd-sow-research` documents in place: callers own a mutable snapshot of\nthe claims rather than the SDK''s view of them. Behaviour is unchanged.\n\nFalsified first: against the previous line the checker reports the error, against this\none it does not.","tree":{"sha":"6d057211ad8edeced9e1150e404270fb1dea8485","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/6d057211ad8edeced9e1150e404270fb1dea8485"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/05b4d30ff107543f685b01c9a609d8a0e9acb20a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","