pos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/0701ec023372ab88831fb693b30be9e89dd3cf37/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T14:17:42Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T14:37:21Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Adopt hex-service-kit v0.0.6\n\nThe 0.0.6 identity knobs -- machine_tenants, subject_from, refuse_unmapped_tenant and a\nhuman-subject allowlist -- have been released and unadopted since 2026-08-28. Every one\ndefaults to what this repository already does, so this bump is the version move and\nnothing else: no behaviour changes until an adopter says so.\n\nThe lockfiles pin the 40-character commit the tag resolved to, not the tag, so what\ninstalls cannot change without a diff.","tree":{"sha":"c30a2637971d35dc1d3133c64f4ddd56f45288ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/c30a2637971d35dc1d3133c64f4ddd56f45288ad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/0701ec023372ab88831fb693b30be9e89dd3cf37","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/0701ec023372ab88831fb693b30be9e89dd3cf37","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh-TdoAKDA3MDFlYzAyMzM3MmFiODg4MzFmYjY5M2IzMGJlOWU4OWRkM2NmMzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/0b5e51c755c091d71685d8aa7722db04336aa888","sha":"0b5e51c755c091d71685d8aa7722db04336aa888","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/0b5e51c755c091d71685d8aa7722db04336aa888"}],"sha":"0701ec023372ab88831fb693b30be9e89dd3cf37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/0701ec023372ab88831fb693b30be9e89dd3cf37"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/0b5e51c755c091d71685d8aa7722db04336aa888/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T08:56:10Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T09:29:39Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Name the platform environment variables for what they are\n\nThe HRZ_ prefix is a retired catalog code. It named nothing an operator could look up:\nHRZ_HUMAN_REVIEW_URL, HRZ7_S2S_TOKEN and HRZ_REGISTRY_* say which internal identifier a\nservice used to carry, not which service they address. The names now say that directly --\nHUMAN_REVIEW_URL, HUMAN_REVIEW_S2S_TOKEN, AGENT_REGISTRY_*, KNOWLEDGE_BASE_URL,\nGUARDRAIL_GATEWAY_URL, QUALITY_GATE_URL, OBSERVABILITY_URL, AUDIT_URL -- so a\n`.env` file can be read without the catalog open beside it.\n\nNothing about the wire contract changes; these are the names of the values, not the\nvalues. Two repositories that had gone their own way (a repo-scoped review-console URL,\na second spelling of the knowledge-base URL) join the fleet-standard names rather than\nkeeping a private variant with the code stripped out.","tree":{"sha":"43ee741972544c9f367897106e1c9eef82917146","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/43ee741972544c9f367897106e1c9eef82917146"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/0b5e51c755c091d71685d8aa7722db04336aa888","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/0b5e51c755c091d71685d8aa7722db04336aa888","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh-TdoAKDBiNWU1MWM3NTVjMDkxZDcxNjg1ZDhhYTc3MjJkYjA0MzM2YWE4ODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/b278b77b6b1297eea73d154b5555d40d9fe9dc2b","sha":"b278b77b6b1297eea73d154b5555d40d9fe9dc2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/b278b77b6b1297eea73d154b5555d40d9fe9dc2b"}],"sha":"0b5e51c755c091d71685d8aa7722db04336aa888","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/0b5e51c755c091d71685d8aa7722db04336aa888"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/b278b77b6b1297eea73d154b5555d40d9fe9dc2b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T07:43:58Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T07:49:28Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Show the display name, not the catalog code\n\nA code like B1 or C3 identifies a repository inside the catalog. It is not\nsomething a user of this console can resolve, and it was being rendered in\nheadings, tab titles, meta descriptions and an aria-label. The display name\nwas already beside it in every case, so the code simply goes.","tree":{"sha":"fad6f3bac6553581bdbdfbe5aec6834dbe672604","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/fad6f3bac6553581bdbdfbe5aec6834dbe672604"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/b278b77b6b1297eea73d154b5555d40d9fe9dc2b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/b278b77b6b1297eea73d154b5555d40d9fe9dc2b","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh-TdoAKGIyNzhiNzdiNmIxMjk3ZWVhNzNkMTU0YjU1NTVkNDBkOWZlOWRjMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/200b11a4b758ab329bdfe6414446ef4fb8ae329f","sha":"200b11a4b758ab329bdfe6414446ef4fb8ae329f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/200b11a4b758ab329bdfe6414446ef4fb8ae329f"}],"sha":"b278b77b6b1297eea73d154b5555d40d9fe9dc2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/b278b77b6b1297eea73d154b5555d40d9fe9dc2b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/200b11a4b758ab329bdfe6414446ef4fb8ae329f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T06:01:40Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T06:07:40Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Serve a console that runs\n\nA production build was already the only mode these consoles worked in: ui/proxy.ts sets a\nstrict nonce CSP on every path, dev included, and it permits no eval, so `npm run dev` rendered\nthe whole interface and React never started. The run sheet still sent a presenter to that dev\nserver.\n\n- ui/lib/csp.mjs gains a dev-only branch, keyed off NODE_ENV, adding unsafe-eval and the HMR\n  websocket. Ported from cdd-sow-research and human-review-console, which already had it. The\n  production policy is unchanged, and the test asserts both halves so a leak into production\n  fails rather than ships.\n- DEMO.md now demonstrates the built console, which is what\n  org-metadata/docs/demos/demo-inventory.md has required all along. `make run-ui` stays the\n  developer loop, and now genuinely works.","tree":{"sha":"16e05a72ba6b05509a5b1641bb762931299ce704","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/16e05a72ba6b05509a5b1641bb762931299ce704"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/200b11a4b758ab329bdfe6414446ef4fb8ae329f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/200b11a4b758ab329bdfe6414446ef4fb8ae329f","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh-TdoAKDIwMGIxMWE0Yjc1OGFiMzI5YmRmZTY0MTQ0NDZlZjRmYjhhZTMyOWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/3f815967c8588e2e0732d784b76efe703cd179ff","sha":"3f815967c8588e2e0732d784b76efe703cd179ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/3f815967c8588e2e0732d784b76efe703cd179ff"}],"sha":"200b11a4b758ab329bdfe6414446ef4fb8ae329f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/200b11a4b758ab329bdfe6414446ef4fb8ae329f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/3f815967c8588e2e0732d784b76efe703cd179ff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T15:54:40Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T16:05:08Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Let the console''s configured API base reach the browser\n\nEvery console read NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE as readEnvSetting(process.env, NAME). A bundler\nsubstitutes a public variable only where it appears as the literal member expression\nprocess.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_X; handing the whole process.env object to a function leaves\nnothing to substitute, so the browser evaluated {}[name], the read reported UNSET, and the\nconsole fell back to its own hard-coded loopback default.\n\nEmbedded in the host portal that meant the console called http://localhost:<its own port>\ninstead of its same-origin mount, which its own connect-src ''self'' then blocked. The page\nrendered in full, reported its backend unreachable, and no request ever left it. Every\nhealth check stayed green throughout, because the failure is entirely in the browser.\n\nThe fix keeps both properties that matter: the read stays a literal at the call site, so\nthe bundler can substitute it, and the three-state decision stays in one place behind the\nnew readEnvValue(name, raw). The scan that forbids two-state reads now recognises that\nform and still reports anything with a default beside it; it was observed failing on the\nold shape before it was trusted.","tree":{"sha":"91c4daf585fd4d0d5ea9bffa96cdab83cbfab684","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/91c4daf585fd4d0d5ea9bffa96cdab83cbfab684"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/3f815967c8588e2e0732d784b76efe703cd179ff","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/3f815967c8588e2e0732d784b76efe703cd179ff","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh-TdoAKDNmODE1OTY3Yzg1ODhlMmUwNzMyZDc4NGI3NmVmZTcwM2NkMTc5ZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/4bd9d5f17705e0029c8b4f54ddf6ef7d95bb2f55","sha":"4bd9d5f17705e0029c8b4f54ddf6ef7d95bb2f55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/4bd9d5f17705e0029c8b4f54ddf6ef7d95bb2f55"}],"sha":"3f815967c8588e2e0732d784b76efe703cd179ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/3f815967c8588e2e0732d784b76efe703cd179ff"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/4bd9d5f17705e0029c8b4f54ddf6ef7d95bb2f55/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T06:06:07Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T06:19:13Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Point Agent Search at a location it serves, and say what that costs residency\n\nAgent Search serves global, us and eu and no Cloud region at all, so the previous\nasia-southeast1 pin could never provision. knowledge_base.location is now its own\nselector, defaulting to global.\n\nThat is a real residency deviation rather than a detail: the retrieval index is unlocated\nwhile everything around it stays in region, and us or eu confines it to one jurisdiction\nwhere an obligation bites. The residency rows and the compliance FAQ now read PARTIAL and\nname the gap. The gcp.resourceLocations width is a deploy-time input, because widening it\nis a jurisdiction statement.","tree":{"sha":"e0f5a06022eccb30cdf1022f68f9aa665a886fb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/e0f5a06022eccb30cdf1022f68f9aa665a886fb6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/4bd9d5f17705e0029c8b4f54ddf6ef7d95bb2f55","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/4bd9d5f17705e0029c8b4f54ddf6ef7d95bb2f55","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh-TdoAKDRiZDlkNWYxNzcwNWUwMDI5YzhiNGY1NGRkZjZlZjdkOTViYjJmNTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/02fa66eb7df99b7d9839b336bb9af15014396dff","sha":"02fa66eb7df99b7d9839b336bb9af15014396dff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/02fa66eb7df99b7d9839b336bb9af15014396dff"}],"sha":"4bd9d5f17705e0029c8b4f54ddf6ef7d95bb2f55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/4bd9d5f17705e0029c8b4f54ddf6ef7d95bb2f55"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/02fa66eb7df99b7d9839b336bb9af15014396dff/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T03:32:33Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T03:32:33Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"message":"Set the profile the serving-path test is actually about\n\nThis test asserted the seeded persona list, and the demo routes that need\nan identity, without ever choosing a profile. An UNSET profile\ndeliberately refuses: the seeded-persona adapter declines to construct\nwhen nobody named a profile, because advertising identities that cannot be\nresolved is worse than advertising none. So the test was asserting the\npersona list of a run that had refused to build one, and it had been red\nfor as long as that refusal has existed, on published main rather than\nfrom anything recent.\n\nThe fix is to set the profile explicitly, which is what a local\ndevelopment run does and what the test''s own docstring describes.\n\nThe other half of that decision had no coverage at all, so it gets a test\nof its own: an unset profile advertises NO personas. That is the half\nworth guarding, because it is the direction where getting it wrong hands a\nseeded identity to a run nobody configured.","tree":{"sha":"30ef6babb659f150e73a5ea7bc5791210279704c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/30ef6babb659f150e73a5ea7bc5791210279704c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/02fa66eb7df99b7d9839b336bb9af15014396dff","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/02fa66eb7df99b7d9839b336bb9af15014396dff","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh-TdoAKDAyZmE2NmViN2RmOTliN2Q5ODM5YjMzNmJiOWFmMTUwMTQzOTZkZmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/971474ca78bfd3fd255cd69b1c9c301278b8e9ef","sha":"971474ca78bfd3fd255cd69b1c9c301278b8e9ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/971474ca78bfd3fd255cd69b1c9c301278b8e9ef"}],"sha":"02fa66eb7df99b7d9839b336bb9af15014396dff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/02fa66eb7df99b7d9839b336bb9af15014396dff"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/971474ca78bfd3fd255cd69b1c9c301278b8e9ef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T03:10:02Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T03:10:02Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"message":"Serve the declared tool catalog over MCP, and package it as a plugin\n\nPhase 3 of the Agent Plugins item.\n\nThis tree declared its capability surface twice over, as an A2A agent card\nand as a governed tool catalog of JSON Schemas, and served neither. There\nwas no MCP server process anywhere in the fleet, so a surface described in\ntwo places could be read by a human and reached by nobody. This serves\nwhat was already declared and packages it; it describes nothing new.\n\nNothing is hand-authored. The handlers only supply the callables that\nanswer the existing catalog, and the manifest is rendered from the agent\ncard, the catalog and .agents/skills. A manifest typed out by hand is a\nsecond description of the service, and a second description can be wrong.\n\nbind() refuses a catalog/handler mismatch in both directions at start-up,\nand both directions are pinned by tests: a declared tool with no handler\nis a capability the service advertises and cannot perform, and a handler\nfor an undeclared tool is a reachable entry point nobody governed.\n\nWhere a tool names a section of a larger computation, the handler returns\nthat section of the one call rather than recomputing it by another route,\nand says so in place. A second path to a number the primary call already\nowns is a second answer to the same question.\n\nMCP stdio verifies no end user, so every handler records a SERVICE caller\nand supplies no entitlement principals. Filtering is fail-closed, so a\ntool call sees the untagged public data and nothing else. Manufacturing\nentitlements to make a tool return more is the one change these modules\nmust never make.\n\nThe tests state what they do NOT prove: no handler is executed, because\nbind checks names rather than behaviour. One handler filtered a value\nobject as though it were a list and bound cleanly regardless; only reading\nthe domain type caught it.\n\nThe kit pin moves to v0.0.5, dereferenced with rev-list rather than\nrev-parse because these are annotated tags, and jsonschema becomes a hard\ndev dependency so the manifest test cannot skip into green.","tree":{"sha":"46243f95e2885d5b3c88833c9741051fc63139b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/46243f95e2885d5b3c88833c9741051fc63139b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/971474ca78bfd3fd255cd69b1c9c301278b8e9ef","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/971474ca78bfd3fd255cd69b1c9c301278b8e9ef","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh-TdoAKDk3MTQ3NGNhNzhiZmQzZmQyNTVjZDY5YjFjOWMzMDEyNzhiOGU5ZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/4758ca0a2108ca13b20c86b798f87a03db6dfcd8","sha":"4758ca0a2108ca13b20c86b798f87a03db6dfcd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/4758ca0a2108ca13b20c86b798f87a03db6dfcd8"}],"sha":"971474ca78bfd3fd255cd69b1c9c301278b8e9ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/971474ca78bfd3fd255cd69b1c9c301278b8e9ef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/4758ca0a2108ca13b20c86b798f87a03db6dfcd8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T00:57:35Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T00:57:35Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"message":"Declare the A2A server extra instead of borrowing it from mcp\n\na2a-sdk moved from >=0.2 to >=1.1 in the 2026-08-26 currency sweep, across\na major version boundary. It lives in the [gcp] extra and every import of\nit is lazy, so the offline gate never installed it and could not have\nproved anything about the bump. It was recorded as unverified. This is the\nverification, run against a real 1.x install.\n\n1.x moved starlette and sse-starlette out of the base package into extras,\nso a bare a2a-sdk>=1.1 declares a client-only SDK. to_a2a still imports,\nwhich is what makes it quiet: the failure lands at ASGI startup as\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named ''sse_starlette'', raised from\na2a.server.routes at the moment the agent would begin serving. Observed by\ninstalling google-adk==2.7.1 with a bare a2a-sdk>=1.1 and starting the\napp. With a2a-sdk[http-server]>=1.1 the same app serves\n/.well-known/agent-card.json with a 200.\n\nThe more useful half is why nothing had broken yet. requirements-gcp.lock\nalready resolves sse-starlette, so installs from the lock serve correctly\ntoday. It is there via mcp, not via a2a-sdk: a separate pin in the same\nextra happens to need the same package. Serving worked by coincidence of\nan unrelated dependency rather than by anything declared here, and would\nhave broken the day mcp dropped it. Installing from pyproject rather than\nthe lock is broken today.\n\nThe guard is static, because an offline gate cannot install the extra and\nwhat is worth pinning is the declared dependency rather than whatever a\nvenv happens to contain. Proved red first against the bare pin.","tree":{"sha":"2db23a79d33cf66c5a3268434d1cdf683661894e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/2db23a79d33cf66c5a3268434d1cdf683661894e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/4758ca0a2108ca13b20c86b798f87a03db6dfcd8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/4758ca0a2108ca13b20c86b798f87a03db6dfcd8","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh-TdoAKDQ3NThjYTBhMjEwOGNhMTNiMjBjODZiNzk4Zjg3YTAzZGI2ZGZjZDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/2546f111227d622ba73388c4d851f927d7e1ab5b","sha":"2546f111227d622ba73388c4d851f927d7e1ab5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/2546f111227d622ba73388c4d851f927d7e1ab5b"}],"sha":"4758ca0a2108ca13b20c86b798f87a03db6dfcd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/4758ca0a2108ca13b20c86b798f87a03db6dfcd8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/2546f111227d622ba73388c4d851f927d7e1ab5b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-28T00:46:37Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-28T00:51:30Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"message":"Assert that this repository samples on purpose\n\nEvery other grounded tree in the fleet now pins temperature to 0.0, because\nthe front page claims the consequential math is deterministic and the model\nnever produces the number. A creative brief is not a consequential number:\nvariation is the product, and pinning it would make the studio return one\nidea forever.\n\nSo the guard here is inverted. It asserts the deliberate 0.4, so that a\nsweep which pins the rest of the fleet cannot quietly pin this one too, and\nso the exception stays a decision somebody made rather than a value nobody\nlooked at.","tree":{"sha":"8aef8656d8f3a59be0eee5f53f0fac9bb4d608ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/8aef8656d8f3a59be0eee5f53f0fac9bb4d608ce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/2546f111227d622ba73388c4d851f927d7e1ab5b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/2546f111227d622ba73388c4d851f927d7e1ab5b","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh-TdoAKDI1NDZmMTExMjI3ZDYyMmJhNzMzODhjNGQ4NTFmOTI3ZDdlMWFiNWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/ad2eb6451c2f304a309d69be1fac534a6cd32397","sha":"ad2eb6451c2f304a309d69be1fac534a6cd32397","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/ad2eb6451c2f304a309d69be1fac534a6cd32397"}],"sha":"2546f111227d622ba73388c4d851f927d7e1ab5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/2546f111227d622ba73388c4d851f927d7e1ab5b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/ad2eb6451c2f304a309d69be1fac534a6cd32397/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T13:00:49Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T13:34:50Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Pin the model plane in-region: gemini-3.5-flash in asia-southeast1\n\nThe settings files asserted that an APAC deployment could not have both a\nGemini 3 model and in-region processing, and had to settle for a 2.5 model or\nthe global endpoint. That was wrong. Google''s data-residency table (page\nupdated 2026-08-26, read 2026-08-27) lists gemini-3.5-flash as served in\nasia-southeast1 WITH a documented Singapore ML-processing commitment.\n\nBecause of that belief every repo here pinned models.location to the `us`\nmulti-region while pinning region to asia-southeast1, so the fleet shipped a\nmostly unstated deviation: prompts left the region on a build whose headline\nclaim is residency. This moves the pins to the newest model the residency\nboundary actually permits.\n\ngemini-3.7-flash serves the `us` and `eu` multi-regions only -- not `asia`,\nand not any single region. It stays reachable through the deviation process\nthe region decision record defines, via the env override.\n\nWorth recording: enterprise-knowledge-base was already internally\ninconsistent. infra/terraform/managed_api.tf preconditions on \"a reviewed\nSingapore single-zone Gemini 3.5 Flash Provisioned Throughput order\", while\nconfig pinned 3.7 at `us` and a drift guard held the config AGAINST the\ninfra. The guard now asserts the pin the infra demands.\n\nVerified: every touched repo returns to its exact pre-change test baseline;\nno new failures. Model ids left alone where they are subject matter rather\nthan a pin (model-quality-gate evaluation targets, the cost calculator''s\nprice table, and the deployment record''s account of what actually ran).","tree":{"sha":"9fcbc86864534fca793b6cd3eacbc078da42683b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/9fcbc86864534fca793b6cd3eacbc078da42683b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/ad2eb6451c2f304a309d69be1fac534a6cd32397","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/ad2eb6451c2f304a309d69be1fac534a6cd32397","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh-TdoAKGFkMmViNjQ1MWMyZjMwNGEzMDlkNjliZTFmYWM1MzRhNmNkMzIzOTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/79ad81eef6cc20281d2b78e9efaa9c9db7a9c5cb","sha":"79ad81eef6cc20281d2b78e9efaa9c9db7a9c5cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/79ad81eef6cc20281d2b78e9efaa9c9db7a9c5cb"}],"sha":"ad2eb6451c2f304a309d69be1fac534a6cd32397","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/ad2eb6451c2f304a309d69be1fac534a6cd32397"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/79ad81eef6cc20281d2b78e9efaa9c9db7a9c5cb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T19:32:38Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T19:32:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Reach Gemini 3.7 by calling the model location, not the compute region (#17)\n\nEvery Gemini client here was constructed with settings.region, so this service\ncould reach only what its own deploy region serves. us-central1 and\nasia-southeast1 serve the 2.5 family and no Gemini 3 at all, while config\npinned Gemini 3 ids -- so the configured model could never have resolved on a\ndeployment. gemini-3.1-pro sat in the hard-reasoning slot resolving in NO\nlocation, and nothing failed because that path is feature-flagged off; the first\ndeployment to switch it on would have been the one to find out.\n\nmodels.location is now separate from the compute region and defaults to `us`,\nthe United States multi-region. That choice is load-bearing: a multi-region\nendpoint pools capacity within one geography and Google documents ML processing\nas staying inside it, where the global endpoint carries no residency guarantee\nat all. Probed against a live project on 2026-08-27: gemini-3.7-flash (GA\n2026-08-13) answers in `us` and `eu`, and 404s in us-central1, us-east5,\neurope-west4, asia-southeast1 and `asia`.\n\nTwo consequences stated rather than buried. There is no Gemini 3 PRO tier in\neither multi-region, so hard reasoning names the flash tier honestly instead of\na pro tier it cannot call. And an APAC deployment cannot have both Gemini 3 and\nin-region processing: it must pin a model its own region serves, or set the\nlocation deliberately and accept what that means. Do not quietly set `global`.\n\nTests that asserted the old id were asserting the config loader, not the model,\nand move with it. The one test that pinned the client to the compute region was\npinning the defect, and now says so in place.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"6d31d35f03b67d6558ac6eec9361d6bec3068923","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/6d31d35f03b67d6558ac6eec9361d6bec3068923"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/79ad81eef6cc20281d2b78e9efaa9c9db7a9c5cb","verification":{"payload":"tree 6d31d35f03b67d6558ac6eec9361d6bec3068923\nparent 2cacb0bcea070a7082c8071ef5a38606cc99da3a\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787772758 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787772758 +0800\n\nReach Gemini 3.7 by calling the model location, not the compute region (#17)\n\nEvery Gemini client here was constructed with settings.region, so this service\ncould reach only what its own deploy region serves. us-central1 and\nasia-southeast1 serve the 2.5 family and no Gemini 3 at all, while config\npinned Gemini 3 ids -- so the configured model could never have resolved on a\ndeployment. gemini-3.1-pro sat in the hard-reasoning slot resolving in NO\nlocation, and nothing failed because that path is feature-flagged off; the first\ndeployment to switch it on would have been the one to find out.\n\nmodels.location is now separate from the compute region and defaults to `us`,\nthe United States multi-region. That choice is load-bearing: a multi-region\nendpoint pools capacity within one geography and Google documents ML processing\nas staying inside it, where the global endpoint carries no residency guarantee\nat all. Probed against a live project on 2026-08-27: gemini-3.7-flash (GA\n2026-08-13) answers in `us` and `eu`, and 404s in us-central1, us-east5,\neurope-west4, asia-southeast1 and `asia`.\n\nTwo consequences stated rather than buried. There is no Gemini 3 PRO tier in\neither multi-region, so hard reasoning names the flash tier honestly instead of\na pro tier it cannot call. And an APAC deployment cannot have both Gemini 3 and\nin-region processing: it must pin a model its own region serves, or set the\nlocation deliberately and accept what that means. Do not quietly set `global`.\n\nTests that asserted the old id were asserting the config loader, not the model,\nand move with it. The one test that pinned the client to the compute region was\npinning the defect, and now says so in place.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjz9WCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2xsQAFGpZBIDZ66Bjg8gYTw0PlHN\nl2+X4rMDYUMIvsxLMqC++pnMRAbOCYShESwBzD8w6rC119xuw8SbGp118UlTiE/L\nR2/NxW4y1u8LYFIx0W8RP/yVFtj2GKMpWHEfZyN6zm0JDdQPqdle8JvBr34oVS/b\nVFPEdxaIsTjhtlWKxCBmGewFUluAtIafCKOJejoXMsSVMabqiyNcY03rAWSRg1U/\nommZXP/ypUoVQXGU9QXFENQAFPoJDD4Rc7GnaSNXjp+yaLW82eibemII3nZmyNuS\nHYA+toK72p7iMW05mVIpWV9VyILg4AmylUQanppSR66ArLkHN8a1cuz8EZ4liFTh\npvVIbvvGmTr/Qf3vhRmN2wWZ5I7nboBJ6cTbvfcotJb5DBcQaNXgcuAQpT+8txYM\nvJzW/VW7i5iL+K77PLU+nkLUJ6saZXyxDIj+vfQ4wInazbuURNXB7dZti1M35BAp\nvaIFgcpCIW+K1kcYUoy+nMY92dqnBaUaeS2I5lBAwkSqG8VG3ATrSykh/3QIyYgv\n+rtdmPJ85riUEDfujqec0x0WeLQOwauaB4nHeSGGFZJX4y7l3RukyfhAFCHDbGwJ\nNds+N+x6WQ32nWqOrPgRjUDP9A85zyhi6500gW1KBFGgXYJ496/dmFUy/fGR+Rny\nkMxTlIOpsquObaYD7njR\n=CvaJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-26T19:32:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/79ad81eef6cc20281d2b78e9efaa9c9db7a9c5cb","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh-TdoAKDc5YWQ4MWVlZjZjYzIwMjgxZDJiNzhlOWVmYWE5YzlkYjdhOWM1Y2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/2cacb0bcea070a7082c8071ef5a38606cc99da3a","sha":"2cacb0bcea070a7082c8071ef5a38606cc99da3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/2cacb0bcea070a7082c8071ef5a38606cc99da3a"}],"sha":"79ad81eef6cc20281d2b78e9efaa9c9db7a9c5cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/79ad81eef6cc20281d2b78e9efaa9c9db7a9c5cb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/2cacb0bcea070a7082c8071ef5a38606cc99da3a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T01:09:00Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T01:09:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Adopt the commons claim half in the IAP adapter (#16)\n\nresolve() no longer builds a Principal. Everything after the signature check\nis one hex_service_kit.federation.principal_from_iap_claims call under a\nreviewed FederationPolicy, and the cryptography stays in the adapter because\nthe kit''s core is stdlib with zero runtime dependencies and verifies nothing.\n\nThe policy states tenant_from_hosted_domain as an opt-in rather than leaving\nit to a fallback: this deployment configures no domain map and IAP already\nrestricts the audience to one organisation, so the hd claim IS the tenant id.\nLeft off, these same assertions resolve to no tenant at all, which is\nfail-closed and closed for every verified user, and no offline gate would see\nit because the local profile never constructs this adapter.\n\nExecuting the commons against this adapter over the same claim sets, rather\nthan reading it, found two behaviour changes. Both are recorded rather than\nnormalised away: assurance now prefers an acr claim where the shipped tail\nhardcoded \"iap\", and the tenant is lower-cased where the shipped tail passed\nhd through with only .strip().\n\ntests/unit/test_iap_claim_half.py was red first in three stages and red again\nagainst three deliberate defects afterwards. The counts are in\ndocs/practices-audit.md under C1.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"88a015183856dbd4f7150dc35f7111579333aab5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/88a015183856dbd4f7150dc35f7111579333aab5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/2cacb0bcea070a7082c8071ef5a38606cc99da3a","verification":{"payload":"tree 88a015183856dbd4f7150dc35f7111579333aab5\nparent 3006371187ae2a19618da45b1e63214d8429185f\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787706540 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787706540 +0800\n\nAdopt the commons claim half in the IAP adapter (#16)\n\nresolve() no longer builds a Principal. Everything after the signature check\nis one hex_service_kit.federation.principal_from_iap_claims call under a\nreviewed FederationPolicy, and the cryptography stays in the adapter because\nthe kit''s core is stdlib with zero runtime dependencies and verifies nothing.\n\nThe policy states tenant_from_hosted_domain as an opt-in rather than leaving\nit to a fallback: this deployment configures no domain map and IAP already\nrestricts the audience to one organisation, so the hd claim IS the tenant id.\nLeft off, these same assertions resolve to no tenant at all, which is\nfail-closed and closed for every verified user, and no offline gate would see\nit because the local profile never constructs this adapter.\n\nExecuting the commons against this adapter over the same claim sets, rather\nthan reading it, found two behaviour changes. Both are recorded rather than\nnormalised away: assurance now prefers an acr claim where the shipped tail\nhardcoded \"iap\", and the tenant is lower-cased where the shipped tail passed\nhd through with only .strip().\n\ntests/unit/test_iap_claim_half.py was red first in three stages and red again\nagainst three deliberate defects afterwards. The counts are in\ndocs/practices-audit.md under C1.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjjysCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtAkQAITtkWBpcUJXP3v97FRJk1+1\nsPPeGwyNarvNBtK5ivA+MfLjdK3DOROnEmzZL78oKpHx1ATzVNPdOPMuWciuWqR3\nqv15HSAAWl6vaTrQK7KMZOHgAZoAgFmiuLjLl/sFzbUgjJUlCmjzxu6p52fdzF7t\nIo0ecW+inDKF52wlgsWBYSUaf3jISBUOXW6ql00+hDGTfuq5TH2AU9+GKbwR0PYW\nhp1GCH0ooC1dG0b90SSGA8hPql/b6radcv7DlagAbOYL+BxpcpwpC7Z0mdzWdAL9\nYSlUdkpQPKCKZ2ZFBCkIZsc5C6klR6De3LLfJIEGagWVpn0pkLBHqURkpvcNuylN\n9Wn5KaPaoBkPlZm+n3760XfUDgpC+sECrHEDD5TSPRYGxeV+I0HN1MZLoE/coxpo\nKnOtBICytjm8BjfgqWUsPdO3/Z8fDVwlLuJyYCRx1aw+oGE5x2rAxGCar2z3/TFB\nh1Ufa1f8cx+cuhRinpYcUDAfPU4it3aInE