hawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/3006371187ae2a19618da45b1e63214d8429185f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T22:50:59Z","email":"72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Ashish Awasthi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T22:56:15Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"message":"Move the MCP surface to the 2026-07-28 stateless era\n\nMCP 2026-07-28 removed the initialize handshake and protocol-level sessions,\nmade server/discover mandatory, and added required resultType, ttlMs and\ncacheScope fields. This repo declared 2025-11-25, the newest revision of the\nera that replaced, so it described a protocol the fleet no longer speaks.\n\n- Declare MCP_PROTOCOL_VERSION = \"2026-07-28\", added where the revision was\n  previously stated only in prose.\n- mcp>=1.2 becomes mcp>=2.1. The 1.x SDK predates the stateless era and cannot\n  speak it, so the old floor permitted a resolution that silently reinstates\n  the handshake this revision removed.\n- a2a-sdk>=0.2 becomes >=1.1. Not verified against a real 1.x install: it lives\n  in the gcp extra, which the offline gate deliberately does not install.","tree":{"sha":"debda3dbfb952f9e665e845fc374df01b511aefe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/debda3dbfb952f9e665e845fc374df01b511aefe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/3006371187ae2a19618da45b1e63214d8429185f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/3006371187ae2a19618da45b1e63214d8429185f","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh-TdoAKDMwMDYzNzExODdhZTJhMTk2MThkYTQ1YjFlNjMyMTRkODQyOTE4NWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/2df652f34c6d582782752fc1714522c06b0e8889","sha":"2df652f34c6d582782752fc1714522c06b0e8889","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/2df652f34c6d582782752fc1714522c06b0e8889"}],"sha":"3006371187ae2a19618da45b1e63214d8429185f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/3006371187ae2a19618da45b1e63214d8429185f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/2df652f34c6d582782752fc1714522c06b0e8889/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T16:01:00Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T16:01:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Record the IAP refusal-split evidence in the C1 audit row (#14)\n\nThe three IAP refusals closed in #12 were never written into\n`docs/practices-audit.md`, and the workspace rule is that a change which closes a practice\ncheck records its evidence there, saying what was observed failing first. This does that and\nnothing else. C1 keeps its PASS verdict: nothing regressed, the evidence behind it was simply\nmissing.\n\nThe row now names the refusal shapes an operator actually got, the exception types that\nreplaced them (`IapAudienceUnconfiguredError` and `IapVerifierUnavailableError`, both\n`EndUserAuthUnavailableError` subclasses carrying `http_status` 503), the subclass-ordering\nhazard in `api/security.py`, and `tests/unit/test_iap_refusal_split.py` as the guard.\n\n## Observed failing first\n\nReproduced offline in a throwaway worktree at `73fab2a^`, with no cloud SDK, no credential and\nno network:\n\n```\naudience unset, assertion present : IdentityError: MKT_CREATIVE_IAP_AUDIENCE is not configured; cannot verify IAP assertion\naudience unset, bare curl         : IdentityError: MKT_CREATIVE_IAP_AUDIENCE is not configured; cannot verify IAP assertion\nheader is ''   ''                   : IdentityError: assertion is not a compact JWS or JWE, so it carries no readable algorithm header\ngoogle-auth blocked               : ModuleNotFoundError: No module named ''google.auth.transport''\n```\n\nThe audience was already checked before the header here, so the bare curl did\nname the unset variable. What it did not do was carry a status that said the fault was the\ndeployment''s.\n\n`api/security.py` answered 401 \"authentication required\" for the first two alike, so an\noperator was told authentication had failed when no credential would have helped.\n\nThree further observations, same worktree method:\n\n* `tests/unit/test_iap_refusal_split.py` does not import against that tree at all: neither\n  `EndUserAuthUnavailableError` nor the two `Iap*Error` types existed.\n* With only those types injected and the pre-fix behaviour left standing: 8 failed, 3 passed.\n* On the fixed tree with the two `except` branches in `api/security.py` reordered: 1 failed,\n  10 passed, and the one failure is\n  `test_the_api_answers_a_deployment_failure_with_its_own_status_and_message`, answering 401\n  where 503 is owed. That is the subclass-ordering hazard, executed.\n\nDocumentation only. No source, test or lockfile is touched.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"b542b8ed1ed865d525c90a8f0f1dc92d2afe8577","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/b542b8ed1ed865d525c90a8f0f1dc92d2afe8577"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/2df652f34c6d582782752fc1714522c06b0e8889","verification":{"payload":"tree b542b8ed1ed865d525c90a8f0f1dc92d2afe8577\nparent aa46a0c7a9134d339989ec3dd6e3e13ff3d916a1\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787673660 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787673660 +0800\n\nRecord the IAP refusal-split evidence in the C1 audit row (#14)\n\nThe three IAP refusals closed in #12 were never written into\n`docs/practices-audit.md`, and the workspace rule is that a change which closes a practice\ncheck records its evidence there, saying what was observed failing first. This does that and\nnothing else. C1 keeps its PASS verdict: nothing regressed, the evidence behind it was simply\nmissing.\n\nThe row now names the refusal shapes an operator actually got, the exception types that\nreplaced them (`IapAudienceUnconfiguredError` and `IapVerifierUnavailableError`, both\n`EndUserAuthUnavailableError` subclasses carrying `http_status` 503), the subclass-ordering\nhazard in `api/security.py`, and `tests/unit/test_iap_refusal_split.py` as the guard.\n\n## Observed failing first\n\nReproduced offline in a throwaway worktree at `73fab2a^`, with no cloud SDK, no credential and\nno network:\n\n```\naudience unset, assertion present : IdentityError: MKT_CREATIVE_IAP_AUDIENCE is not configured; cannot verify IAP assertion\naudience unset, bare curl         : IdentityError: MKT_CREATIVE_IAP_AUDIENCE is not configured; cannot verify IAP assertion\nheader is ''   ''                   : IdentityError: assertion is not a compact JWS or JWE, so it carries no readable algorithm header\ngoogle-auth blocked               : ModuleNotFoundError: No module named ''google.auth.transport''\n```\n\nThe audience was already checked before the header here, so the bare curl did\nname the unset variable. What it did not do was carry a status that said the fault was the\ndeployment''s.\n\n`api/security.py` answered 401 \"authentication required\" for the first two alike, so an\noperator was told authentication had failed when no credential would have helped.\n\nThree further observations, same worktree method:\n\n* `tests/unit/test_iap_refusal_split.py` does not import against that tree at all: neither\n  `EndUserAuthUnavailableError` nor the two `Iap*Error` types existed.\n* With only those types injected and the pre-fix behaviour left standing: 8 failed, 3 passed.\n* On the fixed tree with the two `except` branches in `api/security.py` reordered: 1 failed,\n  10 passed, and the one failure is\n  `test_the_api_answers_a_deployment_failure_with_its_own_status_and_message`, answering 401\n  where 503 is owed. That is the subclass-ordering hazard, executed.\n\nDocumentation only. No source, test or lockfile is touched.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ashish Awasthi <72717+ashishawasthi@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbw8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKOUQAKG+IqNzqdFv3aNNbKTwA7Ir\n4+AuXA1CA0poKpvphjHbSjarX7999iwfDgAlqgj2dUBe9u5tWOiqUiYquLqvnt7F\nwCMqyXfotVprZlM8UBEv2w8ECKAE2A4Js8wN70WX3vW9ekcz59cAwLth6RxQG+UM\nftgoV6PTH0UCcPXuNXUk/T1xDMhUyiYtuIrHdw5f37XcXwpySBYoa06jDENoObB7\nGYlZBD2jI2SdEeONqkgSnBnO59f5P5bhRwMGLnDTpzeA9jkDiPWRzwNRXYUi2C1X\nQ2rvuviRSgmVP9aAB8pXyg26pBOlq0D5Kk5zvl2gsNxTyhvC36lggItD56DH1F46\n0FB9u24tk9qrHPu7H67SIrEFzpvtKl4bVrvgE7ey+OAy1cud3QqALLB94jxrzlsU\nJBGeGbw5v6yycadMxZgtxfZOWuIARPLSU7Yhn28fSt8ByaX/6cnlfCyZuo7WaVoy\nMHuMD06pm6kPYB4Ps0VQSZwI5vE9tCtuHScJSE5UhobBFuJCKGZ9zs5Rj5nBB/us\nltvkvvallAZ0ko/nSCRjJYD7uK09ZqT1AOh152Jh0zSY5SB3/89+5nyK+vMqX5M5\nAEuCsHyVOu5nYyIGTuA5eD/UwCImOySqaMV4oabvzpJS3LKgxS6iYQud/owiOiAt\nepX6prMvlJQMp8jw+Qdx\n=BYvx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T16:01:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/2df652f34c6d582782752fc1714522c06b0e8889","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh-TdoAKDJkZjY1MmYzNGM2ZDU4Mjc4Mjc1MmZjMTcxNDUyMmMwNmIwZTg4ODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/aa46a0c7a9134d339989ec3dd6e3e13ff3d916a1","sha":"aa46a0c7a9134d339989ec3dd6e3e13ff3d916a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/aa46a0c7a9134d339989ec3dd6e3e13ff3d916a1"}],"sha":"2df652f34c6d582782752fc1714522c06b0e8889","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/2df652f34c6d582782752fc1714522c06b0e8889"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/aa46a0c7a9134d339989ec3dd6e3e13ff3d916a1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:47:27Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:47:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Pin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#13)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","tree":{"sha":"601b17c044e1299a9589f30873eefd95c8148529","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/601b17c044e1299a9589f30873eefd95c8148529"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/aa46a0c7a9134d339989ec3dd6e3e13ff3d916a1","verification":{"payload":"tree 601b17c044e1299a9589f30873eefd95c8148529\nparent 73fab2a07dc7f5db25b4ebba69937da2c74f48be\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787672847 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787672847 +0800\n\nPin hex-service-kit v0.0.4 (#13)\n\nv0.0.4 closes a silent widening at a tenancy boundary in the federation module.\n_hosted_domain fell back to the email domain before the policy was consulted, so\ntenant_from_hosted_domain meant \"the hd claim OR the mail domain is the tenant\": a\ntoken carrying no hd went from no tenant to a tenant named after its mail domain.\n\nThis repository does not call principal_from_iap_claims, so it was never exposed to\nthat widening; the bump is for one pin across the fleet, and so the fixed function\nis the one available when the claim half is adopted. It also carries the assurance\nand subject-principal knobs that adoption needs.\n\nLockfiles regenerated by fleet-deps.py, never hand-edited. Gate run against the\nnewly installed pin rather than against whatever was already in the venv.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbkPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACNUQAHbk3Jy2IGt2oE3+vE2on4Mg\nIw+oAvAanTqitWARPExgE36DEZud992lJx4WAj1JNINHPOPmGOr9+5P6cUf2wA1m\ndB+9q8KdlMuZDi5RG0F/Kdgiy7Dlwj8AbG1k/RdP3U5oNKic3cbKmGg5DB6/mbBw\n99OKNXnKV0cQqHywliIMmHyqnbXTK1DohfZuOlR1m9vP3u2lySTKdIkA9qakoO13\nK+mHMsVjtys/Rt2XyYYgbD8Puu/pXJVXUx+K/+0nc+qAxkLPduKhfTk7GK1rUEA5\n2Vt1TCICx8f5Y5FRblJwCCd5AmVzEpo3ZQghlzsisD2aoRc5HHOXfsm2Y4gPmt65\nHBo41NcwGrCsAdLdb6KQZzbOhCCgAEoXP1ixQY+LqO5Tv6qxJuSYf+SRW6XIWmt1\n5CrEZyDYNbb/OzJ9mcIFmBZemNngqxhuYSxCLGOaGmD6V8sDEDPgB3uE9GQF4okY\nxWpKqgRmNzFtPrhX0YDU9cNodnBB/1ONsWyGIl9gtDEL4K5+t1HQrGj6FRPTm2zL\n3yIGcHRZG3jXl6hlzm2UWJTAhtCW6qqAI6hFIn9eMvRuUIKjCXUu8gR+lgI4sw7B\ntqzLvVMrP7NOKLs5DeatskpjxwmBOBRRIuUtZhq8G8CW00x54Dm01NsOeoKUw9GS\n4ZOp+xMN35lItHcQ2a8C\n=Kgly\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T15:47:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/aa46a0c7a9134d339989ec3dd6e3e13ff3d916a1","node_id":"C_kwDOUAh-TdoAKGFhNDZhMGM3YTkxMzRkMzM5OTg5ZWMzZGQ2ZTNlMTNmZjNkOTE2YTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/portable-genai/creative-studio/commit/73fab2a07dc7f5db25b4ebba69937da2c74f48be","sha":"73fab2a07dc7f5db25b4ebba69937da2c74f48be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/73fab2a07dc7f5db25b4ebba69937da2c74f48be"}],"sha":"aa46a0c7a9134d339989ec3dd6e3e13ff3d916a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/aa46a0c7a9134d339989ec3dd6e3e13ff3d916a1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72717?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ashishawasthi","id":72717,"login":"ashishawasthi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNzE3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashishawasthi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/commits/73fab2a07dc7f5db25b4ebba69937da2c74f48be/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:18:11Z","email":"ashish.awasthi@gmail.com","name":"Ashish"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T15:18:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Close the three IAP refusal gaps and bind the transport facts to v0.0.3 (#12)\n\nThis repository carries adapters/gcp/iap_identity.py, the earlier of the two IAP adapter shapes\nin this fleet. Measured against adapters/gcp/identity.py, which most of the fleet carries, it was\nweaker in three ways. All three were reachable with no cloud SDK, no credential and no network,\nand all three are closed here.\n\n**A configuration failure reported as an authentication failure.** An unconfigured audience\nraised a plain IdentityError, which api/security.py answers 401 \"authentication required\". An\noperator reads that and goes hunting for a missing credential; no credential would have helped.\nIt was also checked SECOND, after the assertion header, so the deployment-level failure was only\never reported to callers who already had an assertion. The operator probing with curl and no\nheader got \"missing IAP assertion header\" and learned nothing. The audience check now comes\nfirst and raises IapAudienceUnconfiguredError, an EndUserAuthUnavailableError carrying\nhttp_status 503, and api/security.py answers with that status and that message.\n\n**A whitespace-only header taking a different path.** ctx.header(...) was read without .strip().\nA header a proxy or a deployment template rendered blank is truthy, so it skipped the\nmissing-header refusal and was refused further down by the algorithm pin, which reports a\nmalformed token for what is actually an absent one.\n\n**A missing extra crashing rather than refusing.** The lazy google-auth import sat outside any\ntry. Without the [gcp] extra it raised ModuleNotFoundError out of resolve, past get_principal,\nand FastAPI answered a bare 500 per request. It now raises IapVerifierUnavailableError, also 503.\n\nThe three IAP transport facts are also rebound from hex_service_kit.federation rather than\nre-declared, and the pin moves to @v0.0.3, relocked with org-metadata scripts/fleet-deps.py\nrefresh (commit d28baa1c). No lockfile was hand-edited.\n\n## Observed failing first\n\nAgainst the adapter exactly as it shipped, offline:\n\n    (a) audience unconfigured\n      with an assertion header : IdentityError: <PREFIX>_IAP_AUDIENCE is not configured; cannot verify IAP assertion\n      with NO header (operator): IdentityError: missing IAP assertion header; request did not pass through IAP\n          both plain IdentityError, so api/security.py answers 401 for both\n    (b) header is ''   ''        : IdentityError: assertion is not a compact JWS or JWE, so it carries no readable algorithm header\n          refused as a malformed token, not as a missing one\n    (c) google-auth blocked    : ModuleNotFoundError: No module named ''google.auth.transport''\n          not an IdentityError, so it escapes get_principal: a bare 500\n\ntests/unit/test_iap_refusal_split.py is the same three paths as assertions, plus two that prove\napi/security.py answers the deployment failure 503 with the operator''s message while an ordinary\nrefusal is still a bare 401 that tells a caller nothing they could forge with.\n\n## What is NOT changed\n\nThe fourth difference between the two adapter families, the principals tuple, is deliberately\nleft alone. This adapter grants user:<subject>; the identity.py family grants nothing at all. It\nis THIS one that agrees with hex_service_kit.federation.principal_from_iap_claims, so changing it\ntoward the other family would remove a verified identity''s own principal. The divergence is\nrecorded in the test module rather than closed in the wrong direction.\n\nThis also does not adopt principal_from_iap_claims. Executing this adapter and the kit function\nagainst the same claim sets, with FederationPolicy(tenant_from_hosted_domain=True), shows four\nremaining disagreements, so the tenant and principal half stays local. Details in the wave-2 report.\n\n## Gate\n\nmake gate, exit 0, 373 passed 1 deselected 373 passed 1 deselected. Offline, with the v0.0.3 lock installed.","tree":{"sha":"416edc167135bcc75a2e2ad2796169ce334be9f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/trees/416edc167135bcc75a2e2ad2796169ce334be9f4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/portable-genai/creative-studio/git/commits/73fab2a07dc7f5db25b4ebba69937da2c74f48be","verification":{"payload":"tree 416edc167135bcc75a2e2ad2796169ce334be9f4\nparent d1a789c89ec9db5404c3e6052d2af00c1eae9e04\nauthor Ashish <ashish.awasthi@gmail.com> 1787671091 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787671091 +0800\n\nClose the three IAP refusal gaps and bind the transport facts to v0.0.3 (#12)\n\nThis repository carries adapters/gcp/iap_identity.py, the earlier of the two IAP adapter shapes\nin this fleet. Measured against adapters/gcp/identity.py, which most of the fleet carries, it was\nweaker in three ways. All three were reachable with no cloud SDK, no credential and no network,\nand all three are closed here.\n\n**A configuration failure reported as an authentication failure.** An unconfigured audience\nraised a plain IdentityError, which api/security.py answers 401 \"authentication required\". An\noperator reads that and goes hunting for a missing credential; no credential would have helped.\nIt was also checked SECOND, after the assertion header, so the deployment-level failure was only\never reported to callers who already had an assertion. The operator probing with curl and no\nheader got \"missing IAP assertion header\" and learned nothing. The audience check now comes\nfirst and raises IapAudienceUnconfiguredError, an EndUserAuthUnavailableError carrying\nhttp_status 503, and api/security.py answers with that status and that message.\n\n**A whitespace-only header taking a different path.** ctx.header(...) was read without .strip().\nA header a proxy or a deployment template rendered blank is truthy, so it skipped the\nmissing-header refusal and was refused further down by the algorithm pin, which reports a\nmalformed token for what is actually an absent one.\n\n**A missing extra crashing rather than refusing.** The lazy google-auth import sat outside any\ntry. Without the [gcp] extra it raised ModuleNotFoundError out of resolve, past get_principal,\nand FastAPI answered a bare 500 per request. It now raises IapVerifierUnavailableError, also 503.\n\nThe three IAP transport facts are also rebound from hex_service_kit.federation rather than\nre-declared, and the pin moves to @v0.0.3, relocked with org-metadata scripts/fleet-deps.py\nrefresh (commit d28baa1c). No lockfile was hand-edited.\n\n## Observed failing first\n\nAgainst the adapter exactly as it shipped, offline:\n\n    (a) audience unconfigured\n      with an assertion header : IdentityError: <PREFIX>_IAP_AUDIENCE is not configured; cannot verify IAP assertion\n      with NO header (operator): IdentityError: missing IAP assertion header; request did not pass through IAP\n          both plain IdentityError, so api/security.py answers 401 for both\n    (b) header is ''   ''        : IdentityError: assertion is not a compact JWS or JWE, so it carries no readable algorithm header\n          refused as a malformed token, not as a missing one\n    (c) google-auth blocked    : ModuleNotFoundError: No module named ''google.auth.transport''\n          not an IdentityError, so it escapes get_principal: a bare 500\n\ntests/unit/test_iap_refusal_split.py is the same three paths as assertions, plus two that prove\napi/security.py answers the deployment failure 503 with the operator''s message while an ordinary\nrefusal is still a bare 401 that tells a caller nothing they could forge with.\n\n## What is NOT changed\n\nThe fourth difference between the two adapter families, the principals tuple, is deliberately\nleft alone. This adapter grants user:<subject>; the identity.py family grants nothing at all. It\nis THIS one that agrees with hex_service_kit.federation.principal_from_iap_claims, so changing it\ntoward the other family would remove a verified identity''s own principal. The divergence is\nrecorded in the test module rather than closed in the wrong direction.\n\nThis also does not adopt principal_from_iap_claims. Executing this adapter and the kit function\nagainst the same claim sets, with FederationPolicy(tenant_from_hosted_domain=True), shows four\nremaining disagreements, so the tenant and principal half stays local. Details in the wave-2 report.\n\n## Gate\n\nmake gate, exit 0, 373 passed 1 deselected 373 passed 1 deselected. Offline, with the v0.0.3 lock installed.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjbIzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAO3gQAICyK8VpTuvetA9kp0VPmhwz\n5oO+328Gvxgy5TsRPSsmflWfI3YthOIQY+UnELNZP4FXXRtKvc1nIJlui+FjDiKU\nT5JgPAWhO8vzip8GKyOkIlW9no7T9hVkt8eKVFezdRAP4VfCcSaj6NNPc4BUFt2i\nVkEzXN/qBCGJ5v3w+GXkaxW3+3L55RsozKInol33PTVgTwffi+23Cg4edRgyNbCp\nrCYJ5npwSbOuBemdfhM4AXSruXyDkCcs6fBkTbiAT6jhqBXT/NBscNcTOuNUziQX\nkssAvVnvTAOKXb5oMIhPVsU7Np+HoRpFg+BK5Wd2/GYvYRNP9spkETJDHmqf556r\naV0+vd3LolJUNs9hXHK7dh